postage stamps: mementos from my trip around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four Septembers ago, my husband and I were bundled up in a yurt in the Gobi Desert at the end of a trip around the world. Our journey had included 21 countries, both one- and two-humped camels, swims in the Nile and the Euphrates, and an escape from a herd of wild elephants. It had also included at least a dozen visits to the post offices of the world. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adventures With Post Offices', 'kicker': 'Private Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Postal Service and Post Offices', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T01:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ramona Ausubel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ramona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ausubel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a553460f-ec7a-54ff-ad85-af8c799ddf29', 'word_count': 1020, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a553460f-ec7a-54ff-ad85-af8c799ddf29'}, {'abstract': 'Stories like Donal Ryan’s hearten struggling writers and remind us that there is no science to evaluating literary work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/opinion/47-rejections-then-the-booker-long-list.html', 'snippet': 'Stories like Donal Ryan’s hearten struggling writers and remind us that there is no science to evaluating literary work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donal Ryan, a civil servant from Limerick, Ireland, wrote two novels. He sent them to agents and publishers and got back 47 rejections over three years. Finally an intern at Lilliput Press in Dublin fished “The Thing About December” out of the slush pile. Around the same time, an editor at Doubleday Ireland took interest in “The Spinning Heart.” Suddenly Mr. Ryan had a two-book deal, and from there his fortunes only improved. The Booker Foundation announced last week that “The Spinning Heart” had made the cut for the Man Booker Prize long list. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '47 Rejections, Then the Booker Long List', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '47 Rejections, Then the Booker Long List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Donal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Man Booker Prize', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T01:33:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e37af148-3fdb-5ce5-9e4b-82faca5f24cc', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e37af148-3fdb-5ce5-9e4b-82faca5f24cc'}, {'abstract': 'Reporters have been left searching for words as images emerge of vast tracts of ruins where, until recently, the vibrant residential neighborhood of Khalidiya stood in the country’s third-largest city, Homs.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/07/31/stunning-images-of-destroyed-syrian-city/', 'snippet': 'Reporters have been left searching for words as images emerge of vast tracts of ruins where, until recently, the vibrant residential neighborhood of Khalidiya stood in the country’s third-largest city, Homs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1982, after President Hafez al-Assad’s forces leveled whole sections of Syria’s fourth-largest city, Hama, to suppress a revolt, the first foreign journalists allowed to view the rubble were shocked by the scale of the destruction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/world/middleeast/31lede_homs2/31lede_homs2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/31/world/middleeast/31lede_homs2/31lede_homs2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/world/middleeast/31lede_homs2/31lede_homs2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/world/middleeast/31lede_homs2/31lede_homs2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1473, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/world/middleeast/31lede_homs2/31lede_homs2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/31/world/middleeast/31lede_homs2/31lede_homs2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/31/world/middleeast/31lede_homs2/31lede_homs2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stunning Images of Destroyed Syrian City', 'kicker': 'The Led