eet away, Master-at-Arms First Class Leroy Williams Jr. found himself flying backward in an angry cloud of dirt and debris. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dog of War Makes Ultimate Sacrifice for Sailor', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Improvised Explosive Devices', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Service Dogs and Other Animals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kandahar (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yuma (Ariz)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T02:51:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elliott Garber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elliott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fac67c4-32d3-52ae-be45-b9d60e69f2e3', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fac67c4-32d3-52ae-be45-b9d60e69f2e3'}, {'abstract': 'The manufacturing index, provided by the Chinese authorities, indicated that recent small-scale economic support measures in Beijing might be having some effect on demand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/business/global/chinese-manufacturing-unexpectedly-strengthens.html', 'snippet': 'The manufacturing index, provided by the Chinese authorities, indicated that recent small-scale economic support measures in Beijing might be having some effect on demand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — A manufacturing index published by the Chinese authorities on Thursday provided an unexpectedly solid reading for July but did little to dispel the picture of an economy that is cooling more rapidly than many analysts had expected just months ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Reports Increase in Manufacturing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Reports Increase in Manufacturing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T02:52:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bettina Wassener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bettina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wassener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/722dca2b-48c0-55d7-a3fb-66f121b03468', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/722dca2b-48c0-55d7-a3fb-66f121b03468'}, {'abstract': 'Violence caused by the drug war in Mexico may be abating, making it the first decline in six years, according to figures released by the government this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/world/americas/a-modest-decline-of-homicides-in-mexico.html', 'snippet': 'Violence caused by the drug war in Mexico may be abating, making it the first decline in six years, according to figures released by the government this week.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Violence caused by the drug war in Mexico may be abating, according to figures released this week by the government. The data showed a modest decline in homicides in 2012, the first in six years. Mexico’s census agency, compiling reports of murders from the 32 federal entities, said there were 26,037 homicides last year, a 4.3 percent decline from 27,213 in 2011, which was the most in recent years. The homicide rate was 22 per 100,000 residents, a decline from 24 per 100,000 the previous year. The homicide rate in the United States is 4.7 per 100,000 people, according to United Nations figures, but Mexico’s rate was far lower than several other countries in the hemisphere. A number of analysts believe this data provides a good barometer of overall violence, which had surged because of infighting among criminal gangs and the government’s efforts to suppress them. In 2007, there were 8,867 homicides, the lowest number in the last six years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Modest Decline of Homicides in Mexico', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: A Modest Decline in Homicides', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Archibold, Randal C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T02:54:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4104d83b-0f0e-5bf7-9f54-809d4e495610', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4104d83b-0f0e-5bf7-9f54-809d4e495610'}, {'abstract': 'After months in which candidates have sat beside one another at a seemingly endless series of forums, most of them polite, and few of them memorable, the campaigns are going negative.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/nyregion/primary-is-getting-closer-cue-the-negative-phase.html', 'snippet': 'After months in which candidates have sat beside one another at a seemingly endless series of forums, most of them polite, and few of them memorable, the campaigns are going negative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With just six weeks to go before the primary, the slow burning races for New York City mayor and comptroller have suddenly turned hot.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/nyregion/negative1/negative1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/01/nyregion/negative1/negative1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/nyregion/negative1/negative1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/nyregion/negative1/negative1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1146, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None