ganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8326fa3-f5c2-5360-9d45-1e393fe88c74', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8326fa3-f5c2-5360-9d45-1e393fe88c74'}, {'abstract': 'Last year, a record 36 percent of those 18 to 31 were living in their parents’ home, according to a new Pew Research Center analysis of Census Bureau data.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/millennials-in-their-parents-basements/', 'snippet': 'Last year, a record 36 percent of those 18 to 31 were living in their parents’ home, according to a new Pew Research Center analysis of Census Bureau data.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, a record 36 percent of people 18 to 31 years old — roughly the age range of the generation nicknamed the millennials — were living in their parents’ homes, according to a new Pew Research Center analysis of Census Bureau data. That compares to 32 percent of their same-aged counterparts in 2007, the year the recession began.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Millennials, in Their Parents’ Basements', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T15:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11754c54-85a4-58ed-9744-8a95d11b5ff1', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11754c54-85a4-58ed-9744-8a95d11b5ff1'}, {'abstract': 'Lebanon’s poor see war exiles from Syria as competitors for state services.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/sour-on-syrian-refugees/', 'snippet': 'Lebanon’s poor see war exiles from Syria as competitors for state services.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT — The few Lebanese children who beg regularly around Hamra, a lively neighborhood full of universities, shops and bars, have been pretending recently that they come from Syria. “We’re refugees,” they tell those they approach for money, mainly foreigners like me, hoping to evoke some special sympathy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sour on Syrian Refugees', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T15:04:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Birke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Birke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/402854e3-abbd-573c-8bd4-6f5daaffaba6', 'word_count': 691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/402854e3-abbd-573c-8bd4-6f5daaffaba6'}, {'abstract': 'Guest blogger Mike Abramowitz argues that the Responsibility to Protect, which urges outside intervention to stop mass killing, is in danger of becoming nothing more than a platitude.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/who-will-stand-up-for-the-responsibility-to-protect/', 'snippet': 'Guest blogger Mike Abramowitz argues that the Responsibility to Protect, which urges outside intervention to stop mass killing, is in danger of becoming nothing more than a platitude.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, during her confirmation hearing to be our next Ambassador to the United Nations, Samantha Power was asked about a concept most Americans have never heard of, let alone understand—the Responsibility to Protect. Her cautious response spoke volumes about the ambivalence in the United States government towards a new idea that has gained traction as a tool for addressing conscience-shocking atrocities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Will Stand Up for the Responsibility to Protect?', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T15:19:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Abramowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abramowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/512d4425-f5b2-54fb-b03b-9680028f85b7', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/512d4425-f5b2-54fb-b03b-9680028f85b7'}, {'abstract': 'Fall collections offer seasonal staples with stripes and color blocking in these neutral tones.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/market-report-black-and-white-and-gray-all-over/', 'snippet': 'Fall collections offer seasonal staples with stripes and color blocking in these neutral tones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fall collections now hitting stores include a wealth of seasonal staples with black, white and gray stripes or color blocking that project an air of discreet chic. The elegant arch of a stiletto from Dior and the modern curves on a ring from Cartier add some softness to these graphic swatches, while the shape of a J.W. Anderson sweater and crisp tailoring on a pair of Aquilano-Rimondi pants provide welcome structure.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Market Report | Black and White and Gray All Over', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Market Report: Black Pairs Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Jonathan William (1984- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dior, Christian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cartier SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chloe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Dior SA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T15:22:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edeedd90-67ac-504f-9344-7735c4ac9d8f', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edeedd90-67ac-504f-9344-7735c4ac9d8f'}, {'abstract': 'Depending on timing, there could be competition for investor demand between two British banks as both weigh share sales.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/lloyds-poses-front-running-risk-for-barclays/', 'snippet': 'Depending on timing, there could be competition for investor demand between two British banks as both weigh share sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who’s going to win, Antonio or Antony? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lloyds Poses Front-Running Risk for Barclays', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horta-Osorio, Antonio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jenkins, Antony P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lloyds Banking Group Plc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T15:43:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Hay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/283834b4-af2b-5752-8e85-563ae866164d', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/283834b4-af2b-5752-8e85-563ae866164d'}, {'abstract': 'With many people choosing open kitchens, selecting fixtures takes on more importance. The once-inconspicuous kitchen faucet is now anything but.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/garden/100000002368611/kitchen-faucet-basics.html', 'snippet': 'With many people choosing open kitchens, selecting fixtures takes on more importance. The once-inconspicuous kitchen faucet is now anything but.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With many people choosing open kitchens, selecting fixtures takes on more importance. The once-inconspicuous kitchen faucet is now anything but.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/garden/video-kitc