rents-need-to-worry-more-about-college-choice/', 'snippet': 'Admissions test scores aside, a study finds a huge difference in the completion rate of those who attend a selective college and those who attend an open-access college.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a novel thought: most American families worry too little about what kind of college their children attend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maybe Most Parents Need to Worry More About College Choice', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Aid (Education)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Georgetown University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T16:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af6eb7af-ea21-5c78-a791-18df49803870', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af6eb7af-ea21-5c78-a791-18df49803870'}, {'abstract': 'Our laws on electronic surveillance remain stuck somewhere between the 1950s and the 1980s.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/cell-phones-and-the-expectation-of-privacy/', 'snippet': 'Our laws on electronic surveillance remain stuck somewhere between the 1950s and the 1980s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ninety-one percent of American adults now own a cell phone, according to a survey by the Pew Research Center. Among those 44 and younger, ownership rises to more than 95 percent. The cell phone is as ubiquitous a piece of consumer technology as we have ever had, and may be the most rapidly adopted in history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cell Phones and the Expectation of Privacy', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T16:01:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Wegman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wegman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1dfe3bb-1245-511a-b6f6-a6c1c1cf35de', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1dfe3bb-1245-511a-b6f6-a6c1c1cf35de'}, {'abstract': 'The South Korean, who is seeking her fourth victory in a major this season, three-putted two of her last three holes at the Women’s British Open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/sports/disappointing-finish-slows-inbee-park.html', 'snippet': 'The South Korean, who is seeking her fourth victory in a major this season, three-putted two of her last three holes at the Women’s British Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. ANDREWS, Scotland — Inbee Park’s second shot on the 16th hole Thursday at the Women’s British Open landed in one of the Old Course’s infamous pot bunkers, her ball sitting like a pimple on its face. Park’s emotions on the course run the gamut from A to B, but what her body language and expressions never convey was revealed clearly in her conversation with her caddie, Brad Beecher, on how to play the next shot.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/sports/Y-LPGA/Y-LPGA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/02/sports/Y-LPGA/Y-LPGA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/sports/Y-LPGA/Y-LPGA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/sports/Y-LPGA/Y-LPGA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/sports/Y-LPGA/Y-LPGA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/02/sports/Y-LPGA/Y-LPGA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/sports/Y-LPGA/Y-LPGA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Park’s Quest for a Record Begins, but Part of Her Game Deserts Her ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Park’s Quest for a Record Begins, but Part of Her Game Deserts Her', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's British Open (Golf)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Park, I