ied last month after eating a free lunch provided by their primary school. According to a forensics report, the potato and soya curry they were served on July 16 was contaminated with monocrotophos, a highly toxic compound commonly used as a pesticide.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Root of the Poisonous Tree', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T16:19:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anjali Mody', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anjali', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0a95831-ac90-5c3c-8972-7b9d1ec4a8ce', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0a95831-ac90-5c3c-8972-7b9d1ec4a8ce'}, {'abstract': 'Beyoncé’s “Mrs. Carter Show” tours top at the Izod Center was no tribute to wifely self-effacement, but a celebration of a high-achieving Everywoman balancing love and independence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/arts/music/beyonces-mrs-carter-show-at-izod-center.html', 'snippet': 'Beyoncé’s “Mrs. Carter Show” tours top at the Izod Center was no tribute to wifely self-effacement, but a celebration of a high-achieving Everywoman balancing love and independence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — At first it seemed that Beyoncé was taking one of her pop-star nicknames, Queen Bey, all too seriously. Her show at the Izod Center here on Wednesday night opened with a bombastic orchestral dirge and a video presenting her as a Marie Antoinette figure in a Gothic palace, receiving a crown. But as the queen’s female retinue — wearing white unitards and hoops without skirts — reappeared onstage, the dirge segued into the martial beat of “Run the World (Girls).” Beyoncé, shaking the epaulets on her shoulders and flipping her hair, was taking power not for herself but for her entire gender. The set that followed was not about aristocratic aloofness, but about energy, empathy and a beaming smile.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02beyonce-span/02beyonce-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02beyonce-span/02beyonce-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02beyonce-span/02beyonce-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02beyonce-span/02beyonce-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02beyonce-span/02beyonce-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02beyonce-span/02beyonce-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02beyonce-span/02beyonce-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Enough Resilience to Fill an Arena', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Enough Resilience To Fill an Arena', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Izod Center (East Rutherford, NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knowles, Beyonce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T16:19:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d6ab3b8-93bb-5761-9d37-04ac6f627b3f', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d6ab3b8-93bb-5761-9d37-04ac6f627b3f'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/the-gun-report-august-1-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Did you hear that after seven years, the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms finally has a new chief, B. Todd Jones? Yes, it does. The bureau had been leaderless through the entire Obama administration, thanks to the usual coalition of Republican Senators and the National Rifle Association, which preferred the A.T.F. to be as toothless as possible. Obama’s first-term nominee never even came to a vote.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: August 1, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T16:19:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34760009-65cc-554f-afef-b8117edd5637', 'word_count': 1397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34760009-65cc-554f-afef-b8117edd5637'}, {'abstract': 'A large study finds further evidence that anemia — a common condition in the elderly — increases the risk for dementia.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/anemia-tied-to-dementia-risk/', 'snippet': 'A large study finds further evidence that anemia — a common condition in the elderly — increases the risk for dementia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A large study has found further evidence that anemia — a deficiency of red blood cells and a common condition in the elderly — increases the risk for dementia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/health/well_behavior/well_behavior-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 217, 'width': 216, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/health/well_behavior/well_behavior-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 217, 'width': 216, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/health/well_behavior/well_behavior-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/19/health/well_behavior/well_behavior-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/health/well_behavior/well_behavior-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Anemia Tied to Dementia Risk', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANEMIA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T16:26:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcde42d6-1f4a-52b8-a193-142747f27376', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcde42d6-1f4a-52b8-a193-142747f27376'}, {'abstract': 'An appeals court ruling last week will make it harder for private equity funds to walk away from the unfunded pension liabilities of a portfolio company that goes bankrupt. But the case may have implications for tax law.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/sun-capital-court-ruling-threatens-private-equity-structure/', 'snippet': 'An appeals court ruling last week will make it harder for private equity funds to walk away from the unfunded pension liabilities of a portfolio company that goes bankrupt. But the case may have implications for tax law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Think twice before you bet against the widows and orphans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sun Capital Court Ruling Threatens Structure of Private Equity', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank':