pg', 'height': 507, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/travel/video-frugal-summer13-3/video-frugal-summer13-3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/travel/video-frugal-summer13-3/video-frugal-summer13-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/01/travel/video-frugal-summer13-3/video-frugal-summer13-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/travel/video-frugal-summer13-3/video-frugal-summer13-3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Ozarks, Finding the Local Groove', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ozark Mountains', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Road Trips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kugel, Seth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARKANSAS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liquor', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T17:02:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'John Woo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/ef4640e7-3d77-571e-a73d-11f2de43317c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/ef4640e7-3d77-571e-a73d-11f2de43317c'}, {'abstract': 'In Part 3 of his summer road trip, the Frugal Traveler hops between Missouri and Arkansas, dropping in on a fiddle jam, sipping spirits and tuning into the region’s relaxed groove.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/travel/music-and-moonshine-in-the-mellow-ozarks.html', 'snippet': 'In Part 3 of his summer road trip, the Frugal Traveler hops between Missouri and Arkansas, dropping in on a fiddle jam, sipping spirits and tuning into the region’s relaxed groove.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dinnertime comes early in the Ozarks, even during the long days of summer. So after I lingered over smoked trout, fried chicken liver and blackberry cobbler at Rockbridge Trout and Game Ranch’s friendly restaurant, wandered around its barn-red 19th-century grist mill and drove off to look for a motel, there was still daylight to spare. At 8 p.m., as I reached the utterly rural intersection of Missouri Routes 5 and 95, the sun had still not quite yet set. It was what photographers and filmmakers call the golden hour, when the last light of the day gives whatever land it falls on a temporary visual upgrade. So I stopped, parked, and sat on the hood of my car. Sloping pastures glinted and cattle grazed halfway to the horizon, beyond them purplish pink clouds hovered over barely distinguishable low-slung hills. The Ozarks were, finally, stunning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/travel/01-frugal-ozarks-span/01-frugal-ozarks-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/01/travel/01-frugal-ozarks-span/01-frugal-ozarks-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/travel/01-frugal-ozarks-span/01-frugal-ozarks-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/travel/01-frugal-ozarks-span/01-frugal-ozarks-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 1184, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/travel/01-frugal-ozarks-span/01-frugal-ozarks-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/01/travel/01-frugal-ozarks-span/01-frugal-ozarks-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/travel/01-frugal-ozarks-span/01-frugal-ozarks-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Music and Moonshine in the Mellow Ozarks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ozark Mountains', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liquor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARKANSAS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Canoes and Canoeing', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T17:03:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31fd2fe1-0cfd-58bd-ab3c-a2acb066f7ae', 'word_count': 1569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31fd2fe1-0cfd-58bd-ab3c-a2acb066f7ae'}, {'abstract': '“The Canyons,” Paul Schrader’s new film, written by Bret Easton Ellis and starring Lindsay Lohan, is a dispiriting work that addresses the dirty business of making movies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/movies/the-canyons-is-an-erotic-thriller-with-lindsay-lohan.html', 'snippet': '“The Canyons,” Paul Schrader’s new film, written by Bret Easton Ellis and starring Lindsay Lohan, is a dispiriting work that addresses the dirty business of making movies.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Canyons” — directed by Paul Schrader, written by Bret Easton Ellis and starring Lindsay Lohan — is a dispiriting, unpleasurable work punctuated with flashes of vitalizing vulgarity. It isn’t a good movie in terms of the conventional norms (acting for starters), but it also exhibits a crude integrity. If you take the characters seriously or at their word, a mistake for such a dissembling, venal group, you may think that this is just another story about the dirty business of making movies. Hollywood types have been rolling around in the muck about as long as there’s been an industry (that’s what made Sammy run); the twist here is that no one here seems to care anymore.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cellphone Gets Its Close-Up', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cellphone Gets Its Close-Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lohan, Lindsay', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schrader, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deen, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellis, Bret Easton', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Canyons (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T17:11:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8311df8d-b0be-5eb1-87ac-4bc0b130f153', 'word_count': 1138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8311df8d-b0be-5eb1-87ac-4bc0b130f153'}, {'abstract': 'Russia’s decision was absurd.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/does-snowden-deserve-asylum/', 'snippet': 'Russia’s decision was absurd.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard not to feel for Edward Snowden. A young and perhaps not terribly worldly-wise man, he revealed documents to the world that contained information about government misbehavior that was of vital interest to Americans, as well as citizens of other countries. Being stuck in the departure zone at Moscow’s Sheremetyevo Airport cannot have been thrilling.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Does Snowden Deserve Asylum?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 1, 'major': 