season of “Breaking Bad,” the best (by far, since “Mad Men” is in clear decline) of the current crop of anti-heroic television dramas, it’s interesting to read Emily Nussbaum’s case for why Carrie Bradshaw of “Sex in the City” deserves a place in the pantheon of television protagonists that includes Tony Soprano, Walter White, Don Draper, Al Swearengen and other so-called\xa0“difficult men.”\xa0Nussbaum’s point, and it’s a good one, is that Carrie’s arc on “Sex and the City” was often more troubled, and her character’s development more complicated, than the frothy Jimmy Choo stereotypes about the show would lead one to suggest. She writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carrie Bradshaw, Anti-Heroine?', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Breaking Bad (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Sarah Jessica', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T19:46:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bba4ea6e-1343-593a-83c2-927cec93ea9c', 'word_count': 1325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bba4ea6e-1343-593a-83c2-927cec93ea9c'}, {'abstract': 'The press secretary, Jay Carney, said the Obama administration was “extremely disappointed” with the Russian government’s granting temporary asylum to Edward J. Snowden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000002369122/white-house-reacts-to-snowden-asylum.html', '