els (whom he called his “living brushes”) to roll themselves in blue paint and press their bodies against sheets of paper lining the walls and floors. When the music stopped, the models froze.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02JPVOGEL_SPAN/JPVOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02JPVOGEL_SPAN/JPVOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 424}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02JPVOGEL_SPAN/JPVOGEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02JPVOGEL_SPAN/JPVOGEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 901, 'width': 1275, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02JPVOGEL_SPAN/JPVOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02JPVOGEL_SPAN/JPVOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02JPVOGEL_SPAN/JPVOGEL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yves Klein’s ‘Monotone’ Symphony Is Headed to New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Artist’s Symphony\r\nWill Reverberate Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None},