ington and Mark Wahlberg, one of the better odd couples to bond and bicker since Mel met Danny. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Good Guys (or So They Seem) Behaving Badly', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Good Guys (Or So They Seem) Behaving Badly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washington, Denzel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wahlberg, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kormakur, Baltasar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T20:49:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7abca1b2-2152-5a16-86a1-2ca3a5ebf81f', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7abca1b2-2152-5a16-86a1-2ca3a5ebf81f'}, {'abstract': 'John A. Koskinen, who managed a bankrupt Freddie Mac at the height of the financial crisis, is President Obama’s choice to lead the troubled Internal Revenue Service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/us/politics/ex-chairman-of-freddie-mac-nominated-to-lead-irs.html', 'snippet': 'John A. Koskinen, who managed a bankrupt Freddie Mac at the height of the financial crisis, is President Obama’s choice to lead the troubled Internal Revenue Service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama said on Thursday that he would nominate John A. Koskinen, a widely respected manager who took charge of a bankrupt Freddie Mac, to head another troubled institution, the Internal Revenue Service.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/us/02irs_inline/02irs_inline-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 875, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/02/us/02irs_inline/02irs_inline-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 875}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/us/02irs_inline/02irs_inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 703, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/us/02irs_inline/02irs_inline-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1405, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/us/02irs_inline/02irs_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/02/us/02irs_inline/02irs_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/us/02irs_inline/02irs_inline-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Chairman of Freddie Mac Nominated to Lead I.R.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koskinen, John A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T20:50:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db6611db-14c5-55a3-9116-69f11603a42c', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db6611db-14c5-55a3-9116-69f11603a42c'}, {'abstract': 'Crazy Legs and his Rock Steady Crew presented the premiere of “Ghetto Made,” a hip-hop history lesson of sorts, at SummerStage on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/arts/dance/crazy-legs-and-his-rock-steady-crew-teach-hip-hop.html', 'snippet': 'Crazy Legs and his Rock Steady Crew presented the premiere of “Ghetto Made,” a hip-hop history lesson of sorts, at SummerStage on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What do you call a B-boy when he’s a middle-aged man? Richard Colón was 13 in 1979, when he joined the two-year-old Rock Steady Crew. He wasn’t much older when, under the descriptive moniker Crazy Legs, he became world famous for spinning on his back. By then he was president of this group, and decades later he still is. For a long time he was the only original member performing. On Wednesday at Central Park SummerStage, he danced his final show.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02RSC/02RSC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02RSC/02RSC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02RSC/02RSC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02RSC/02RSC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02RSC/02RSC-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02RSC/02RSC-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02RSC/02RSC-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nostalgic Finale, With Latin Touch, for a B-Boy Original', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nostalgic Finale, With Latin Touch, for a B-Boy Original', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Central Park Summerstage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Break Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rock Steady Crew', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T20:53:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d96e43b2-cf54-5c40-a08d-d7c91499aec7', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d96e43b2-cf54-5c40-a08d-d7c91499aec7'}, {'abstract': 'The essayist David Rakoff’s final work is fiction in verse about a group of interlocking characters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/books/review/david-rakoffs-love-dishonor-marry-die-cherish-perish.html', 'snippet': 'The essayist David Rakoff’s final work is fiction in verse about a group of interlocking characters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s an absolutely essential video available on YouTube, of a 2012 segment from the public radio program “This American Life,” in which the writer and frequent guest David Rakoff walks onstage with his left hand tucked into his pocket. Rakoff has recently undergone surgery, his “fourth in as many years” for cancer, he explains, and now possesses a “flail limb.” Aside from “being able to shrug talmudically,” he says, “I can neither move nor feel my left arm.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/0804-RUDNICK/0804-RUDNICK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 511, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/0804-RUDNICK/0804-RUDNICK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 511}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/0804-RUDNICK/0804-RUDNICK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 714, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/0804-RUDNICK/0804-RUDNICK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 714, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': N