et': 'Juan Gabriel Vásquez’s new novel, built on Colombia’s tragic history, features the cold, bitter poetry of Bogotá and the hushed intensity of young married love.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The author of this book is from Colombia, but he is nothing like Gabriel García Márquez. Juan Gabriel Vásquez’s brilliant new novel rejects the vivid colors and mythical transformations of his older countryman’s Caribbean masterpiece, “One Hundred Years of Solitude,” in favor of the cold, bitter poetry of Bogotá and the hushed intensity of young married love. In “The Sound of Things Falling,” we are closer to the noir palette of the Uruguayan genius Juan Carlos Onetti, whose fiction was apt to be set in a bankrupt shipyard or to feature a desperate writer striving to raise money for his wife’s cancer surgery.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/04white-190/04white-190-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 931, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/04white-190/04white-190-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 931}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/04white-190/04white-190-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 661, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/04white-190/04white-190-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1596, 'width': 1029, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/04white-190/04white-190-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/04white-190/04white-190-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/04white-190/04white-190-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Requiem for the Living', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Requiem for the Living', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vasquez, Juan Gabriel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T21:02:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edmund White', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edmund', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'White', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d01bf4d-6704-538d-a4ba-e6c53455da08', 'word_count': 1211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d01bf4d-6704-538d-a4ba-e6c53455da08'}, {'abstract': 'As part of a drive to win women’s votes, Christine C. Quinn distributed a video of Gloria Steinem saying her election as mayor would inspire girls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/nyregion/steinem-makes-a-video-for-quinn.html', 'snippet': 'As part of a drive to win women’s votes, Christine C. Quinn distributed a video of Gloria Steinem saying her election as mayor would inspire girls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seeking to capitalize on the historic nature of her candidacy, Christine C. Quinn sent out a video on Thursday of the feminist icon Gloria Steinem lauding Ms. Quinn and saying her election as mayor would inspire young women. Ms. Quinn, the City Council speaker, would be the first woman elected mayor of New York.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steinem Makes a Video for Quinn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Steinem Makes A Video for Quinn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinem, Gloria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T21:05:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/850b100c-de23-5969-935b-4c0b7fd1fe66', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/850b100c-de23-5969-935b-4c0b7fd1fe66'}, {'abstract': 'Rats, named for the Big Apple’s unofficial mascots, offers a curated selection of products from the city’s coolest designers and artists.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/in-store-a-berlin-boutique-that-pays-tribute-to-new-york-creative-culture/', 'snippet': 'Rats, named for the Big Apple’s unofficial mascots, offers a curated selection of products from the city’s coolest designers and artists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As any New York denizen knows, the rat is both the city’s unofficial mascot and the ruler of its underground domain. That’s why the artist Keren Richter and the art director Gabriel Kuo chose Rats as the name for their new curated pop-up shop in Berlin, which pays tribute to the underground creative culture of the Big Apple.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Store | A Berlin Boutique That Pays Tribute to New York Creative Culture', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valentine, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T21:08:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nadja Sayej', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nadja', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayej', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fcf3161-7dea-5688-b73f-5244e77f0893', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fcf3161-7dea-5688-b73f-5244e77f0893'}, {'abstract': 'Two global warming researchers say natural gas leaks are a problem, but not a big part of the climate problem.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/two-climate-analysts-fault-gas-leaks-but-not-as-a-big-warming-threat/', 'snippet': 'Two global warming researchers say natural gas leaks are a problem, but not a big part of the climate problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two prominent analysts of human-driven global warming have offered fresh criticisms of the way Anthony Ingraffea, a Cornell University engineering professor, has been portraying the contribution of natural gas leaks to climate change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Climate Analysts Fault Gas Leaks, but Not as a Big Warming Threat', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'ke