dance dramas — Henry Purcell’s “Dido and Aeneas” and Benjamin Britten’s “Curlew River” — in a double bill at Tanglewood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LENOX, Mass. — The coupling of Henry Purcell’s “Dido and Aeneas” and Benjamin Britten’s “Curlew River” — English music dramas composed almost three centuries apart — makes a superlative double bill. It’s not unreasonable to claim that Purcell and Britten are the two greatest English-born composers, and in this centenary year of Britten’s birth, it’s good to link him to a composer he often championed. More than that, these are two intricate, tragic masterpieces. Each houses death and violent emotional affliction within several outer shells that, paradoxically, make anguish at once more bearable and more inexorable.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02MORRIS-SPAN/MORRIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02MORRIS-SPAN/MORRIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02MORRIS-SPAN/MORRIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02MORRIS-SPAN/MORRIS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02MORRIS-SPAN/MORRIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02MORRIS-S