selected guide to pop, rock, metal and R&B performances in the New York area.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Prices may not reflect ticketing service charges. For full reviews of recent concerts: nytimes.com/music. A searchable guide to these and other shows is at nytimes.com/events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pop & Rock Listings for Aug. 2-8', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T21:59:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/514c4845-a8d8-5549-a3f0-af29e4a86675', 'word_count': 1218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/514c4845-a8d8-5549-a3f0-af29e4a86675'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s New York City mayor’s race bears a lot of resemblance to the one 36 years ago, when Ed Koch, a little-known liberal, emerged to win the election.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/is-it-77-all-over-again/', 'snippet': 'This year’s New York City mayor’s race bears a lot of resemblance to the one 36 years ago, when Ed Koch, a little-known liberal, emerged to win the election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not just the psychiatrists and talk-show hosts. Political scientists are also watching Anthony Weiner’s downward spiral and shaking their heads, searching for analogs in the annals of N.Y.C. politics. But throughout the months I tracked this year’s race for City Hall, one historical parallel did keep cropping up: It’s ’77, all over again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/01/magazine/01-1977-mayor-1/01-1977-mayor-1-ar