er’s artistry, and the story of two people who collected his art, Sterling and Francine Clark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WILLIAMSTOWN, Mass. — Winslow Homer was America’s first great post-God landscape painter. Before the Civil War, successful artists like Frederic Church and Asher B. Durand made pictures of New World vistas bathed in transcendental light. Theirs was an art of religious theater. In that art, Nature was a colossal, purposeful moral consciousness; the human presence, if visible at all, an awe-struck speck.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/design/20130802-DAYTRIP-slide-X3A3/20130802-DAYTRIP-slide-X3A3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/design/20130802-DAYTRIP-slide-X3A3/20130802-DAYTRIP-slide-X3A3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/design/20130802-DAYTRIP-slide-X3A3/20130802-DAYTRIP-slide-X3A3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/design/20130802-DAYTRIP-slide-X3A3/20130802-DAYTRIP-slide-X3A3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1296, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/design/20130802-DAYTRIP-slide-X3A3/20130802-DAYTRIP-slide-X3A3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/design/20130802-DAYTRIP-slide-X3A3/2013080