n by the final “yes” vote needed to reach 60. And who knows how things would have turned out if the National Rifle Association hadn’t decided to stay neutral.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finally, the A.T.F. Has a Permanent Director', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, B Todd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T22:18:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorothy J. Samuels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Samuels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8b1461d-a4b7-556b-b6a1-1e3af5eb14a0', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8b1461d-a4b7-556b-b6a1-1e3af5eb14a0'}, {'abstract': 'A pair of solo shows at Bard College illuminate different, and similar, perspectives on the ready-made.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/arts/design/haim-steinbachs-and-helen-martens-solos-at-bard-college.html', 'snippet': 'A pair of solo shows at Bard College illuminate different, and similar, perspectives on the ready-made.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANNANDALE-ON-HUDSON, N.Y. — Exactly 100 years ago, Marcel Duchamp inverted a bicycle wheel, mounted it on a kitchen stool and anointed it as art. It was the first of his revolutionary ready-mades, so it is perhaps with that centenary in mind that the Center for Curatorial Studies at Bard College has come up with two substantial solo shows devoted to artists from different generations whose ties to the ready-made are complex and deep. Together their displays combust into a more than suitable celebration.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/JPDAYTRIP-BARD/JPDAYTRIP-BARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/JPDAYTRIP-BARD/JPDAYTRIP-BARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/JPDAYTRIP-BARD/JPDAYTRIP-BARD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/JPDAYTRIP-BARD/JPDAYTRIP-BARD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/JPDAYTRIP-BARD/JPDAYTRIP-BARD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/JPDAYTRIP-BARD/JPDAYTRIP-BARD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/JPDAYTRIP-BARD/JPDAYTRIP-BARD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Assembled in Planned Jumbles of Found Creation', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Assembled in Planned Jumbles of Found Creation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinbach, Haim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hessel Museum of Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T22:21:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/934355de-518b-549e-a1db-a9be5f754462', 'word_count': 1366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/934355de-518b-549e-a1db-a9be5f754462'}, {'abstract': 'A listing of walking tours, speaking engagements, cultural events and more in the New York area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/arts/around-town-for-aug-2-8.html', 'snippet': 'A listing of walking tours, speaking engagements, cultural events and more in the New York area.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘The Fence’ in Brooklyn Bridge Park (through Oct. 1) When is a fence not a fence? When it is the backdrop for a free display of over 200 images of people, animals and daily life by 39 photographers from the United States and abroad. Presented for the second year by United Photo Industries, a Brooklyn arts cooperative, as a showcase for young photographers, the display consists of a 1,000-foot-long waterproof mesh banner superimposed with color and black-and-white photos. Among the shots are images, above, of working people in Hoboken, N.J., by John Delaney.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Around Town for Aug. 2-8', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 