always taken to heart some passages in Raymond Chandler’s The Simple Art of Murder, especially the passage in which he distinguishes between the inherent importance of themes and the extent to which they are a good subject for writers:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chaos Looms', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-01T23:57:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63b3fc13-47c1-5343-886a-d58473ab10da', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63b3fc13-47c1-5343-886a-d58473ab10da'}, {'abstract': 'A survey of what has been written about, and by, the two leading candidates to be the next head of the Federal Reserve, Lawrence H. Summers and Janet L. Yellen.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/01/the-fed-contenders-a-reading-list/', 'snippet': 'A survey of what has been written about, and by, the two leading candidates to be the next head of the Federal Reserve, Lawrence H. Summers and Janet L. Yellen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We know, you can’t get enough. So here are some suggestions for further reading about Lawrence H. Summers and Janet L. Yellen, the leading candidates to replace Ben S. Bernanke as chairman of the Federal Reserve. President Obama has said that a third candidate, Donald L. Kohn, a former vice chairman, is also under consideration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fed Contenders: A Reading List', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Summers, Lawrence H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yellen, Janet L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T00:03:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fecf243-7b98-5f8c-8e7c-2127720fde71', 'word_count': 1525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fecf243-7b98-5f8c-8e7c-2127720fde71'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations said July was Iraq’s deadliest month in more than five years, describing a series of bombings and shootings as an epidemic of sectarian-tinged violence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/world/middleeast/iraq-1057-killed-in-july-un-says.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations said July was Iraq’s deadliest month in more than five years, describing a series of bombings and shootings as an epidemic of sectarian-tinged violence.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United Nations said Thursday that July was Iraq’s deadliest month in more than five years, describing a series of bombings and shootings as an epidemic of sectarian-tinged violence that had killed 1,057 Iraqis and wounded 2,326. The organization’s acting special representative for Iraq, Gyorgy Busztin, said in a statement that the severity of the mayhem was the worst since 2008, when Iraq verged on civil war after the American-led invasion that toppled Saddam Hussein and his Sunni minority from power. Many of the attacks in July were aimed at members of the Shiite majority that has dominated Iraq’s politics since the withdrawal of the American military at the end of 2011. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: 1,057 Killed in July, U.N. Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: 1,057 Killed in July, U.N. Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T00:03:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ccad625-559d-55f2-9d68-6155fbf6381b', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ccad625-559d-55f2-9d68-6155fbf6381b'}, {'abstract': 'Officials gave few details about what prompted the temporary closings but cited “credible” information that an Al Qaeda affiliate might be plotting an attack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/us/some-american-embassies-to-close-on-sunday-over-security-concerns.html', 'snippet': 'Officials gave few details about what prompted the temporary closings but cited “credible” information that an Al Qaeda affiliate might be plotting an attack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A terrorism threat has prompted the United States to close dozens of American diplomatic missions in the Middle East, North Africa and elsewhere through the weekend, American officials said Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Terror Threat Prompts U.S. to Close Diplomatic Missions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Terror Threat Prompts U.S. To Close Diplomatic Missions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mazzetti, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T00:05:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Mazzetti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzetti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/018608cf-ce9c-5746-a2be-18f4339e2d5c', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/018608cf-ce9c-5746-a2be-18f4339e2d5c'}, {'abstract': 'Iran’s Foreign Ministry said the legislation passed by the House of Representatives on Wednesday would complicate efforts to settle the nuclear standoff diplomatically.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/world/middleeast/iran-assails-house-sanctions-bill-saying-it-will-complicate-nuclear-dispute.html', 'snippet': 'Iran’s Foreign Ministry said the legislation passed by the House of Representatives on Wednesday would complicate efforts to settle the nuclear standoff diplomatically.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Iran reacted angrily on Thursday to the overwhelming approval of harsh legislation on sanctions by the House of Representatives, saying the action would further complicate stalled negotiations aimed at resolving the protracted dispute over the Iranian nuclear energy program.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Assails House Sanctions Bill, Saying It Will Complicate Nuclear Dispute', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran Assails House Sanctions Bill, Saying It Will Complicate Nuclear Dispute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T00:12:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbc26349-92b4-5a1e-84a6-c9e35f8e211a', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbc26349-92b4-5a1e-84a6-c9e35f8e211a'}, {'abstract': 'As the size of a family grows in Joachim Lafosse’s film “Our Children,” stress rises to a dangerous level.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/movies/in-our-children-from-joachim-lafosse-life-turns-tragic.html', 'snippet': 'As the size of a family grows in Joachim Lafosse’s film “Our Children,” stress rises to a dangerous level.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At once beautifully realized and brutally uncompromising, “Our Children” opens with a young woman weeping. She’s a lovely young thing, her features almost obscured by the grayness of her skin, the puffiness around her eyes and the oxygen tubes threaded into her nose. “You’ll bury them in Morocco,” she says to someone hovering nearby and then, as her tears begin to fall, she repeats her appeal. The intensity of the plea is a tug at the heart, a tug that turns into a jolt with a blunt cut to four little coffins being loaded on a plane. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Household Grows, and Life Becomes Unbearable', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Household Grows, And Life Becomes Unbearable', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Our Children (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lafosse, Joachim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T00:16:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/35de7083-4328-51fd-9c43-d7deccbf239e', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35de7083-4328-51fd-9c43-d7deccbf239e'}, {'abstract': 'Duke Energy, citing a change in Florida’s regulations, said that a $24.7 billion reactor project would be delayed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/us/florida-nuclear-project-is-dropped.html', 'snippet': 'Duke Energy, citing a change in Florida’s regulations, said that a $24.7 billion reactor project would be delayed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Duke Energy said Thursday that it had dropped plans for a $24.7 billion nuclear reactor complex in Levy County, Fla., on which the company has already spent $1 billion, most of it collected from customers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida Nuclear Project Is Dropped', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida Nuclear Project Is Dropped', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duke Energy Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T00:18:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a10107fd-74bb-5ab2-acb3-7c28d055ca1e', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a10107fd-74bb-5ab2-acb3-7c28d055ca1e'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Beitz was well known for his efforts to save hundreds of Jews and Poles from the Nazis while stationed in Poland during World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/business/berthold-beitz-german-steel-industrialist-who-saved-jews-dies-at-99.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Beitz was well known for his efforts to save hundreds of Jews and Poles from the Nazis while stationed in Poland during World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — The rise of Berthold Beitz to the head of ThyssenKrupp, the steel conglomerate, is the stuff of modern German legend. He played a critical role in the rebuilding of postwar Germany into an industrial powerhouse.', 'print_sect