apse in Chile Ends With No Charges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T01:04:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pascale Bonnefoy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pascale', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bonnefoy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82c34333-e6ee-5586-ab5d-705b19744cb9', 'word_count': 648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82c34333-e6ee-5586-ab5d-705b19744cb9'}, {'abstract': '“Jamel Shabazz Street Photographer” pays tribute to a New York chronicler and his subjects, especially hip-hop artists of the 1980s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/movies/jamel-shabazz-street-photographer-a-new-york-portrait.html', 'snippet': '“Jamel Shabazz Street Photographer” pays tribute to a New York chronicler and his subjects, especially hip-hop artists of the 1980s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anybody who doesn’t appreciate the spirit captured in Jamel Shabazz’s photographs doesn’t get New York. In a city that increasingly seems to squander the homegrown cultures that have defined it, “Jamel Shabazz Street Photographer,” Charlie Ahearn’s rough-and-ready, almost familial documentary, pays tribute to this pavement portraitist of the late-20th century.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02RDP_SHABAZZ_SPAN/SHABAZZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height