 {'main': 'Test Yourself | Editing Practice, Aug. 2, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T08:34:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fe55af7-5219-5da0-8ded-0fd2a2a4c4c7', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fe55af7-5219-5da0-8ded-0fd2a2a4c4c7'}, {'abstract': 'It’s all a simple math equation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/magazine/steve-schmidt-says-republican-campaigns-havent-changed-but-they-will.html', 'snippet': 'It’s all a simple math equation.', 'lead_paragraph': ' You’ve been hired by the A.C.L.U. to win over Republicans on same-sex marriage. What’s the argument that you make to those who are resistant?  A few years ago, there was universal agreement in the party that marriage is between one man and one woman. It was a position that appealed to the middle of the electorate. That’s not true anymore. Politicians have an acutely honed instinct for self-preservation. Over time I am convinced this issue will be a political liability for people who are opposed to it.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04talk/04talk-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 1709, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04talk/04talk-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1709}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04talk/04talk-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 360, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04talk/04talk-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 719, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04talk/mag-04Talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04talk/mag-04Talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04talk/mag-04Talk-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Steve Schmidt Says Republican Campaigns Haven’t Changed. But They Will.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘This is a Simple Math Equation’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Draper, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Steve', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'ar