'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b048cc8c-f5b4-55dd-8154-6b7b6b20725f', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b048cc8c-f5b4-55dd-8154-6b7b6b20725f'}, {'abstract': 'At farmers’ markets everywhere, now is the time to spend on whatever looks good.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/magazine/its-a-buyers-market.html', 'snippet': 'At farmers’ markets everywhere, now is the time to spend on whatever looks good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although there are areas of the country where farmers’ markets feature loads of fresh vegetables year round, those of us who live in regions with a different set of blessings experience long stretches when farmers’ markets (at least those that remain open) offer only cider, apples, root vegetables, frozen meat and things like candles and sweaters made of the coarsest wool. Which is all fine, but it mostly serves to enhance the excitement we can feel when we hit the big time: a farmers’ market loaded with stuff that was picked not only nearby but yesterday.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04eat/04eat-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 434, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04eat/04eat-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 434}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04eat/04eat-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/magazine/04eat/04eat-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1445, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit'