at his trial, which he called a “sham,” prompting a cry of “coward” in the courtroom from the widow of a man he is accused of killing. His decision also deflated the hopes of many in this city who had yearned to hear him tell his story in his own words. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bulger Declines to Testify, but Gets Something Off His Mind: ‘This Is a Sham’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bulger Declines to Testify, but Gets Something Off His Mind: ‘This Is a Sham’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bulger, James J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casper, Denise J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakes, Stephen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Camuti, William', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T13:58:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f4ca7e1-f33c-5696-a9d4-888db41feb82', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f4ca7e1-f33c-5696-a9d4-888db41feb82'}, {'abstract': 'A Toyota subsidiary in charge of melting down old catalytic converters is suing a California-based auto salvage company for selling it fake catalytic converters.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/toyota-subsidiary-finds-dogs-in-its-cats/', 'snippet': 'A Toyota subsidiary in charge of melting down old catalytic converters is suing a California-based auto salvage company for selling it fake catalytic converters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Toyota subsidiary is suing a California company for fraud, asserting it imported counterfeit catalytic converters from China as part of a recycling scheme that resulted in “substantial damages.” The suit was filed last month by Toyota Tsusho America of Georgetown, Ky., against Sino Scrap, a California-based business also known as Autocats of Harbor City, Calif.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/automobiles/wheels/catalytic-converter/catalytic-converter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/02/automobiles/wheels/catalytic-converter/catalytic-converter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/automobiles/wheels/catalytic-converter/catalytic-converter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/automobiles/wheels/catalytic-converter/catalytic-converter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/automobiles/wheels/catalytic-converter/catalytic-converter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/02/automobiles/wheels/catalytic-converter/catalytic-converter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailhe