'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ef69cb8-25c4-5187-8f2b-789b80cc5e09', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ef69cb8-25c4-5187-8f2b-789b80cc5e09'}, {'abstract': 'The director Urich Seidl and his collaborators talk about the experience of filming “Faith,”which opens on Friday in American theaters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/movies/ulrich-seidls-paradise-trilogy-pushes-boundaries.html', 'snippet': 'The director Urich Seidl and his collaborators talk about the experience of filming “Faith,”which opens on Friday in American theaters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The work of Ulrich Seidl can perhaps be summed up by his preferred camera perspective: head-on, often boxed in, warts and all. This Austrian filmmaker has made a 30-year career of confronting us with people you don’t usually see on screen (much less naked) and stories you don’t expect to see played out. Scenes from his latest project, the “Paradise” trilogy, depict a part-time Catholic missionary rousing the ire of a belligerent drunk, an adolescent girl at a weight-loss clinic pining for her doctor, and middle-aged sex tourists manhandling their Kenyan boy toy.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/arts/04SEIDL1_SPAN/04SEIDL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/arts/04SEIDL1_SPAN/04SEIDL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/arts/04SEIDL1_SPAN/04SEIDL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'supe