y has found Fabrice Tourre, a former midlevel employee of Goldman Sachs, liable for six of seven civil fraud charges brought against him by the Securities and Exchange Commission. The charges stemmed from his role in a single mortgage-related transaction in the run up to the financial crisis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wall Street Scapegoat Goes Down', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tourre, Fabrice P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T15:29:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teresa Tritch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teresa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tritch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0595d899-8987-537e-886a-8f16030a8261', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0595d899-8987-537e-886a-8f16030a8261'}, {'abstract': 'Conservative management is often recommended for back pain, but doctors are performing more CT and M.R.I. scans, prescribing more opiates and referring more patients to specialists, which may lead to expensive and ineffective surgeries.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/back-pain-remains-overtreated/', 'snippet': 'Conservative management is often recommended for back pain, but doctors are performing more CT and M.R.I. scans, prescribing more opiates and referring more patients to specialists, which may lead to expensive and ineffective surgeries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Well-established guidelines for the treatment of back pain require very conservative management — in most cases, no more than aspirin or acetaminophen (Tylenol) and physical therapy. Advanced imaging procedures, narcotics and referrals to other physicians are recommended only for the most refractory cases or those with serious other symptoms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/26/health/well-regimens/well-regimens-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 233, 'width': 225, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/26/health/well-regimens/well-regimens-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 233, 'width': 225, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/26/health/well-regimens/well-regimens-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/04/26/health/well-regimens/well-regimens-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/26/health/well-regimens/well-regimens-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Back Pain Remains Overtreated', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Back (Human Body Part)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T15:36:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article