tening another with jail. In its failed effort to persuade Russia to return another leaker, Edward J. Snowden, it felt compelled to say that he would not be tortured or executed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Rulings Blur the Line Between a Spy and a Leaker', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Rulings, Spy vs. Leaker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'First Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pentagon Papers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Treason', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Bradley E', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosen, James', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Risen, James', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T15:46:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/da62fb87-fb56-5eaf-b7f5-2a598663089f', 'word_count': 1290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da62fb87-fb56-5eaf-b7f5-2a598663089f'}, {'abstract': 'The loan portfolio consists mostly of commercial real estate loans in Ireland and Britain but also includes residential mortgage loans in those countries as well as Irish corporate loans.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/liquidator-to-sell-29-billion-in-anglo-irish-loans/', 'snippet': 'The loan portfolio consists mostly of commercial real estate loans in Ireland and Britain but also includes residential mortgage loans in those countries as well as Irish corporate loans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The nationalized Irish lender Anglo Irish Bank plans to sell $29 billion worth of loans as part of its liquidation, the bank’s special liquidator said on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liquidator to Sell $29 Billion in Anglo Irish Loans', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nationalization of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anglo Irish Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'KPMG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T15:48:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68138268-532c-5915-8acd-d46aa3243826', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68138268-532c-5915-8acd-d46aa3243826'}, {'abstract': 'A floor-through residence with 4,207 square feet of space and 40 feet of frontage on Gramercy Park was the most expensive residential sale of the week.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/big-ticket-a-floor-with-a-key-to-a-park-for-15-175-million/', 'snippet': 'A floor-through residence with 4,207 square feet of space and 40 feet of frontage on Gramercy Park was the most expensive residential sale of the week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The princely proportions of a floor-through residence at the repurposed 18 Gramercy Park South — previously a Salvation Army housing depot for as many as 300 women but now a sought-after destination with just 16 luxury condominiums — attracted a buyer with $15,175,000 to spend and was the most expensive sale of the week, according to city records.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/realestate/04TICKET/04TICKET-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/realestate/04TICKET/04TICKET-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 621}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/realestate/04TICKET/04TICKET-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 990, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/realestate/04TICKET/04TICKET-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1979, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/realestate/04TICKET/04TICKET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/04/realestate/04TICKET/04TICKET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/realestate/04TICKET/04TICKET-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Ticket | A Floor With a Key to a Park for $15.175 Million', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gramercy Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T15:50:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffde3b79-465f-5f15-ae56-801d57690efa', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffde3b79-465f-5f15-ae56-801d57690efa'}, {'abstract': 'A small change to Israel’s electoral rules may transform its political life.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/the-tyranny-of-the-minority/', 'snippet': 'A small change to Israel’s electoral rules may transform its political life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — This week, the Knesset approved several changes to Israel’s election laws, including an increase, from 2 percent to 4 percent, in the minimum share of votes needed to get into Parliament. More debates and more voting are required before this decision becomes law, but it already shows that after many years o