casts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T16:58:40+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/24456c60-7246-5cbf-bab8-799ba5ff331b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/24456c60-7246-5cbf-bab8-799ba5ff331b'}, {'abstract': 'A weekly capsule of events around the globe curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/calendar-coming-events-in-latrobe-pa-germany-italy/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of events around the globe curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Great American Banana Split Celebration, Latrobe, Pa.\xa0Latrobe, a small city 40 miles southeast of Pittsburgh that considers itself the birthplace of the banana split, will host a weekend celebration from Aug. 23 to 25 for the 109th anniversary of the famous triple-scoop dessert. In 1904, David Strickler, then a 23-year-old apprentice pharmacist at what became Strickler’s Drug Store, above, invented the sundae, which quickly became popular with students of nearby St. Vincent College, according to organizers of the Great American Banana Split Celebration. The three-day event will feature tastings, a banana-themed multimedia art show and street fair, era-themed events like a car rally and sock hop, and, of course, a do-it-yourself banana split bar. Most activities are free.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calendar: Coming Events in Latrobe, Pa.; Germany; Italy', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T17:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63a4d431-53bb-5d72-beb7-b4fe306fe8f8', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63a4d431-53bb-5d72-beb7-b4fe306fe8f8'}, {'abstract': 'When what you’re looking for in a weekend getaway is rustic comfort rather than stimulation and adventure, you can’t do better than the Wheatleigh Hotel in Lenox, Mass.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/feeling-for-an-old-school-hotel-in-the-berkshires-thats-perfect-for-just-staying-put/', 'snippet': 'When what you’re looking for in a weekend getaway is rustic comfort rather than stimulation and adventure, you can’t do better than the Wheatleigh Hotel in Lenox, Mass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sure, it’s fun to traverse a city in 36 hours or explore some far-flung land over a luxurious two weeks. But when it comes to vacations, sometimes it’s nice to just pick a spot and stay put. If that’s what you’re in the mood for, the Wheatleigh Hotel, in Lenox, Mass. is the place for you. It’s not new, or of the moment, or even remotely cool, and that’s exactly the point.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling For | An Old-School Hotel in the Berkshires That’s Perfect for Just Staying Put', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKown, Zack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olmsted, Frederick Law', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsao, Calvin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berkshires (Mass)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_