oletta Mantovani.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/newly-discovered-early-pavarotti-recording-will-be-released/', 'snippet': 'The 1961 recording of “Che Gelida Manina” from “La Bohème,” was discovered by the tenor’s widow, Nicoletta Mantovani.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A recently discovered recording by Luciano Pavarotti from a 1961 performance at the Reggio Emilia Theater, in Italy, will have its first release in October, when Decca Records includes it on a new compilation of Pavarotti favorites. The company is releasing the set to commemorate the 50th anniversary of his British television debut on on “Sunday Night at the London Palladium,” a popular weekly variety show, as well as his Covent Garden debut the following month. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02artsbeat-pavarotti/02artsbeat-pavarotti-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 490, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02artsbeat-pavarotti/02artsbeat-pavarotti-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 490}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02artsbeat-pavarotti/02artsbeat-pavarotti-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 836, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02artsbeat-pavarotti/02artsbeat-pavarotti-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1671, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/arts/02artsbeat-pavarotti/02artsbeat-pavarotti-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': '