Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/244e0382-9e80-5488-8f29-dbcfd4211dab', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/244e0382-9e80-5488-8f29-dbcfd4211dab'}, {'abstract': 'The next Little Night Music programs are coming right up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/arts/music/like-a-nightclub-only-its-schubert.html', 'snippet': 'The next Little Night Music programs are coming right up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Little Night Music is the popular series of late-night concerts presented by the Mostly Mozart Festival in the intimate Kaplan Penthouse. The programs start at 10 p.m. and typically last an hour or less. The penthouse has picture windows with nighttime vistas of the city. Patrons sit at small round tables drinking complimentary wine. Only about 230 people can be accommodated; tickets go fast.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Like a Nightclub, Only It’s Schubert', 'kicker': 'Classical', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Like a Nightclub, Only It’s Schubert', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mostly Mozart Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T18:14:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6accef9d-0229-51cc-8fc0-a94099a2d0b4', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6accef9d-0229-51cc-8fc0-a94099a2d0b4'}, {'abstract': 'The writer Chad Beguelin is largely known for lighter fare, so his domestic comedy “Harbor” offers a chance to see another side of him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/theater/life-was-idyllic-then-sis-arrived.html', 'snippet': 'The writer Chad Beguelin is largely known for lighter fare, so his domestic comedy “Harbor” offers a chance to see another side of him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The writer Chad Beguelin is largely known for lighter fare like “The Wedding Singer” (book and lyrics) and “Elf” (lyrics), so his domestic comedy “Harbor” offers a chance to see another side of him. And there were some positive reviews of the play’s premiere at the Westport Country Playhouse last year, directed by Mark Lamos, so this first production of the 2013-14 Primary Stages season is worth a look.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Life Was Idyllic, Then Sis Arrived', 'kicker': 'Theater', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Life Was Idyllic, Then Sis Arrived', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beguelin, Chad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T18:14:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55ae833e-818f-586b-8438-afc5d22b01c3', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55ae833e-818f-586b-8438-afc5d22b01c3'}, {'abstract': 'TLC brings us an instant-history look at a real-life case involving Zumba and prostitution out of Kennebunk, Me.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/arts/television/a-zumba-lesson-with-um-perks.html', 'snippet': 'TLC brings us an instant-history look at a real-life case involving Zumba and prostitution out of Kennebunk, Me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For producers of the kind of quickie docu-shows that certain cable outlets thrive on, seeing “Zumba” and “prostitution” in the same sentence has the feel of Christmas morning. And TLC brings us an instant-history look at a real-life case involving those two things out of Kennebunk, Me., when it broadcasts “Sex, Lies & Zumba” on Tuesday at 10 p.m.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Zumba Lesson With, Um, Perks', 'kicker': 'Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Zumba Lesson With, Um, Perks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T18:16:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8264947-48bf-5d23-b8a1-da14ba51b3e3', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8264947-48bf-5d23-b8a1-da14ba51b3e3'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees’ highest-paid hitters have produced few hits this season. Compare hits and salaries across the league.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/08/02/sports/baseball/bang-for-your-buck.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees’ highest-paid hitters have produced few hits this season. Compare hits and salaries across the league.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees’ highest-paid hitters have produced few hits this season. Compare hits and salaries across the league.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/sports/baseball/bang-for-your-buck-image/bang-for