 year, John Heginbotham probably has a few years to go before we stop comparing him to Mr. Morris. In his 14 years with the company, this dancer turned choreographer clearly inherited some of Mr. Morris’s trademark musicality and wit. These qualities stand out in the repertory of his own troupe, Dance Heginbotham. Since its debut in 2012, critics have also noted a distinctively Heginbothian zaniness. And when was the last time Mr. Morris choreographed to Daft Punk?', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crackling Wit of an Up-and-Comer', 'kicker': 'Dance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crackling Wit Of an Up-and-Comer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T18:25:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c4a0864-7efc-5351-8ac2-36a84921d36d', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c4a0864-7efc-5351-8ac2-36a84921d36d'}, {'abstract': 'The Modern’s “Soundings” isn’t the only aural art show in town this month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/arts/design/sounds-that-bridge-disparate-worlds.html', 'snippet': 'The Modern’s “Soundings” isn’t the only aural art show in town this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Modern’s “Soundings” isn’t the only aural art show in town this month. Lisa Cooley, a Lower East Side gallery on the former site of Tonic, the experimental music club, has just opened “The String and the Mirror,” a group exhibition of sonic works by 19 artists. Organized by Justin Luke, director of the gallery Audio Visual Arts, and Lawrence Kumpf, artistic director at Issue Project Room, it includes a few veterans like Marina Rosenfeld and Rolf Julius but mainly focuses on emerging artists.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sounds That Bridge Disparate Worlds', 'kicker': 'Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sounds That Bridge Disparate Worlds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T18:27:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f33138e-f022-5c38-89d0-754071adf857', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f33138e-f022-5c38-89d0-754071adf857'}, {'abstract': 'Looking to bolster their popularity among Latinos, candidates are preparing advertisements and appearances aimed at Spanish-speaking New Yorkers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/nyregion/courting-hispanic-voters-in-spanish.html', 'snippet': 'Looking to bolster their popularity among Latinos, candidates are preparing advertisements and appearances aimed at Spanish-speaking New Yorkers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fans of Spanish-language news shows and telenovelas, get ready: The mudslinging and fist-fighting long associated with New York City politics will soon be invading your airwaves.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/trailside/trailside-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400,