{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southeastern Asset Management', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T18:32:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fb2e14b-69fd-5573-b65b-2921f7963fe5', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fb2e14b-69fd-5573-b65b-2921f7963fe5'}, {'abstract': 'Early results from the vote, which observers gave a mixed report, showed ZANU-PF, President Robert G. Mugabe’s party, earning a big majority in Parliament. There was no word yet on the presidential race.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/world/africa/mugabes-party-zimbabwe.html', 'snippet': 'Early results from the vote, which observers gave a mixed report, showed ZANU-PF, President Robert G. Mugabe’s party, earning a big majority in Parliament. There was no word yet on the presidential race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARARE, Zimbabwe — The party of Robert G. Mugabe, Zimbabwe’s long-ruling president, appeared to be on track to win a huge majority in Parliament after Wednesday’s election, the Zimbabwe Election Commission announced Friday, allowing it to recapture parliamentary control from its main challenger, the Movement for Democratic Change.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/world/03zimbabwe/03zimbabwe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/03/world/03zimbabwe/03zimbabwe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/world/03zimbabwe/03zimbabwe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/world/03zimbabwe/03zimbabwe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/world/03zimbabwe/03zimbabwe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/03/world/03zimbabwe/03zimbabwe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/world/03zimbabwe/03zimbabwe-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mugabe’s Party Appears Headed for Parliamentary Victory in Zimbabwe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mugabe’s Party Appears Headed for Parliamentary Victory in Zimbabwe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zimbabwe African National Union-Patriotic Front (ZANU-PF)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polgreen, Lydia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zimbabwe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mugabe, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsvangirai, Morgan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T18:35:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4e33f82-e48b-504a-9145-2775a5e33057', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4e33f82-e48b-504a-9145-2775a5e33057'}, {'abstract': 'The forgotten history behind “The New Gospel of Peace,” one of the war’s hottest-selling satires.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/war-in-the-land-of-unculpsalm/', 'snippet': 'The forgotten history behind “The New Gospel of Peace,” one of the war’s hottest-selling satires.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was in the book stacks of the Harry Ransom Center at the University of Texas when the title of an otherwise unassuming green volume, “The New Gospel of Peace,” caught my eye. I had been looking for an edition of Abraham Lincoln’s speeches to include in an exhibition tracing the King James Bible’s influence on literature and culture. Like many other major Civil War-era figures — Frederick Douglass, Harriet Beecher Stowe — Lincoln was beholden to the language and style of the King James Bible. But Lincoln would have to wait.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘War in the Land of Unculpsalm’', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bible', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ransom, Harry, Center, The University of Texas at Austin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T18:36:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Brune Sigler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': 'Brune', 'lastname': 'Sigler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/113ea5a1-a1d6-5705-8fde-345f3657a1be', 'word_count': 1556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/113ea5a1-a1d6-5705-8fde-345f3657a1be'}, {'abstract': 'The fighting, in Nangarhar Province, started with the killing of a tribal elder by the Taliban.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/world/asia/clashes-leave-scores-of-afghan-police-and-taliban-dead.html', 'snippet': 'The fighting, in Nangarhar Province, started with the killing of a tribal elder by the Taliban.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Taliban fighters killed 22 Afghan police officers on Thursday in an ambush of their convoy in an eastern province bordering Pakistan, officials said Friday. It was one of the deadliest episodes in a power struggle between insurgents and the government that has intensified as American-led forces prepare to leave Afghanistan after more than a decade of war.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scores Killed in 2 Days of Clashes Between Afghan Police and Taliban Fighters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scores Killed in 2 Days of Clashes Between Afghan Police and Taliban Fighters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahmed, Azam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sahak, Sharifullah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Afghan National Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Afghan Local Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T18:41:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed and Sharifullah Sahak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sharifullah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sahak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8d06235-f12c-50c6-b4a0-a3bf41d7e409', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8d06235-f12c-50c6-b4a0-a3bf41d7e409'}, {'abstract': 'William MacLeod once disliked pigeons as much as most New Yorkers — now several of them are his pets, and he has trained them not to soil his suits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/nyregion/not-flying-rats-to-him.html', 'snippet': 'William MacLeod once disliked pigeons as much as most New Yorkers — now several of them are his pets, and he has trained them not to soil his suits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'William MacLeod says he was always in the “rats with wings” camp regarding New York City pigeons, until one day six years ago in Washington Square Park, where he spied a pair of chicks on the ground. He nurtured them for weeks and released them back into the park.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04CHARACTER_SPAN/04CHARACTER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04CHARACTER_SPAN/04CHARACTER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04CHARACTER_SPAN/04CHARACTER_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': '