ne': 'Onstage Together at Last', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Lois Smith', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vows (Times Column)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T19:24:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lois Smith Brady', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lois', 'middlename': 'Smith', 'lastname': 'Brady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef5e7b49-1bbc-5e68-9962-ffcf0f70d514', 'word_count': 1917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef5e7b49-1bbc-5e68-9962-ffcf0f70d514'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge has dismissed a libel complaint against The New Yorker magazine for an article it published about a forensic art expert.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/forensic-art-experts-libel-case-against-new-yorker-magazine-is-dismissed/', 'snippet': 'A federal judge has dismissed a libel complaint against The New Yorker magazine for an article it published about a forensic art expert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge in New York has dismissed a libel suit brought against The New Yorker magazine and one of its writers by Peter Paul Biro, a forensic art expert who was the subject of a long article in July 2010.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Forensic Art Expert’s Libel Case Against New Yorker Magazine Is Dismissed', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libel and Slander', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T19:25:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19c66ba9-24cd-53fe-b03e-a43336cc6356', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19c66ba9-24cd-53fe-b03e-a43336cc6356'}, {'abstract': 'Readers write their own over-the-top odes to the temperature in response to an article about the summer heat that was published in this newspaper in 1852.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/odes-to-heat-struck-new-york/', 'snippet': 'Readers write their own over-the-top odes to the temperature in response to an article about the summer heat that was published in this newspaper in 1852.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In last Sunday’s Metropolitan section, Benjamin Weiser exhumed an article about the summer heat that was published in this newspaper in 1852. No mere weather story, it combined meticulous detail, social commentary and references to art and literature — all rendered in spectacularly overwrought prose. We asked readers to write their own over-the-top odes to the temperature in response; a selection is below.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04METCOMMENTS_SPAN/04METCOMMENTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04METCOMMENTS_SPAN/04METCOMMENTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08