rse/', 'snippet': 'Paul Rudnick discusses David Rakoff’s final book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In The New York Times Book Review, Paul Rudnick reviews “Love, Dishonor, Marry, Die, Cherish, Perish,” the final book by David Rakoff, who died of cancer last year at the age of 47. Mr. Rudnick said he was prepared to hate the book, “and not just because it’s so awful to contemplate a world without any more David Rakoff books, or any more David Rakoff.” He writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/04cover-shadow/04cover-shadow-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/04cover-shadow/04cover-shadow-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/04cover-shadow/04cover-shadow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/04cover-shadow/04cover-shadow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/books/review/04cover-shadow/04cover-shadow-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Review Podcast: David Rakoff’s Farewell in Verse', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject'