nhattan woman with a liberal bent hosts her daughter’s beau, an evangelical Christian educator.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/nyregion/a-review-of-saving-kitty-at-the-new-jersey-repertory-company.html', 'snippet': 'In the romantic comedy “Saving Kitty,” at the New Jersey Repertory Company, a daffy, well-off Manhattan woman with a liberal bent hosts her daughter’s beau, an evangelical Christian educator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RUTHLESS MOTHERS of all degrees have long been a forceful presence in dramatic literature. Oscar Wilde’s Lady Bracknell, Tennessee Williams’s Amanda Wingfield and Gypsy Rose Lee’s mama are among the maternal monsters who command the stage.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN/04ARTSNJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN/04ARTSNJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN/04ARTSNJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN/04ARTSNJ1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN/04ARTSNJ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN/04ARTSNJ1-thumbStandard.jpg