ence agency, but by a private citizen with a few hundred dollars to spare? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/technology/bits-creepydol/bits-creepydol-articleLarge.png', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/02/technology/bits-creepydol/bits-creepydol-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/technology/bits-creepydol/bits-creepydol-jumbo.png', 'height': 620, 'width': 961, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/technology/bits-creepydol/bits-creepydol-superJumbo.png', 'height': 620, 'width': 961, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/technology/bits-creepydol/bits-creepydol-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/02/technology/bits-creepydol/bits-creepydol-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/technology/bits-creepydol/bits-creepydol-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cheap Spying Tool With a High Creepy Factor', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Connor, Brendan", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Malice Afterthought Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T20:58:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f95c548-022a-567a-ad7e-17286e952b7d', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f95c548-022a-567a-ad7e-17286e952b7d'}, {'abstract': 'The celebrity chefs visited the impoverished Caribbean nation to find out about new sustainable farming practices and many delicious varieties of rice.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/travel-diary-aaron-sanchez-and-john-besh-discover-haitis-evolving-food-culture/', 'snippet': 'The celebrity chefs visited the impoverished Caribbean nation to find out about new sustainable farming practices and many delicious varieties of rice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this week, the TV personalities and James Beard Award-winning chefs Aarón Sánchez and John Besh headed to Haiti on behalf of Oxfam’s GROW program, which seeks to promote sustainable practices for food production around the world. While there, they checked out urban gardens in Port-au-Prince, and new rice-growing techniques that require less water in the countryside. They also made headlines when they were turned away from a farmers market by a mayor who feared they would take unflattering pictures. In between their various activities, the duo — who happen to be best friends and are planning to open a Mexican restaurant together — cooked up local dishes alongside Haitian chefs, farmers and culinary students. Here, Sánchez and Besh share their adventures.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aaron Sanchez and John Besh Discover Haiti’s Evolving Food Culture', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T21:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ca1cc13-bd12-5068-a299-f1e20d087405', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ca1cc13-bd12-5068-a299-f1e20d087405'}, {'abstract': '“Coney Night Maze,” featuring a monumental structure inspired by the underside of the Cyclone roller coaster at Coney Island, is on view at the Neuberger Museum of ArtPurchase.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/nyregion/donna-dennis-coney-night-maze-exhibition-in-purchase.html', 'snippet': '“Coney Night Maze,” featuring a monumental structure inspired by the underside of the Cyclone roller coaster at Coney Island, is on view at the Neuberger Museum of ArtPurchase.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1996, during an outing to Coney Island, Donna Dennis found herself unexpectedly captivated by the Cyclone roller coaster. But it wasn’t the thrill of the ride or the enthusiasm of the crowds that drew her; it was the strange landscape beneath.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04ARTSWE1_SPAN/04ARTSWE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04ARTSWE1_SPAN/04ARTSWE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}