 it happened, there was a place on the shore for her far from the world of Further Lane, a place with its own codes and dignities and manner of exclusion on the western tip of the Rockaway peninsula called Breezy Point. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04BIGCITY_SPAN/0804BIGCITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04BIGCITY_SPAN/0804BIGCITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04BIGCITY_SPAN/0804BIGCITY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 618, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04BIGCITY_SPAN/0804BIGCITY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1236, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04BIGCITY_SPAN/0804BIGCITY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04BIGCITY_SPAN/0804BIGCITY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/nyregion/04BIGCITY_SPAN/0804BIGCITY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tested by Water and Fire, Yet Staying Put', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tested by Water and Fire, Yet Staying Put', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Breezy Point (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Irish-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T21:15:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1140df5e-56b3-5264-9613-94a7d1e9a051', 'word_count': 1113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1140df5e-56b3-5264-9613-94a7d1e9a051'}, {'abstract': 'From The Handsome Family’s album “Wilderness” on Carrot Top Records.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/08/03/opinion/sparks-wildebeest.html', 'snippet': 'From The Handsome Family’s album “Wilderness” on Carrot Top Records.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From The Handsome Family’s album “Wilderness” on Carrot Top Records.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '“Wildebeest”', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T21:16:06+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/d699ff1d-0ba0-5c07-9f45-b9901dc811b7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/d699ff1d-0ba0-5c07-9f45-b9901dc811b7'}, {'abstract': 'How’s that supposed to work?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/models-and-mechanisms-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'How’s that supposed to work?', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, traffic is mysterious — and yes, I have read Tom Vanderbilt. Last week I fought rolling traffic jams all across CT in the middle of the day; today I zipped into Manhattan with barely a delay, late on a Friday afternoon. So I have a bit of time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Models and Mechanisms (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T21:16:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82f4bdf1-2968-5015-8337-1ba71c4a4beb', 'word_count': 991, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82f4bdf1-2968-5015-8337-1ba71c4a4beb'}, {'abstract': 'On a small street in East Williamsburg, a Mexico City artist has created a work of art representing New York City’s diversity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/nyregion/east-williamsburg-wall-is-canvas-for-smithe-an-artist-from-mexico.html', 'snippet': 'On a small street in East Williamsburg, a Mexico City artist has created a work of art representing New York City’s diversity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On one side, an eagle reaches its claws out toward a big red apple. On the other side, a creature wearing multiple masks moves toward the apple. These are images in a mural meant to depict the struggles of people of different backgrounds to make it to New York City.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/nyregion/mural/mural-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/03/nyregion/mural/mural-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/nyregion/mural/mural-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/nyregion/mural/mural-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/nyregion/mural/mural-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/03/nyregion/mural/mural-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/nyregion/mural/mural-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Cities and Cultures, Linked on a Brooklyn Wall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Cities and Cultures, Linked on a Brooklyn Wall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bond, Michaelle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smithe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'All City Canvas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name