 who was hospitalized after an eight-foot fall during a performance of Gounod’s “Faust,” is suing for damages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, Aug. 5 | Wendy White, the Metropolitan Opera mezzo-soprano who was hospitalized in December 2011 after an eight-foot fall when a piece of scenery broke during a performance, is suing the Met for damages as a result of the accident. The lawsuit was filed on Thursday, but the Met will not be served with papers until Monday, Ms. White’s lawyer, Martin Edelman, said on Friday afternoon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Singer Files Suit Against Met Opera Over Fall', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Wendy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T22:18:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69cc4422-bb1d-5fb8-bf2c-688cd33b459d', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69cc4422-bb1d-5fb8-bf2c-688cd33b459d'}, {'abstract': 'Hassan Nasrallah said his Shiite followers would not bend in the face of rising anti-Shiite sentiment among those who oppose his support for the Syrian government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/world/middleeast/under-fire-on-syria-hezbollah-leader-urges-focus-on-israel.html', 'snippet': 'Hassan Nasrallah said his Shiite followers would not bend in the face of rising anti-Shiite sentiment among those who oppose his support for the Syrian government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — In a rare public appearance on Friday, Hezbollah’s leader, Hassan Nasrallah, urged Arabs and Muslims to stay focused on opposing Israel despite bitter disagreements over the Syrian war, and declared that his Shiite followers would not bend in the face of rising anti-Shiite sentiment among those who oppose his support for the Syrian government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pressed on Syria, Hezbollah Leader Urges Focus on Israel ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pressed on Syria, Hezbollah Leader Urges Focus on Israel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hezbollah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nasrallah, Hassan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T22:19:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/222a1d45-eab5-5a22-bd2f-03aa0ff05505', 'word_count': 820, 'uri': 'nyt://article/222a1d45-eab5-5a22-bd2f-03aa0ff05505'}, {'abstract': 'The journalist, Chen Min, who had pressed for the release of a prominent human rights activist, was called to a meeting with security officials in Beijing at around noon on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/world/asia/chinese-journalist-is-detained-in-beijing.html', 'snippet': 'The journalist, Chen Min, who had pressed for the release of a prominent human rights activist, was called to a meeting with security officials in Beijing at around noon on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — A Chinese journalist who had pressed for the release of a prominent human rights activist was detained Friday, one day after the United States completed annual discussions with China on human rights.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Journalist Detained in Beijing, One Day After Human Rights Talk With U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chinese Journalist Detained in Beijing, One Day After Human Rights Talk With U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen Min', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perlez, Jane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T22:19:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Perlez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b47c294c-4b64-5621-9ee4-99d99b497bbd', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b47c294c-4b64-5621-9ee4-99d99b497bbd'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for important and peculiar items. Friday’s selections include Facebook at the DefCon hacker conference and criticism of sexually charged advertisements for Motorola’s new smartphone.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/todays-scuttlebot-facebook-at-defcon-and-selling-the-moto-x-with-innuendo/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for important and peculiar items. Friday’s selections include Facebook at the DefCon hacker conference and criticism of sexually charged advertisements for Motorola’s new smartphone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for interesting and peculiar items. Here’s what they noticed today. More Scuttlebot can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Facebook at DefCon and Selling the Moto X With Innuendo', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T22:24:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b91a9ac-290f-526a-ba76-f4bafd9b60cb', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b91a9ac-290f-526a-ba76-f4bafd9b60cb'}, {'abstract': 'Readers react to recent articles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/fashion/letters-bike-helmets-please.html', 'snippet': 'Readers react to recent articles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks for “My Mademoiselle Summer” by Meg Wolitzer (Sunday Styles, July 21). It brought me back 50 years to my days as a Mademoiselle guest editor in 1963. Her description of her time at the magazine rang true for me. To be sure, the June heat in the tiny rooms of the Barbizon Hotel for Women was grueling. But New York in 1963 seemed wondrous and innocent. Anything was possible. It was a blast. It was an honor. I made lifelong friends.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: Bike Helmets, Please', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Letters: A Special Summer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T22:33:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf0503a4-1d34-5af9-a6ee-bf257035de75', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf0503a4-1d34-5af9-a6ee-bf257035de75'}, {'abstract': 'The editorial board is composed of journalists with wide-ranging areas of expertise. Their primary responsibility is to write The Times’s editorials, which represent the voice of the board, its editor and the publisher. The board is part of the Times’s Opinion department, which is operated separately from the Times newsroom, and includes the Letters to the Editor and Op-Ed sections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/opinion