d 37 people and injured more than 120 others at the headquarters of Petróleos Mexicanos, or Pemex, on Jan. 31.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Mexican attorney general’s office said Friday that methane gas combined with vapors emitted by solvents caused the deadly explosion at the headquarters of Mexico’s state-owned oil monopoly, Petróleos Mexicanos, or Pemex, on Jan. 31. The basement blast killed 37 people and injured more than 120 others. In a statement summarizing the results of its investigation, the attorney general’s office said that hydrocarbons that had leaked into the ground decades before the building was constructed had contributed to the buildup of methane gas and that an electrical spark had probably ignited the combustible mix. Pemex is suffering from declining production and has long had a poor safety record. President Enrique Peña Nieto has said he hopes to win approval from Mexico’s Congress to open up the company to private investment before the end of the year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Blast Caused by Methane Gas, Report Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Blast Caused by Methane Gas, Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Explosions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Methane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Petroleos Mexicanos', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pena Nieto, Enrique', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pemex', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T23:58:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/909d7c1d-3aa0-5365-88c3-bcae7bd9d16d', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/909d7c1d-3aa0-5365-88c3-bcae7bd9d16d'}, {'abstract': 'A damaged subway tunnel between Manhattan and Brooklyn will be closed for work expected to last until October 2014 and to cost over $300 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/nyregion/repairs-to-a-storm-damaged-tunnel-will-disrupt-r-line-service-for-a-year.html', 'snippet': 'A damaged subway tunnel between Manhattan and Brooklyn will be closed for work expected to last until October 2014 and to cost over $300 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Extensive repair work on a subway tunnel connecting Brooklyn and Manhattan is scheduled to start this weekend, making many R train riders adjust their commutes for more than a year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Repairs to a Storm-Damaged Tunnel Will Disrupt R Line Service for a Year', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Repairs to a Storm-Damaged Tunnel Will Disrupt R Line Service for a Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delays (Transportation)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-02T23:59:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe8afe81-e84f-5b0f-ac3c-012a9d1ec5b7', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe8afe81-e84f-5b0f-ac3c-012a9d1ec5b7'}, {'abstract': 'The alarms went off inside the train that crashed last week in northwestern Spain moments before it derailed, prompting the panicked driver to activate the brakes three times, an examination revealed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/world/europe/spain-alarms-warned-trains-driver-before-accident.html', 'snippet': 'The alarms went off inside the train that crashed last week in northwestern Spain moments before it derailed, prompting the panicked driver to activate the brakes three times, an examination revealed.', 'lead_paragraph': ' At least three alarms went off inside the train that crashed last week in northwestern Spain moments before it derailed, prompting the panicked driver to activate the brakes three times even as he talked on the telephone with another employee, an examination of the train’s two black boxes released Friday revealed. The driver, Francisco José Garzón Amo, had answered a ticket inspector’s call on his cellphone and was traveling at a permitted speed of 199 kilometers per hour, or 123 miles per hour, before the train switched to another track in a reduced-speed zone. During the call, an alarm went off in the driver’s cabin. The black boxes recorded Mr. Garzón screaming as he tried to activate the brake. The train’s speed dropped to 195 k.p.h., or 121 m.p.h., but another alarm sounded, 500 yards from the curve where the accident took place. Mr. Garzón activated an emergency brake three seconds later. A third alarm sounded, and 13 train cars started derailing. Mr. Garzón activated another emergency brake as the train careened from the tracks and then slammed into a wall at 153 k.p.h., or 95 m.p.h., nearly twice the speed limit. Mr. Garzón was arrested last week and charged with reckless homicide in the deaths of 79 people. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spain: Alarms Warned Train’s Driver Before Accident', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spain: Alarms Warned Train’s Driver Before Accident', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garzon Amo, Francisco Jose', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T00:04:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e1e35f9-b4c5-56af-a68b-6391e8555d7b', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e1e35f9-b4c5-56af-a68b-6391e8555d7b'}, {'abstract': 'Stakeholders, including the New York City officials Linda I. Gibbs and Vincent N. Schiraldi, discuss policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/opinion/the-decline-of-the-prison-population.html', 'snippet': 'Stakeholders, including the New York City officials Linda I. Gibbs and Vincent N. Schiraldi, discuss policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New Yo