dicted there would be as many as a million of them on the nation’s roads by the middle of the decade.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/business/AUTOS/AUTOS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/03/business/AUTOS/AUTOS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/business/AUTOS/AUTOS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/business/AUTOS/AUTOS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1257, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/business/AUTOS/AUTOS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/03/business/AUTOS/AUTOS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/business/AUTOS/AUTOS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hankering for Hybrids', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Hankering for Hybrids', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fuel Efficiency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T00:32:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jaclyn Trop and Bill Vlasic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jaclyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vlasic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90802c18-c30b-563c-866d-3d91f69c6176', 'word_count': 1312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90802c18-c30b-563c-866d-3d91f69c6176'}, {'abstract': 'Consumers will have help calculating the best deal as they shop for insurance, but some are skeptical of the new system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/nyregion/confusion-greets-new-yorks-health-exchange.html', 'snippet': 'Consumers will have help calculating the best deal as they shop for insurance, but some are skeptical of the new system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fear and confusion seized Dolores Persky in July when she received a letter announcing that Healthy NY, a state-subsidized program of private insurance that covers her family and 90,000 other New Yorkers, would end Dec. 31. They can seek other options for affordable coverage on the New York Health Benefit Exchange under the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act starting Oct. 1, the letter from her insurer explained.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/nyregion/Y-insure/Y-insure-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/03/nyregion/Y-insure/Y-insure-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/nyregion/Y-insure/Y-insure-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/nyregion/Y-insure/Y-insure-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1406, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/nyregion/Y-insure/Y-insure-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/03/nyregion/Y-insure/Y-insure-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/nyregion/Y-insure/Y-insure-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Political Fight, Confusion and Fear About New York’s Health Exchange', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid Political Fight, Confusion and Fear About New York’s Health Exchange', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernstein, Nina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Health Benefit Exchange', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T00:34:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nina Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/263bd1ab-e74f-55da-9a97-b96b77b7987b', 'word_count': 1064, 'uri': 'nyt://article/263bd1ab-e74f-55da-9a97-b96b77b7987b'}, {'abstract': 'A corner drugstore, an extension of the family kitchen, closes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/opinion/appalachian-hope-and-heartbreak.html', 'snippet': 'A corner drugstore, an extension of the family kitchen, closes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BIG STONE GAP, Va. — A PERSON just passing through Big Stone Gap may not notice the corner drugstore on Wood Avenue with the fading sign, its windows dark and hollow like so many others in these rural coal towns. But for people who live here in the heart of central Appalachia, the Mutual Drug Cafeteria was a community hub, an extension of the family kitchen. It’s where residents could fill a prescription, pick up an oil lamp or a strawberry huller, find a plastic pirate sword for the school play and get a good cup of coffee with a plate of pork chops, soup beans, pickled beets and blackberry cobbler. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Appalachian Hope and Heartbreak', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Appalachian Hope and Heartbreak', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Amy D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'APPALACHIAN REGION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T00:41:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy D. Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c232c7b3-7d7d-5330-88ad-33323951c793', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c232c7b3-7d7d-5330-88ad-33323951c793'}, {'abstract': 'Companies that market themselves as Christian or faith-based often incorporate religion, sometimes by printing Bible verses on wrappers or by closing on Sundays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/us/at-christian-companies-religious-principles-complement-business-practices.html', 'snippet': 'Companies that market themselves as Christian or faith-based often incorporate religion, sometimes by printing Bible verses on wrappers or by closing on Sundays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In June, a federal court ruled that Hobby Lobby, the art-supply chain, could not be fined for refusing to offer its employees morning-after contraception coverage. This challenge to the Affordable Care Act will surely go to the Supreme Court, where Hobby Lobby’s lawyers will argue that a commercial company can, legally speaking, be Christian — with the same rights to religious freedom that a person has.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/us/BELIEFS-1/BELIEFS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width'