nd security forces continued in and near Cairo, the Egyptian government threatened to block entrances to a large protest camp.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — The Egyptian government threatened on Saturday to block the entrances to a large protest camp where supporters of Mohamed Morsi, the ousted president, have been calling for his return as the Obama administration sought help from Persian Gulf nations to help end Egypt’s political crisis.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/world/egypt2/egypt2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/03/world/egypt2/egypt2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/world/egypt2/egypt2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/world/egypt2/egypt2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/world/egypt2/egypt2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/03/world/egypt2/egypt2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/world/egypt2/egypt2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt Says It May Shut Entrances to Camps', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt Says It May Shut Entrances To Camps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T00:57:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Hubbard and Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hubbard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba32e91e-0034-5e54-afd1-a7e47ac88e9c', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba32e91e-0034-5e54-afd1-a7e47ac88e9c'}, {'abstract': 'Or how I began a song about animal swarms that ended up being a song about songs.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/stephen-foster-the-wildebeest-and-me/', 'snippet': 'Or how I began a song about animal swarms that ended up being a song about songs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The difference between the way a swarm or herd moves and the way, say, a crowd of panicked people disperses is this: individuals in a swarming herd have no need to understand why they’re running before they run. Each creature in the herd reacts to the movements of her immediate neighbors so that when one caribou tenses because she sees a wolf on the ridge, a ripple of tensing muscles travels through the herd, one caribou at a time, at lightning speed. They are all running before most of them have considered why they’re moving or where they’re going. This mad dashing makes for quick escapes, but it has drawbacks. The wildebeest herds sometimes gallop straight off a cliff and hundreds are dead before they can manage to come to a stop.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stephen Foster, the Wildebeest and Me', 'kicker': 'Measure for Measure', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wilderness Areas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foster, Stephen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T01:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rennie Sparks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rennie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sparks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f244a2b-d22e-5e9c-b08d-82dee1dd935e', 'word_count': 1564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f244a2b-d22e-5e9c-b08d-82dee1dd935e'}, {'abstract': 'Archaeologists do not hunt objects. We hunt lost worlds. Sadly, those worlds are slipping away under the relic-hunter’s shovel, all for the sake of a few bucks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/opinion/open-season-on-history.html', 'snippet': 'Archaeologists do not hunt objects. We hunt lost worlds. Sadly, those worlds are slipping away under the relic-hunter’s shovel, all for the sake of a few bucks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHESTER, Va. — FOR archaeologists like me, the Flowerdew Hundred Plantation near Williamsburg, Va., is our Woodstock, a sentimental spot where dozens of professionals earned their trowels. The farm’s incredible archaeological wealth ranges from 12,000-year-old Native American tools to a tree that shaded Union soldiers in June 1864.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/opinion/0803OPEDmcdonald/0803OPEDmcdonald-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/03/opinion/0803OPEDmcdonald/0803OPEDmcdonald-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 819}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/opinion/0803OPEDmcdonald/0803OPEDmcdonald-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/opinion/0803OPEDmcdonald/0803OPEDmcdonald-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/opinion/0803OPEDmcdonald/0803OPEDmcdonald-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/03/opinion/0803OPEDmcdonald/0803OPEDmcdonald-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/opinion/0803OPEDmcdonald/0803OPEDmcdonald-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Open Season on History', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'conten