or': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGinn, Colin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Miami', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T01:43:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83ab45a4-16fd-5055-b4e4-f5c2e113e09c', 'word_count': 1454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83ab45a4-16fd-5055-b4e4-f5c2e113e09c'}, {'abstract': 'Larry Summers’s intelligence, analytical mind and extensive experience make him the top candidate to head the Federal Reserve.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/02/the-right-leader-for-the-fed/', 'snippet': 'Larry Summers’s intelligence, analytical mind and extensive experience make him the top candidate to head the Federal Reserve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let me start by getting the disclosure stuff out of the way. I’ve known Larry Summers for 20 years and have watched with particular interest as his multifaceted career has unfolded. More recently, I worked for him in the Obama administration, when he was director of the National Economic Council and I was the lead adviser on the auto bailout.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Right Leader for the Fed', 'kicker': 'Steven Rattner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Summers, Lawrence H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T01:43:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Rattner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rattner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ffe31dc-a5ac-5650-8c7a-fdc25bf520c2', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ffe31dc-a5ac-5650-8c7a-fdc25bf520c2'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Ansara had a busy career as a guest star on many of the best-known television series in the 1950s, ’60s and ’70s, everything from “Broken Arrow” to “Star Trek” to “I Dream of Jeannie” to “Kojak.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/arts/michael-ansara-actor-who-played-cochise-and-kang-dies-at-91.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Ansara had a busy career as a guest star on many of the best-known television series in the 1950s, ’60s and ’70s, everything from “Broken Arrow” to “Star Trek” to “I Dream of Jeannie” to “Kojak.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Ansara, a busy and widely recognizable character actor who was best known for portraying American Indians and later a Klingon in three different “Star Trek” series, died on Wednesday at his home in Calabasas, Calif. He was 91.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/03/arts/annsara-obit-1/annsara-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/03/arts/annsara-obit-1/annsara-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 695}}