 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6628233-2f9f-5629-8fe8-487503224d03', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6628233-2f9f-5629-8fe8-487503224d03'}, {'abstract': 'The City of Detroit expects to file a plan to adjust its debts by year’s end, a lawyer said Friday during a bankruptcy hearing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/us/michigan-another-hearing-on-the-detroit-bankruptcy.html', 'snippet': 'The City of Detroit expects to file a plan to adjust its debts by year’s end, a lawyer said Friday during a bankruptcy hearing.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0The City of Detroit expects to file a plan to adjust its debts by year’s end, a lawyer said Friday during a bankruptcy hearing. And a retiree committee will represent city retirees in bankruptcy proceedings, Judge Stephen Rhodes of Federal Bankruptcy Court ruled. But the judge said that it would be up to federal trustee officials to decide who will serve on the committee and to establish deadlines. The hearing touched on a litany of\xa0preliminary issues leading up to what is expected to be a long fight over the city’s eligibility to file for bankruptcy. Those hearings will begin Oct. 23 amid concerns that bankruptcy could lead to diminished pension benefits for more than 23,000 retirees.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan: Another Hearing on the Detroit Bankruptcy', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michigan: Another Hearing On the Detroit Bankruptcy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'va