ngs and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T13:47:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'Samantha Stark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/bf3cdb07-5a9d-59e4-b6cf-a3831d2218c5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/bf3cdb07-5a9d-59e4-b6cf-a3831d2218c5'}, {'abstract': 'Two trends — learning vacations and nostalgia for good old-fashioned Americana — collide at Paws Up in western Montana, which is kicking off its first pie camp Oct. 11 to Oct. 14.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/a-camp-thats-easy-as/', 'snippet': 'Two trends — learning vacations and nostalgia for good old-fashioned Americana — collide at Paws Up in western Montana, which is kicking off its first pie camp Oct. 11 to Oct. 14.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two trends — learning vacations and nostalgia for good old-fashioned Americana — come together at one resort this fall. Paws Up in western Montana is kicking off its first pie camp Oct. 11 to Oct. 14.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Camp That’s Easy as …', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T14:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfcc0d3d-b477-56ce-9d34-81f1a6200f66', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfcc0d3d-b477-56ce-9d34-81f1a6200f66'}, {'abstract': '“No proposals were specified”.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/chronicle-of-an-impasse-foretold/', 'snippet': '“No proposals were specified”.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The big if hard-to-report story in DC last week was the ongoing collapse in governance, as Republicans proved themselves unable to reconcile their ideological commitment to drastically lower government spending with the reality that they and their constituents actually benefit from said spending. They’re willing to impose savage cuts on the poor — but even that gets them nothing like the spending cuts they claim they’ll make. Yet rather than acknowledge this reality, they’re basically sticking their heads in the sand. As the Times puts it:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chronicle of an Impasse Foretold', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T14:55:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/143bf0d6-cdf4-50df-96f9-77e0fe9d1222', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/143bf0d6-cdf4-50df-96f9-77e0fe9d1222'}, {'abstract': 'Hyperinflation and soaring rates!', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/remembering-the-wrongness/', 'snippet': 'Hyperinflation and soaring rates!', 'lead_paragraph': 'I harp a lot in this blog on the wrongness of the inflation-and-soaring rates crowd — and I do so with a purpose. The reason Very Serious People have so much damaging influence is that they come across as, well, Very Serious; yet they have in fact been not just wrong but ludicrously so, and pointing that out, repeatedly, is one way to help get our economic conversation back on track.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering the Wrongness', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T15:12:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b3a85f5-c805-5c2c-a448-9e48fe84c8bd', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b3a85f5-c805-5c2c-a448-9e48fe84c8bd'}, {'abstract': 'Titus Ryan, one of 13 receivers in the Jets’ camp, was a champion sprinter in high school who caught only six passes in college.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/sports/football/at-29-with-a-5th-team-jets-receiver-hoping-finally-to-stick.html', 'snippet': 'Titus Ryan, one of 13 receivers in the Jets’ camp, was a champion sprinter in high school who caught only six passes in college.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CORTLAND, N.Y. — Scroll down the Jets’ training camp roster, past the players with the recognizable names. Past Mark Sanchez. Past Geno Smith. Past Antonio Cromartie and D’Brickashaw Ferguson and Nick Mangold, until there, a few rows from the bottom, is No. 86.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/sports/DOG-jets/DOG-jets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'