ance” in bold Chinese characters. Nearby, in glass jars that are slightly out of reach, 10-inch fins go for $488 a pound, down from $580. For 13-inch fins, the price is now $638 a pound. Like other shops and restaurants in the city’s Chinese communities, this store is selling off its stock of shark fins.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/sunday-review/04editorial/04editorial-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 525, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/sunday-review/04editorial/04editorial-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 525}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/sunday-review/04editorial/04editorial-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 896, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/sunday-review/04editorial/04editorial-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1792, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/sunday-review/04editorial/04editorial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/04/sunday-review/04editorial/04editorial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/sunday-review/04editorial/04editorial-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shark Fins or Champagne?', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shark Fins or Champagne?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Randolph, Eleanor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sharks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruelty to Animals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T18:18:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eleanor Randolph', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eleanor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Randolph', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/77a7ddad-5d31-54ed-827c-530e5a01cd82', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77a7ddad-5d31-54ed-827c-530e5a01cd82'}, {'abstract': 'While Congress is in recess, advocates are pressing Republicans in their home districts to act on immigration reform.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/opinion/sunday/of-courage-and-cantaloupes.html', 'snippet': 'While Congress is in recess, advocates are pressing Republicans in their home districts to act on immigration reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the Senate passed a comprehensive immigration bill in June, hope for reform shifted to the House. That is where hope sits, on ice, getting freezer burn. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Of Courage and Cantaloupes', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Of Courage and Cantaloupes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Steven A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T18:18:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/79c3d285-7b5a-597a-a7f7-42eff384c7a1', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79c3d285-7b5a-597a-a7f7-42eff384c7a1'}, {'abstract': 'Apparently everyone inside the Beltway knows what isn’t so.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/03/structural-humbug/', 'snippet': 'Apparently everyone inside the Beltway knows what isn’t so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, this is really depressing. The PBS Newshour isn’t always a good place to get the best analysis, but it’s a terrific place to take the pulse of Washington conventional wisdom — and as Dean Baker notes, that conventional wisdom has clearly swung to the view that our high unemployment is “structural”, not something that could be solved simply by boosting demand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Structural Humbug', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywor