forms it into a moment of civic pride, when New Yorkers of all stripes came together to fight the disease. It’s a lovely story, if only it were true. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/sunday-review/04AIDS/04AIDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/04/sunday-review/04AIDS/04AIDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 475}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/sunday-review/04AIDS/04AIDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/sunday-review/04AIDS/04AIDS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1622, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/sunday-review/04AIDS/04AIDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/04/sunday-review/04AIDS/04AIDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/04/sunday-review/04AIDS/04AIDS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Whitewash a Plague', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Whitewash a Plague', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Hugh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New-York Historical Society', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACT UP', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, Edward I', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashton, Jean', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-03T18:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugh Ryan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bdbd2ed-a008-5cfa-9c2b-d1789a8b2425', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bdbd2ed-a008-5cfa-9c2b-d1789a8b2425'}, {'abstract': 'Our failure to provide adequate care to psychiatric patients affects us all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/04/opinion/sunday/the-woman-who-ate-cutlery.html', 'snippet': 'Our failure to provide adequate care to psychiatric patients affects us all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PROVIDENCE, R.I. — M is a 33-year old woman who swallowed silverware. She wasn’t psychotic, or out of touch with reality. She knew it was not a good idea to swallow forks and knives and she wasn’t trying to kill herself. In fact, each time she ingested utensils, she went to the emergency room so that doctors could remove them from her esophagus and stomach. Then the hospital transferred M to the psychiatric unit, where she was assigned to my care. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multime