umer. It doesn’t wash.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/business/media/time-warner-and-cbs-fighting-for-themselves.html', 'snippet': 'Both sides in the standoff over programming fees for CBS content on Time Warner Cable claim to be defending the consumer. It doesn’t wash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As consumers in the modern age, we’ve become accustomed to the brinkmanship between cable distributors and programmers. Most of the time, there is much rattling of sabers and then some accommodation is reached. But sometimes, the war of words turns into an actual war, as it did on Friday when Time Warner Cable announced it would turn off CBS stations for three million of its customers in New York, Los Angeles and Dallas.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/carr-headshot-new/carr-headshot-new-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/13/business/carr-headshot-new/carr-headshot-new-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/carr-headshot-new/carr-headshot-new-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/carr-headshot-new/carr-headshot-new-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/carr-headshot-new/carr-headshot-new-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/13/business/carr-headshot-new/carr-headshot-new-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/carr-headshot-new/carr-headshot-new-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Self-Serving War of Words by 2 Giants in Television', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Self-Serving War of Words By 2 Giants In Television', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carr, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Cable Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-04T23:36:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7bd385b-09d7-5c13-b20a-c5b1d4714fe3', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7bd385b-09d7-5c13-b20a-c5b1d4714fe3'}, {'abstract': 'Silvio Berlusconi, the former Italian prime minister, said his center-right party would continue to support Italy’s coalition government, releasing some political tension that has built since his definitive conviction for tax fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/world/europe/berlusconi-says-party-to-back-italys-coalition.html', 'snippet': 'Silvio Berlusconi, the former Italian prime minister, said his center-right party would continue to support Italy’s coalition government, releasing some political tension that has built since his definitive conviction for tax fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — A visibly shaken Silvio Berlusconi, the former Italian prime minister, said Sunday that his center-right party would continue to support Italy’s fragile coalition government, releasing some of the political tension that has built in the country since his definitive conviction for tax fraud last week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Berlusconi Says Party to Back Italy’s Coalition', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Berlusconi Says Party to Back Italy’s Coalition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pianigiani, Gaia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'People of Liberty Party (Italy)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-04T23:42:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e689041-ae7c-57d5-8599-ed8022a06b97', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e689041-ae7c-57d5-8599-ed8022a06b97'}, {'abstract': 'Parents at risk of having preterm or disabled babies need guidance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/opinion/end-of-life-at-birth.html', 'snippet': 'Parents at risk of having preterm or disabled babies need guidance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — FIFTY years ago this Wednesday, Americans were gripped by the fate of a baby — Patrick Bouvier Kennedy, the first child born to a sitting president since the 19th century, and John F. Kennedy’s last. He arrived on Aug. 7, 1963, five and a half weeks premature. Despite medical heroics, including the use of a hyperbaric oxygen chamber, he died 39 hours later. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/05/opinion/0805OPEDallsbrook/0805OPEDallsbrook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 907, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/05/opinion/0805OPEDallsbrook/0805OPEDallsbrook-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 907}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/05/opinion/0805OPEDallsbrook/0805OPEDallsbrook-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/05/opinion/0805OPEDallsbrook/0805OPEDallsbrook-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/05/opinion/0805OPEDallsbrook/0805OPEDallsbrook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/05/opinion/0805OPEDallsbrook/0805OPEDallsbrook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/05/opinion/0805OPEDallsbrook/0805OPEDallsbrook-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'End of Life, at Birth', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'End of Life, at Birth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dworetz, April R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Premature Babies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Patrick Bouvier', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-04T23:48:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By April R. Dworetz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'April', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Dworetz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee092469-9f31-5668-a52c-5d9f3b195e4a', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee092469-9f31-5668-a52c-5d9f3b195e4a'}, {'abstract': 'A virus deadly only to young pigs, with no danger for humans, appeared in the United States last spring in Ohio and in weeks had spread to four other states.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/us/hog-producers-battling-to-contain-virus-that-has-killed-piglets-by-the-thousands.html', 'snippet': 'A virus deadly only to young pigs, with no danger for humans, appeared in the United States last spring in Ohio and in weeks had spread to four other states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANNAWAN, Ill. — The outside world is not allowed in a sanitized and isolated pig farm here