d Abu Hashem, 17, was sleeping in a sleeveless undershirt when the Israeli soldiers stormed into his home here at 4 a.m. on the second Monday in July. As they led him away moments later, Muhammad’s mother rushed after with a long-sleeved shirt: they both knew it would be cold in the interrogation room.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a West Bank Culture of Conflict, Boys Wield the Weapon at Hand', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘My Hobby Is Throwing Stones’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudoren, Jodi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T01:23:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e7fbe4d-46e6-5898-9ec3-95ca3297bbc0', 'word_count': 2027, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e7fbe4d-46e6-5898-9ec3-95ca3297bbc0'}, {'abstract': 'The economy is still years away from a strong recovery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/opinion/the-long-stall.html', 'snippet': 'The economy is still years away from a strong recovery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After last week’s barrage of economic data, the best response anyone could muster was that conditions were likely to improve in the rest of the year. But even that looks like wishful thinking. Worse, though corrective government action is crucial, sound policy cures have not been forthcoming. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Long Stall', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Long Stall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T01:23:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7067c451-4769-533c-8a46-16654aba7823', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7067c451-4769-533c-8a46-16654aba7823'}, {'abstract': 'New York is expected to report a drop in student performance this week as a result of tougher testing standards, giving Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg a potential public relations problem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/nyregion/results-of-new-testing-standard-could-complicate-bloombergs-final-months.html', 'snippet': 'New York is expected to report a drop in student performance this week as a result of tougher testing standards, giving Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg a potential public relations problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael R. Bloomberg has staked much of his reputation as the mayor of New York City on improving students’ test scores, and has trumpeted gains in math and reading as validation of his 12-year effort to remake the city’s schools.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Results of New Testing Standard Could Complicate Bloomberg’s Final Months', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Results of Tougher Tests, A Challenge for Bloomberg', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Javier C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Federation of Teachers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T01:24:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Javier C. Hernández', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hernández', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/928f5e3c-1b39-5b57-b89a-7592f62eecb5', 'word_count': 891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/928f5e3c-1b39-5b57-b89a-7592f62eecb5'}, {'abstract': 'If a state chooses to put a man to death, it should at the very least adhere to the Constitution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/opinion/florida-ignores-the-supreme-court.html', 'snippet': 'If a state chooses to put a man to death, it should at the very least adhere to the Constitution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once again, a state is attempting to put to death a man who is clearly ineligible for execution under the Constitution. Once again, state and federal courts are ignoring uncontested facts by hiding behind the draperies of legal procedure. And once again we are forced to wonder why the Supreme Court is so reluctant to step in when a man’s life is at stake. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida Ignores the Supreme Court', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida Ignores the Supreme Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferguson, John Errol', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Warren Lee Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T01:32:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d869a399-7d9e-566e-8356-d349117df550', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d869a399-7d9e-566e-8356-d349117df550'}, {'abstract': 'A suit over a plan to open new schools is the union’s way of sending a message to the next mayor of New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/opinion/teachers-union-v-city-hall.html', 'snippet': 'A suit over a plan to open new schools is the union’s way of sending a message to the next mayor of New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since taking office in 2002, Mayor Michael Bloomberg has pursued an aggressive policy of replacing large, failing schools with smaller, specialized ones and greatly expanding the number of charter schools, which receive public money but are exempt from some state rules. In all, Mr. Bloomberg has shut down or begun to phase out 142 schools. In addition, the city now has 159 charters schools, up from just 17 when he took office.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teachers’ Union v. City Hall', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Teachers’ Union v. City Hall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Charter Schools', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Federation of Teachers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T01:38:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a79e531d-f330-5e71-8afb-a76f6b370290', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a79e531d-f330-5e71-8afb-a76f6b370290'}, {'abstract': 'Only one woman holds elective office in the entire government of Los Angeles, and the overwhelmingly male lineup has become a subject of chagrin and impassioned discussion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/us/in-los-angeles-few-women-in-top-posts.html', 'snippet': 'Only one woman holds elective office in the entire government of Los Angeles, and the overwhelmingly male lineup has become a subject of chagrin and impassioned discussion.', 'lead_para