': 'Early detection of cancer helps some patients but not others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/opinion/mixed-blessings.html', 'snippet': 'Early detection of cancer helps some patients but not others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pity the poor patient who tries to make sense of federal advisory committee reports that appear headed in opposite directions. For at least three decades, Americans have been told that it’s best to detect cancers early, when they are theoretically most curable. So it was not all that surprising when an authoritative advisory group recommended that very heavy smokers get an annual CT scan to check for early signs of lung cancer. It was much more surprising, however, when a separate group of experts suggested that for several cancers — including potential lung cancers — early scans are detecting too many abnormalities that aren’t dangerous and should not be treated.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mixed Blessings', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mixed Blessings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lung Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preventive Medicine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Preventive Services Task Force', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Cancer Institute', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T02:07:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '