re-storm-repairs.html', 'snippet': 'A disruption in service to fix damage caused by Hurricane Sandy has been difficult for regular passengers to accept.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In late May, executives from the Metropolitan Transportation Authority boarded an A train to the Rockaways to celebrate a hard-won milestone. For the first time since October, when Hurricane Sandy leveled the subway system with unprecedented damage, train service had been made whole again.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/05/nyregion/TUNNEL/TUNNEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/05/nyregion/TUNNEL/TUNNEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/05/nyregion/TUNNEL/TUNNEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/05/nyregion/TUNNEL/TUNNEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/05/nyregion/TUNNEL/TUNNEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/05/nyregion/TUNNEL/TUNNEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/05/nyregion/TUNNEL/TUNNEL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On R Train, Unwelcome Reminder of Storm’s Impact', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On R Train, Unwelcome Reminder of Storm’s Impact', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T02:49:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16e5095b-6734-5612-9e54-57a99ad5b76e', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16e5095b-6734-5612-9e54-57a99ad5b76e'}, {'abstract': 'The governors said that a standoff in Washington could backfire on the party if it is seen as being responsible for bringing the government to a halt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/us/politics/gop-governors-warn-party-members-in-congress-not-to-shut-government.html', 'snippet': 'The governors said that a standoff in Washington could backfire on the party if it is seen as being responsible for bringing the government to a halt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILWAUKEE — Worried about the potential impact on the fragile economies in their states, Republican governors this weekend warned their counterparts in Congress not to shut down the federal government as part of an effort to block financing for President Obama’s health care law.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/05/us/GOVERNORS-1/GOVERNORS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/05/us/GOVERNORS-1/GOVERNORS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/05/us/GOVERNORS-1/GOVERNORS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/05/us/GOVERNORS-1/GOVERNORS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1450, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Governors Warn Party Members in Congress Not to Shut Government', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.O.P. Governors Warn Party Members in Congress Not to Shut Government', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Jonathan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T02:59:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84b5a25f-d012-519b-8464-8349f17d35bd', 'word_count': 1142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84b5a25f-d012-519b-8464-8349f17d35bd'}, {'abstract': 'New York’s vote for a new mayor is also a verdict on the old one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/opinion/keller-the-referendum.html', 'snippet': 'New York’s vote for a new mayor is also a verdict on the old one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In New York’s search for a mayor to succeed Michael Bloomberg, you’d think Bill de Blasio would loom large, and not just because he’s 6-foot-5. He is policy-smart, progressive, politically savvy and untouched by scandal. He’s connected. (He ran Hillary Clinton’s first Senate campaign.) He holds a citywide job, public advocate, that, while not very demanding, is nominally next in line to the mayor. From that post he has been none-too-subtly campaigning for the top job since 2010. As the city emerges from 20 years of Republican and independent leadership and shows its true colors — which are, by most indications, deep blue — candidates don’t come much bluer than Bill de Blasio.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 350, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',