Mr. Tourre was liable on six of the seven counts. “Ultimately, the jurors said, their decision came down to what they saw as the letter of the law and, for some, a broader concern that Mr. Tourre’s actions underscored a fundamental problem with society: Wall Street greed,” Susanne Craig, Ben Protess and Alexandra Stevenson report in DealBook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Focus on Greed in Tourre Case', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T11:50:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/727f28af-7106-5c19-b4fe-cdf5edbaf9f3', 'word_count': 1752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/727f28af-7106-5c19-b4fe-cdf5edbaf9f3'}, {'abstract': 'EADS, the parent company of Airbus, confirmed on Monday that it had received a letter from the hedge fund TCI urging it to sell its 46 percent stake in Dassault Aviation.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/hedge-fund-urges-eads-to-sell-dassault-stake/', 'snippet': 'EADS, the parent company of Airbus, confirmed on Monday that it had received a letter from the hedge fund TCI urging it to sell its 46 percent stake in Dassault Aviation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 11:45 a.m. | ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hedge Fund Urges EADS to Sell Dassault Stake', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pressure To Sell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 