ealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Owner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APAX PARTNERS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HELLMAN & FRIEDMAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T13:34:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d7e5cc2-092f-57e5-8bb2-10860abdd6f0', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d7e5cc2-092f-57e5-8bb2-10860abdd6f0'}, {'abstract': 'Regular consumption of sugar-sweetened beverages has been linked to a higher body mass index in young children. Causation? Correlation? Does it matter?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/sugary-beverages-linked-to-higher-b-m-i-in-young-children/', 'snippet': 'Regular consumption of sugar-sweetened beverages has been linked to a higher body mass index in young children. Causation? Correlation? Does it matter?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It sounds like another page from the files of obvious research: a study published in the journal Pediatrics reveals a link between regular consumption of sugar-sweetened beverages (dubbed S.S.B.’s) and higher body mass index scores in 2- to 5-year-olds. Children who regularly drank sugar-sweetened sodas, sports beverages or fruit juice (as opposed to 100 percent fruit juice drinks) had both higher B.M.I.’s and “higher weight status” than those who drank them infrequently or not at all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sugary Beverages Linked to Higher B.M.I. in Young Children', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pediatrics (Journal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T13:41:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2378336b-5a05-5cab-a3bc-db4e17ae70f2', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2378336b-5a05-5cab-a3bc-db4e17ae70f2'}, {'abstract': 'Before there were satellites and personal computers, General Motors’ researchers had set up a system that, using magnets, sensors and C.B. radios, did almost everything OnStar does today.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/g-m-had-a-version-of-onstar-in-1966/', 'snippet': 'Before there were satellites and personal computers, General Motors’ researchers had set up a system that, using magnets, sensors and C.B. radios, did almost everything OnStar does today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been nearly two decades since General Motors introduced OnStar. Since then, it has served as electronic emergency nurse, computerized auto theft detective and binary butler for millions of motorists. Sure, it’s had its problems – as when G.M. decided to make the switch to digital in 2008 and told all the analog customers their equipment would no longer work. But for the most part, it has been a functional system. It must be; OnStar has already cycled through nearly a dozen hardware and software updates over the years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/automobiles/wheels/DAIR-General-Motors/DAIR-General-Motors-articleLarge.png', 'height': 446, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/02/automobiles/wheels/DAIR-General-Motors/DAIR-General-Motors-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 446}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/automobiles/wheels/DAIR-General-Motors/DAIR-General-Motors-jumbo.png', 'height': 450, 'width': 606, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/automobiles/wheels/DAIR-General-Motors/DAIR-General-Motors-superJumbo.png', 'height': 450, 'width': 606, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/automobiles/wheels/DAIR-General-Motors/DAIR-General-Motors-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/02/automobiles/wheels/DAIR-General-Motors/DAIR-General-Motors-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/02/automobiles/wheels/DAIR-General-Motors/DAIR-General-Motors-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'G.M. Had a Version of OnStar in 1966', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'na