eral states in the wake of the Newtown, Conn., school shooting, some manufacturers are relocating to more gun-friendly states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRISTOL, Conn. — Even gun makers want to be liked. So governors and other politicians from states eager to embrace the industry have descended on places where they are not so popular — like Connecticut, Maryland, New York and Colorado — offering tax breaks and outright cash grants to persuade them to relocate.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Some Gun Makers, Moving Lock, Stock and Barrel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moving Lock, Stock and Barrel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Nelson D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beretta SpA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PTR Industries', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T17:32:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson D. Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc57d1b5-fb4f-5222-8592-674fd8b0dd58', 'word_count': 1380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc57d1b5-fb4f-5222-8592-674fd8b0dd58'}, {'abstract': 'On Fox News Sunday, Eric Cantor defended his party’s shenanigans with the debt limit by arguing that the “ultimate problem” is the “growing deficit.”', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/someone-tell-cantor-the-deficit-is-shrinking/', 'snippet': 'On Fox News Sunday, Eric Cantor defended his party’s shenanigans with the debt limit by arguing that the “ultimate problem” is the “growing deficit.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Fox News Sunday, Chris Wallace asked Eric Cantor, the House Majority Leader, for a preview of what will happen the next time Congress needs to raise the debt ceiling. It was a remarkable exchange, in part because Mr. Cantor made a remarkable error.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Someone Tell Cantor: The Deficit Is Shrinking', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cantor, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T17:35:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20d40c25-45df-51b2-a01f-bfbfa4900f7a', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20d40c25-45df-51b2-a01f-bfbfa4900f7a'}, {'abstract': 'A thing everyone intuitively understands — how mysterious and subjective the experience of passing time is — gets a closer look in Claudia Hammond’s entertaining book “Time Warped.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/science/how-we-perceive-and-misperceive-time.html', 'snippet':