nk': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnival Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Norwegian Cruise Line', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Caribbean Cruises Ltd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T22:33:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afff62fe-e907-52c8-b07d-dcb184a799f7', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afff62fe-e907-52c8-b07d-dcb184a799f7'}, {'abstract': 'The Hamptons will play host to not one but two potential 2016 presidential aspirants this month, with Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. vacationing in Southampton and Hillary Rodham Clinton renting a house in East Hampton for August.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/biden-vacationing-in-the-hamptons/', 'snippet': 'The Hamptons will play host to not one but two potential 2016 presidential aspirants this month, with Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. vacationing in Southampton and Hillary Rodham Clinton renting a house in East Hampton for August.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST HAMPTON — The Hamptons will play host to not one but two potential 2016 presidential aspirants this month, with Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. arriving this week for a vacation in Southampton. Former Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton has rented a house for August here in East Hampton, the next township over.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden Vacationing in the Hamptons', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamptons (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T22:34:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05f6abd9-1454-5efb-a7b8-baef99558d65', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05f6abd9-1454-5efb-a7b8-baef99558d65'}, {'abstract': 'Facing possible bankruptcy, Detroit has hired the auction house Christie’s to evaluate the value of part of its collection at the Detroit Institute of Arts.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/detroit-manager-hires-christies-to-appraise-holdings-at-city-art-museum/', 'snippet': 'Facing possible bankruptcy, Detroit has hired the auction house Christie’s to evaluate the value of part of its collection at the Detroit Institute of Arts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The city of Detroit, which has filed for bankruptcy, has formally hired the international auction house Christie’s to appraise part of the city-owned art collection held by the Detroit Institute of Arts, the auction house said Monday.Any decision about whether to sell the art to satisfy creditors has not been made, city officials have said, though all the city’s assets are being evaluated in light of the situation in Detroit, the largest American city ever to file for bankruptcy.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Detroit Manager Hires Christie’s to Appraise Holdings at City Art Museum', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Christie’s to Appraise Holdings at Detroit Art Museum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Institute of Arts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T22:38:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58e88059-b263-56e5-8e6e-f4684eeadfdc', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58e88059-b263-56e5-8e6e-f4684eeadfdc'}, {'abstract': 'Rodriguez’s numbers have become irrelevant in measuring who he is as a baseball player.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/how-a-rod-doesnt-add-up/', 'snippet': 'Rodriguez’s numbers have become irrelevant in measuring who he is as a baseball player.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before I played a single game of professional baseball, I was a fan. If my brother and I weren’t chipping the paint off our parents’ garage door with wayward pitches during an extra-inning session of Wiffle ball, we were playing simulated games like Strat-O-Matic or baseball on our then popular ’80s Intellivision video game system. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How A-Rod Doesn’t Add Up', 'kicker': 'Doug Glanville', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T22:50:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'secti