’s biggest investors, the activist hedge fund manager Daniel S. Loeb.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/sony-rejects-loeb-proposal-for-splitting-off-entertainment-unit/', 'snippet': 'Sony plans to hold onto all of its vast entertainment arm, rejecting a proposal by one of the Japanese conglomerate’s biggest investors, the activist hedge fund manager Daniel S. Loeb.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 6:31 a.m. | Sony said late on Monday that it planned to keep all of its vast entertainment arm, rejecting a proposal by one of its biggest investors, the activist hedge fund manager Daniel S. Loeb.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sony Rejects Loeb Proposal for Splitting Off Entertainment Unit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sony Decides It Will Keep All of Entertainment Arm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirai, Kazuo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loeb, Daniel S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T23:47:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/391659df-d1cd-55ec-be8e-77899d490a5e', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/391659df-d1cd-55ec-be8e-77899d490a5e'}, {'abstract': 'Two children were killed in their sleep by a python that escaped from a pet shop, the Royal Canadian Mounted Police said Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/world/americas/canada-escaped-snake-kills-2-children-police-say.html', 'snippet': 'Two children were killed in their sleep by a python that escaped from a pet shop, the Royal Canadian Mounted Police said Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Two children were killed in their sleep by a python that escaped from a pet shop, the Royal Canadian Mounted Police said Monday. The boys, 5 and 7 years old, were sleeping over at a friend’s apartment above the store in Campbellton, New Brunswick, when the snake apparently made its way in through a ventilation shaft. An autopsy will determine the exact cause of death, but a police spokeswoman said it appeared that the children had been suffocated. It was not immediately clear how the snake had escaped from the store, but police officers recaptured it. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Escaped Snake Kills 2 Children, Police Say', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Escaped Snake Kills 2 Children, Police Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asphyxiation, Choking, and Suffocation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Brunswick (Canada)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-05T23:57:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad0cb0b4-b2a8-55a7-a57c-f9dc08dcca7d', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad0cb0b4-b2a8-55a7-a57c-f9dc08dcca7d'}, {'abstract': 'Lynne Stewart, who was sentenced in 2010 to 10 years in prison for smuggling messages from an imprisoned client to his violent followers in Egypt, is seeking to have her sentence vacated because she has cancer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/nyregion/dying-lawyer-asks-judge-to-release-her-from-prison.html', 'snippet': 'Lynne Stewart, who was sentenced in 2010 to 10 years in prison for smuggling messages from an imprisoned client to his violent followers in Egypt, is seeking to have her sentence vacated because she has cancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lynne F. Stewart, the outspoken former defense lawyer and a polarizing figure in the criminal justice system, is fighting her final battle.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/nyregion/y-STEWART/y-STEWART-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 522, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/nyregion/y-STEWART/y-STEWART-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 522, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/nyregion/y-STEWART/y-STEWART-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStanda