p-in-new-york/', 'snippet': 'Letters are sent to 35 online lenders for charging more than New York State’s 25 percent interest rate cap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Government authorities are homing in on a lucrative loophole that allows online lenders to offer short-term loans at interest rates that often exceed 500 percent annually, the latest front in a crackdown on the payday lending industry.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Tells Online Lenders to Abide by State’s Interest Rate Cap', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Online Lenders Told to Abide By Interest Cap In New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payday Loans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawsky, Benjamin M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T00:06:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Silver-Greenberg and Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cda77b7-5973-5288-9e84-c2304aa4b765', 'word_count': 1209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cda77b7-5973-5288-9e84-c2304aa4b765'}, {'abstract': 'Compensation deferral was meant to give employees less incentive to take the kinds of short-term risks that led to the financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/05/pay-deferrals-for-bankers-are-tougher-in-europe/', 'snippet': 'Compensation deferral was meant to give employees less incentive to take the kinds of short-term risks that led to the financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soon after the financial crisis, international regulators identified Wall Street’s lush pay packages as one of the culprits and proposed an overhaul that was meant to apply equally to employees of American investment banks and their big European rivals.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bankers’ Pay Deferrals Are Tougher in Europe', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pay Deferrals For Bankers Are Tougher In Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T00:12:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b1f88a0-e003-5e66-b3b0-f1734793ba35', 'word_count': 1121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b1f88a0-e003-5e66-b3b0-f1734793ba35'}, {'abstract': 'I’m an attorney with bipolar disorder. That’s nothing to worry about.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/opinion/lawyers-of-sound-mind.html', 'snippet': 'I’m an attorney with bipolar disorder. That’s nothing to worry about.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RALEIGH, N.C. — LAST week, swarms of sun-starved, soon-to-be lawyers emerged from hiding to celebrate completing the bar exam. Passing the exam, however, won’t guarantee them admission to the bar. They also have to demonstrate that they possess the requisite fitness and moral character for the practice of law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/opinion/0806OPEDparini/0806OPEDparini-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 933, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/06/opinion/0806OPEDparini/0806OPEDparini-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 933}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/opinion/0806OPEDparini/0806OPEDparini-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/opinion/0806OPEDparini/0806OPEDparini-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/opinion/0806OPEDparini/0806OPEDparini-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/06/opinion/0806OPEDparini/0806OPEDparini-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/opinion/0806OPEDparini/0806OPEDparini-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'th