bject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T00:24:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f3bf5a7-ad92-551b-8d19-6e7f77137c61', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f3bf5a7-ad92-551b-8d19-6e7f77137c61'}, {'abstract': 'The Transportation Security Administration issued justification for conducting searches outside airports without probable cause, but an audit raised issues about the training and deployments of the VIPR teams.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/08/06/us/06vipr-documents.html', 'snippet': 'The Transportation Security Administration issued justification for conducting searches outside airports without probable cause, but an audit raised issues about the training and deployments of the VIPR teams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Transportation Security Administration issued justification for conducting searches outside airports without probable cause, but an audit raised issues about the training and deployments of the VIPR teams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyond the Airport: The T.S.A.’s VIPR Team', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Security Administration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T00:24:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/4d01a3f3-e4d5-55ab-b9a4-872944b2abc3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/4d01a3f3-e4d5-55ab-b9a4-872944b2abc3'}, {'abstract': 'In 2003, Dr. Morwood and his team dug up remains of Homo floresiensis, or the little people of Flores who were nicknamed the hobbits, in an Indonesian island cave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/science/michael-j-morwood-archaeologist-who-helped-find-new-human-dies-at-62.html', 'snippet': 'In 2003, Dr. Morwood and his team dug up remains of Homo floresiensis, or the little people of Flores who were nicknamed the hobbits, in an Indonesian island cave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ten years ago, Mike Morwood was a leader of archaeological excavations in a limestone cavern on the Indonesian island of Flores, about midway between the continents of Asia and Australia. That was when he had the experience of a lifetime, as he said many times, the discovery of what he called “a new human.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/world/MORWOOD-3-obit/MORWOOD-3-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 534, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/06/world/MORWOOD-3-obit/MORWOOD-3-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 534}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/world/MORWOOD-3-obit/MORWOOD-3-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 911, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/