bject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T00:53:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6e5e80f-fe71-5f91-b293-215c1408cd37', 'word_count': 1222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6e5e80f-fe71-5f91-b293-215c1408cd37'}, {'abstract': 'Donovan, a 300-pound tackle on the Baltimore Colts’ championship teams in 1958 and 1959, was known for his self-deprecating modesty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/sports/football/art-donovan-a-behemoth-of-modesty-dies-at-89.html', 'snippet': 'Donovan, a 300-pound tackle on the Baltimore Colts’ championship teams in 1958 and 1959, was known for his self-deprecating modesty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art Donovan, a 300-pound tackle for the Baltimore Colts whose nimble brutality helped propel him to the Hall of Fame and his team to two championships in the 1950s, and whose humor-laced tales about himself and the game won him an equal helping of celebrity, died on Sunday in Baltimore. He was 89.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/sports/DONOVAN-1-obit/DONOVAN-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/06/sports/DONOVAN-1-obit/DONOVAN-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/sports/D