tname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46660b29-3252-59d5-89a5-a3052dac9b31', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46660b29-3252-59d5-89a5-a3052dac9b31'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/arts/television/whats-on-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:50 A.M. (Cinemax) MATCH POINT (2005) Chris (Jonathan Rhys Meyers), an Irish tennis player recently retired from the professional circuit, climbs the British social ladder after taking a job at a London club, helping its rich members polish their strokes. Soon, he has befriended Tom (Matthew Goode), an heir to a business fortune; has wooed his sister, Chloe (Emily Mortimer); and maneuvered himself into the family firm and into the family as Tom’s brother-in-law. But then Chris meets Tom’s fiancée, a scrappy American actress, Nola (Scarlett Johansson, above, with Mr. Rhys Meyers), and suddenly the temperature of his life increases from a polite simmer to a full sexual boil. “What passes between Chris and Nola is not only desire, but also recognition, which makes their connection especially volatile,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times, describing this drama as “a Champagne cocktail laced with strychnine.” He added: “As their affair advances, Ms. Johansson and Mr. Rhys Meyers manage some of the best acting seen in a Woody Allen movie in a long time, escaping the archness and emotional disconnection that his writing often imposes. It is possible to identify with both of them — and to feel an empathetic twinge as they are ensnared in the consequences of their own heedlessness — without entirely liking either one. But it is the film’s brisk, chilly precision that makes it so bracingly pleasurable. The gloom of random, meaningless existence has rarely been so much fun, and Mr. Allen’s bite has never been so sharp, or so deep. A movie this good is no laughing matter.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c7fbabf-de6b-5f9d-9029-5ecf18f86e3e', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c7fbabf-de6b-5f9d-9029-5ecf18f86e3e'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes a meeting with our youthful selves reminds us of the roads yet to be explored.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/booming/a-reunion-with-my-younger-hitchhiking-self.html', 'snippet': 'Sometimes a meeting with our youthful selves reminds us of the roads yet to be explored.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Summer of 1972: a slender 19-year-old (curly black hair, florid beard, 155 pounds) stood beside a Montana highway, thumb in the air. A truck pulled over. “Going as far as Missoula,” the driver said, opening the cargo doors. In the hold, others crouched, blinking back at him. “Thanks, man,” he said, hopping in. The doors shut; the latch turned.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/booming/06mystory-booming-hitchhike1/06mystory-booming-hitchhike1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/06/booming/06mystory-booming-hitchhike1/06mystory-booming-hitchhike1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/booming/06mystory-booming-hitchhike1/06mystory-booming-hitchhike1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/booming/06mystory-booming-hitchhike1/06mystory-booming-hitchhike1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1415, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/booming/06mystory-booming-hitchhike1/06mystory-booming-hitchhike1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/06/booming/06mystory-booming-hitchhike1/06mystory-booming-hitchhike1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/booming/06mystory-booming-hitchhike1/06mystory-booming-hitchhike1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Reunion With My Younger, Hitchhiking Self', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hitchhiking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f604a12-a26c-518a-bb30-cb22b2eae8c0', 'word_count': 1464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f604a12-a26c-518a-bb30-cb22b2eae8c0'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/news-quiz-august-6-2013/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | August 6, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T05:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/934ab5cb-ca40-528b-9d2c-dc3aa5232e09', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/934ab5cb-ca40-528b-9d2c-dc3aa5232e09'}, {'abstract': 'A new Vietnamese decree appears to limit the ability of people to share news stories critical of the government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/world/asia/us-assails-new-limits-on-internet-in-vietnam.html', 'snippet': 'A new Vietnamese decree appears to limit the ability of people to share news stories critical of the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — American officials criticized the Vietnamese government on Tuesday for its new limits on political dissent on the Internet, citing a decree that appears to restrict people from sharing news articles on social media and personal Web sites.', 'print_section': 'A