rticle', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ab5b833-18fc-5dd1-8d2f-ec035b03827d', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ab5b833-18fc-5dd1-8d2f-ec035b03827d'}, {'abstract': 'But addressing this issue lays bare a vexing issue: Why should my employees work harder for my benefit? How can I enforce the changes in culture I want to implement?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/i-want-to-make-a-profit/', 'snippet': 'But addressing this issue lays bare a vexing issue: Why should my employees work harder for my benefit? How can I enforce the changes in culture I want to implement?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have a problem: my business is not very profitable. Over the last three full years, 2010-12, our sales totaled $5,606,056. But our profits were only $81,646. That’s a pathetic 1.4-percent profit margin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Want to Make a Profit', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Downs, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paul Downs Cabinetmakers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T11:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcacb47b-c1b8-55d4-a734-ed439195d562', 'word_count': 1592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcacb47b-c1b8-55d4-a734-ed439195d562'}, {'abstract': 'Benny Napoleon was the top vote-getter among 14 candidates on the ballot, and a strong write-in vote propelled Mike Duggan, who will face Mr. Napoleon in a November runoff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/us/detroit-mayoral-primary.html', 'snippet': 'Benny Napoleon was the top vote-getter among 14 candidates on the ballot, and a strong write-in vote propelled Mike Duggan, who will face Mr. Napoleon in a November runoff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — Benny Napoleon, the sheriff of Wayne County, and Mike Duggan, the former chief executive of the Detroit Medical Center, will vie for the post of mayor after getting the most votes in a crowded field of primary candidates Tuesday in this blighted city seeking bankruptcy protection.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/us/subDETROIT/subDETROIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/07/us/subDETROIT/subDETROIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/us/subDETROIT/subDETROIT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/us/subDETROIT/subDETROIT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', '