nization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/e24c828d-aa19-521d-8cd6-300435369769', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/e24c828d-aa19-521d-8cd6-300435369769'}, {'abstract': 'The currency has been in a slide against the dollar since May, when the United States said it might scale back bond purchases and foreign capital began to flee India.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/business/global/indian-rupee-falls-to-record-low.html', 'snippet': 'The currency has been in a slide against the dollar since May, when the United States said it might scale back bond purchases and foreign capital began to flee India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The Indian rupee lurched to a record low against the dollar on Tuesday, shrugging off recent measures aimed at propping it up and underscoring the severe problems facing the economy as the country heads toward an election next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian Rupee Falls to Record Low', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indian Rupee Falls to Record Low', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian Rupee (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T11:22:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bettina Wassener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bettina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wassener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/427786c2-d773-5c07-bad3-ab7d75d5a28d', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/427786c2-d773-5c07-bad3-ab7d75d5a28d'}, {'abstract': 'The founder of Amazon.com is buying The Washington Post for $250 million in cash. | Sony plans to keep all of its entertainment arm, rejecting a proposal by an investor. | European banks appear to be deferring more banker pay than their American counterparts. | New York State’s financial regulator is cracking down on high-interest lending.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/morning-agenda-bezos-buys-a-landmark-in-washington/', 'snippet': 'The founder of Amazon.com is buying The Washington Post for $250 million in cash. | Sony plans to keep all of its entertainment arm, rejecting a proposal by an investor. | European banks appear to be deferring more banker pay than their American c...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeffrey P. Bezos, the founder of Amazon.com, has agreed to buy The Washington Post for $250 million in cash, in a deal that has shocked the newspaper industry. Donald E. Graham, chairman and chief executive of The Washington Post Company, said he and the publisher “decided to sell only after years of familiar newspaper-industry challenges made us wonder if there might be another owner who would be better for the Post.” The sale is expected to be completed within 60 days.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bezos Buys a Landmark in Washington', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T11:46:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/032a97e1-94be-5c50-a229-41bca433a983', 'word_count': 1998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/032a97e1-94be-5c50-a229-41bca433a983'}, {'abstract': 'The playwright Young Jean Lee performs a monologue from her pop-music cabaret, at the Claire Tow Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/in-performance-young-jean-lee-of-were-gonna-die/', 'snippet': 'The playwright Young Jean Lee performs a monologue from her pop-music cabaret, at the Claire Tow Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The downtown playwright Young Jean Lee asks some darkly comic existential questions in her pop-music cabaret “We’re Gonna Die.” Charles Isherwood called the show a “bizarre combination of pop concert and autobiographical lament for the human condition” when it ran at Joe’s Pub in 2011. It’s now playing (through Aug. 17) at the Claire Tow Theater at Lincoln Center, and is also available as an album. In this scene, Ms. Lee performs “Henry,” a monologue about a painful breakup. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Young Jean Lee of ‘We’re Gonna Die’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Young Jean', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T12:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e86bbc78-0d2f-5d51-98ef-b7b2dbc8e96c', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e86bbc78-0d2f-5d51-98ef-b7b2dbc8e96c'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A woman’s encounter with an acquaintance at the Museum of Modern Art proved awkward.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/spotted-with-a-man-who-wasnt-her-husband/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A woman’s encounter with an acquaintance at the Museum of Modern Art proved awkward.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spotted With a Man Who Wasn’t Her Husband', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T12:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth Epstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Epstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36c4765f-21f0-55b4-a131-2d6e31c07769', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36c4765f-21f0-55b4-a131-2d6e31c07769'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama endorsed efforts in the Senate to wind down the two mortgage finance giants and end their longtime implicit guarantee of a federal government bailout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/us/politics/obama-fannie-mae-freddie-mac.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama endorsed efforts in the Senate to wind down the two mortgage finance giants and end their longtime implicit guarantee of a federal government bailout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — President Obama hailed both this city’s and the country’s comeback from the housing bust on Tuesday, and said it was now time to reduce the federal role and risk in the mortgage market “to make sure the kind of crisis we went through never happens again.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia