Blasio’s stance on stop-and-frisk in a written endorsement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/nyregion/soros-to-endorse-de-blasio-for-mayor.html', 'snippet': 'The billionaire financier George Soros praised Bill de Blasio’s stance on stop-and-frisk in a written endorsement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a move that could excite left-leaning New Yorkers — but turn away some more centrist ones — the billionaire financier and liberal icon George Soros endorsed Bill de Blasio, the public advocate, on Tuesday as the next mayor of New York.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Soros Endorses de Blasio for Mayor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Soros Endorses\r\nDe Blasio for Mayor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soros, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T13:03:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47624888-6201-5086-86a4-efe7b95479a9', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47624888-6201-5086-86a4-efe7b95479a9'}, {'abstract': 'Former President George W. Bush underwent a surgical procedure Tuesday morning in which doctors inserted a stent to open a blocked artery, aides said.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/george-w-bush-undergoes-heart-procedure/', 'snippet': 'Former President George W. Bush underwent a surgical procedure Tuesday morning in which doctors inserted a stent to open a blocked artery, aides said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 10:39 a.m. | Former President George W. Bush was released from a Dallas hospital on Wednesday morning, a day after undergoing a surgical procedure to open up a clogged artery.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'George W. Bush Released from Hospital After Heart Procedure', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: George W. Bush Has Procedure to Open Artery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stents (Medical Devices)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T13:38:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c241373-9cc2-589a-b808-98694971ede2', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c241373-9cc2-589a-b808-98694971ede2'}, {'abstract': 'More Americans are traveling to Europe and Asia to undergo elective surgery like a hip replacement, which can save tens of thousands of dollars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/us/the-growing-popularity-of-having-surgery-overseas.html', 'snippet': 'More Americans are traveling to Europe and Asia to undergo elective surgery like a hip replacement, which can save tens of thousands of dollars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As health care costs in the United States rise, an increasing