ubject', 'value': 'Medical Devices', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zimmer Holdings Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Implants', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Warsaw (Ind)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T14:01:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5b5f95e-3063-50dc-8d8f-1b4041b2a401', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5b5f95e-3063-50dc-8d8f-1b4041b2a401'}, {'abstract': 'Sportswriters confronted a sad but unforgettable day in baseball in different ways, with some wondering whether Alex Rodriguez’s entire career is a fiction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/sports/baseball/biogenesis-day-at-the-ballpark.html', 'snippet': 'Sportswriters confronted a sad but unforgettable day in baseball in different ways, with some wondering whether Alex Rodriguez’s entire career is a fiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the end, the lasting feeling on baseball’s big drug day was sadness. It was sad to read the apologies from the players caught, suspended and accepting their fate. It was sad that some were so obscure that they did not need to apologize. It was sad that people in Chicago bought tickets to a White Sox game only to jeer the saddest spectacle of all, the Yankees’ Alex Rodriguez left on his own to tilt at the windmills of his imagination.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biogenesis Day at the Ballpark', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peralta, Jhonny', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Nelson', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T14:12:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41452093-3ef4-518e-8367-4673865726a6', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41452093-3ef4-518e-8367-4673865726a6'}, {'abstract': 'When the utterly false is “half true”.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/politifact-and-the-shape-of-the-planet-deficit-edition/', 'snippet': 'When the utterly false is “half true”.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steve Benen catches PolitiFact falling down on the job. But it’s actually even worse than he says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'PolitiFact and the Shape of the Planet, Deficit Edition', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T14:25:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25d568af-0fcd-5bf3-921f-2955df6b2151', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25d568af-0fcd-5bf3-921f-2955df6b2151'}, {'abstract': 'Uncertainty? Never mind.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/another-bad-story-bites-the-dust/', 'snippet': 'Uncertainty? Never mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the remarkable things about the ongoing economic crisis is the endless search for explanations of something that’s actually quite simple — the sluggish pace of recovery. You have a large overhang of private debt; you have a still-depressed housing sector; and you have contractionary fiscal policy. Add to this the well-established fact that recovery tends to be slow after recessions caused not by tight money but by private-sector overreach, and there’s just no mystery that needs explaining.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Bad Story Bites The Dust', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T14:42:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11002c6c-8d3b-50a7-ae3a-9c129a0ac66c', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11002c6c-8d3b-50a7-ae3a-9c129a0ac66c'}, {'abstract': 'A rare 1931 Blower Bentley and a one-off 1953 Ferrari were shown in New York last week in advance of the Aug. 16 auction at Pebble Beach.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/two-cars-destined-for-pebble-beach-auction-shown-in-manhattan/', 'snippet': 'A rare 1931 Blower Bentley and a one-off 1953 Ferrari were shown in New York last week in advance of the Aug. 16 auction at Pebble Beach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two cars destined for the auction block at Bonhams Quail Lodge auction during the Pebble Beach Concours d’Élégance on Aug. 16 showed up at Bonhams’ Madison Avenue offices last week for a sneak preview. They were a one-off 1953 Ferrari 250 Europa Coupé and a rare 1931 Bentley 4½ Liter Supercharged Le Mans car.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/automobiles/wheels/Blower-Bentley-1962/Blower-Bentley-1962-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/06/automobiles/wheels/Blower-Bentley-1962/Blower-Bentley-1962-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/automobiles/wheels/Blower-Bentley-1962/Blower-Bentley-1962-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/automobiles/wheels/Blower-Bentley-1962/Blower-Bentley-1962-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1056, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/automobiles/wheels/Blower-Bentley-1962/Blower-Bentley-1962-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/06/automobiles/wheels/Blower-Bentley-1962/Blower-Bentley-1962-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thum