 companies would assume responsibility for these defined benefit plans, offering annuities to beneficiaries in exchange for employer-paid premiums. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pension Reform Could Disrupt Investment Funds', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T14:56:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Fleischer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fleischer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66ef2d67-385c-593e-8611-5cee1314f1f9', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66ef2d67-385c-593e-8611-5cee1314f1f9'}, {'abstract': 'An 11-year-old who has a bow-tie business. Why unions may hate the new health care law. Why your business needs an app.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/today-in-small-business-budget-bedlam-looming/', 'snippet': 'An 11-year-old who has a bow-tie business. Why unions may hate the new health care law. Why your business needs an app.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s affecting me, my clients and other small-business owners today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today in Small Business: Budget Bedlam Looming', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T15:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Bu