web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/the-cartes-de-visite-craze/', 'snippet': 'How these small, personal photographs helped change the way Northerners saw the Civil War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most indelible images of the Civil War show us the ditches of Antietam, the fields of Gettysburg and the ruins of Richmond. They tell us about modern photography and modern war, but the staple photographs of the home front were not the battlefield views we now know so well. Cartes de visite, the 2 1/2-by-4-inch portraits that dominated commercial photography in the 1860s, both unified and contested wartime visions of the nation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cartes de Visite Craze', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Mathew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T18:11:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrea L. Volpe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrea', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Volpe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec4c9fd2-3c8e-56c8-aeee-afb8d72bf256', 'word_count': 1715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec4c9fd2-3c8e-56c8-aeee-afb8d72bf256'}, {'abstract': 'Readers question if technologies that can hack our brains, removing our memories, take technology too far.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/does-altering-the-human-mind-take-technology-too-far/', 'snippet': 'Readers question if technologies that can hack our brains, removing our memories, take technology too far.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my column this week, “Computer-Brain Interfaces Making Big Leaps,” I noted that a number of researchers and scientists were coming closer to technology usually reserved for science fiction: hacking our brains to remove unwanted and sad memories.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/technology/bits-brain/bits-brain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 287, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/technology/bits-brain/bits-brain-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 287, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/technology/bits-brain/bits-brain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/06/technology/bits-brain/bits-brain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/technology/bits-brain/bits-brain-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Drawing the Line on Altering Human Minds', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memory', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T18:14:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d759c39a-6a7b-50f1-9bc4-45093ff2df29', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d759c39a-6a7b-50f1-9bc4-45093ff2df29'}, {'abstract': 'Liz Cheney’s early purchase of a resident fishing license in Wyoming has inflamed her critics in the state, who have already accused her of being an interloper who should not dare challenge Senator Michael B. Enzi in next year’s Republican primary.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/fishing-license-becomes-issue-for-liz-cheney-in-wyoming-senate-race/', 'snippet': 'Liz Cheney’s early purchase of a resident fishing license in Wyoming has inflamed her critics in the state, who have already accused her of being an interloper who should not dare challenge Senator Michael B. Enzi in next year’s Republican primary...', 'lead_paragraph': 'It sounds like a small-bore infraction: Liz Cheney, a United States Senate candidate in Wyoming, bought a state fishing license last summer even though she had not lived in the state for a year, as required.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fishing License Becomes Issue for Liz Cheney in Wyoming Senate Race', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T18:24:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard L. Berke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Berke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df52099e-60b9-5630-89e6-f01e6f60bc7d', 'word_count': 448, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df52099e-60b9-5630-89e6-f01e6f60bc7d'}, {'abstract': 'The online retailer will sell original and limited-edition art ranging in price from a $10 screen print to a $4.85 million painting by Norman Rockwell.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/amazon-expands-to-sell-art-online/', 'snippet': 'The online retailer will sell original and limited-edition art ranging in price from a $10 screen print to a $4.85 million painting by Norman Rockwell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A day after the news that Amazon’s founder and chief executive,\xa0Jeff Bezos,\xa0is buying The Washington Post, his company officially entered another cultural arena: art. On Tuesday, the online retailer announced the start of Amazon Art, where customers can buy original and limited-edition art from more than 150 dealers and 4,500 artists, ranging in price from a $10 screen print by the up-and-comer Ryan Humphrey to a\xa0 $4.85 million\xa0painting by Norman Rockwell.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/arts3/arts3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 486, 'width': 391, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/arts3/arts3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 486, 'width': 391, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/arts3/arts3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/arts3/arts3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/arts3/arts3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazon Re-Enters Online Art Market', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amazon Returns to Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T18:26:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3427bb3-b206-5fef-a964-8e9d540d1c02', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3427bb3-b206-5fef-a964-8e9d540d1c02'}, {'abstract': 'For $49 a year, TripIt Pro offers useful perks like reminders about travel plans and alerts about flight delays, gate changes and fare refunds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/technology/personaltech/a-travel-organizer-for-families-and-frequent-fliers.html', 'snippet': 'For $49 a year, TripIt Pro offers useful perks like reminders about travel plans and alerts about flight delays, gate changes and fare refunds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'August is a time for families to wind down the summer with a final trip before school starts. Keeping on top of travel arrangements and changes is crucial.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/technology/personaltech/GW-TripIt-Pro-iPad/GW-TripIt-Pro-iPad-articleLarge.png', 'height': 458, 'w