13/08/07/dining/vegetables-and-pasta-summer-love.html', 'snippet': 'When light, bright and fresh is what you’re after.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s for Dinner? answers that universal question, offering recipes for simple, relatively quick dishes that use ingredients you can pick up on the way home.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/dining/07DINNER/07DINNER-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/07/dining/07DINNER/07DINNER-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/dining/07DINNER/07DINNER-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/dining/07DINNER/07DINNER-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/dining/07DINNER/07DINNER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/07/dining/07DINNER/07DINNER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/dining/07DINNER/07DINNER-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vegetables and Pasta: Summer Love', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vegetables and Pasta: Summer Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pasta', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zucchini', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T18:49:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f817b3d8-3a63-5cdf-b613-b18163f0f70a', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f817b3d8-3a63-5cdf-b613-b18163f0f70a'}, {'abstract': 'The mustachioed Brazilian baritone brings swashbuckling star power to a weeklong engagement at the Midtown supper club 54 Below.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/after-hours-paulo-szots-outsize-broadway-grandeur/', 'snippet': 'The mustachioed Brazilian baritone brings swashbuckling star power to a weeklong engagement at the Midtown supper club 54 Below.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A major swath of New York fell in love with Paulo Szot when he appeared in the 2008 Lincoln Center revival of South Pacific. The mustachioed baritone won a Tony for his gravitas-laden turn as Emile de Becque, the French plantation owner who captures the heart of young Navy nurse Nellie Forbush. Last night, in the high-class-bordello setting of the Midtown supper club 54 Below, Szot, kicking off a weeklong stint there, captured several more hearts… of a certain age. Szot, who has a booming operatic voice and is built like a massive rectangle, swashbuckled into the room from the back, schmoozing his way to a stage where a jazz trio awaited him. Even amid his opening number, a playful mash-up of “Summertime” and “Too Darn Hot,” many a well-heeled matron shrieked or moaned aloud for him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Hours | Paulo Szot’s Outsize Broadway Grandeur', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Szot, Paulo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '54 Below (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T18:51:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60b8ecb0-bdc5-5ba3-9d59-e28e6518c584', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60b8ecb0-bdc5-5ba3-9d59-e28e6518c584'}, {'abstract': 'Would it be immoral and divisive for the G.O.P. to exploit liberalism’s white working class weakness?', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/republicans-white-voters-and-racial-polarization/', 'snippet': 'Would it be immoral and divisive for the G.O.P. to exploit liberalism’s white working class weakness?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This National Journal piece, the latest to misread Sean Trende’s columns on the “missing white voters” of 2012 as an argument that the G.O.P. should try to build a “whites-only” majority, reminds that I’ve been meaning to write about some of the various liberal responses to Trende’s argument. Not the responses saying that he’s factually or analytically wrong, but the responses that either imply or state that even if he were right that there are a lot of up-for-grabs white votes that the G.O.P. might pursue effectively, it would be immoral, tragic, and/or ruinously divisive\xa0if Republicans were to actually try to win this way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans, White Voters and Racial Polarization', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dorgan, Byron L', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T18:56:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a71dd2f1-0a4b-566f-aa9a-ee7432bbe722', 'word_count': 1285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a71dd2f1-0a4b-566f-aa9a-ee7432bbe722'}, {'abstract': 'Tell us: Who is the unofficial mayor of your community?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/a-call-for-the-unofficial-mayors-of-new-york/', 'snippet': 'Tell