'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d743273-a971-5a0c-a159-8599fc20ae50', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d743273-a971-5a0c-a159-8599fc20ae50'}, {'abstract': 'The government accused the bank of defrauding investors by vastly understating the risks of the mortgages backing about $850 million worth of mortgage-backed securities.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/justice-sues-bank-of-america-over-mortgage-securities/', 'snippet': 'The government accused the bank of defrauding investors by vastly understating the risks of the mortgages backing about $850 million worth of mortgage-backed securities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department sued Bank of America on Tuesday, accusing the bank of defrauding investors by vastly understating the risks of the mortgages backing about $850 million in securities.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice Dept. Sues Bank of America Over Mortgage Securities', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justice Dept. Sues Bank Of America', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T20:02:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Silver-Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93b98ad7-21fe-5b0e-b267-df8749049382', 'word_count': 891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93b98ad7-21fe-5b0e-b267-df8749049382'}, {'abstract': 'For almost two decades, Rockne Newell battled with town officials over his junk-strewn property, a feud that led to gun violence at a municipal meeting.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/pennsylvania-gunman-feuded-with-officials-for-almost-two-decades-over-land/', 'snippet': 'For almost two decades, Rockne Newell battled with town officials over his junk-strewn property, a feud that led to gun violence at a municipal meeting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Angry that town officials in northeastern Pennsylvania took over his junk-strewn, wooded property at a sheriff’s sale last month, Rockne Newell opened fire at a township supervisors meeting on Monday night, killing three people and wounding two others before he was wrestled to the ground by two men, state police officials said on Tuesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pennsylvania Gunman Feuded With Officials for Almost Two Decades Over Land', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T20:14:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44f66ca7-6dab-56e3-bfa3-08a213fe15d3', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44f66ca7-6dab-56e3-bfa3-08a213fe15d3'}, {'abstract': 'A wide range of wines can work to complement a mellow tomato crostata, though cool reds fare best.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/dining/with-cooked-tomatoes-stick-with-cool-reds-or-rose.html', 'snippet': 'A wide range of wines can work to complement a mellow tomato crostata, though cool reds fare best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Raw tomatoes, high in acid, demand high-acid wines. But cooked-tomato dishes like this crostata are altogether mellower, and so welcome a wider range of wines. A high-acid wine like an unoaked barbera from Asti or Alba would still go beautifully, but so would a Sicilian nerello mascalese from Mount Etna or a good Provençal rosé. Serve the reds cool. White wines would work well, too, like a falanghina or fiano di Avellino from Campania, or a good sauvignon blanc on the herbal side. Personally, because I imagine the flavors of this crostata as broad rather than sharp, I would probably stick with reds or rosé. Other red options include Beaujolais, lighter pinot noirs like those from Sancerre or the range of light reds from northern Italy, like teroldego, lagrein, grignolino and those from the Valle d’Aosta.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Cooked Tomatoes, Stick With Cool Reds or Rosé', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'And to Drink...', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asimov, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tomatoes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T20:17:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9687389-4c29-5077-a160-2efd86cd0ca9', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9687389-4c29-5077-a160-2efd86cd0ca9'}, {'abstract': 'I’ve never considered myself a “woman composer,” but I suspect that over the years being female has helped more than it’s hurt.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/confessions-of-a-composeress/', 'snippet': 'I’ve never considered myself a “woman composer,” but I suspect that over the years being female has helped more than it’s hurt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is the role of the ”woman composer” and why, after all these years, is she such a burning issue?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Confessions of a ‘Composeress’', 'kicker': 'The Score', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Musical Instruments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zorn, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T20:20:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Gosfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gosfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/570c23f9-aa7d-543c-893a-5121007d8fb0', 'word_count': 2111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/570c23f9-aa7d-543c-893a-5121007d8fb0'}, {'abstract': '“Broadchurch,” an eight-episode series about a criminal investigation, comes to BBC America on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/arts/television/broadchurch-a-dark-drama-arrives-on-bbc-america.html', 'snippet': '“Broadchurch,” an eight-episode series about a criminal investigation, comes to BBC America on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Broadchurch” comes to BBC America on Wednesday, riding a wave of good tidings. The ratings in Britain this spring were very strong — just shy of what “Downton Abbey” earned in its first season — and the reviews were rhapsodic. Fox announced last week that it would develop a version of the show, even though the original is getting its own highly publicized American run.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/jpbroadchurch/jpbroadchurch-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/jpbroadchurch/jpbroadchurch-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/jpbroadchurch/jpbroadchurch-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/jpbroadchurch/jpbroadchurch-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/jpbroadchurch/jpbroadchurch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/jpbroadchurch/jpbroadchurch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'