ival – he has promoted a libertarian brand of Republican politics featuring a less aggressive foreign policy, a more tolerant social policy, and smaller government.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '10 Questions for Rand Paul', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T22:01:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Harwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/159b0c9b-882c-51ef-8d70-7590df2d2938', 'word_count': 1166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/159b0c9b-882c-51ef-8d70-7590df2d2938'}, {'abstract': 'In cross-pairings of different troupes, artists performed relatively short pieces with bravura touches on Saturday at the Vail International Dance Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/arts/dance/vail-dance-festival-has-an-international-evening.html', 'snippet': 'In cross-pairings of different troupes, artists performed relatively short pieces with bravura touches on Saturday at the Vail International Dance Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VAIL, Colo. — A number of Romantic ballets have central scenes set in the woods. Far from the madding crowd, within the realm of nature, the hero discovers the otherworldly heroine who satisfies his longing as the women of his own milieu do not. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/SUBINTERNATIONAL/SUBINTERNATIONAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legac