ri': 'nyt://video/f790f263-ee4d-51c9-9702-bf7427738a9a'}, {'abstract': 'Sounds of Korea treated New Yorkers to a program of traditional music and dance at Lincoln Center Out of Doors on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/arts/dance/heritage-sunday-blooms-at-lincoln-center-out-of-doors.html', 'snippet': 'Sounds of Korea treated New Yorkers to a program of traditional music and dance at Lincoln Center Out of Doors on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s soul, and then there’s “S(e)oul.” On Sunday afternoon, Lincoln Center Out of Doors teamed up with the Center for Traditional Music and Dance to showcase “The S(e)oul of Korea,” a program with more to it than an embarrassing title. (What on earth were the presenters thinking?) This three-tiered presentation, which took place at Hearst Plaza, included two musical groups — the New York Korean Traditional Marching Band and Ensemble Sinawi — as well as the dance and music troupe Sounds of Korea. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/07heritage-web/07heritage-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/07heritage-web/07heritage-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/07heritage-web/07heritage-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/07heritage-web/07heritage-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/07heritage-web/07heritage-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/07heritage-web/07heritage-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/arts/07heritage-web/07heritage-web-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Drums and Fans, the Spirit of Korea', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Drums and Fans, the Spirit of Korea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Out of Doors Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Traditional Music and Dance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T22:30:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ded346f-eb6e-5d04-b15a-b742af3ed269', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ded346f-eb6e-5d04-b15a-b742af3ed269'}, {'abstract': 'These artisanal products will upgrade late-summer outdoor dining experiences, from the backyard to the park.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/by-design-modern-picnic-wares-for-photo-worthy-alfresco-dining/', 'snippet': 'These artisanal products will upgrade late-summer outdoor dining experiences, from the backyard to the park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Too often, picnic wares are an afterthought — cheap wicker baskets, plastic gingham blankets, throwaway utensils. Of course, the primary attractions of do-it-yourself alfresco dining are a lavish spread, a natural setting and good company. But now, thanks to a handful of artisans, there are attractive, handcrafted goods for a decidedly modern (and Instagram-friendly) outdoor culinary experience.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Modern Picnic Wares for Photo-Worthy Alfresco Dining', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-06T22:31:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Bellman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1fd9660-6788-5eb0-8be3-ced7696b625d', 'word_count': 60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1fd9660-6788-5eb0-8be3-ced7696b625d'}, {'abstract': 'Both deals illustrate the rise of shareholder power, as well as the devilish issues that emerge when management tries to buy a public company.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/in-american-greetings-deal-echoes-of-larger-buyout-for-dell/', 'snippet': 'Both deals illustrate the rise of shareholder power, as well as the devilish issues that emerge when management tries to buy a public company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is a tale of two management-led buyouts.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In American Greetings Deal, Echoes of Larger Buyout for Dell', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In American Greetings Deal, Echoes of Larger Dell Buyout', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 's