nstrated Rodriguez was guilty of something.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Length of Rodriguez’s Suspension Was Sticking Point', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Length of Rodriguez’s Suspension Was Sticking Point', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Michael S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball Players Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Biogenesis of America LLC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T02:39:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8eddbc15-96c4-5cb4-9c29-f15fd043cf7f', 'word_count': 330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8eddbc15-96c4-5cb4-9c29-f15fd043cf7f'}, {'abstract': 'Russia’s Supreme Court on Tuesday reduced by two months the sentence of Mikhail B. Khodorkovsky, the former oil tycoon and political opponent of President Vladimir V. Putin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/world/europe/russia-tycoons-prison-sentence-is-cut-by-two-months.html', 'snippet': 'Russia’s Supreme Court on Tuesday reduced by two months the sentence of Mikhail B. Khodorkovsky, the former oil tycoon and political opponent of President Vladimir V. Putin.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Russia’s Supreme Court on Tuesday reduced by two months the sentence of Mikhail B. Khodorkovsky, the former oil tycoon and political opponent of President Vladimir V. Putin, but declined to release him immediately as his lawyers had requested in an appeal. Mr. Khodorkovsky, who was convicted of fraud and tax evasion in 2005 and money laundering and theft in 2010, is now scheduled for release in August 2014. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Tycoon’s Prison Sentence Is Cut by Two Months', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Tycoon’s Prison Sentence Is Cut by Two Months', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khodorkovsky, Mikhail B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T02:54:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0ceca9f-3133-5ba1-8a5e-feced14f740d', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0ceca9f-3133-5ba1-8a5e-feced14f740d'}, {'abstract': 'In an appearance on NBC’s “Tonight Show,” President Obama told Jay Leno that the government is not overreacting in locking down nearly 20 diplomatic posts and issuing a worldwide travel warning after intercepted electronic conversations raised concerns of terrorist attacks abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/06/obama-tells-leno-closure-of-embassies-is-no-overreaction/', 'snippet': 'In an appearance on NBC’s “Tonight Show,” President Obama told Jay Leno that the government is not overreacting in locking down nearly 20 diplomatic posts and issuing a worldwide travel warning after intercepted electronic conversations raised con...', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a late-night comic Jay Leno certainly covered some serious ground with President Obama on Tuesday evening.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Tells Leno Closure of Embassies Is No Overreaction', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leno, Jay', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T02:56:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b4ac363-adfa-5924-bd1e-55c6b5bfd0ce', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b4ac363-adfa-5924-bd1e-55c6b5bfd0ce'}, {'abstract': 'Twelve people died and at least 60 more were injured, officials said Tuesday, in an explosion in the center of Rosario, Argentina’s third-largest city, with 1.2 million people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/world/americas/argentina-gas-leak-causes-deadly-residential-blast.html', 'snippet': 'Twelve people died and at least 60 more were injured, officials said Tuesday, in an explosion in the center of Rosario, Argentina’s third-largest city, with 1.2 million people.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Twelve people died and at least 60 more were injured, officials said Tuesday, in an explosion in the center of Rosario, Argentina’s third largest city, with 1.2 million people. A gas leak from the ground floor of a residential building caused the blast on Tuesday morning, Mónica Fein, the mayor of Rosario, confirmed. Witnesses said it felt like an earthquake. “I woke up and there were no walls,” said Franco Járiton, who lived on the seventh floor. News channels showed that the middle block of the building, which was nine stories tall, had collapsed. There are fears that two adjoining blocks, which are badly damaged, will also fall. Fifteen people were missing. Neighbors said they had called the provincial gas company hours before the explosion, warning of a strong gas smell. The company, Litoral Gas, said it had not received any calls. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Argentina: Gas Leak Causes Deadly Residential Blast', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Argentina: Gas Leak Causes Deadly Residential Blast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Explosions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T02:56:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Gilbert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gilbert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/08be509f-7e5e-522f-a4f9-6ab053c28f09', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08be509f-7e5e-522f-a4f9-6ab053c28f09'}, {'abstract': 'From the Fountains of Wayne album “Utopia Parkway.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/08/10/opinion/collingwood-amity-gardens.html', 'snippet': 'From the Fountains of Wayne album “Utopia Parkway.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the Fountains of Wayne album “Utopia Parkway.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '“Amity Gardens”', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T02:58:24+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/a9849c4d-0d5f-5c95-a980-1d7bffc1e29a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/a9849c4d-0d5f-5c95-a980-1d7bffc1e29a'}, {'abstract': 'With the Yankees playing substandard baseball in recent weeks, Derek Jeter and Joe Girardi addressed the team in a postgame meeting on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/sports/baseball/in-team-meeting-the-yankees-vent-and-face-reality.html', 'snippet': 'With the Yankees playing substandard baseball in recent weeks, Derek Jeter and Joe Girardi addressed the team in a postgame meeting on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — With a nightmarish season lurching into its final two months, the Yankees were at a crossroad on Monday when Derek Jeter and Joe Girardi decided to address the team in a brief postgame meeting, according t