/db022c60-7ea0-5492-a6cd-996f7b049c5b'}, {'abstract': 'Is it better to exercise before you learn something new? What about during? And should the exercise be vigorous or gentle? Two new studies helpfully tackle those questions.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/how-exercise-can-help-us-learn/', 'snippet': 'Is it better to exercise before you learn something new? What about during? And should the exercise be vigorous or gentle? Two new studies helpfully tackle those questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past decade, in study after study in animals and people, exercise has been shown to improve the ability to learn and remember. But the specifics of that process have remained hazy. Is it better to exercise before you learn something new? What about during? And should the exercise be vigorous or gentle? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/health/07well_physed/07well_physed-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/07/health/07well_physed/07well_physed-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/health/07well_physed/07well_physed-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/health/07well_physed/07well_physed-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1374, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/health/07well_physed/07well_physed-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/07/health/07well_physed/07well_physed-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/07/health/07well_physed/07well_physed-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Exercise Can Help Us Learn', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T04:01:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/689cf8ed-02f5-5354-8b16-5a7c37f15584', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/689cf8ed-02f5-5354-8b16-5a7c37f15584'}, {'abstract': 'Data and arithmetic make clear that the Affordable Care Act could have negative effects on employment, despite the optimism of the law’s supporters, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/health-care-inflation-and-the-arithmetic-of-labor-taxes/', 'snippet': 'Data and arithmetic make clear that the Affordable Care Act could have negative effects on employment, despite the optimism of the law’s supporters, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Casey B. Mulligan is an economics professor at the University of Chicago. He is the author of “The Redistribution Recession: How Labor Market Distortions Contracted the Economy.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Care Inflation and the Arithmetic of Labor Taxes', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T04:01:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Casey B. Mulligan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Casey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa2e5858-4943-508d-bfd3-50221d78f517', 'word_count': 1345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa2e5858-4943-508d-bfd3-50221d78f517'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 504 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/word-of-the-day-deposition/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 504 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'deposition •\\ˌde-pə-ˈzi-shən, ˌde-pə-\\• noun', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | deposition', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T04:03:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b599d5a5-f753-5a2e-b9c2-25e53bef07e6', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b599d5a5-f753-5a2e-b9c2-25e53bef07e6'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (BET) LUV (2013) A recent parolee (the rapper Common) dreaming of a better life decides to take his 11-year-old nephew (Michael Rainey Jr., above left, with Common) out of school for a day and teach him how to be a man in this crime thriller from the director Sheldon Candis. But as the boy eats his first oyster, tastes his first beer and learns how to steer a car, he also ends up being an accomplice — and perhaps a hostage — to a man who turns out to be a desperate criminal. “Mr. Candis, who wrote the script with Justin Wilson, balances the more sensationalistic aspects of the movie — guns are pointed and fired, blood is shed, and threats are issued with heavy, macho menace — with keen attention to details of character and place,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “The landscape of Baltimore’s African-American neighborhoods may be familiar to fans of ‘The Wire’ (as will the faces of a few of the actors), but ‘Luv’ is telling a different kind of tale about drugs, the law and urban life. It is, as the title suggests, a love story, focused on the complicated bonds between men who regard one another as family and whose lives are scarred and shadowed by violence.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T04:15:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/be9b07c6-aab1-58b0-85a7-d005e5a1e0fe', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be9b07c6-aab1-58b0-85a7-d005e5a1e0fe'}, {'abstract': 'Hiroki Kuroda allowed three runs over seven innings and the Yankees offense struggled to put hits together in a loss to the White Sox.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/sports/baseball/yankees-bats-contribute-to-the-quiet-on-day-2-of-rodriguezs-return.html', 'snippet': 'Hiroki Kuroda allowed three runs over seven innings and the Yankees offense struggled to put hits together in a loss to the White Sox.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — A day after a news media circus descended on U.S. Cellular Field to chronicle the dueling narratives of Alex Rodriguez’s season debut and Major League Baseball’s announcement that it had suspended him, the Yankees faced a decidedly less frenetic atmosphere on Tuesday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees’ Bats Contribute to the Quiet on Day 2 of Rodriguez’s Return', 'kicker': 'White Sox 3, Yankees 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees’ Bats Contribute to the Quiet on Day 2 of Rodriguez’s Return', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss, Ben', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago White Sox', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T04:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization':