ium', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute for Science and International Security', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yongbyon (North Korea)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T08:57:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone and Gerry Mullany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mullany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c6624b7-3c36-5044-a3a9-46beaffa001e', 'word_count': 954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c6624b7-3c36-5044-a3a9-46beaffa001e'}, {'abstract': 'A decade after they left their careers in favor of full-time lives at home, working mothers reflect on the choice they made and what it cost them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/magazine/the-opt-out-generation-wants-back-in.html', 'snippet': 'A decade after they left their careers in favor of full-time lives at home, working mothers reflect on the choice they made and what it cost them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sheilah O’Donnel tells herself that her new home, a townhouse in a development in Chevy Chase, Md., just a stone’s throw from a Safeway, isn’t really all that bad. Sure, it’s near a gas station. And the front window, with its cheerily upholstered cushions, overlooks a dreary parking lot. And yes, it’s kind of small — “an apartment,” O’Donnel, who is 44, sometimes says bitterly, when she’s reminded of her former life with her ex-husband in their custom-built, six-bedroom home. But then again, it’s perfectly maintained and impeccably furnished, and most important, it’s rented with her own money, from the first real job she has had in almost a decade.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/magazine/11optout2/mag-11optout-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/11/magazine/11optout2/mag-11optout-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/magazine/11optout2/mag-11optout-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/magazine/11optout2/mag-11optout-t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 934, 'width': 1400, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/magazine/11optout2/11optout2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/11/magazine/11optout2/11optout2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/magazine/11optout2/11optout2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Opt-Out Generation Wants Back In', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ready to Rejoin the Rat Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Part-Time Employment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T09:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Warner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Warner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c7e3473-23db-58ee-8e3c-1dbb644f216d', 'word_count': 6528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c7e3473-23db-58ee-8e3c-1dbb644f216d'}, {'abstract': 'Edwin J. Torres, born and raised in the Bronx, moved from documenting urban life to focusing on intimate moments closer to home.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/a-quiet-moment-a-dramatic-turning-point/', 'snippet': 'Edwin J. Torres, born and raised in the Bronx, moved from documenting urban life to focusing on intimate moments closer to home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Edwin J. Torres, a 23-year-old photographer and filmmaker, is based in Manhattan but was born and raised in the Bronx. “I might move back,” he said. “I love it there.” He received a degree in American Studies from Colby College in Waterville, Me., but studied film and photography as well. He volunteers frequently at the Bronx Documentary Center and