he law that they are not already doing, and the law provides temporary tax credits to the smallest companies for offering health coverage. That said, in at least one situation small companies may be forced to confront a surprising dilemma.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Affordable Care Act, Some Children Left Behind', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Liazon Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T11:15:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb8dd905-59cf-5d7f-9972-4602170ff83c', 'word_count': 1169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb8dd905-59cf-5d7f-9972-4602170ff83c'}, {'abstract': 'Learn more about hurricanes by playing our crossword, either online or in print.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/student-crossword-hurricanes/', 'snippet': 'Learn more about hurricanes by playing our crossword, either online or in print.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Learn more about hurricanes by playing our crossword (PDF). You can find the answers here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cred