r earlier, but the result fell short of expectations.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/carlyle-profits-rose-in-2nd-quarter-as-firm-continued-to-cash-out/', 'snippet': 'The investment giant said on Wednesday that it earned $155.8 million for the quarter ended June 30, up nearly fourfold from the period a year earlier, but the result fell short of expectations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Carlyle Group posted big gains for its second quarter on Wednesday, including a sizable jump in payouts to investors. But analysts expected a little more from its results.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carlyle Profit Rose in 2nd Quarter as Firm Continued to Cash Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carlyle Group LP', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T11:47:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f204945-65ed-5995-8e7b-7e20e786c39d', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f204945-65ed-5995-8e7b-7e20e786c39d'}, {'abstract': '“Lee Daniels’ The Butler,” opening on Friday, is a story that should be told, say its stars, Forest Whitaker and Oprah Winfrey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/movies/oprah-winfrey-and-forest-whitaker-on-the-butler.html', 'snippet': '“Lee Daniels’ The Butler,” opening on Friday, is a story that should be told, say its stars, Forest Whitaker and Oprah Winfrey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oprah Winfrey was winding up her long-running talk show when the director Lee Daniels came calling. Mr. Daniels, who had worked with Ms. Winfrey when she was an executive producer and supporter of his 2009 film, “Precious: Based on the Novel ‘Push’ by Sapphire,” told her that he had a part for her in his new film. Despite pleading time constraints — she was starting her television network, OWN — Ms. Winfrey said she was ultimately compelled to embrace the project because it represented “something bigger than ourselves.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/movies/11butler_span/20130811_BUTLER-slide-S41P-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/11/movies/11butler_span/20130811_BUTLER-slide-S41P-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/movies/11butler_span/20130811_BUTLER-slide-S41P-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/movies/11butler_span/20130811_BUTLER-slide-S41P-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/movies/11butler_span/11butler_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/11/movies/11butler_span/11butler_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images