nyt://article/7814e5af-9ce5-5eec-a61a-5e9a130d6061'}, {'abstract': 'Casey Mulligan’s negativity about the Affordable Care Act fails to acknowledge how it is likely to reduce health care expenditures, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/the-economics-of-the-affordable-care-act/', 'snippet': 'Casey Mulligan’s negativity about the Affordable Care Act fails to acknowledge how it is likely to reduce health care expenditures, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David M. Cutler is Otto Eckstein Professor of Applied Economics at Harvard University. He served as senior health care adviser to the Obama presidential campaign in 2008.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Economics of the Affordable Care Act', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T15:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Cutler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5db19445-3d96-56c2-91dc-82ba3b52930b', 'word_count': 1453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5db19445-3d96-56c2-91dc-82ba3b52930b'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Wolman, a real estate developer, fulfilled his childhood dream of owning the N.F.L.’s Philadelphia Eagles in 1963, at age 36, and also was a co-founder of the N.H.L.’s Philadelphia Flyers in the 1960s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/sports/football/jerry-wolman-former-eagles-owner-dies-at-86.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Wolman, a real estate developer, fulfilled his childhood dream of owning the N.F.L.’s Philadelphia Eagles in 1963, at age 36, and also was a co-founder of the N.H.L.’s Philadelphia Flyers in the 1960s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jerry Wolman, a small-town grocer’s son who made a fortune as a Washington real estate developer, owned the National Football League’s Philadelphia Eagles and helped found the National Hockey League’s Philadelphia Flyers in the 1960s, but who saw his financial empire crumble and his pro sports franchises pass from his hands by decade’s end, died on Tuesday in Potomac, Md. He was 86. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/sports/WOLMAN-obit/WOLMAN-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/08/sports/WOLMAN-obit/WOLMAN-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/sports/WOLMAN-obit/WOLMAN-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/sports/WOLMAN-obit/WOLMAN-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/sports/WOLMAN-obit/WOLMAN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thu