events for the mayoral candidates, according to the campaigns and organizations they are affiliated with. Times are listed as scheduled but frequently change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 7: Where the Candidates Are Today', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T15:06:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8174953f-2d82-57a0-b7e9-593392ec7906', 'word_count': 3517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8174953f-2d82-57a0-b7e9-593392ec7906'}, {'abstract': 'The ashes of Richie Havens, who opened the Woodstock festival in 1969, will be scattered over the site of his performance later this month.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/a-final-return-to-woodstock-for-richie-havens/', 'snippet': 'The ashes of Richie Havens, who opened the Woodstock festival in 1969, will be scattered over the site of his performance later this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The life of Richie Havens, the folk musician who opened the Woodstock festival in 1969, will be honored on Aug. 18 with a free concert at that famous site and his ashes will be scattered by plane, the Bethel Woods Center for the Arts announced. According to Mr. Havens’s family, he had requested that his ashes be spread over the original site where he performed, which is now known as Bethel Woods, before he died of a heart attack in April at his home in Jersey City. He was 72.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Final Return to Woodstock for Richie Havens', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Woodstock Music Festivals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Havens, Richie (1941-2013)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bethel Woods Center for the Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T15:08:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/718185d0-45d7-55bf-9746-7744cb6fd6e8', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/718185d0-45d7-55bf-9746-7744cb6fd6e8'}, {'abstract': 'Apparently all those years of not-profit-making paid off.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/jeff-bezos-a-capitalist-indifferent-to-money/', 'snippet': 'Apparently all those years of not-profit-making paid off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeff Bezos, the founder of Amazon.com, is worth $28 billion, Forbes estimates. In other words, he’s good for the $250 million he’s spending personally to buy The Washington Post, even if the purchase, announced this week, is being described as making little financial sense. Maybe he was on to something 14 years ago, when, as Peter de Jonge wrote in an entertaining and still relevant cover story for the magazine, Bezos and his company were fostering a “forced and incongruous indifference to money” among Amazon’s work force. They had lots of morale-boosting mottos but a volatile stock price. (When de Jonge expressed skepticism about the company, one Amazon executive told him, “I can tell you’re not a believer.”) De Jonge imagined that being employed there must have been “a little like living in Pompeii 2,000 years ago.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/magazine/06-jeff-bezos-1998/06-jeff-bezos-1998-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 914, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/06/magazine/06-jeff-bezos-1998/06-jeff-bezos-1998-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 914}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/magazine/06-jeff-bezos-1998/06-jeff-bezos-1998-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 673, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/magazine/06-jeff-bezos-1998/06-jeff-bezos-1998-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1448, 'width': 951, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/magazine/06-jeff-bezos-1998/06-jeff-bezos-1998-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/06/magazine/06-jeff-bezos-1998/06-jeff-bezos-1998-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/06/magazine/06-jeff-bezos-1998/06-jeff-bezos-1998-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeff Bezos, a Capitalist ‘Indifferent’ to Money?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'se