, 'lastname': 'Egner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18a99032-bfb8-5615-9a29-76ab6faae04a', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18a99032-bfb8-5615-9a29-76ab6faae04a'}, {'abstract': 'His sixth studio album is his first to reach the chart’s summit.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/for-robin-thicke-the-no-1-song-and-album/', 'snippet': 'His sixth studio album is his first to reach the chart’s summit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the last two months, Robin Thicke has had the No. 1 song in the country with “Blurred Lines,” a smooth disco tune inspired by Marvin Gaye’s “Got to Give It Up.” This week the song entered its ninth week at No. 1, the longest run by a male solo act since Flo Rida’s “Low” in 2008, which stayed on top for 10 weeks. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Robin Thicke, the No. 1 Song and Album', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thicke, Robin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen SoundScan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T19:51:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2da4d38-7f8d-5cd8-8334-1a3ed15e211b', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2da4d38-7f8d-5cd8-8334-1a3ed15e211b'}, {'abstract': 'The writer of “At Ease With a Body Fighting Gravity” for My Story goes on TV and finds even more kindred spirits.', '