mes.com/2013/08/07/pictures-of-the-day-kenya-and-elsewhere-14/', 'snippet': 'Photos from Kenya, Afghanistan, Thailand and India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from Kenya, Afghanistan, Thailand and India.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Kenya and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T20:28:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49712041-cef9-51ce-a2f8-b6b8a2fa3d25', 'word_count': 12, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49712041-cef9-51ce-a2f8-b6b8a2fa3d25'}, {'abstract': 'In which an attempted rehabilitation of the term “scientism” actually vindicates scientism’s critics.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/the-scientism-of-steven-pinker/', 'snippet': 'In which an attempted rehabilitation of the term “scientism” actually vindicates scientism’s critics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steven Pinker has an interesting and revealing essay in The New Republic dismissing the charges of “scientism” that are often leveled by the philosophically, artistically and religiously-minded against certain authors, polemicists and science popularizers. “The term,” he writes, “is anything but clear, more of a boo-word than a label for any coherent doctrine,” which inspires him to try to reappropriate “scientism” as a positive descriptor — denoting, he suggests, a belief in the intelligibility of the world and a commitment to the\xa0difficult-but-necessary quest for real objectivity about its workings, both of which which should inform our understanding of non-scientific spheres as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Scientism of Steven Pinker', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinker, Steven', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T20:29:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a45ff0af-d550-5c4b-a839-6efb905c57b4', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a45ff0af-d550-5c4b-a839-6efb905c57b4'}, {'abstract': 'The search for a new chairman of the National Endowment for the Arts seems to have stalled at a crucial point, some advocates say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/arts/design/vacancies-hamper-agencies-for-arts.html', 'snippet': 'The search for a new chairman of the National Endowment for the Arts seems to have stalled at a crucial point, some advocates say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The week before the Broadway producer Rocco Landesman was scheduled to deliver his first Congressional testimony as chairman of the National Endowment for the Arts, he traveled 2,000 miles from Washington to Jerome, Idaho, to take in a production of “Othello” at a high school. Sitting next to him that spring day in 2010