 Syria’s largest city, by months of ferocious combat between the government of President Bashar al-Assad and his rebel opponents. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Satellite Images Show Destruction in Aleppo', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN ASSN FOR THE ADVANCEMENT OF SCIENCE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMNESTY INTERNATIONAL', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEPPO (SYRIA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T21:22:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b40048a7-4c59-5037-97ee-f80e9217c315', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b40048a7-4c59-5037-97ee-f80e9217c315'}, {'abstract': 'Imagine my surprise when I discovered that a list of the best sports films, written by Kareem Abdul-Jabbar, turned out not to be all that bad.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/07/the-best-sports-movies-abdul-jabbar-tested-vecsey-approved/', 'snippet': 'Imagine my surprise when I discovered that a list of the best sports films, written by Kareem Abdul-Jabbar, turned out not to be all that bad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is it about so-called best-of lists that riles us up so? Why do we take such offense? They are clearly harmless opinions, compiled by whomever and have no bearing on our own predilections of film, music or whatever. The whole exercise of ranking things flies in the face of art, this idea of quantification and qualification.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 156, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/17/magazine/17-dailydogear/17-dailydogear-thumbLarge-v3.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best Sports Movies: Abdul-Jabbar Tested, Vecsey Approved', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T21:23:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Vecsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vecsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/393c2fd1-c445-5eb2-93a6-99538855be2e', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/393c2fd1-c445-5eb2-93a6-99538855be2e'}, {'abstract': 'A Dior show last month was notable for its increased use of black models, but not much has changed five years after a Vogue article asked, “Is Fashion Racist?”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/fashion/fashions-blind-spot.html', 'snippet': 'A Dior show last month was notable for its increased use of black models, but not much has changed five years after a Vogue article asked, “Is Fashion Racist?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five years ago, the fashion industry faced a reckoning over the startling lack of diversity among the models on major designer runways. Reacting to complaints that many shows and magazines included nothing but white models, Vogue, in its July 2008 issue, featured a substantial article that asked, in its headline, “Is Fashion Racist?”', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/fashion/08RACESUB_SPAN/08RACESUB_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/08/fashion/08RACESUB_SPAN/08RACESUB_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/fashion/08RACESUB_SPAN/08RACESUB_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/fashion/08RACESUB_SPAN/08RACESUB_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/fashion/08RACESUB_SPAN/08RACESUB_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/08/fashion/08RACESUB_SPAN/08RACESUB_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/fashion/08RACESUB_SPAN/08RACESUB_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion’s Blind Spot', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fashion’s Blind Spot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vogue', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T21:24:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39ae5ef2-6f27-5a86-a2bb-b732b3e00be5', 'word_count': 1856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39ae5ef2-6f27-5a86-a2bb-b732b3e00be5'}, {'abstract': '“Mathew Brady: Portraits of a Nation,” Robert Wilson’s new biography of the photographer, relates how his skill and charm made him the favorite of politicians and generals from the 1840s onward.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/books/mathew-brady-a-biography-by-robert-wilson.html', 'snippet': '“Mathew Brady: Portraits of a Nation,” Robert Wilson’s new biography of the photographer, relates how his skill and charm made him the favorite of politicians and generals from the 1840s onward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Salman Rushdie, in his novel  “The Ground Beneath Her Feet”  (1999), described what we see in a photograph as “a moral decision taken in one-eighth of a second.”In the early days of photography, those moral decisions took longer to process. When Mathew Brady, the Civil War-era photographer, took a portrait, the shutter remained open for 10 to 15 seconds or more, long enough for a bit of wind, or the hint of a smile, to ruin everything. His subjects often had their heads stabilized by an unseen vise. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/arts/08BOOK1/08BOOK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 987, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/08/arts/08BOOK1/08BOOK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 987}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/arts/08BOOK1/08BOOK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 623, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/arts/08BOOK1/08BOOK1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1245, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/arts/08BOOK1/08BOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height'