destination.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Oh little town of Uzès!” the French novelist André Gide wrote affectionately of his father’s hometown in the South of France in his 1924 memoir, “Unless the Seed Dies.” “If you were in Umbria, Parisians would be visiting you in herds!” Gide, who was born into a middle-class Protestant family and scandalized France with a blunt but elegant defense of his homosexuality in “Corydon,” also published in 1924, was a wry and astute observer of Parisian snobberies. So he’d surely be amused to learn that today a taste-making coterie of Parisians is falling in love with Uzès and settling there, despite the fact that it’s not in Umbria.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Verge | Uzes, the Hidden Gem of the South of France', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T22:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Lobrano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lobrano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7320769b-f0d9-5a2c-8a9d-a0e43d575283', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7320769b-f0d9-5a2c-8a9d-a0e43d575283'}, {'abstract': 'When a luxury boutique is in the business of “cool,” a larger new store helps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/fashion/for-a-talent-scout-big-league-space.html', 'snippet': 'When a luxury boutique is in the business of “cool,” a larger new store helps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAST WEEK WAS a busy week in the life of Nevena Borissova, who opened her first Curve bout