types-a-look-inward.html', 'snippet': 'Brooklyn’s literary scene gives birth to a novel about itself in “The Love Affairs of Nathaniel P.” by Adelle Waldman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At around 7 on a recent weekday evening, the day’s oppressive heat only just beginning to ebb, Adelle Waldman walked out among the picnic tables on the patio of the Hot Bird, a Brooklyn bar repurposed from an old garage, self-consciously carrying her just-published book, “The Love Affairs of Nathaniel P.” ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/fashion/08ENCOUNTERS_SPAN/08zENCOUNTERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/08/fashion/08ENCOUNTERS_SPAN/08zENCOUNTERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/fashion/08ENCOUNTERS_SPAN/08zENCOUNTERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/fashion/08ENCOUNTERS_SPAN/08zENCOUNTERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/fashion/08ENCOUNTERS_SPAN/08zENCOUNTERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/08/fashion/08ENCOUNTERS_SPAN/08zENCOUNTERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/fas