 a new Yale University report holds the organization responsible for a recent outbreak and concludes that it should help the victims. Sewage from a United Nations camp contaminated one of Haiti’s largest rivers, the report said. The United Nations has steadfastly denied causing the epidemic, which has killed more than 8,000 people since it began in 2010, and has resisted paying any compensation. By not holding itself accountable to victims, the report stated, the United Nations is violating its obligations under international law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haiti: Report Blames U.N. Camp for Deadly Cholera Outbreak', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Haiti: Report Blames U.N. Camp For Causing Deadly Cholera Outbreak', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cholera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Department of Peacekeeping Operations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-07T23:55:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Zabludovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zabludovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c079634-6eec-5172-acc9-65274b88b73f', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c079634-6eec-5172-acc9-65274b88b73f'}, {'abstract': 'Once a year, Gover