ubtedly learned more in the past couple of months about the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court and its extensive powers than in the previous 35 years of the court’s existence. But it shouldn’t have taken the renegade intelligence analyst Edward J. Snowden to let us in on a fact that, while hardly secret, had been little noticed: in establishing the court, Congress gave the authority to name its judges to one individual, the chief justice of the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Much Work?', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Courts (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Anthony M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Resnik, Judith', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, John G Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruger, Theodore', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T01:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/498d38f6-fa86-5701-89ba-f1ef721ff7df', 'word_count': 1571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/498d38f6-fa86-5701-89ba-f1ef721ff7df'}, {'abstract': 'The Food and Drug Administration finally required that mefloquine hydrochloride, brand name Lariam, carry a “black box” for side effects. But it’s too little, too late.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/opinion/crazy-pills.html', 'snippet': 'The Food and Drug Administration finally required that mefloquine hydrochloride, brand name Lariam, carry a “black box” for side effects. But it’s too little, too late.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — ON Oct. 16, 2002, at 4 p.m., I walked out of my apartment in Secunderabad, India, leaving the door wide open, the lights on and my laptop humming. I don’t remember doing this. I know I did it because the building’s night watchman saw me leave. I woke up the next day in a train station four miles away, with no idea who I was or why I was in India. A policeman found me, and I ended up strapped down, hallucinating in a mental hospital for three days. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/opinion/0808OPEDsampson/0808OPEDsampson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 835, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/08/opinion/0808OPEDsampson/0808OPEDsampson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 835}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/opinion/0808OPEDsampson/0808OPEDsampson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/opinion/0808OPEDsampson/0808OPEDsampson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', '