.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/opinion/from-criminal-to-unlikely-hero.html', 'snippet': 'Officials hope the trial of Bo Xilai will put a full stop to the party’s most embarrassing political scandal in decades. But even if the trial goes as planned, Mr. Bo could end up an unlikely hero.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANY day now — the authorities won’t say precisely when — China will begin one of the most sensational trials in its modern political history, when Bo Xilai, the former rising star in the Politburo and Communist Party boss in the megacity of Chongqing, faces corruption charges. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Maoist Criminal to Popular Hero? ', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Maoist Criminal to Popular Hero?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bo Xilai', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pin Ho', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T01:03:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pin Ho', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ho', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/20e49b14-60e8-580d-aed9-f0cbdef65d4b', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20e49b14-60e8-580d-aed9-f0cbdef65d4b'}, {'abstract': 'The French president’s high hopes of beginning to reverse the country’s No. 1 problem by the end of the year have been met with pessimism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/business/global/hollande-vows-to-tackle-rising-unemployment-but-the-french-are-skeptical.html', 'snippet': 'The French president’s high hopes of beginning to reverse the country’s No. 1 problem by the end of the year have been met with pessimism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — President François Hollande visited an employment center in France’s heartland this week, armed with promises to reduce record unemployment. That was not enough for Nathalie, a 50-year-old who has long struggled to find work.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/business/Franceecon/Franceecon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/08/business/Franceecon/Franceecon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/business/Franceecon/Franceecon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/business/Franceecon/Franceecon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 947, 'width': 1636, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/business/Franceecon/Franceecon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/08/business/Franceecon/Franceecon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/business/Franceecon/Franceecon-t