ted States Senate seat in New Jersey, should disclose the full details of his involvement in an Internet start-up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Cory Booker of Newark, who wants to be the next senator from New Jersey, has an obligation to give a full and personal accounting of his involvement in an Internet start-up that he formed with the help of several high-powered investors from Silicon Valley. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Disclosures From Mr. Booker', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Disclosures From Mr. Booker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Booker, Cory A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Waywire', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T01:09:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/300e02ec-c7d3-5d28-84d4-2b01b2e7084d', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/300e02ec-c7d3-5d28-84d4-2b01b2e7084d'}, {'abstract': 'Strikes by fast-food workers demanding higher wages are sure to continue until corporate and political leaders listen, and act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/opinion/fast-food-fight.html', 'snippet': 'Strikes by fast-food workers demanding higher wages are sure to continue until corporate and political leaders listen, and act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fast-food workers who have been walking off their jobs illustrate a central fact of contemporary work life in America: As lower-wage occupations have proliferated in the past several years, Americans are increasingly unable to make a living at their jobs. They work harder and are paid less than workers in other advanced countries. And their wages have stagnated even as executive pay has soared. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fast-Food Fight', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fast-Food Fight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "McDonald's Corporation", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T01:09:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a9a7129-2849-5422-8ccd-85404826a38d', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a9a7129-2849-5422-8ccd-85404826a38d'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the results from the first round of exams linked to new learning standards show that the state has a long way to go in adequately educating students.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/opinion/new-yorks-common-core-test-scores.html', 'snippet': 'A look at the results from the first round of exams linked to new learning standards show that the state has a long way to go in adequately educating students.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last decade or so, most states deceived the public about the dismal quality of public schools by adopting pathetically weak learning standards that made children appear better prepared than they actually were. Not surprisingly, when states like Kentucky dropped the charade and embraced more challenging standards, scores dropped precipitously. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s Common Core Test Scores', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York’s Common Core Test Scores', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T01:10:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c32b52ff-c0e7-5990-913b-9606f88e3cb4', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c32b52ff-c0e7-5990-913b-9606f88e3cb4'}, {'abstract': 'The Théâtre de l’Étoile du Nord is not just a popular cafe in the Tunisian capital, but also a haunt for actors, intellectuals, freethinkers and revolutionaries, and it never closes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/world/africa/a-cafe-where-the-spirit-of-the-arab-spring-lives-on.html', 'snippet': 'The Théâtre de l’Étoile du Nord is not just a popular cafe in the Tunisian capital, but also a haunt for actors, intellectuals, freethinkers and revolutionaries, and it never closes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUNIS — In the heat of the afternoon, especially this past month of Ramadan, downtown Tunis plays dead. Offices and shops close at 2 p.m. and life is suspended as everyone, parched and hungry, waits for sunset and the breaking of the fast.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/world/tunis1/tunis1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/08/world/tunis1/tunis1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/world/tunis1/tunis1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/world/tunis1/tunis1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/world/tunis1/tunis1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/08/world/tunis1/tunis1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/world/tunis1/tunis1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cafe Where the Spirit of the Arab Spring Lives On', 'kicker': 'Tunis Journal', 'content_ki