ures and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Cars (Compact, Subcompact and Microcars)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Insurance Institute for Highway Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T04:01:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cheryl Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b46f31d-1fcc-58bb-b952-a0464ad56740', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b46f31d-1fcc-58bb-b952-a0464ad56740'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in two New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/word-of-the-day-viscid/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in two New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'viscid •\\ˈvi-səd\\• adjective', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | viscid', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T04:05:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bfb92e4-b35b-5cb1-aa49-410b31d472d9', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bfb92e4-b35b-5cb1-aa49-410b31d472d9'}, {'abstract': 'Just as the Yankees appeared to have regained some sense of normalcy, their stalwart closer, Mariano Rivera, faltered while trying to protect a ninth-inning lead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/sports/baseball/yankees-one-constant-only-adds-to-the-chaos.html', 'snippet': 'Just as the Yankees appeared to have regained some sense of normalcy, their stalwart closer, Mariano Rivera, faltered while trying to protect a ninth-inning lead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — For eight and two-thirds innings Wednesday night, the Yankees appeared to have regained some sense of normalcy. Alex Rodriguez, they found out, will likely be with them for the rest of the season after appealing his 211-game suspension for violating baseball’s drug policy. The offense finally showed signs of stirring, and C. C. Sabathia delivered his best outing in a month. The Yankees had a one-run lead with the stalwart closer Mariano Rivera in to pitch the ninth inning.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/sports/ALT-YANKS/ALT-YANKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/08/sports/ALT-YANKS/ALT-YANKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/sports/ALT-YANKS/ALT-YANKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/sports/ALT-YANKS/ALT-YANKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1527, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/sports/ALT-YANKS/ALT-YANKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/08/sports/ALT-YANKS/ALT-YANKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/sports/ALT-YANKS/ALT-YANKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees’ One Constant Only Adds to the Chaos', 'kicker': 'White Sox 6, Yankees 5 (12 Innings)', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees’ One Constant Only Adds to the Chaos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss, Ben', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago White Sox', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Mariano', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T04:40:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5347bbe0-02be-571e-87a0-3820e344908d', 'word_count': 779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5347bbe0-02be-571e-87a0-3820e344908d'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/arts/television/whats-on-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (13) CASE HISTORIES In this “Masterpiece Mystery!” presentation, Jason Isaacs (“Harry Potter,” “Brotherhood”) portrays Jackson Brodie, a cop turned private eye plucked from the pages of Kate Atkinson’s novels. In the series’s first episode, Brodie struggles to balance the personal and professional as he tries to solve a case involving a girl who went missing 30 years earlier. “\xa0‘Case Histories’ is trying for something lighter (while remaining artfully blood soaked), and some mystery fans might find it a welcome change,” Mike Hale wrote in The New York Times when the series made its debut in 2011. Mr. Isaacs (above with Millie Innes) is “very likable as Brodie,” he added. “If you can ignore that he’s playing a character built on spare parts from Raymond Chandler novels and Willie Nelson songs, that may be enough.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/647add41-99c6-52fb-89e1-31f17b9d5c26', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/647add41-99c6-52fb-89e1-31f17b9d5c26'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/news-quiz-august-8-2013/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | August 8, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T05:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de09b40f-f72e-5ca0-91d2-187cc3cab852', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de09b40f-f72e-5ca0-91d2-187cc3cab852'}, {'abstract': 'The National Security Agency is hunting for Americans’ messages that mention foreigners under surveillance, not just communications with the targeted individuals themselves, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/us/broader-sifting-of-data-abroad-is-seen-by-nsa.html', 'snippet': 'The National Security Agency is hunting for Americans’ messages that mention foreigners under surveillance, not just communications with the targeted individuals themselves, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The National Security Agency is searching the contents of vast amounts of Americans’ e-mail and text communications into and out of the country, hunting for people who mention information about foreigners under surveillance, according to intelligence officials.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.S.A. Said to Search Content of Messages to and From U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Broader Sifting Of Message Data By N.S.A. Is Seen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act (FISA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T06:45:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c666b358-f920-566e-8416-e05da8bd37c3', 'word_count': 1467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c666b358-f920-566e-8416-e05da8bd37c3'}, {'abstract': 'The company added contract subscribers and stemmed financial losses in the second quarter after adding the iPhone and focusing on common customer complaints.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/technology/t-mobile-us-reports-largest-customer-growth-in-four-years.html', 'snippet': 'The company added contract subscribers and stemmed financial losses in the second quarter after adding the iPhone and focusing on common customer complaints.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — T-Mobile US, the fourth-largest American carrier, lost thousands of customers over the last few years to rivals that offered more popular phones. But it appears to be rebounding.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/business/subPhone/subPhone-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/09/business/subPhone/subPhone-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':