at/', 'snippet': 'JPMorgan Chase faces criminal and civil investigations into sales of mortgage securities. | Hilton Worldwide, the hotel company owned by the Blackstone Group, has begun preparations for an I.P.O. | Carl C. Icahn is bolstering his assault on the De...', 'lead_paragraph': 'JPMorgan Chase disclosed in a regulatory filing on Wednesday that it faced a criminal and civil investigation into whether it sold shoddy mortgage securities to investors before the financial crisis, Jessica Silver-Greenberg and Ben Protess report in DealBook. The investigation is the latest legal threat to the bank and one of several mortgage-related problems for the industry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan’s Latest Legal Challenge', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T11:44:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fc6322d-e43d-530b-80d9-947c84b62ee3', 'word_count': 1549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fc6322d-e43d-530b-80d9-947c84b62ee3'}, {'abstract': 'The buyout firm said on Thursday that its earnings for the second quarter jumped nearly tenfold, to $197.8 million, from the period a year earlier, as its core private equity portfolio performed well and it cashed out of a number of investments.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/apollo-shows-strong-gains-as-investments-rise-in-value/', 'snippet': 'The buyout firm said on Thursday that its earnings for the second quarter jumped nearly tenfold, to $197.8 million, from the period a year earlier, as its core private equity portfolio performed well and it cashed out of a number of investments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 12:02 p.m. | ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apollo Shows Strong Gains as Investments Rise in Value', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surging Profit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apollo Global Management', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T11:53:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ec904e3-08b5-524b-8c83-3e18ac827074', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ec904e3-08b5-524b-8c83-3e18ac827074'}, {'abstract': 'Jim McCarthy and Brian Williamson’s new graphic biography, “Gabba Gabba Hey!,” details scenes from the Ramones’ lives filled in with some imagination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/arts/music/part-ramones-biography-part-dreamscape.html', 'snippet': 'Jim McCarthy and Brian Williamson’s new graphic biography, “Gabba Gabba Hey!,” details scenes from the Ramones’ lives filled in with some imagination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1979, the Ramones were recording at a studio in Los Angeles with the producer Phil Spector, whose work with the Ronettes, the Righteous Brothers and the Beatles had earned him a reputation as both a musical genius and an exacting, combustible egomaniac. He hadn’t produced a hit since John Lennon’s “Imagine” in 1971, and the Ramones, who had released four critically acclaimed albums of exuberant punk rock, were still searching for a commercial breakthrough. The sessions for the resulting album, “End of the Century,” were tumultuous, and the opening pages of the new book, “Gabba Gabba Hey!: The Graphic Story of the Ramones,” written by Jim McCarthy and illustrated by Brian Williamson, details some of Mr. Spector’s more notorious moments: forcing the guitarist Johnny Ramone to play the opening chord to “Rock ’N’ Roll High School” more than 70 times; pointing a gun at the bassist Dee Dee Ramone. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11MCCARTHY_SPAN/11MCCARTHY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 264, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11MCCARTHY_SPAN/11MCCARTHY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 264}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11MCCARTHY_SPAN/11MCCARTHY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11MCCARTHY_SPAN/11MCCARTHY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11MCCARTHY_SPAN/11MCCARTHY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11MCCARTHY_SPAN/11MCCARTHY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11MCCARTHY_SPAN/11MCCARTHY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150,