ted with. Times are listed as scheduled but frequently change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 8: Where the Candidates Are Today', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T15:16:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Leigh Cowan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'Leigh', 'lastname': 'Cowan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fba3037-9194-54c9-a722-d3c1e02f916c', 'word_count': 3926, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fba3037-9194-54c9-a722-d3c1e02f916c'}, {'abstract': 'Weekends, an interiors firm run by a pair of California expats, is bringing a distinctly West Coast flavor to Paris’s flourishing cafe-bar scene.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/by-design-paris-restaurants-cali-vibes/', 'snippet': 'Weekends, an interiors firm run by a pair of California expats, is bringing a distinctly West Coast flavor to Paris’s flourishing cafe-bar scene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A can-can kick away from the Moulin Rouge sits Le Dépanneur, a new restaurant in a corner of Pigalle, the red-light district in north-central Paris. The wraparound chrome siding suggests it’s an American-style diner, but the place, which opened last month after being shuttered for several years, has a different kind of stateside flavor. The clean palette, vast airiness and abundant flora creates a Palm Springs-by-way-of-Big Sur resort feel. On the main floor, a wealth of natural wood — slatted tables, floors painted with pastel geometric shapes, siding made of reclaimed timber and a polished bar — is complemented by potted succulents and painted white accents. Upstairs, there are hexagonal tables and vintage Modernist daybeds where guests can sip the restaurant’s agave cocktails and eat its organic burgers.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'By Design | Paris Restaurants, Cali Vibes', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'By Design: CaliPari Dreamin’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T15:17:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Pike', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pike', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dedf01de-7a80-5b0d-becf-b44e239c3acd', 'word_count': 575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dedf01de-7a80-5b0d-becf-b44e239c3acd'}, {'abstract': 'Emotions, particularly those that steep over years, can act like vapors that cloud our judgment, despite our best intentions. But when your father asks for your help, it’s hard to say no.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/a-doctor-in-the-family/', 'snippet': 'Emotions, particularly those that steep over years, can act like vapors that cloud our judgment, despite our best intentions. But when your father asks for your help, it’s hard to say no.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My father died earlier this year. It was sudden, and in what some of our friends described as every wife’s worst fear, my mom came home from work to discover him collapsed on the kitchen floor, lifeless. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/health/24well_sekkeres/24well_sekkeres-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/24/health/24well_sekkeres/24well_sekkeres-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/health/24well_sekkeres/24well_sekkeres-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/health/24well_sekkeres/24well_sekkeres-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/health/24well_sekkeres/24well_sekkeres-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/24/health/24well_sekkeres/24well_sekkeres-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/24/health/24well_sekkeres/24well_sekkeres-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Doctor in the Family', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T15:22:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mikkael A. Sekeres, M.d', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mikkael', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Sekeres', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8243e13d-fc8a-5678-a016-7fca965307e7', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8243e13d-fc8a-5678-a016-7fca965307e7'}, {'abstract': 'Oxycodone toxicity and degenerative brain disease were found in an autopsy of Cullen Finnerty, who played for Grand Valley State University.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/sports/ncaafootball/star-college-quarterback-who-went-missing-died-of-pneumonia.html', 'snippet': 'Oxycodone toxicity and degenerative brain disease were found in an autopsy of Cullen Finnerty, who played for Grand Valley State University.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The autopsy results for Cullen Finnerty, the star college quarterback found dead in the Michigan woods in late May, revealed Thursday that he had chronic traumatic encephalopathy, or C.T.E., the degenerative brain disease found in the autopsies of several former N.F.L. players.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pneumonia Seen as Star’s Cause of Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pneumonia Is Blamed In Quarterback’s Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finnerty, Cullen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Michigan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chronic Traumatic Encephalopathy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grand Valley State University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T15:30:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b629f058-5790-588e-8070-e191267c88bc', 'word_count': 872, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b629f058-5790-588e-8070-e191267c88bc'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/the-gun-report-august-8-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most of us who have boarded a plane in the years since Sept. 11 fret about bringing more than 3.4 ounces of shampoo in their carry-on. So it may come as a surprise that some Americans still try to board flights with loaded weapons.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: August 8, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T15:44:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/228adffe-d25a-5e30-978a-5c20087529ce', 'word_count': 1187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/228adffe-d25