: 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Wendy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sweden', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T17:46:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d12f0df1-c536-5062-96b9-5c62e82e5d1d', 'word_count': 1324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d12f0df1-c536-5062-96b9-5c62e82e5d1d'}, {'abstract': 'He wants to make sure the 2016 moderators will be “interested in the future of the Republican Party.”', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/reince-priebus-on-republican-debates/', 'snippet': 'He wants to make sure the 2016 moderators will be “interested in the future of the Republican Party.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Presidential debates have not been debates for a long time. In the primaries, they’re cattle shows where a half dozen or more would-be nominees recite talking points hoping for a sound bite that sticks for 24 hours. In the general election, they’re press conferences with two participants trying to avoid stepping on landmines. The most memorable moments have had less to do with substantive discussion than appearance, like President Obama sleepwalking through his first encounter with Mitt Romney in 2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reince Priebus on Republican Debates', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Priebus, Reince R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T17:50:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56d04668-a996-5a11-b7e1-8ba8fbbc59a0', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56d04668-a996-5a11-b7e1-8ba8fbbc59a0'}, {'abstract': 'Tesla Motors has exceeded Wall Street analysts’ estimates for two consecutive quarters — that’s an auspicious start even if the most recent quarterly profit relied on a number of one-offs.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/echoes-of-steve-jobs-in-elon-musk/', 'snippet': 'Tesla Motors has exceeded Wall Street analysts’ estimates for two consecutive quarters — that’s an auspicious start even if the most recent quarterly profit relied on a number of one-offs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elon Musk is beginning to exude hints of Steven P. Jobs, Apple’s late chief executive. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Echoes of Steve Jobs in Elon Musk', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Musk, Elon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tesla Motors Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T18:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Antony Currie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Currie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf3e0477-292c-5bdc-866b-32c522296917', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf3e0477-292c-5bdc-866b-32c522296917'}, {'abstract': 'A positive nudge can set off a bandwagon of approval, researchers found, but negative reaction does not spur others to “dislike.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/science/internet-study-finds-the-persuasive-power-of-like.html', 'snippet': 'A positive nudge can set off a bandwagon of approval, researchers found, but negative reaction does not spur others to “dislike.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you “like” this article on a site like Facebook, somebody who reads it is more likely to approve of it, even if the reporting and writing are not all that great.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/0