BHP Billiton, the world’s largest mining company, sits atop a sector that is deeply out of favor with investors, and it is aggressively curtailing its spending in hopes of winning them over.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/after-going-all-in-during-mining-boom-bhp-cuts-its-ambitions/', 'snippet': 'BHP Billiton, the world’s largest mining company, sits atop a sector that is deeply out of favor with investors, and it is aggressively curtailing its spending in hopes of winning them over.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BHP Billiton, the world’s largest mining company, was willing to spend big in early 2012. It was building new mines and upgrading old ones, at a cost of $18 billion. It considered a potential expansion of its copper and uranium mine, Olympic Dam, which could have cost as much as $20 billion. It proposed a deepwater extension of Port Hedland, its iron ore port, an estimated $10 billion or more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Going All In During Mining Boom, BHP Cuts Its Ambitions', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Metals and Minerals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kloppers, Marius', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mackenzie, Andrew S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anglo American Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BHP Billiton PLC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rio Tinto PLC', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vale S A', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T18:38:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William MacNamara', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacNamara', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b12342db-09df-52e7-8d85-992a9c6e2c4a', 'word_count': 1196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b12342db-09df-52e7-8d85-992a9c6e2c4a'}, {'abstract': 'The airport in Burlington, Vt., installs a private place to nurse or pump. Will other businesses and facilities follow?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/breast-feeding-in-the-airport-a-new-lactation-station-solution/', 'snippet': 'The airport in Burlington, Vt., installs a private place to nurse or pump. Will other businesses and facilities follow?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many of us who have breast-fed a baby know quite keenly the obstacles involved in pulling off such an intimate task in public. Even with all the nifty tools meant to provide privacy — the nursing bras and tops, the capes, the scarves artfully draped over baby and breast — accomplishing a feed without exposing yourself to strangers can be a changing-into-your-bathing-suit-poolside-esque feat. Ta-da! Happy, drooly baby, and you didn’t see a thing!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/style/motherlode-mamava/motherlode-mamava-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/08/style/motherlode-mamava/motherlode-mamava-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/08/style/motherlode-mamava/motherlode-mamava-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'c