 'Lecce (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T19:58:37+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/f0986405-0805-5535-a02b-c7e95eaa0313', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/f0986405-0805-5535-a02b-c7e95eaa0313'}, {'abstract': 'Stroll past churches, take a midday break at the beach and sip a glass of regional wine in the “Florence of the South.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/travel/36-hours-in-lecce-italy.html', 'snippet': 'Stroll past churches, take a midday break at the beach and sip a glass of regional wine in the “Florence of the South.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks to dozens of mostly Baroque-era churches packing its maze of narrow streets, Lecce, the “Florence of the South,” dazzles with elaborately carved facades and interiors that erupt with symphonies of angels, cherubs, saints, saviors and Madonnas. But this small gem in Italy’s heel is far from a haven of monkish abstemiousness. A capital of southern Italian cooking, the city brims with rustic restaurants serving the hearty peasant cuisine and robust red wines of the Puglia (Apulia in English) region. Throw in a buzzing bar scene and nearby beaches of sun-bronzed bodies and you have a city fit for holy men and hedonists alike.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/travel/11HOURS_SPAN-sf/11HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 542, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/11/travel/11HOURS_SPAN-sf/11HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 542}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/travel/11HOURS_SPAN-sf/11HOURS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 926, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/travel/11HOURS_SPAN-sf/11HOURS_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1851, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/travel/11HOURS_SPAN-sf/11HOURS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/11/travel/11HOURS_SPAN-sf/11HOURS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/travel/11HOURS_SPAN-sf/11HOURS_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Lecce, Italy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours: Lecce, Italy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sherwood, Seth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lecce (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T19:58:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Sherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9a67788-2b7d-572a-89b3-42800ec4a77a', 'word_count': 1704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9a67788-2b7d-572a-89b3-42800ec4a77a'}, {'abstract': 'In Rouen, where Gustave Flaubert was born and Joan of Arc was burned, past and present create a layered texture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/travel/near-paris-a-city-of-flaubert-and-joan-of-arc.html', 'snippet': 'In Rouen, where Gustave Flaubert was born and Joan of Arc was burned, past and present create a layered texture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gustave Flaubert reportedly once said that he wrote his novels to resemble a particular color. “In ‘Madame Bovary,’\xa0” he remarked, “all I was after was to render a special tone, that color of the moldiness of a wood-louse’s existence.” He may well have achieved that with his depiction of illusory love in his novel. But Rouen, France — Flaubert’s birthplace and the setting for a good portion of “Madame Bovary” — evokes a different mood altogether.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/travel/11OVERNIGHTER6/11OVERNIGHTER6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/11/travel/11OVERNIGHTER6/11OVERNIGHTER6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/travel/11OVERNIGHTER6/11OVERNIGHTER6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/travel/11OVERNIGHTER6/11OVERNIGHTER6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/travel/11OVERNIGHTER6/11OVERNIGHTER6-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75