'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/nyregion/09deaf-web/09deaf-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/09/nyregion/09deaf-web/09deaf-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/nyregion/09deaf-web/09deaf-web-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Deaf Patrons’ Suit Accuses Starbucks of Discrimination', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deaf Patrons’ Suit Accuses Starbucks of Discrimination', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu, Winnie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starbucks Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deafness', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of the Deaf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T21:07:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9070a6c6-a2ef-58de-b53e-041d5bf598d3', 'word_count': 1145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9070a6c6-a2ef-58de-b53e-041d5bf598d3'}, {'abstract': 'What happened to the colossus of yore?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/milton-friedman-unperson/', 'snippet': 'What happened to the colossus of yore?', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Glasner has been making a series of posts on the legacy of Milton Friedman, some of them in response to Scott Sumner; they’re interesting if you want to delve into the intellectual history. I’m not personally big on such things — in general, what people thought Keynes or Friedman meant ends up being more important than what they turn out, on close reading, to (maybe, possibly) actually have meant. For what it’s worth, I think Glasner makes a good case that Friedman was indeed more or less a Keynesian, or maybe Hicksian — certainly that was the message everyone took from his Monetary Framework, which was disappointingly conventional. And Friedman’s attempts to claim that Keynes added little that wasn’t already in a Chicago oral tradition don’t hold up well either.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milton Friedman, Unperson', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T21:09:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00bda2e2-7ca9-562c-b502-5b046a77a1c0', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00bda2e2-7ca9-562c-b502-5b046a77a1c0'}, {'abstract': 'This salad delivers lightly smoky swagger and is an excellent foil for the earthy-yet-fruity Sicilian frappato wines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/dining/a-seafood-salad-from-the-grill.html', 'snippet': 'This salad delivers lightly smoky swagger and is an excellent foil for the earthy-yet-fruity Sicilian frappato wines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This seafood salad, sizzled on a grill (or in a grill pan or under the broiler), delivers lightly smoky swagger and, thanks to radicchio, a welcome edge of bitterness. It is an excellent foil for the earthy-yet-fruity and often-light Sicilian frappato and Cerasuolo di Vittoria wines. A substantial salad, it can be a curtain raiser or part of a buffet for summer dinner at home. It might even be carried to a picnic. But it begs to be served a bit warm, and the wine cool.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/dining/14PAIR_SPAN/14PAIR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/14/dining/14PAIR_SPAN/14PAIR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/dining/14PAIR_SPAN/14PAIR_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/dining/14PAIR_SPAN/14PAIR_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1374, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/dining/14PAIR_SPAN/14PAIR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/14/dining/14PAIR_SPAN/14PAIR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/dining/14PAIR_SPAN/14PAIR_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Seafood Salad From the Grill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T21:13:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5f2001a-7ed5-5a8b-9637-b2eaffb7bfeb', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5f2001a-7ed5-5a8b-9637-b2eaffb7bfeb'}, {'abstract': 'A terrific selection from one of the most exciting wine regions in the world shows off the grace and energy of wines that showcase the frappato grape.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/dining/reviews/from-sicily-reds-worth-the-hunt.html', 'snippet': 'A terrific selection from one of the most exciting wine regions in the world shows off the grace and energy of wines that showcase the frappato grape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The transformation of the world of wine in the last 20 years has been simply astounding. Consumers have been blessed with a profusion of wonderful wines from sources that few would have predicted as recently as the turn of the century. Case in point: Sicily. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/dining/14WINE_SPAN/14WINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/14/dining/14WINE_SPAN/14WINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/dining/14WINE_SPAN/14WINE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/dining/14WINE_SPAN/14WINE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/dining/14WINE_SPAN/14WINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/14/dining/14WINE_SPAN/14WINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/dining/14WINE_SPAN/14WINE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Sicily, Reds Worth the Hunt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sicilian Reds Worth the Hunt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asimov, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sicily (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T21:15:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Dining & Wine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd172e28-6ec5-5407-8306-7399e1e8e983', 'word_count': 1025, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd172e28-6ec5-5407-8306-7399e1e8e983'}, {'abstract': 'In a meeting in the Oval Office on Thursday, President Obama told Antonis Samaras, the Greek prime minister, that policies focused only on spending reductions would not help Greece return to economic prosperity.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/obama-urges-greece-to-grow-its-economy/', 'snippet': 'In a meeting in the Oval Office on Thursday, President Obama told Antonis Samaras, the Greek prime minister, that policies focused only on spending reductions would not help Greece return to economic prosperity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama on Thursday urged Greece to find ways to grow its economy even as it continues to cut spending in an effort to recover from a debt-driven economic crisis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Urges Greece to Grow Its Economy', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samaras, Antonis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T21:19:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization':