-5334-5512-86e0-d345ad2cf2c5', 'word_count': 1274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddaf62f8-5334-5512-86e0-d345ad2cf2c5'}, {'abstract': 'The 20 playful drawings in “Robert Pruitt: Women” at the Studio Museum in Harlem hint at the confusion between solo and group identity, and individual and collaborative action.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/arts/design/drawings-by-robert-pruitt-at-studio-museum-in-harlem.html', 'snippet': 'The 20 playful drawings in “Robert Pruitt: Women” at the Studio Museum in Harlem hint at the confusion between solo and group identity, and individual and collaborative action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The subjects of “Robert Pruitt: Women,” his playful solo show at the Studio Museum in Harlem, look as if they’ve walked out of a street-style blog from a distant galaxy. One wears a track jacket, a feathered skirt and a Rubix cube perched on her head like a pillbox hat; another sports a tunic emblazoned with stars and planets and a spiraling headdress in the shape of Tatlin’s Constructivist “Monument to the Third International.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09PRUITT01/0809PRUITT01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1186, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09PRUITT01/0809PRUITT01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1186}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09PRUITT01/0809PRUITT01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 519, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09PRUITT01/0809PRUITT01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1037, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJu