tps://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/08/bouchard-canadas-rising-star-takes-spotlight-at-rogers-cup/', 'snippet': 'After a strong performance at Wimbledon, Eugenie Bouchard, a 19-year-old from Quebec, is becoming a household name, particularly in Canada.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TORONTO — If there was any question about the face of women’s tennis in Canada, one only had to look up while entering the main gates at this week’s Rogers Cup. Emblazoned across the top of the Rexall Centre is the youngest entry at this week’s event, the 19-year-old Eugenie Bouchard. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Young Canadian Takes Spotlight at Rogers Cup', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rogers Cup (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bouchard, Eugenie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Women's Tennis Assn", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T23:10:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dhiren Mahiban', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dhiren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahiban', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1c67d01-5a67-535e-bb92-7cc3d4a069a2', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1c67d01-5a67-535e-bb92-7cc3d4a069a2'}, {'abstract': 'The Bollywood superstar Shah Rukh Khan plays a man kidnapped by hoods and taken to an Indian village in “Chennai Express.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/movies/chennai-express-with-the-bollywood-star-shah-rukh-khan.html', 'snippet': 'The Bollywood superstar Shah Rukh Khan plays a man kidnapped by hoods and taken to an Indian village in “Chennai Express.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“Chennai Express” feels like a sumptuous meal with carefully chosen wine and tasty appetizers but a botched main course. Money and visual care have been lavished on this Bollywood action-comedy-romance and glossy stars engaged (Shah Rukh Khan and Deepika Padukone). But the movie chugs along for most of its 2 hours and 20 minutes searching for comedy and characters in a frantically overplotted story.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09CHENNAI_SPAN/0809CHENNAI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09CHENNAI_SPAN/0809CHENNAI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09CHENNAI_SPAN/0809CHENNAI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09CHENNAI_SPAN/0809CHENNAI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09CHENNAI_SPAN/09CHENNAI_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09CHENNAI_SPAN/09CHENNAI_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09CHENNAI_SPAN/09CHENNAI_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking the Fast Train to Win a Mob Princess', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking the Fast Train To Win a Mob Princess', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shetty, Rohit', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rukh Khan, Shah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T23:12:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6678ab89-bbf9-5d36-8a37-d2f794eeb7a4', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6678ab89-bbf9-5d36-8a37-d2f794eeb7a4'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Lewis took on Mozart and Schubert in one night at Avery Fisher Hall and the Kaplan Penthouse as part of the Mostly Mozart festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/arts/music/paul-lewis-plays-mozart-and-schubert-at-mostly-mozart.html', 'snippet': 'Paul Lewis took on Mozart and Schubert in one night at Avery Fisher Hall and the Kaplan Penthouse as part of the Mostly Mozart festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mostly Mozart festival provides shifts of perspective and scale swifter than anything else on New York’s musical calendar. I began Wednesday evening listening to the pianist Paul Lewis play Mozart with the festival’s house orchestra from the last row of Avery Fisher Hall, and two hours later I was just a few feet from him as he played Schubert, solo, in the Kaplan Penthouse.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image