}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/nyregion/11DINECT2/11DINECT2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seafood With a Clam Shack Atmosphere', 'kicker': 'Dining Review | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seafood With a Clam Shack Atmosphere', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Haven (Conn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Lenny and Joe's Fish Tale at Long Wharf (New Haven, Conn, Restaurant)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T23:25:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Lyness', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyness', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2c43094-1379-5fe9-99c8-1b59b85dc0ad', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2c43094-1379-5fe9-99c8-1b59b85dc0ad'}, {'abstract': 'In “Jug Face,” a pregnant teenager tries to flee a backwoods community when she learns that she may be sacrificed to a mysterious pit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/movies/jug-face-directed-by-chard-crawford-kinkle.html', 'snippet': 'In “Jug Face,” a pregnant teenager tries to flee a backwoods community when she learns that she may be sacrificed to a mysterious pit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shirley Jackson’s short story “The Lottery” has nothing on the grisly compulsory rituals of a backcountry settlement in Chad Crawford Kinkle’s handily made debut feature, “Jug Face.” Periodically, a designated potter creates a jug bearing the likeness of an unlucky villager, who is then sacrificed to appease a hallowed pit in the ground. The practice has been going on for ages, which might account for the village’s small population, but it takes just one person to jam the process.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09RDP_JUGFACE_SPAN/0809FILM02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 299, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09RDP_JUGFACE_SPAN/0809FILM02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 299}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09RDP_JUGFACE_SPAN/0809FILM02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 510, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09RDP_JUGFACE_SPAN/0809FILM02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 528, 'width': 1061, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09RDP_JUGFACE_SPAN/0809FILM02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09RDP_JUGFACE_SPAN/0809FILM02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09RDP_JUGFACE_SPAN/0809FILM02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hole in the Ground, Worshiped and Feared', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jug Face', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kinkle, Chad Crawford', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-08T23:26:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicolas Rapold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicolas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rapold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c58094d6-6c29-5710-a486-958604f1b421', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c58094d6-6c29-5710-a486-958604f1b421'}, {'abstract': 'Here in the 200th birthday year for “Pride and Prejudice,” Jane Austen has become an insatiable cottage industry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/books/on-austen-new-books-banknotes-and-board-games.html', 'snippet': 'Here in the 200th birthday year for “Pride and Prejudice,” Jane Austen has become an insatiable cottage industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oh, Jane. What a summer it’s been for your insatiable cottage industry — a cottage about the size of Darcy’s pile at Pemberley, at this point. Here in the 200th birthday year for “Pride and Prejudice,” it seems as if not a week goes by without new grist. Last month the Bank of England announced that it would feature Jane Austen on the £10 note, making Jane the only woman besides the queen and an obscure prison reformer to be honored on British currency; a Twitter war erupted, with the most extreme position taken by someone who tweeted rape and death threats against the woman who’d lobbied the bank to feature a woman.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09janegame-image1/09janegame-image1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 393, 'w