2fa-575a-8125-af2cab6fbadd', 'word_count': 1233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d113a951-d2fa-575a-8125-af2cab6fbadd'}, {'abstract': 'Former lawyers for Maj. Nidal Malik Hasan, who has admitted being the gunman in the 2009 rampage, said that helping him achieve his death-sentence goal violates their ethics as defense lawyers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/us/judge-denies-ex-defense-teams-bid-to-limit-role-in-fort-hood-suspects-trial.html', 'snippet': 'Former lawyers for Maj. Nidal Malik Hasan, who has admitted being the gunman in the 2009 rampage, said that helping him achieve his death-sentence goal violates their ethics as defense lawyers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KILLEEN, Tex. — The judge overseeing the military trial of the Army psychiatrist charged in a deadly shooting rampage at the Fort Hood base denied on Thursday his former lawyers’ request to limit their role in the case. The ruling came a day after the lawyers said they could no longer assist him because he was seeking the same goal as prosecutors — to be sentenced to death. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Denies Ex-Defense Team’s Bid to Limit Role in Fort Hood Suspect’s Trial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Denies Ex-Defense Team’s Bid to Limit Role in Fort Hood Suspect’s Trial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fernandez, Manny', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hasan, Nidal Malik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Hood (Tex)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts-Martial', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osborn, Tara A', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poppe, Kris R', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gross, Gregory', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-09T00:12:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62526e69-05fc-540c-afec-eaa21548fe56', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62526e69-05fc-540c-afec-eaa21548fe56'}, {'abstract': '“The United States of Autism” follows Richard Everts, the director, whose son is autistic, as he journeys across the country to visit families affected by autism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/movies/richard-evertss-united-states-of-autism.html', 'snippet': '“The United States of Autism” follows Richard Everts, the director, whose son is autistic, as he journeys across the country to visit families affected by autism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The spectrum of autism is wide, as the low-budget documentary “The United States of Autism” shows. Its host, Richard Everts (also the director and the father of an autistic son), introduces 20 families dealing with the disorder, visited during 40 days of road travel across the country. He meets the highly verbal, troubled only in social situations. He meets the nonverbal, whose physical struggles exhaust financial and emotional resources. He meets parents displaying pain or pride, or both, about their children.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/arts/09RDP_UNITED_SPAN/0809FILM07-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, '