ount': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c549fe1-6736-5e7f-993e-918358453e31'}, {'abstract': 'Presidents generally choose the leaders of independent commissions, but the other members are picked on Capitol Hill, which means that the leaders can find it difficult to accomplish anything.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/business/independent-agencies-sometimes-in-name-only.html', 'snippet': 'Presidents generally choose the leaders of independent commissions, but the other members are picked on Capitol Hill, which means that the leaders can find it difficult to accomplish anything.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1985, President Ronald Reagan had to fill a Democratic slot on the Securities and Exchange Commission. He chose a young lawyer and economist, Joseph A. Grundfest. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Independent Agencies, Sometimes in Name Only', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Independent Agencies, Sometimes In Name Only', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'