y': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Impressions of Life in the Gulag', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-09T02:33:51+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c23e4ad1-abfa-58bd-9ef6-e6d8b5d771d4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c23e4ad1-abfa-58bd-9ef6-e6d8b5d771d4'}, {'abstract': 'Two 19-year-olds who have been held on a criminal complaint in the Boston Marathon bombings investigation were indicted by a federal grand jury on obstruction of justice charges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/us/massachusetts-bombing-suspects-friends-indicted.html', 'snippet': 'Two 19-year-olds who have been held on a criminal complaint in the Boston Marathon bombings investigation were indicted by a federal grand jury on obstruction of justice charges.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Two 19-year-olds who have been held on a criminal complaint in the investigation of the Boston Marathon bombings were indicted by a federal grand jury on Thursday on obstruction of justice charges. The two, Dias Kadyrbayev and Azamat Tazhayakov, attended the University of Massachusetts, Dartmouth, with Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, who the authorities say worked with his brother, Tamerlan, to set off bombs at the marathon, killing 3 and wounding more than 260. The indictment says the teenagers, friends with Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, removed items including a laptop and a backpack with fireworks from his dormitory room and put them in trash in New Bedford, Mass. The two could face up to 20 years in prison, a $250,000 fine and deportation, as they are both Kazakh nationals. A third friend of Mr. Tsarnaev’s, Robel Phillipos, has been charged with lying to investigators. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Bombing Suspect’s Friends Indicted', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Bombing Suspect’s Friends Indicted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kadyrbayev, Dias', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tazhayakov, Azamat', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phillipos, Robel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Dzhokhar A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Tamerlan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-09T02:35:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6cbbc68-982e-5294-863f-6fcdd43aa185', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6cbbc68-982e-5294-863f-6fcdd43aa185'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the day for Friday, August 9, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-friday-august-9-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Friday, August 9, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': '“When we as African Americans look at our history, our own Dr. Martin Luther King, or own Dr. Adam Clayton Powell, there has always been something in a person’s life that others sought to use against their greater good.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, August 9, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-09T02:43:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe3c7404-93e5-5a97-a828-d7c1d1a81aea', 'word_count': 55, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe3c7404-93e5-5a97-a828-d7c1d1a81aea'}, {'abstract': 'The Red Bulls reached down under to sign a new player: defender/midfielder David Carney, 29, who has played 46 times for Australia’s national team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/sports/red-bulls-sign-australian.html', 'snippet': 'The Red Bulls reached down under to sign a new player: defender/midfielder David Carney, 29, who has played 46 times for Australia’s national team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Red Bulls reached down under to sign a new player: defender/midfielder David Carney, 29, who has played 46 times for Australia’s national team. He and his Socceroo and Red Bulls teammate Tim Cahill are likely to be with Australia when it plays in next summer’s World Cup in Brazil. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Red Bulls Sign Australian', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Soccer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Red Bulls Sign Australian', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bell, Jack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carney, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-09T02:49:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0facda4-73d8-549b-af29-c392a27afac0', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0facda4-73d8-549b-af29-c392a27afac0'}, {'abstract': 'About 130 paddleboarders have entered for a 25-mile event that will circle almost the entire island of Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/nyregion/standing-up-to-currents-in-support-of-charities.html', 'snippet': 'About 130 paddleboarders have entered for a 25-mile event that will circle almost the entire island of Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paddleboarding would seem a tricky endeavor under the best conditions. A cross between kayaking and surfing, paddleboarding — in which the practitioner stands on a long board and paddles — was born in Hawaii and has spread across the United States in recent years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/nyregion/paddle/paddle-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/09/nyregion/paddle/paddle-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/09/nyregion/paddle/paddle-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp