: 'The Securities and Exchange Commission is seeking to extract a rare admission of wrongdoing from JPMorgan Chase. | SAC Capital Advisors agreed to keep most of its money in its fund while operating under a criminal indictment. | América Móvil offered to buy the stake in KPN it did not already own. | William A. Ackman urged J.C. Penney to speed up a search for a permanent chief.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/morning-agenda-s-e-c-s-new-tack-in-jpmorgan-inquiry/', 'snippet': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission is seeking to extract a rare admission of wrongdoing from JPMorgan Chase. | SAC Capital Advisors agreed to keep most of its money in its fund while operating under a criminal indictment. | América Móvil offer...', 'lead_paragraph': 'S.E.C. SAID TO PRESS JPMORGAN FOR ADMISSION OF WRONGDOING \xa0|\xa0The Securities and Exchange Commission is seeking to level civil charges against JPMorgan Chase and extract a rare admission of wrongdoing, as an investigation into last year’s multibillion-dollar trading loss enters its final stage, Ben Protess and Jessica Silver-Greenberg report in DealBook. If JPMorgan concedes to some wrongdoing, such an admission would set an important precedent for the S.E.C., which for decades allowed defendants to “neither admit nor deny wrongdoing.” An agreement could come as soon as this fall, people briefed on the case said, adding that the agency had not threatened to charge JPMorgan executives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C.’s New Tack in JPMorgan Inquiry', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-09T11:53:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b8a90f0-afbc-563d-befa-f10d4705b14b', 'word_count': 1495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b8a90f0-afbc-563d-befa-f10d4705b14b'}, {'abstract': 'Eric Bogosian will perform at Bank Street Theater Oct. 1-20 as part of the Labyrinth Theater Company’s 2013-14 season.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/09/100-monologues-from-bogosian-to-kick-off-labyrinth-theater-season/', 'snippet': 'Eric Bogosian will perform at Bank Street Theater Oct. 1-20 as part of the Labyrinth Theater Company’s 2013-14 season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Labyrinth Theater Company announced on Friday that in October, as part of its 2013-14 season, the Obie Award-winning playwright Eric Bogosian would perform roughly 100 monologues from his popular one-man shows from the 1980s and ’90s. The monologues, culled from plays like “Sex, Drugs, Rock & Roll” and “Pounding Nails in the Floor With My Forehead,” will differ for each performance, which will run Oct. 1-20 at the Bank Street Theater.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '100 Monologues From Bogosian to Kick Off Labyrinth Theater Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bogosian, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morisseau, Dominique', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LAByrinth Theater Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-09T12:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9674cc86-5456-5d80-b97e-