aterial': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/303df0ba-5d40-5db5-a8de-28b92490275a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/303df0ba-5d40-5db5-a8de-28b92490275a'}, {'abstract': 'American companies are making more money than ever, but workers’ salaries have been at the lowest percentage of the gross domestic product since 1929.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/10/business/economy/us-companies-thrive-as-workers-fall-behind.html', 'snippet': 'American companies are making more money than ever, but workers’ salaries have been at the lowest percentage of the gross domestic product since 1929.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMERICAN companies are more profitable than ever — and more profitable than we thought they were before the government revised the national income accounts last week. Wage earners are making less than we thought, in part because the government now thinks it was overestimating the amount of income not reported by taxpayers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Companies Thrive as Workers Fall Behind', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Companies Thrive As Workers Fall Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '