.com/2013/08/11/magazine/eternal-bragging-rights.html', 'snippet': 'A tradition based on fantasy is tested by reality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since 1991 I’ve competed in a fantasy football league with my college buddies, most of whom hail from the great state of New Jersey. Fantasy football leagues typically draft online, but we still conduct our business face to face, convening once a year, in late August, at a faded South Jersey hotel, thick with cigarette smoke. It’s a weekend filled with steaks, beer, Bruce Springsteen bootlegs and affectionately toothless insults; a weird alternate universe where I wash down Cool Ranch Doritos with Mountain Dew and occasionally sleep in my clothes. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/magazine/11lives/11lives-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/magazine/11lives/11lives-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/magazine/11lives/11lives-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/11/magazine/11lives/11lives-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/magazine/11lives/11lives-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eternal Bragging Rights', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eternal Bragging Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gervino, Tony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Games', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-09T14:36:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Gervino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gervino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b5a8b8e-aec7-5db1-8608-4a1c5a666e00', 'word_count': 746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b5a8b8e-aec7-5db1-8608-4a1c5a666e00'}, {'abstract': 'And why you just can’t beat a good list on a piece of paper in your pocket.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/magazine/harrison-ford-on-fanboys-and-fat-suits.html', 'snippet': 'And why you just can’t beat a good list on a piece of paper in your pocket.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Your new movie, “Paranoia,” is about corporate espionage and greed. Do you think we’ve seen the end of the days when Hollywood could make an upbeat movie about corporate life like “Working Girl”?  I shouldn’t think so. I think businesspeople are like every other type of character — they come in all varieties. And “Working Girl” depended on the glass ceiling for women, and what a pleasure it was to see someone break through. And it was funny. But now, I’m sure there’s more demand for movies about how corporations are dictating our lives in many ways.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'