h a pair of star-crossed lovers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the writer Jeanette Winterson says, “Men have been writing about women forever.” This was in an interview in The Guardian with A. M. Homes, whom Winterson describes as “a woman writing dangerously.” What Winterson means is that Homes is fearless about writing from a male point of view. (Think of Harry, the narrator of Homes’s recent novel, “May We Be Forgiven.”)', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/books/review/0811-bks-IRVING/0811-bks-IRVING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 343, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/11/books/review/0811-bks-IRVING/0811-bks-IRVING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 343}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/books/review/0811-bks-IRVING/0811-bks-IRVING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 585, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/books/review/0811-bks-IRVING/0811-bks-IRVING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1170, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/books/review/0811-bks-IRVING/0811-bks-IRVING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/11/books/review/0811-bks-IRVING/0811-bks-IRVING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/books/review/0811-bks-IRVING/0811-bk