b_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/arts/music/nashville-singer-finds-her-voice.html', 'snippet': 'Maggie Rose’s debut album, “Cut to Impress” (RPM), is one of the year’s best country release, and she plays this week at the Emporium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four years ago, a singer named Margaret Durante tried to have a go at Nashville. She released a tepid country cover of “Use Somebody,” the desperate Kings of Leon anthem — an uncommitted way to begin a career — and that was that. She kicked around the city for a while, jumping among independent labels, but only this year, remade as Maggie Rose, has she sounded anything like herself. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nashville Singer Finds Her Voice', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nashville Singer Finds Her Voice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Country Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-09T18:29:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffb6b488-087f-5597-bdd1-7ade3deba4cc', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffb6b488-087f-5597-bdd1-7ade3deba4cc'}, {'abstract': 'New plays these days tend to come in slimmed-down sizes. But not the latest work from the Amoralists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/theater/disorderly-conduct.html', 'snippet': 'New plays these days tend to come in slimmed-down sizes. But not the latest work from the Amoralists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New plays these days tend to come in slimmed-down sizes, the better to accommodate the worrying economics of producing theater, both on Broadway and off, and at the country’s major regional theaters. The Amoralists, an exuberantly iconoclastic Off Off Broadway company known for a raw, aggressive, hypertheatrical style, is, naturally, running off in the opposite direction.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Disorderly Conduct', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Theater', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Disorderly Conduct', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Amoralists, The (Theater Co)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-09T18:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6aa830cb-ff2d-575c-a769-aa786bd10ceb', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aa830cb-ff2d-575c-a769-aa786bd10ceb'}, {'abstract': 'A member of New York City’s intrepid corps of window washers has been at it for over 35 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/realestate/the-grime-fighter-brent-weingard-does-windows.html', 'snippet': 'A member of New York City’s intrepid corps of window washers has been at it for over 35 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The unforgiving pavement of Greenwich Street unspooled half a dozen stories below. But Brent Weingard, who had strapped himself into an olive-green harness and attached himself to a canvas belt that in turn was attached to a hook on the facade of No. 55, seemed oblivious to the fact that gravity was not his friend. Dangling outside the oversize double-hung window, the belt his only protection, Mr. Weingard didn’t bat an eye. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/realestate/11DEBRIEF1/11superrefer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/11/realestate/11DEBRIEF1/11superrefer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/realestate/11DEBRIEF1/11superrefer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/realestate/11DEBRIEF1/11superrefer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1382, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/realestate/11DEBRIEF1/11superrefer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/11/realestate/11DEBRIEF1/11superrefer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/realestate/11DEBRIEF1/11superrefer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Grime Fighter: Brent Weingard Does Windows', 'kicker': 'Debriefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Grime Fighter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenblum, Constance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'pers