es', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11IVAN1_SPAN/11IVAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11IVAN1_SPAN/11IVAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11IVAN1_SPAN/11IVAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11IVAN1_SPAN/11IVAN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11IVAN1_SPAN/11IVAN1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11IVAN1_SPAN/11IVAN1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11IVAN1_SPAN/11IVAN1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cloaking an Opera in a New Identity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cloaking an Opera in a New Identity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mostly Mozart Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fischer, Ivan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-09T18:45:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ade0f81-adb3-5e3d-820d-81c8dbcb7c93', 'word_count': 1561, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ade0f81-adb3-5e3d-820d-81c8dbcb7c93'}, {'abstract': '“Then She Fell” derives its fractured narratives, its doppelgängers and mirror images, from “Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland” and “Through the Looking Glass.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/theater/then-she-fell-is-inspired-by-lewis-carrolls-life-and-work.html', 'snippet': '“Then She Fell” derives its fractured narratives, its doppelgängers and mirror images, from “Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland” and “Through the Looking Glass.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“Eat,” the White Queen barks, as you wonder what to do with the waferlike snack she has handed you. In the midst of this tumultuous feast, there’s no time for questions. Heaping bowls of fruit and diminutive cocktails materialize from who knows where, as she clambers onto tabletops and chairs, ricochets among cabinets and walls. A creaky lantern hangs from the ceiling; she reaches toward it and, with a brisk shove, sets it swinging on its precarious hinges. When Alice appears, our careening hostess gives her one drink, then another, luring the girlish visitor into a state as wild as her own.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11FELL2_SPAN/11FELL2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11FELL2_SPAN/11FELL2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11FELL2_SPAN/11FELL2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11FELL2_SPAN/11FELL2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11FELL2_SPAN/11FELL2_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11FELL2_SPAN/11FELL2_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11FELL2_SPAN/11FELL2_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Adventures in a Sinister Wonderland', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Adventures in a Sinister Wonderland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Then She Fell (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Third Rail Projects', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carroll, Lewis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-09T18:49:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e341c21-a7e6-57ee-b6e5-56bbb87ba737', 'word_count': 989, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e341c21-a7e6-57ee-b6e5-56bbb87ba737'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Kelly and Mr. Baldwin are at the center of unconfirmed reports about planned programming changes at Fox News and MSNBC.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/10/business/media/reports-see-new-roles-for-megyn-kelly-and-alec-baldwin.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Kelly and Mr. Baldwin are at the center of unconfirmed reports about planned programming changes at Fox News and MSNBC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Fox News anchor Megyn Kelly and the actor Alec Baldwin were at the center of unconfirmed reports this week about programming changes said to be planned at two of the cable news networks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reports See New Roles for Megyn Kelly and Alec Baldwin', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MSNBC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Megyn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldwin, Alec', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-09T19:04:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/807d5c35-14f4-5e3d-bf1b-65fad5c349e2', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/807d5c35-14f4-5e3d-bf1b-65fad5c349e2'}, {'abstract': 'David Lowery, having edited films for indie directors like Shane Carruth and Amy Siemetz, returns to the director’s chair for “Ain’t Them Bodies Saints.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/movies/david-lowery-directs-aint-them-bodies-saints.html', 'snippet': 'David Lowery, having edited films for indie directors like Shane Carruth and Amy Siemetz, returns to the director’s chair for “Ain’t Them Bodies Saints.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even when David Lowery was a movie-mad teenager in Dallas, he was training himself to be a storyteller. Using the clumsy, now blessedly defunct method of VCR-to-VCR editing — record tape from one machine to the other, stop, rewind, repeat — he learned the basics of cinematic rhythm and narrative. “It’s just arduous enough that it forces you to think in advance about what you’re trying to do — about the big picture, and about how one shot is going to lead to the next,” he said. “I think a lot of my editorial tendencies were born out of that process.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11SAINTS1_SPAN/11SAINTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11SAINTS1_SPAN/11SAINTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 314}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11SAINTS1_SPAN/11SAINTS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 536, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/arts/11SAINTS1_SPAN/11SAINTS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1072, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', '