rs to pick up the dress — the wedding was 10 days off. I flipped on the radio, and was greeted with the Grateful Dead’s “Scarlet Begonias,” an unusual but much-welcomed selection from a station known more for playing Lynyrd Skynyrd and Bad Company. “Nice,” I said. “A good omen.” We were young and in love and getting married, and the sky was yellow and the sun was blue!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Day Jerry Garcia Died', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Jerry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grateful Dead', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-09T20:42:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Vecsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vecsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fd4948d-39c2-5548-9281-e8f729a15af4', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fd4948d-39c2-5548-9281-e8f729a15af4'}, {'abstract': 'Three of track’s biggest stars have tested positive for banned substances in recent months and will miss the world championships in Moscow, which begin Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/10/sports/track-championships-put-russia-and-doping-in-spotlight.html', 'snippet': 'Three of track’s biggest stars have tested positive for banned substances in recent months and will miss the world championships in Moscow, which begin Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Thirty-three years after the American high jumper Dwight Stones missed the Moscow Olympics because of a United States boycott, he was standing in front of the stadium in which he would have competed and answering questions about another pr