 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shanker, Thom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagel, Chuck', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-10T00:42:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker and Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/447a8704-e644-54c5-85cf-4639654ce5bb', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/447a8704-e644-54c5-85cf-4639654ce5bb'}, {'abstract': 'President Sebastián Piñera apologized for serious mistakes in the nationwide census last year, which, despite intense efforts, failed to survey over 9 percent of the population.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/10/world/americas/chilean-president-apologizes-for-census.html', 'snippet': 'President Sebastián Piñera apologized for serious mistakes in the nationwide census last year, which, despite intense efforts, failed to survey over 9 percent of the population.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANTIAGO, Chile — President Sebastián Piñera’s administration had promised the “best census ever.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chilean President Apologizes for Census', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chilean President Apologizes for Census', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinera, Sebastian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachelet, Michelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-10T00:44:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pascale Bonnefoy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pascale', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bonnefoy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63042d6b-0d9c-56a8-9b8c-444358843f06', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63042d6b-0d9c-56a8-9b8c-444358843f06'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Barbara Boxer published an open letter to Mayor Bob Filner of San Diego, asking him to step down amid more allegations of inappropriate conduct.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/10/us/california-senator-castigates-san-diego-mayor.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Barbara Boxer published an open letter to Mayor Bob Filner of San Diego, asking him to step down amid more allegations of inappropriate conduct.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Barbara Boxer published an open letter to Mayor Bob Filner of San Diego on Friday, asking him to step down amid more allegations of inappropriate conduct. This week, female veterans, including two women who were victims of sexual assault while in the military, claimed that Mr. Filner tried to use his position in public office to gain dates or intimate contact. Ms. Boxer, along with California’s other senator, Dianne Feinstein, had already called for Mr. Filner’s resignation, as have many other officials in San Diego and in Washington. In the letter, Ms. Boxer made a direct appeal to the mayor, a fellow Democrat. “The latest revelations regarding your behavior toward women recovering from sexual assault — women who desperately need our help – have shaken me to my core,” Ms. Boxer wrote in the letter posted on her Web site. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Senator Castigates San Diego Mayor', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Senator Castigates San Diego Mayor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Filner, Bob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boxer, Barbara', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Diego (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-10T00:45:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/033914ea-e7f6-5ab1-8898-7be7bcff057c', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/033914ea-e7f6-5ab1-8898-7be7bcff057c'}, {'abstract': 'Rafael Caro Quintero, a drug kingpin convicted of masterminding an American’s death, was unexpectedly released from prison on Friday after his conviction was overturned.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/10/world/americas/mexican-tied-to-killing-of-dea-agent-is-freed.html', 'snippet': 'Rafael Caro Quintero, a drug kingpin convicted of masterminding an American’s death, was unexpectedly released from prison on Friday after his conviction was overturned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY — A drug kingpin convicted of masterminding the murder of an American drug agent in 1985 — a killing that helped accelerate the modern drug war and that remains an emotional touchstone for law enforcement agents — was unexpectedly released from prison on Friday after his conviction was overturned.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/world/mexico/mexico-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 274, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/world/mexico/mexico-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 274, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/world/mexico/mexico-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/10/world/mexico/mexico-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/world/mexico/mexico-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexican Tied to Killing of D.E.A. Agent Is Freed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexican Tied to Killing of D.E.A. Agent Is Freed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caro Quintero, Rafael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Archibold, Randal C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Camarena, Enrique', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drug Enforcement Administration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-10T00:47:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold and Karla Zabludovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zabludovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bcf0d06-f1fe-543c-a9d9-48142de066fc', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bcf0d06-f1fe-543c-a9d9-48142de066fc'}, {'abstract': 'The Committee to Protect Journalists has reported at least 14 journalists who are missing or have been abducted, but the total number of kidnappings is believed to be much higher.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/10/world/middleeast/journalists-in-syria-face-dangers-of-war-and-rising-risk-of-abduction.html', 'snippet': 'The Committee to Protect Journalists has reported at least 14 journalists who are missing or have been abducted, but the total number of kidnappings is believed to be much higher.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Abductions of journalists inside Syria have increased sharply this year as the ravages of the conflict have worsened and the insurgency has turned more jihadist and chaotic, making the country one of the most hostile conflict zones for news gatherers in recent memory, according to news media advocacy organizations, rights workers and veteran correspondents.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/world/abductions1/abductions1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/10/world/abductions1/abductions1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/world/abductions1/abductions1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/world/abductions1/abductions1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/world/abductions1/abductions1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/10/world/abductions1/abductions1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/world/abductions1/abductions1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Journalists in Syria Face Dangers of War and Rising Risk of Abduction', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Journalists in Syria Face Dangers of War and Rising Risk of Abduction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'S