d with warming temperatures portending rising sea levels and disruptions to food production, the centrally planned Communist country is experimenting with a capitalist approach to address the problem: it is creating incentives so that the market — and not the government — will force reductions in emissions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pollution Economics', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pollution Economics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shenzhen (China)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-10T01:01:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dirk Forrister and Paul Bledsoe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Forrister', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bledsoe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8076fce4-f3e8-58ba-8424-d7542d5e0bdf', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8076fce4-f3e8-58ba-8424-d7542d5e0bdf'}, {'abstract': 'Consumers are the ultimate losers in the CBS-Time Warner Cable negotiations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/10/opinion/cable-customers-as-collateral-damage.html', 'snippet': 'Consumers are the ultimate losers in the CBS-Time Warner Cable negotiations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CBS and Time Warner Cable have been engaged in a contract fight that has left millions of residents in cities like New York, Los Angeles and Dallas without access to the network’s programming on their TVs and computers for almost a week. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cable Customers as Collateral Damage', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cable Customers as Collateral Damage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Cable Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-10T01:01:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b895b5ee-c1f5-52df-be32-41035207acd6', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b895b5ee-c1f5-52df-be32-41035207acd6'}, {'abstract': 'A plan to transfer female inmates from a federal prison in Danbury, Conn., to a remote location needs much closer scrutiny.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/10/opinion/bad-prison-policy-for-women.html', 'snippet': 'A plan to transfer female inmates from a federal prison in Danbury, Conn., to a remote location needs much closer scrutiny.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The decision by the Federal Bureau of Prisons to transfer more than 1,100 women from a federal prison in Danbury, Conn., to other locations, including a remote facility in 