device” and from my consciousness too. It’s very odd.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Books to Have and to Hold', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Books to Have and to Hold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinkenborg, Verlyn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-10T17:40:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verlyn Klinkenborg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verlyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klinkenborg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0815d3ee-00eb-5cfa-aa22-ec8393644176', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0815d3ee-00eb-5cfa-aa22-ec8393644176'}, {'abstract': 'Lessons for Egypt from the French Revolution of 1848.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/opinion/sunday/marxs-lesson-for-the-muslim-brothers.html', 'snippet': 'Lessons for Egypt from the French Revolution of 1848.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KARL MARX wrote that history repeats itself, first as tragedy, then as farce. He had in mind the Revolution of 1848, when a democratic uprising against the French monarchy collapsed into a Bonapartist dictatorship just as the French Revolution had six decades earlier. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/sunday-review/11EGYPT/11EGYPT-ar