 Steroids?', 'kicker': 'Loose Ends', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What if Novelists Took Steroids?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-10T17:53:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Farris Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'Farris', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a6bc95e-0149-5906-919c-3694d9dd3b01', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a6bc95e-0149-5906-919c-3694d9dd3b01'}, {'abstract': 'Twelve of the last 25 P.G.A. Championship titlists, including Shaun Micheel, the winner at Oak Hill in 2003, have not taken a second major.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/sports/golf/better-to-have-won-only-once.html', 'snippet': 'Twelve of the last 25 P.G.A. Championship titlists, including Shaun Micheel, the winner at Oak Hill in 2003, have not taken a second major.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PITTSFORD, N.Y. — The footsteps of champions are not erased when the tide goes out, which Rich Beem pointed out to Shaun Micheel on a rainy Friday the way one might call attention to a rainbow.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/sports/SUB-DOG-WONDER/SUB-DOG-WONDER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/11/sports/SUB-DOG-WONDER/SUB-DOG-WONDER-articleLarge.jpg