d a responsibility to give back and help make life better for others.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/business/11-BOSSSUB/11-BOSSSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 589, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/business/11-BOSSSUB/11-BOSSSUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 589, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/business/11-BOSSSUB/11-BOSSSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/11/business/11-BOSSSUB/11-BOSSSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/business/11-BOSSSUB/11-BOSSSUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Responsibility to Give Back', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Responsibility to Give Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olson, Elizabeth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AARP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rand, A Barry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-10T19:53:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. Barry Rand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'Barry', 'lastname': 'Rand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72d33972-34a9-5518-8aba-6f8a1b8eee70', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72d33972-34a9-5518-8aba-6f8a1b8eee70'}, {'abstract': 'Not really there.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/10/the-pigou-effect-double-super-special-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'Not really there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Via Brad DeLong, Robert Waldmann weighs in on the contributions or lack thereof of Milton Friedman, arguing that much of what he said was already there in Samuelson and Solow 1960. Actually, I’d give him more credit than that; the S-S paper — very unusually for both men, and for Bob Solow in particular — is one of those pieces sometimes described as “rich”, with many points alluded to but not many takeaway lines; to the extent that people did take something away, it was the crude notion of a usable downward-sloping Phillips curve, which turned out to be wrong. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pigou Effect (Double-super-special-wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-10T20:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b65d152b-a7e5-5fef-bffe-5cacd99ff292', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b65d152b-a7e5-5fef-bffe-5cacd99ff292'}, {'abstract': 'As the administration considers approval of the much-debated Keystone XL pipeline, cleanup efforts in two communities portend the potential hazards of transporting heavy Canadian crude.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/us/amid-pipeline-debate-two-costly-cleanups-forever-change-towns.html', 'snippet': 'As the administration considers approval of the much-debated Keystone XL pipeline, cleanup efforts in two communities portend the potential hazards of transporting heavy Canadian crude.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MARSHALL, Mich. — As the Obama administration inches closer to a decision on whether to approve construction of the much-debated Keystone XL pipeline, costly cleanup efforts in two communities stricken by oil spills portend the potential hazards of transporting heavy Canadian crude.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/us/PIPELINE-2/PIPELINE-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/11/us/PIPELINE-2/PIPELINE-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/us/PIPELINE-2/PIPELINE-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/us/PIPELINE-2/PIPELINE-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1311, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/us/PIPELINE-2/PIPELINE-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'h