et with President Vladimir V. Putin next month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, Aug. 11', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martinez, Lulu', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-10T20:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44f49255-d3d2-548c-830e-6faf217f5bd5', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44f49255-d3d2-548c-830e-6faf217f5bd5'}, {'abstract': 'The Pirate Bay announced that it was releasing PirateBrowser, a free Web browser that will give access to people in countries where the site is currently blocked.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/10/the-pirate-bay-offers-piratebrowser-to-avoid-censorship/', 'snippet': 'The Pirate Bay announced that it was releasing PirateBrowser, a free Web browser that will give access to people in countries where the site is currently blocked.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The\xa0Pirate Bay, one of the largest and most famous piracy sites on the Web for illegally downloading copyrighted material, has been in a constant game of cat and mouse with legal authorities from around the globe for the past decade. Government agencies have often tried to shut the site down, or thwart people from reaching it\xa0— because people use it to download movies, music, digital books and other intellectual property — only to see the site retaliate with new doorways for people to access its wares.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/technology/bits-pirate/bits-pirate-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 283, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/technology/bits-pirate/bits-pirate-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 283, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/technology/bits-pirate/bits-pirate-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/10/technology/bits-pirate/bits-pirate-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/technology/bits-pirate/bits-pirate-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pirate Bay Offers Web Browser to Avoid Censorship', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pirate Bay', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-10T20:47:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10e31948-066c-5deb-a261-d4768a3b853a', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10e31948-066c-5deb-a261-d4768a3b853a'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my column about mass incarceration, through the case of a man serving 15 years for possessing seven shotgun shells.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/10/a-victim-of-mass-incarceration/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my column about mass incarceration, through the case of a man serving 15 years for possessing seven shotgun shells.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column looks at America’s failed policy of mass incarceration, through the case of a man who was recently sentenced to a mandatory minimum of 15 years in federal prison as an ex-felon in possession of seven shotgun shells. To me, it just seemed nutty. If he had burglarized storage containers, then state authorities should have prosecuted him for that. But 15 years in federal prison, at a cost of more than $400,000, for innocent possession of seven shotgun shells with no gun to go with them? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Victim of Mass Incarceration', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-10T20:54:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c44a3775-27e5-5866-97ac-0b6b99762f88', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c44a3775-27e5-5866-97ac-0b6b99762f88'}, {'abstract': '“From One Second to the Next,” a short documentary about texting and driving commissioned by AT&T from the acclaimed director Werner Herzog, tells four deeply harrowing tales of lives altered by a driver’s focus on a phone rather than on the road.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/10/texting-and-driving-the-aftermath-in-a-movie/', 'snippet': '“From One Second to the Next,” a short documentary about texting and driving commissioned by AT&T from the acclaimed director Werner Herzog, tells four deeply harrowing tales of lives altered by a driver’s focus on a phone rather than on the road.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Corporate videos are not often noted for their searing emotional content. But “From One Second to the Next,” a short documentary about texting and driving commissioned by AT&T from the acclaimed director Werner Herzog, tells four deeply harrowing tales of lives altered by a driver’s focus on a phone rather than on the road. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texting and Driving, the Aftermath in a Movie', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Driver Distraction and Fatigue', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herzog, Werner', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-10T20:56:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cdbefea-c9f8-5ae5-880f-261eb59a7bf2', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cdbefea-c9f8-5ae5-880f-261eb59a7bf2'}, {'abstract': 'Edoardo Nesi, a former businessman turned author, tells the story of the textile industry of Prato, Italy, in a memoir filled with musings as finely woven as his company’s woolens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/business/in-story-of-my-people-recalling-an-industry-and-way-of-life.html', 'snippet': 'Edoardo Nesi, a former businessman turned author, tells the story of the textile industry of Prato, Italy, in a memoir filled with musings as finely woven as his company’s woolens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EDOARDO NESI has written a short memoir of great charm, for all its sadness a pleasure to read. A born writer, Mr. Nesi was also by birthright a manufacturer of fine woolens. He was bred from an early age to take over the Tuscan textile business that his grandfather and great-uncle began in the 1920s.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/business/11SHELF/11SHELF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/11/business/11SHELF/11SHELF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 840}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/business/11SHELF/11SHELF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/business/11SHELF/11SHELF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1463, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/11/business/11SHELF/11SHELF-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/11/business/11SHELF/11SHELF-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailhei