-august-11.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Sunday, August 11.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We are living in a state of constant terror, but we see nothing from the police or the army.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Sunday, August 11', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of The Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-11T04:18:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/9860416a-66ab-50fa-abcb-a42d198c4091', 'word_count': 42, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9860416a-66ab-50fa-abcb-a42d198c4091'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on August 11, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/pageoneplus/corrections-august-11-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on August 11, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUSINESS', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: August 11, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-11T04:20:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NewsDesk', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/583c5ecf-7afd-55f5-a351-477c4862602d', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/583c5ecf-7afd-55f5-a351-477c4862602d'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/11/arts/whats-on-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (AMC) LOW WINTER SUN Frank Agnew (Mark Strong), a Detroit homicide detective with a tragic past, is persuaded by a colleague, Joe Geddes (Lennie James, above), to help him kill another cop, who he claims murdered a loved one of Frank’s. But as holes surface in Joe’s story, Frank starts to worry that he has been played in this new series, based on a 2006 British mini-series of the same title. Ruben Santiago-Hudson portrays the precinct commander, who assigns Frank to lead the investigation into the cop’s death. David Costabile is an Internal Affairs detective delving into corruption. And James Ransone is a thug who, with his wife (Sprague Grayden), and a police officer on his payroll, looks to set up a drug and prostitution business. “It’s a deadly serious drama, but some of the early scenes are so overwrought that they are almost laughable,” Alessandra Stanley wrote in The New York Times. The series, she said, “doesn’t need to overreach. It has an intriguing story, an aptly sinister setting and an excellent cast.” She added: “It’s inevitable for viewers to yearn for the kind of odyssey that series like ‘The Wire’ and ‘Breaking Bad’ provided. ‘Low Winter Sun’ isn’t that, but it’s an entertaining way station.” The fifth, and final, season premiere of “Breaking Bad” leads in at 9. “Talking Bad,” a companion show hosted by Chris Hardwick that analyzes the series’s last eight episodes, follows at 11.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-11T06:23:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/52496246-5b