influential group released results of a poll showing that drugs and integrity concerns loom larger to bettors than any other issue facing the sport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SARATOGA SPRINGS, N.Y. — The Jockey Club, horse racing’s most influential group, will pay up to $500,000 for out-of-competition drug testing over the next two years, and its chairman warned horsemen, regulators and racetracks that doping and cheating would decimate the sport’s bottom line unless complete national reform began immediately.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/12/sports/RACING/RACING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 481, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/12/sports/RACING/RACING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 481}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/12/sports/RACING/RACING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 821, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/12/sports/RACING/RACING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1391, 'width': 1735, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Concerns Over Drugs Mount, the Jockey Club Says It Will Pay for Testing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Concerns Over Drugs Mount, the Jockey Club Says It Will Pay for Testing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jockeys, Drivers and Trainers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jockey Club 