 American dream for his family of four. He could earn a living on the sweat of his brow, afford to send his children to college and even see them rise to the professional class.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wrong Lesson From Detroit’s Bankruptcy', 'kicker': 'The Great Divide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T03:44:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph E. Stiglitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Stiglitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be6669f0-5777-5522-ac2d-bed04bb902f7', 'word_count': 2056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be6669f0-5777-5522-ac2d-bed04bb902f7'}, {'abstract': 'Recent legislation in Russia has spurred an international furor and a national debate on gays in society.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/world/europe/tell-us-about-your-experiences-being-gay-in-russia.html', 'snippet': 'Recent legislation in Russia has spurred an international furor and a national debate on gays in society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Russia’s adoption of legislation that outlaws “propaganda on nontraditional sexual relationships” among minors has spurred an international furor and a national debate on gays in society. As the Times reporter David M. Herszenhorn writes, the law is widely understood as an effort to suppress homosexuality, but it has galvanized Russia’s gay rights advocates and cast an unfavorable light on the discrimination and abuse gay people must contend with in Russia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tell Us About Your Experiences Being Gay in Russia / Быть геем в России: расскажите о вашем личном опыте', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T03:48:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb959bea-c18a-57bb-9de0-bf875ee67545', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb959bea-c18a-57bb-9de0-bf875ee67545'}, {'abstract': 'Despite the breathtaking wealth and vibrant culture in its metropolises, Russia remains a country where discrimination and violence against gay people are widely tolerated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/world/europe/gays-in-russia-find-no-haven-despite-support-from-the-west.html', 'snippet': 'Despite the breathtaking wealth and vibrant culture in its metropolises, Russia remains a country where discrimination and violence against gay people are widely tolerated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — If this article were published in a newspaper based in Russia, it could be labeled 18+ — like an X-rated movie — and start with the following disclaimer: “This article contains information not suitable for readers younger than 18 years of age, according to Russian legislation.”'