who becomes a prostitute, at 2:15 a.m.; and “The Hunger” (1983), Tony Scott’s film in which a female vampire falls for a research doctor (Susan Sarandon), at 4:15.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T04:15:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4bfbebb-29ac-5d30-8529-b64810e572ab', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4bfbebb-29ac-5d30-8529-b64810e572ab'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, August 12.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-monday-august-12.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, August 12.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The era of the lawn in the West is over.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, August 12', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T04:15:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ae6a598-3d3f-5ee3-a001-a1419a1d081b', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ae6a598-3d3f-5ee3-a001-a1419a1d081b'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on August 12, 2013.