ine': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efd17a04-85c2-58f7-b36e-0a22c54eac29', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efd17a04-85c2-58f7-b36e-0a22c54eac29'}, {'abstract': 'A daughter whose mother is 94 cares for the generations before and after her, living their lives and preserving their memories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/booming/the-memory-ladys-daughter-tries-to-fill-the-gaps.html', 'snippet': 'A daughter whose mother is 94 cares for the generations before and after her, living their lives and preserving their memories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reading was my mother’s escape from the Texas farm where she grew up. As a child, she memorized poems and recited them in her school auditorium. Later, she memorized whole books and performed them for women’s clubs. She stood alone onstage in high heels and a large hat while her voice transported her listeners to another world. You couldn’t take your eyes or ears off of her. Our home was a house of books, hundreds of which she knew by memory. Now she’s 94 and her once famous memory is slipping away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/booming/13mystory-booming-memorykids/13mystory-booming-memorykids-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 317, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/13/booming/13mystory-booming-memorykids/13mystory-booming-memorykids-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 317}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/booming/13mystory-booming-memorykids/13mystory-booming-memorykids-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 541, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/booming/13mystory-booming-memorykids/13mystory-booming-memorykids-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1058, 'width': 2002, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/booming/13mystory-booming-memorykids/13mystory-booming-memorykids-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/13/booming/13mystory-booming-memorykids/13mystory-booming-memorykids-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/booming/13mystory-booming-memorykids/13mystory-booming-memorykids-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Memory Lady’s Daughter Tries to Fill the Gaps', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T11:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Beth Thompson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Beth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thompson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/831bc073-8879-5213-a5e5-a0bdf1afa7a7', 'word_count': 1382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/831bc073-8879-5213-a5e5-a0bdf1afa7a7'}, {'abstract': 'The A.C.A. will require employers with more than 50 employees to estimate their employees’ household incomes. How are they supposed to do that?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/its-the-affordable-care-act-but-what-is-affordable/', 'snippet': 'The A.C.A. will require employers with more than 50 employees to estimate their employees’ household incomes. How are they supposed to do that?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Under the Affordable Care Act, if a company with 50 employees hopes to avoid the penalty in the so-called employer mandate, it is not enough to merely offer those workers health insurance. The insurance must be “affordable,” among other things, and the law is very specific about what affordable means: It means the employee’s share of the premium cannot exceed 9.5 percent of the employee’s household income.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s the Affordable Care Act. But What Is Affordable?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aon Hewitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T11:00:37+0