f_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b4aee08-117e-5007-8bde-d27f77ba90b8', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b4aee08-117e-5007-8bde-d27f77ba90b8'}, {'abstract': 'For its final three weeks of performances, the critically praised Off Broadway play will sell $10 tickets for patrons 30 and under.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/discount-tickets-for-my-name-is-asher-lev/', 'snippet': 'For its final three weeks of performances, the critically praised Off Broadway play will sell $10 tickets for patrons 30 and under.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For its final three weeks of performances, the critically praised Off Broadway play “My Name Is Asher Lev” will be one of the cheapest tickets in town for patrons 30 and under. The producer Darren Bagert announced on Sunday that the production would sell $10 tickets to that group two hours before performances. Most Off Broadway shows sell such discounted rush tickets in the $20 to $30 range; $10 tickets for a well-reviewed Off Broadway play are rare. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/12/theater/12lev/12lev-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/12/theater/12lev/12lev-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/12/theater/12lev/12lev-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/12/theater/12lev/12lev-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None