oss. | A look at the Wall Street experiences of Lawrence H. Summers. | The...', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, Wall Street research analysts have been barred from pitching initial public offering business. But with the market for I.P.O.’s making a comeback, some analysts say Wall Street is slipping back to its old ways, Peter Lattman and Susanne Craig report in DealBook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fresh Scrutiny for Wall Street Analysts', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T12:11:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdcec151-5688-5b76-9f1a-d335bfc51351', 'word_count': 1506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdcec151-5688-5b76-9f1a-d335bfc51351'}, {'abstract': 'BlackBerry says it is exploring a potential sale of the company or a joint venture, as the faded smartphone maker continues to cast about for a solution to its troubles.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/blackberry-to-explore-strategic-alternatives-including-a-sale-again/', 'snippet': 'BlackBerry says it is exploring a potential sale of the company or a joint venture, as the faded smartphone maker continues to cast about for a solution to its troubles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 9:03 p.m. |  It is an unforgiving law of modern business: adapt or die.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Once Dominant, BlackBerry Seeks to Avoid Oblivion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'BlackBerry Sends a Message', 'name': None, 