units, the latest setback for the once-powerful hedge fund run by the billionaire Steven A. Cohen.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/sac-capital-closes-a-trading-unit/', 'snippet': 'Hobbled by a criminal indictment, SAC Capital has shuttered one of its stock trading units, the latest setback for the once-powerful hedge fund run by the billionaire Steven A. Cohen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAC Capital Advisors, once the envy of Wall Street for its investment returns, is adjusting to life as a criminal defendant.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SAC Capital Closes a Trading Unit as It Starts to Retrench', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Steven A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SAC Capital Advisors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T16:59:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess and Alexandra Stevenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6437e260-a4b1-5219-b969-a3300c5beeab', 'word_count': 934, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6437e260-a4b1-5219-b969-a3300c5beeab'}, {'abstract': 'A reader questions how effective incubators are at creating successful companies.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/assessing-the-impact-of-business-incubators/', 'snippet': 'A reader questions how effective incubators are at creating successful companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In our July 17 post about Austin’s start-up scene, we wrote that there were “at least 15” incubators and accelerators in the region. A reader in Austin questioned the effectiveness of incubators at creating successful companies in the long term. He compiled a list of the top 150 publicly traded software companies by top-line sales — his measure of success — and found that not one on his list had come out of an incubator.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Assessing the Impact of Business Incubators', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kauffman Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T17:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eilene Zimmerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eilene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6fb3448-7dde-551b-9b0a-13e14f27be41', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6fb3448-7dde-551b-9b0a-13e14f27be41'}, {'abstract': '“Sentimental Value,” an exhibition of garments purchased on eBay alongside stories the sellers shared in their listings, reveals the profound meaning we attach to our clothes.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/on-view-the-hilarious-poignant-humanity-of-ebay-auction-listings/', 'snippet': '“Sentimental Value,” an exhibition of garments purchased on eBay alongside stories the sellers shared in their listings, reveals the profound meaning we attach to our clothes.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Clothing is an overlooked way of telling stories,” said Emily Spivack, a 35-year-old curator, editor, writer and social entrepreneur. “Sentimental Value,” her Internet found-art project (on display at the Philadelphia Art Alliance through Aug. 23), is all about sartorial narratives. It gathers some 40 of the more than 60 garments she has purchased on eBay and pairs them with revealing tales the sellers shared when they listed them.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On View | The Hilarious, Poignant Humanity of eBay Auction Listings', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'View: Clothes Story', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'eBay Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T17:06:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50277f3f-0f8c-5df7-b847-5aee47a3e80b', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50277f3f-0f8c-5df7-b847-5aee47a3e80b'}, {'abstract': 'Publicis Dallas hired a new senior vice president and director for consumer insights, while TripAdvisor, Boston, snagged a new vice president for brand strategy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/business/media/accounts-and-people-of-note-in-the-advertising-industry.html', 'snippet': 'Publicis Dallas hired a new senior vice president and director for consumer insights, while TripAdvisor, Boston, snagged a new vice president for brand strategy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tyler Beck joined Publicis Dallas in a new post, senior vice president and director for consumer insights. He had most recently been executive director for strategy at Cheil USA, New York, part of Cheil Worldwide. Publicis Dallas is part of the Publicis Worldwide in the USA division of Publicis Worldwide, which is owned by the Publicis Groupe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Advertising Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T17:20:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8241238a-c149-5a80-9157-209b66a787d6', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8241238a-c149-5a80-9157-209b66a787d6'}, {'abstract': 'Who is the voice of the camel on Geico’s “Hump Day” commercial?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/business/media/q-and-a-with-stuart-elliott.html', 'snippet': 'Who is the voice of the camel on Geico’s “Hump Day” commercial?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stuart Elliott, the advertising columnist, answers questions from readers each week. Questions can be sent to stuarte@nytimes.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/05/27/business/media/stuart-elliott-headshot/stuart-elliott-headshot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 234, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo',