et': 'After holding steady through much of the 2000s, deal-making has picked up in health care, raising concerns about the power of large hospital systems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hospitals across the nation are being swept up in the biggest wave of mergers since the 1990s, a development that is creating giant hospital systems that could one day dominate American health care and drive up costs.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/business/HOSPITAL/HOSPITAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/13/business/HOSPITAL/HOSPITAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/business/HOSPITAL/HOSPITAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/business/HOSPITAL/HOSPITAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1201, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/business/HOSPITAL/HOSPITAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/13/business/HOSPITAL/HOSPITAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/business/HOSPITAL/HOSPITAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Laws and Rising Costs Create a Surge of Supersizing Hospitals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Laws and Rising Costs Create a Surge of Supersizing Hospitals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abelson, Reed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Community Health Systems Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Catholic Health East', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health Management Associates Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trinity Health (Livonia, Mich)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T18:41:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Creswell and Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Creswell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b2e2d0f-f9e6-5bdf-9792-4f09f6a0208c', 'word_count': 1057, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b2e2d0f-f9e6-5bdf-9792-4f09f6a0208c'}, {'abstract': 'Issues from Palestinian stone-throwing to a profile of Katharine Weymouth came up last week while the public editor was on vacation.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/a-roundup-of-what-happened-while-the-public-editor-was-away/', 'snippet': 'Issues from Palestinian stone-throwing to a profile of Katharine Weymouth came up last week while the public editor was on vacation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back from an intentionally unplugged vacation – where I got my news mostly through the print editions of newspapers and an occasional glance at the Twitter feed on my phone – I’m catching up with some of the issues that crossed the public editor’s desk in the past week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Roundup of What Happened While the Public Editor Was Away', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T18:42:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fe564b2-d973-5a5a-8acb-768212921f88', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fe564b2-d973-5a5a-8acb-768212921f88'}, {'abstract': 'A ring once owned by Jane Austen and bought last year by the singer Kelly Clarkson might stay in Britain after all.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/anonymous-donation-may-keep-austens-ring-in-britain/', 'snippet': 'A ring once owned by Jane Austen and bought last year by the singer Kelly Clarkson might stay in Britain after all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A gold and turquoise ring once owned by Jane Austen and purchased last year at auction by the singer Kelly Clarkson may find a permanent home in Britain after all, thanks to an anonymous donor. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anonymous Donation May Help Keep Austen’s Ring in Britain', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Jane', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T18:42:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c51883e-bf11-5fd3-a216-51d0f03dc7e5', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c51883e-bf11-5fd3-a216-51d0f03dc7e5'}, {'abstract': 'JP McCary, general manager for the Americas of Make Up For Ever, is used to questions on the products he carries. Even from airport security.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/business/the-travel-questions-raised-by-make-up.html', 'snippet': 'JP McCary, general manager for the Americas of Make Up For Ever, is used to questions on the products he carries. Even from airport security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’VE flown for the business for about the last 18 years. I’m in the beauty business and now work with Make Up For Ever. When I was with another brand, I used to oversee 23 countries, and was traveling to five or six countries a month. One time I had to go to six countries in three days. Fortunately, I don’t have to do those kinds of whirlwind trips anymore, but I’m still flying all the time.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/business/13flier-inline/13flier-inline-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/13/business/13flier-inline/13flier-inline-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/business/13flier-inline/13flier-inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/business/13flier-inline/13flier-inline-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/business/13flier-inline/13flier-inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/13/business/13flier-inline/13flier-inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/business/13flier-inline/13flier-inline-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Questions Raised by Makeup', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Questions Raised by Makeup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Make Up For Ever', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T18:46:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. P. McCary', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'McCary', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d75234e6-091d-594f-9917-845923e2c900', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d75234e6-091d-594f-9917-845923e2c900'}, {'abstract': 'On the strength of a YouTube video, the Indiana siblings who go by Lily and Madeleine have become an overnight sensation, with a debut album out this fall. The first single has its exclusive premiere here.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/listen-up-teenage-folk-singing-sisters-hit-the-big-time/', 'snippet': 'On the strength of a YouTube video, the Indiana siblings who go by Lily and Madeleine have become an overnight sensation, with a debut album out this fall. The first single has its exclusive premiere here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Indianapolis-based sister folk duo Lily and Madeleine recorded their debut EP, “Weight of the Globe” (which came out in January), entirely on the weekends. That’s because on weekdays, they were too busy with high-school homework. “It’s weird that we’re, like, business partners now,” said Madeleine Jurkiewicz, 18, the older sister. Not long ago, she and 16-year-old Lily were anonymous bedroom singers; now they’re signed to Sufjan Stevens’ Asthmatic Kitty Records, with a namesake debut album on the way (on Oct. 29). “Devil We Know,” which makes its world premiere here, is the centerpiece of the record, an appealing back-country portrait comprised of a slow-rolling piano melody, deftly plucked acoustic guitar and the teens’ tender, swirling voices.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Listen Up | Teenage Folk-Singing Sisters Hit the Big Time', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Listen Up: Sing Out, Sisters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mellencamp, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevens, Sufjan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reddit Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T18:46:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Hyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbd0d205-9d81-511d-88f2-bcdd3cfa9b60', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbd0d205-9d81-511d-88f2-bcdd3cfa9b60'}, {'abstract': 'The following is a collection of memorable quotations from the trial of James (Whitey) Bulger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/10/us/memorable-quotes-from-the-trial-of-james-whitey-bulger.html', 'snippet': 'The following is a collection of memorable quotations from the trial of James (Whitey) Bulger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The following is a collection of memorable quotations from the trial of James (Whitey) Bulger, the notorious Boston crime boss who was found guilty of gangland crimes, including murder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/us/10bulgerquotes-span/10bulgerquotes-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/10/us/10bulgerquotes-span/10bulgerquotes-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/10/us/10bulgerquotes-span/10bulgerq