wear style that is precisely executed, but disrupted with spontaneous flourishes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last spring, the 25-year-old London-based designer Yang Li debuted his first runway collection, a line of reimagined street-wear staples with a gothic influence. For someone so young, Li has accomplished quite a lot: after dropping out of Central Saint Martins, he interned for Raf Simons, and by the tender age of 23 had already caught the eye of Michèle Montagne, the in-demand French publicist and stylist who helped shape the careers of Ann Demeulemeester and Haider Ackermann. Li’s clothes are made in Italy, and finished with absolute precision — except when they aren’t. He loves an element of spontaneity, like slashing the two front pockets of a slim-cut classic bouclé jacket. “Art is not all clean lines, but has a human touch,” he said. “Same with fashion.” ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '100', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Verge | Yang Li’s Deliberately Imperfect Style', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Feeling for: Deliberately Imperfect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Demeulemeester, Ann', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simons, Raf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T20:59:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malina Joseph Gilchrist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malina', 'middlename': 'Joseph', 'lastname': 'Gilchrist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34c468c4-300d-5443-acb4-236ee81ad753', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34c468c4-300d-5443-acb4-236ee81ad753'}, {'abstract': 'Mayoral candidate Jo