 percent results is handmade and requires multiple IV doses, making it impractical for the worst-hit areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new type of malaria vaccine gave 100 percent protection against infection to a small number of volunteers in recent tests — but under conditions that would be nearly impossible to reproduce in the countries where most malaria victims live.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Malaria Vaccine Works, With Limits', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Malaria Vaccine Works, With Limits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malaria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T21:15:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/630f1a14-9cb9-583c-9520-50153005e90a', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/630f1a14-9cb9-583c-9520-50153005e90a'}, {'abstract': 'In his first television ad, “Powerful Voices,” mayoral candidate Anthony D. Weiner casts himself as an underdog hounded by the establishment and urges voters to ignore his critics.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/the-ad-campaign-weiners-powerful-voices/', 'snippet': 'In his first television ad, “Powerful Voices,” mayoral candidate Anthony D. Weiner casts himself as an underdog hounded by the establishment and urges voters to ignore his critics.', 'lead_paragraph': ' SUMMARY Once an improbable frontrunner in the Democratic primary, Anthony D. Weiner has fallen to fourth place in many polls, his campaign engulfed by fresh revelations of online liaisons with women. In his first television ad, “Powerful Voices,” Mr. Weiner speaks directly to the viewer for a full 30 seconds, casting himself as an underdog hounded by the establishment and urging voters to ignore his critics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ad Campaign: Weiner’s ‘Powerful Voices’', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T21:15:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75fc909d-31a7-5a0e-a3a5-7b8f3d42004d', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75fc909d-31a7-5a0e-a3a5-7b8f3d42004d'}, {'abstract': 'In a portrait of John F. Kennedy, Thurston Clarke argues that during Kennedy’s last few months, he finally began to realize his potential as a man and a president, with morality and emotion tempering ambition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/books/jfks-last-hundred-days-by-thurston-clarke.html', 'snippet': 'In a portrait of John F. Kennedy, Thurston Clarke argues that during Kennedy’s last few months, he finally began to realize his potential as a man and a president, with morality and emotion tempering ambition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the 50th anniversary this November of the assassination of John F. Kennedy looms on the horizon, the debates over his legacy and presidency continue: a procession of “what ifs” and “might have beens,” accompanied by contradictory arguments, and informed and not-so-informed speculation. Would Kennedy have avoided Lyndon B. Johnson’s tragic escalation of the war in Vietnam? Would he have found a way to propel his stalled tax-cut bill and civil rights legislation through Congress and start a war on poverty, or was Johnson able to achieve these historic goals only through a combination of his bare-knuckled, tactical knowledge of Congress; his personal relationships on Capitol Hill; and his ability to use the momentum of sentiment generated by Kennedy’s death?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/arts/book/book-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 924, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/13/arts/book/book-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 924}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 665, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/arts/book/book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1330, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/13/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailhe