-called Hyperloop and the shutdown of a controversial London plan to track residents through their recycling.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/12/todays-scuttlebot-hullabaloo-over-the-hyperloop/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for interesting and peculiar items. Monday’s selections include early speculation on the so-called Hyperloop and the shutdown of a controversial London plan to track residents through their recycling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day, The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for interesting and peculiar items. On Monday, much of the Internet and Twitterverse was aflutter in anticipation of an announcement by Elon Musk, a co-founder of PayPal and chairman of Tesla Motors, about the so-called Hyperloop, an alternative to high-speed rail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Hullabaloo Over the ‘Hyperloop’', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-12T22:56:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_