, 'snippet': 'Milos Raonic addressed his decision not to confess that his foot had touched the net in a match.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MASON, Ohio — Milos Raonic came into the Cincinnati Masters having just made the finals in Montreal and become the first Canadian in the top ten. So it would have been easy for Raonic to focus only on his current highs. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Raonic Has Second Thoughts on a Montreal Net Controversy', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rogers Cup (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'del Potro, Juan Martin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raonic, Milos', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T01:22:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/141118e7-723e-5fde-a599-45a9f8b975b8', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/141118e7-723e-5fde-a599-45a9f8b975b8'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama should sign an executive order to raise the pay of millions of poorly paid employees of government contractors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/opinion/the-government-as-a-low-wage-employer.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama should sign an executive order to raise the pay of millions of poorly paid employees of government contractors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1965, in a nation torn by racial strife, President Johnson signed an executive order mandating nondiscrimination in employment by government contractors. Now, as President Obama has observed, the nation is divided by  a different threat: widening income inequality. He could respond much as Mr. Johnson did — with an executive order aimed, this time, at raising the pay of millions of poorly paid employees of government contractors. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Government as a Low-Wage Employer', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Government as a Low-Wage Employer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Procurement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T01:25:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c0541e7-4e73-5132-a704-b01911f48193', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c0541e7-4e73-5132-a704-b01911f48193'}, {'abstract': 'Giving the green light to new settlement construction days before scheduled peace talks with the Palestinians is not a sign of being committed to the negotiations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/opinion/shortsighted-thinking-on-israeli-settlements.html', 'snippet': 'Giving the green light to new settlement construction days before scheduled peace talks with the Palestinians is not a sign of being committed to the negotiations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a certain internal political logic to two announcements made by the Israeli government, just days before Wednesday’s scheduled resumption of peace talks with the Palestinians. Early Monday, the government released a list of 26 Palestinian prisoners to be released Tuesday, most serving sentences for murder and other violent crimes. A few hours before that, the government published bids for the construction of more than 1,000 new housing units in East Jerusalem and existing West Bank settlements — a move apparently designed to mollify right-wingers who would oppose the prisoner release. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shortsighted Thinking on Israeli Settlements', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shortsighted Thinking on Israeli Settlements', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T01:25:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5429fa4b-587e-5863-9ad8-d2cb57ff4fb4', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5429fa4b-587e-5863-9ad8-d2cb57ff4fb4'}, {'abstract': 'A federal court rejects unconstitutional overreach by the Bloomberg administration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/opinion/racial-discrimination-in-stop-and-frisk.html', 'snippet': 'A federal court rejects unconstitutional overreach by the Bloomberg administration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Judge Shira Scheindlin of Federal District Court in New York upheld the bedrock principle of individual liberty on Monday when she ruled that the tactics underlying New York City’s stop-and-frisk program violated the constitutional rights of minority citizens. She found that the city had been “deliberately indifferent” to police officers illegally detaining and frisking minority residents on the streets over many years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Racial Discrimination in Stop-and-Frisk', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Racial Discrimination in Stop-and-Frisk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scheindlin, Shira A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T01:25:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/073dc3fe-5411-52ba-90ed-355cc27edba4', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/073dc3fe-5411-52ba-90ed-355cc27edba4'}, {'abstract': 'Clint Dempsey, the United States national team captain, will try to raise his level of play and that of Major League So