 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T08:16:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a24b898-ae19-53fb-a23a-eda6d145c0a9', 'word_count': 41, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a24b898-ae19-53fb-a23a-eda6d145c0a9'}, {'abstract': 'What are the arguments people make for and against the policy? How do you feel about the judge’s decision?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/6-qs-about-the-news-citys-stop-and-frisk-practice-violated-rights-judge-finds/', 'snippet': 'What are the arguments people make for and against the policy? How do you feel about the judge’s decision?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the article “Stop-and-Frisk Practice Violated Rights, Judge Rules,” Joseph Goldstein writes about Monday’s ruling about New York City’s stop-and-frisk policy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '6 Q’s About the News | New York’s Stop-and-Frisk Practice Violated Rights, Judge Finds', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T08:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dda84d72-3600-5217-ad25-23a329a595bb', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dda84d72-3600-5217-ad25-23a329a595bb'}, {'abstract': 'Or is it just good economics?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/magazine/is-it-nuts-to-give-to-the-poor-without-strings-attached.html', 'snippet': 'Or is it just good economics?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bernard Omondi lives in a small Kenyan village in a rural district called Siaya that sits right on the Equator and is almost impossible to get to. He has spent years working on and off as a day laborer, moving stones on construction sites, and commuting long distances over rough dirt roads. When he could find work, he made about $2 a day. When he couldn’t, his two sons sometimes went hungry. Then one morning last year, Omondi woke up to an unusual text message. “When I saw the message, I jumped up,” he recalled. “My wife said, ‘Bernard, what is it?’ ” He told her he had just been given $500 with no strings attached. “ It’s here! ” he said.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/magazine/18economy/mag-18Economy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/18/magazine/18economy/mag-18Economy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/magazine/18economy/mag-18Economy-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/magazine/18economy/mag-18Economy-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1396, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/magazine/18economy/mag-18Economy-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name':