 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poitras, Laura', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenwald, Glenn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guardian (British Newspaper)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T09:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Peter Maass', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Peter', 'lastname': 'Maass', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2563f6bc-436c-5e9f-a429-487854898fe6', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2563f6bc-436c-5e9f-a429-487854898fe6'}, {'abstract': 'Every Saturday for nearly eight years, Che’ Ahmad Azhar has ambled three streets in his native Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, photographing and identifying with their residents.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/a-street-level-view-of-kuala-lumpur/', 'snippet': 'Every Saturday for nearly eight years, Che’ Ahmad Azhar has ambled three streets in his native Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, photographing and identifying with their residents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Che’ Ahmad Azhar sits so quietly in the corner of a room, you might not notice him. But take him to the lively streets of Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, and he becomes a maestro, conducting a symphony of noise, action, light and shadow in the best tradition of street photography.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Street-Level View of Kuala Lumpur', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kuala Lumpur (Malaysia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T09:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maggie Steber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maggie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90663afe-d2d3-5b6d-acf2-af5ff7ad55f6', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90663afe-d2d3-5b6d-acf2-af5ff7ad55f6'}, {'abstract': 'A leading official at the United States Commission on International Religious Freedom talks about their insistence on keeping Narendra Modi, chief minister of Gujarat State, off American soil.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/a-conversation-with-u-s-c-i-r-f-vice-chairwoman-katrina-lantos-swett/', 'snippet': 'A leading official at the United States Commission on International Religious Freedom talks about their insistence on keeping Narendra Modi, chief minister of Gujarat State, off American soil.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few Indian politicians evoke dislike and admiration as intense as that inspired by Narendra Modi, the chief minister of the western state of Gujarat. Mr. Modi is the de facto prime ministerial candidate for India’s leading opposition party, the Bharatiya Janata Party, in the 2014 parliamentary elections. Mr. Modi has been remodeling himself as a pro-business, pro-development leader who can bring about economic growth and make difficult decisions. Yet the ghosts of the 2002 sectarian violence, in which more than\xa0 1,000 Muslims were killed and tens of thousands displaced from their homes under his watch in Gujarat, along with his continuing use of derogatory language to refer to India’s Muslims, has raised concerns about his political rise. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/world/asia/13-katrina-swett-IndiaInk/13-katrina-swett-IndiaInk-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 556, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/13/world/asia/13-katrina-swett-IndiaInk/13-katrina-swett-IndiaInk-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 556}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/world/asia/13-katrina-swett-IndiaInk/13-katrina-swett-IndiaInk-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 949, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/world/asia/13-katrina-swett-IndiaInk/13-katrina-swett-IndiaInk-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1899, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/world/asia/13-katrina-swett-IndiaInk/13-katrina-swett-IndiaInk-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/13/world/asia/13-katrina-swett-IndiaInk/13-katrina-swett-IndiaInk-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/world/asia/13-katrina-swett-IndiaInk/13-katrina-swett-IndiaInk-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With Katrina Lantos Swett, on Religious Freedom in India', 'kic