ebcc26c'}, {'abstract': 'My previous practice had been to hand out bonuses when I felt “rich and happy.” But that seemed arbitrary.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/my-search-for-a-smart-way-to-share-profits/', 'snippet': 'My previous practice had been to hand out bonuses when I felt “rich and happy.” But that seemed arbitrary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I explained last week, I recently decided to use profit-sharing to reward my people for changing our ways on the shop floor. Once I came to that conclusion, I started looking at a variety of approaches.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Search for a Smart Way to Share Profits', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paul Downs Cabinetmakers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vistage International Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T11:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62afb40f-c0bf-5f50-881a-5a5b66c6c1dd', 'word_count': 1261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62afb40f-c0bf-5f50-881a-5a5b66c6c1dd'}, {'abstract': 'Consumer prices rose by 2.8 percent in July after hitting a 14-month high in June of 2.9 percent, a government office reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/business/global/rise-of-inflation-eases-in-britain.html', 'snippet': 'Consumer prices rose by 2.8 percent in July after hitting a 14-month high in June of 2.9 percent, a government office reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Consumer prices in Britain increased at a slower rate in July after hitting a 14-month high in June, relieving some pressure on households but remaining well above the central bank’s inflation target.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rise of Inflation Eases in Britain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of England', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carney, Mark J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T11:05:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2022ff0-b841-5bf6-a2d9-3e75c71408b1', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2022ff0-b841-5bf6-a2d9-3e75c71408b1'}, {'abstract': 'Kenneth Bae, a Christian tour operator accused of hostile acts against the North, made the request in a video, but it was unclear if he was speaking of his own free will.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/world/asia/american-inmate-in-north-korea-asks-for-high-level-us-visit.html', 'snippet': 'Kenneth Bae, a Christian tour operator accused of hostile acts against the North, made the request in a video, but it was unclear if he was speaking of his own free will.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — An American tour operator imprisoned in North Korea on charges of plotting to harm the socialist country through Christian missionary activities has appealed to Washington to send a high-ranking official to North Korea to help free him, according to a videotaped interview made public on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/world/KOREA/KOREA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 847, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/14/world/KOREA/KOREA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 847}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/world/KOREA/KOREA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 726, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/world/KOREA/KOREA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1090, 'width': 772, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/world/KOREA/KOREA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/14/world/KOREA/KOREA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/world/KOREA/KOREA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop