ype': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/13/opinion/global/13-iht-heng/13-iht-heng-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/opinion/global/13-iht-heng/13-iht-heng-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/opinion/global/13-iht-heng/13-iht-heng-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1462, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/opinion/global/13-iht-heng/13-iht-heng-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/13/opinion/global/13-iht-heng/13-iht-heng-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/opinion/global/13-iht-heng/13-iht-heng-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Obama Foreign Policy Show', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T11:20:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Global Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b055811d-8184-50a7-87c1-7e81e0a62994', 'word_count': 11, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b055811d-8184-50a7-87c1-7e81e0a62994'}, {'abstract': 'William A. Ackman steps down from the J.C. Penney board. | The question of who should foot the legal bill in white-collar cases has become an increasingly common one. | Six years after the peak of the housing boom, subprime borrowers continue to struggle. | It is not clear that anyone will want to buy BlackBerry.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/morning-agenda-ackman-parts-ways-with-penneys-directors/', 'snippet': 'William A. Ackman steps down from the J.C. Penney board. | The question of who should foot the legal bill in white-collar cases has become an increasingly common one. | Six years after the peak of the housing boom, subprime borrowers continue to s...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hedge fund manager William A. Ackman has stepped down from the board of J.C. Penney, after a public clash with his fellow directors, the company announced on Tuesday morning. In its statement, Penney said that it had added Ronald W. Tysoe, a former vice chairman of Federated Department Stores, to its board, and said it planned to add another director in the near future.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ackman and Penney Directors Part Ways', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T11:54:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39dc52be-d6a2-50ba-b172-d87a399da200', 'word_count': 1571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39dc52be-d6a2-50ba-b172-d87a399da200'}, {'abstract': 'The actors perform the number “First Impressions” from the new Broadway musical at the Longacre Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/in-performance-zachary-levi-and-krysta-rodriguez-of-first-date/', 'snippet': 'The actors perform the number “First Impressions” from the new Broadway musical at the Longacre Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the new Broadway musical “First Date,” Zachary Levi plays Aaron, an awkward but cute finance guy who is set up on a blind date with Casey, a pretty, dark-edged art chick played by Krysta Rodriguez. In the number “First Impressions,” they size each other up right after meeting. “First Date,” written by Austin Winsberg (book) and Alan Zachary and Michael Weiner (music and lyrics), is at the Longacre Theater. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Zachary Levi and Krysta Rodriguez of ‘First Date’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levi, Zachary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Krysta', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T12:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e4a4d15-dd4b-5ba7-af8e-0d0a728b342a', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e4a4d15-dd4b-5ba7-af8e-0d0a728b342a'}, {'abstract': 'Google lends me a hand.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/what-people-dont-know-about-the-deficit/', 'snippet': 'Google lends me a hand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A little while back I expressed a desire to see a poll of voters asking whether they knew about the plunging federal budget deficit. Just as a reminder, here’s what the CBO numbers for the recent past and projections for the near future look like:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What People (Don’t) Know About The Deficit', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T12:06:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/361c1b8a-0ea6-5bfe-b659-c14131cbca21', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/361c1b8a-0ea6-5bfe-b659-c14131cbca21'}, {'abstract': 'Who has rights to a dead economist’s legacy?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/wish-id-said-that-rand-paul-edition/', 'snippet': 'Who has rights to a dead economist’s legacy?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matt O’Brien follows up on Rand Paul and Milton Friedman, and finds the senator trying– in the face of all the facts — to claim that Friedman would have supported his monetary views. Again, Paul is a self-proclaimed Austrian, and Friedman was contemptuous of the Austrians:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wish I’d Said That, Rand Paul Edition', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T12:24:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c38575c5-1ddc-5eeb-8e25-08a1f84651fd', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c38575c5-1ddc-5eeb-8e25-08a1f84651fd'}, {'abstract': 'Israel shouldn’t submit to the E.U.’s restrictions on cooperating with entities operating beyond the 1967 line.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/the-price-of-settling/', 'snippet': 'Israel shouldn’t submit to the E.U.’s restrictions on cooperating with entities operating beyond the 1967 line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — The European Union adopted guidelines in June that bar Israeli entities from grants, prizes or loans if they operate in the areas of the West Bank, East Jerusalem and the Golan Heights that Israel occupied in 1967. Naturally, the Israeli government is not pleased — so much so that on Friday it decided not to sign any new deals with the E.U. until the E.U. “clarifies” the new regulations (read: alters them). The government said it was “ready to negotiate” with the Europeans, but that “if the terms are the way they are today” then “we won’t be able to do it.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Price of Settling', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barnea, Nahum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Galon, Zehava', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hebrew University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yediot Aharonot', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Jerusalem', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank':