e, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/arts/arts3/arts3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1336, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/arts/arts3/arts3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/14/arts/arts3/arts3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/arts/arts3/arts3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lady Gaga Releases a New Song After It Leaks Online', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Song From Lady Gaga', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T16:29:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7113f6ba-e617-5e57-a355-090bbe54e1bc', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7113f6ba-e617-5e57-a355-090bbe54e1bc'}, {'abstract': 'Despite the 5,000 miles separating Gettysburg and Honolulu, the island kingdom played a surprising role in the conflict.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/the-civil-war-and-hawaii/', 'snippet': 'Despite the 5,000 miles separating Gettysburg and Honolulu, the island kingdom played a surprising role in the conflict.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost 5,000 miles and half an ocean away from the killing fields of Gettysburg, Chickamauga, or Spotsylvania, Hawaii and Hawaiians might be assumed to have not played a role in the Civil War. Yet regardless of proud protestations of neutrality by the Hawaiian monarchy – the islands were not American territory at the time – many of the islands’ residents participated in the conflict, on both sides. And for good reason: though they lived on one of the most geographically isolated island chains in the world, Hawaiians kept abreast of international events, knowing that the outcome of the war could greatly affect Hawaii as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Civil War and Hawaii', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sugar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T16:30:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Allen Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': 'Allen', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b524a00-0a9f-51de-94bb-f4a33b68245e', 'word_count': 1332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b524a00-0a9f-51de-94bb-f4a33b68245e'}, {'abstract': 'In “Mother Daughter Me,” Katie Hafner tells a sad story of good intentions gone awry.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/discord-in-an-intergenerational-home/', 'snippet': 'In “Mother Daughter Me,” Katie Hafner tells a sad story of good intentions gone awry.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Mother Daughter Me,” Katie Hafner’s new memoir about her attempt to form a multigenerational household, reminds me of those horror movies where the heroine (it’s always a heroine) is about to plunge heedlessly into a darkened basement/attic/forest instead of sensibly dialing 911. You want to yell, “Nooooo!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/health/hafnerbook190/hafnerbook190-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 422, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/health/hafnerbook190/hafnerbook190-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 422, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/health/hafnerbook190/hafnerbook190-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/13/health/hafnerbook190/hafnerbook190-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/13/health/hafnerbook190/hafnerbook190-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Discord in an Intergenerational Home', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'ran