, {'abstract': 'Manuscripts, sketches and ephemera of Robert E. Howard, the creator of Conan, have been purchased by the Harry Ransom Center at the University of Texas Austin.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/conan-the-barbarian-rampages-into-prestigious-archive/', 'snippet': 'Manuscripts, sketches and ephemera of Robert E. Howard, the creator of Conan, have been purchased by the Harry Ransom Center at the University of Texas Austin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Conan the Barbarian, the pulp fiction action hero introduced in 1932 by Robert E. Howard, will soon be rubbing shoulders with the spindlier literary characters of David Foster Wallace, Don DeLillo and Norman Mailer, thanks to the recent acquisition of a large Howard collection by the Harry Ransom Center at the University of Texas at Austin. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/12/arts/12ransom/12ransom-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/12/arts/12ransom/12ransom-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 452}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/12/arts/12ransom/12ransom-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/12/arts/12ransom/12ransom-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1542, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/12/arts/12ransom/12ransom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy'