': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b185afa7-e675-5f47-927d-994296347d65', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b185afa7-e675-5f47-927d-994296347d65'}, {'abstract': '“The Circle” features a woman who works for “the world’s most powerful Internet company.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/new-novel-by-dave-eggers-due-in-october/', 'snippet': '“The Circle” features a woman who works for “the world’s most powerful Internet company.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dave Eggers is perfecting the art of sneaking onto bookshelves. His new novel, “The Circle,” will be published in October, according to the Web site of his publisher Alfred A. Knopf. Like his last book, “A Hologram for the King,” which was published less than a month after its existence was announced, “The Circle” will appear without much lead time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/books/14thecircle/14thecircle-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 210, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/books/14thecircle/14thecircle-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 210, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/books/14thecircle/14thecircle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/14/books/14thecircle/14thecircle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/books/14thecircle/14thecircle-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Novel by Dave Eggers Due in October', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eggers, Dave', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knopf, Alfred A, Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T18:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42f6db20-54f5-51c4-971b-f87c7c7f7f62', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42f6db20-54f5-51c4-971b-f87c7c7f7f62'}, {'abstract': 'The mother of an uninsured 24-year-old, Manny Lanza, who died in 2005 while awaiting surgery speaks emotionally about how through the legislative work of Christine C. Quinn, “Manny didn’t die in vain.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/the-ad-campaign-quinn-supporters-testimonial-of-her-effectiveness/', 'snippet': 'The mother of an uninsured 24-year-old, Manny Lanza, who died in 2005 while awaiting surgery speaks emotionally about how through the legislative work of Christine C. Quinn, “Manny didn’t die in vain.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'First aired: August 13, 2013 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ad Campaign: Quinn Supporter’s Testimonial of Her Effectiveness', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Ad Campaign: A Quinn Supporter Testifies to Her Effectiveness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NEW YORK CITY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T18:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/282f71cc-698c-5393-83f0-9709224c65a2', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/282f71cc-698c-5393-83f0-9709224c65a2'}, {'abstract': 'The world’s first famous biracial model, the subject of a new biography, graced the cover of French Vogue and served in the Italian resistance during World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/close-read-toto-koopman-model-spy/', 'snippet': 'The world’s first famous biracial model, the subject of a new biography, graced the cover of French Vogue and served in the Italian resistance during World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All but forgotten today, in her time Toto Koopman shocked the world. As the first famous biracial model (she was half-Javanese, half-Dutch), Koopman posed for Chanel in Paris and appeared on the cover of French Vogue in the 1930s. She was fluent in six languages, which served her well when she later became a spy for the Italian resistance during World War II — until she was thrown in a Nazi concentration camp. In his new biography, “The Many Lives of Miss K.,” Jean-Noël Liaut likens the secretive Koopman to “a squid hiding behind its cloud of ink.” Though she was never monogamous — she took lovers into her 70s, including the actress Tallulah Bankhead, Winston Churchill‘s son Randolph and the press baron Lord Beaverbrook — she devoted the second half of her life to Erica Brausen, the visionary art dealer, who, with Koopman’s help, launched Francis Bacon’s career from her Hanover Gallery in London. The couple never concealed their relationship, even though homosexuality was a criminal offense in Britain at the time. “Being around them,” a friend recalled, “I really came to understand the meaning of freedom.” ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '102', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toto Koopman, Model Spy', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Close Read: The Model Spy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'French Vogue', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T18:04:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efd431b8-3124-5c08-a08f-86d81f1c9390', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efd431b8-3124-5c08-a08f-86d81f1c9390'}, {'abstract': 'The Capture Pro is a refined version of a crowdfunded device for attaching a camera to any belt or strap.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/technology/personaltech/capture-a-camera-strap-attachment-gets-an-update.html', 'snippet': 'The Capture Pro is a refined version of a crowdfunded device for attaching a camera to any belt or strap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Capture, a device from Peak Design that attaches a camera to any belt or strap, has become a bit smarter. A refined version, called the Capture Pro, is now being shipped to some Kickstarter investors, and will be available to the public in September.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/15/technology/personaltech/15capture-span/15capture-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/15/technology/personaltech/15capture-span/15capture-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/15/technology/personaltech/15capture-span/15capture-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/15/technology/personaltech/15capture-span/15capture-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/15/technology/personaltech/15capture-span/15capture-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/15/technology/personaltech/15capture-span/15capture-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/15/technology/personaltech/15capture-span/15capture-spa