yt://article/76e59654-b35b-500e-be26-75c1a50a4151'}, {'abstract': 'This month’s recipe from Kevin West’s cookbook “Saving the Season” features a vibrant jam with lime to bring back the sweet-tart balance of the berries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/dining/getting-started-with-blueberry-jam.html', 'snippet': 'This month’s recipe from Kevin West’s cookbook “Saving the Season” features a vibrant jam with lime to bring back the sweet-tart balance of the berries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recipe Lab, a monthly feature, invites you to cook with the Dining section. We’ll publish a standout recipe from a cookbook for you to try; the next week, the book’s author will join Julia Moskin and readers in a live video chat.  If you’re interested in participating in the chat, please fill out this form. You can watch this month’s chat on Wednesday, Aug. 21, at 2 p.m. Eastern time, at nytimes.com/dining.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Started With Blueberry Jam', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Getting Started With Jam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moskin, Julia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jams and Jellies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Canning and Preserving', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blueberries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Saving the Season (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Kevin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T18:42:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/675c984c-38c9-5e07-8a73-8b5898d318fc', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/675c984c-38c9-5e07-8a73-8b5898d318fc'}, {'abstract': 'In-home family child-care providers often make it possible for minimum-wage parents to go to work, but don’t always make minimum wage themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/13/subsidized-child-care-for-the-poor-by-the-poor/', 'snippet': 'In-home family child-care providers often make it possible for minimum-wage parents to go to work, but don’t always make minimum wage themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a parent with a minimum-wage job in retail or fast food, finding a really good in-home child-care provider is like choosing the Auntie or Gramma of your dreams: loving, secure and available for emergencies. Find the right woman (and it is almost invariably a woman) and she’s got your back. If Dunkin’ Donuts calls with a shift change, or the painful tooth you couldn’t afford to have the dentist treat turns into a trip to the E.R., you have one less thing to worry about.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Subsidized Child Care: For the Poor, By the Poor', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-13T18:48:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'