mise of Communism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/books/in-times-of-fading-light-spans-generations-in-germany.html', 'snippet': 'Eugen Ruge’s “In Times of Fading Light” is a multigenerational saga of East Germans before and after the demise of Communism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Suffused with the odors of coal fire and hot bockwurst; resonant with the clanks of Lada and Trabant automobiles; replete with references to Trotsky, Gorbachev, Erich Honecker, Sputnik and the gulag, Eugen Ruge’s “In Times of Fading Light” might sound like an edifying but ultimately dour Eastern Bloc affair. Yet one of the most remarkable things about this multigenerational saga of an East German family before and after the demise of Communism is how contemporary and, well, Western it seems. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/arts/jpbook/jpbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/14/arts/jpbook/jpbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 733}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/arts/jpbook/jpbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 839, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/arts/jpbook/jpbook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1311, 'width': 1073, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/14/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thum