030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a9a0b86-c734-56b0-9cd4-ed8adf4a24ef'}, {'abstract': 'The end of the era of Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg has been greeted with consternation in any number of New York’s professional subcultures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/nyregion/seeking-a-mayor-friendly-to-films.html', 'snippet': 'The end of the era of Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg has been greeted with consternation in any number of New York’s professional subcultures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The end of the era of Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg has been greeted with consternation in any number of New York’s professional subcultures, including the real estate and banking industries and the rarefied sphere of art museums and cultural groups.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking a Mayor Friendly to Films', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeking a Mayor\r\nFriendly to Films', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldwin, Alec', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-14T02:53:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b9c0163-31b3-57c0-8d35-1ad56f722d0a', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b9c0163-31b3-57c0-8d35-1ad56f722d0a'}, {'abstract': 'Two college friends of Dzhokhar Tsarnaev pleaded not guilty in federal court Tuesday to charges that they hindered the investigation into the bombings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/us/massachusetts-two-plead-not-guilty-to-aiding-marathon-bomb-defendant.html', 'snippet': 'Two college friends of Dzhokhar Tsarnaev pleaded not guilty in federal court Tuesday to charges that they hindered the investigation into the bombings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two college friends of Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, the 20-year-old accused of working with his brother to place two bombs at the Boston Marathon, pleaded not guilty in federal court Tuesday to charges that they hindered the investigation into the bombings. The two men, Dias Kadyrbayev and Azamat Tazhayakov, both 19, each face a count of obstructing justice and conspiracy to obstruct justice, which carry maximum penalties of 20 years and 5 years in prison, respectively. Prosecutors say the two removed items including a laptop and a backpack containing fireworks from Mr. Tsarnaev’s dormitory and that Mr. Kadyrbayev later put the backpack in trash outside the New Bedford, Mass., apartment the two shared. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Two Plead Not Guilty to Aiding Marathon Bomb Defendant', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Two Plead Not Guilty To Aiding Marathon Bomb Defendant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Dzhokhar A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kadyrbayev, Dias', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tazhayakov, Azamat', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-14T02:53:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/438ee399-24b6-5ada-aa50-c2c8fe3540c5', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/438ee399-24b6-5ada-aa50-c2c8fe3540c5'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Quinn is known for a brash style that can often abrade, and her sidestepping of intimate settings like those at forums can be strategic, political analysts say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/nyregion/quinn-is-chided-for-missing-forum.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Quinn is known for a brash style that can often abrade, and her sidestepping of intimate settings like those at forums can be strategic, political analysts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On stage at a mayoral forum in Harlem on Tuesday, the moderator strode along a line of cushy Ultrasuede chairs, stopping at each with a pointed question: What percentage of government contracts should be reserved for businesses owned by members of minority groups and women?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/nyregion/quinn-img/quinn-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/14/nyregion/quinn-img/quinn-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 40