 was the clearest sign yet that the old Egyptian police state was re-emerging in full force.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/world/middleeast/egypt.html', 'snippet': 'The scale and brutality of the attack on supporters of the ousted president, Mohamed Morsi, was the clearest sign yet that the old Egyptian police state was re-emerging in full force.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Egyptian security officers stormed two encampments packed with supporters of the ousted president, Mohamed Morsi, on Wednesday in a scorched-earth assault that killed hundreds, set off a violent backlash across Egypt and underscored the new government’s determination to crush the Islamists who dominated two years of free elections.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hundreds Die as Egyptian Forces Attack Islamist Protesters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hundreds of Egyptians Killed In Government Raids; Emergency Declared As Sectarian Violence Spreads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkpatrick, David D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sisi, Abdul-Fattah el-', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ElBaradei, Mohamed', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-14T06:30:10+0000', 'documen