er siege back home? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking the Stands', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organizations, Societies and Clubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slogans and Mottoes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Everywhere LLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galatasaray (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taksim Square (Istanbul, Turkey)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-14T13:45:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Finkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ac94251-b7fa-5c78-bcf9-b56cb83e0511', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ac94251-b7fa-5c78-bcf9-b56cb83e0511'}, {'abstract': 'At a news conference announcing the arrest of two former traders at JPMorgan Chase, the authorities also criticized the bank’s oversight of the London office where they worked.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/government-charges-two-former-jpmorgan-employees/', 'snippet': 'At a news conference announcing the arr