is fall, the center said as it released its schedule of events for the upcoming season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new series of recitals by rising opera stars will be among the leading attractions in the 2013-2014 season at Pace University’s Michael Schimmel Center for the Arts, the center in lower Manhattan has announced.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pace Arts Center’s Upcoming Season Will Feature New Opera Series', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pace University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-14T18:47:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba2e800d-fd31-5d3e-be1e-8d3b2f0b038e', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba2e800d-fd31-5d3e-be1e-8d3b2f0b038e'}, {'abstract': 'The fashion photography duo teamed with the cult jewelry brand on a new collection that’s all about affection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/perfect-pairing-jewelry-forged-by-love-from-tenthousandthings-and-inez-van-lamsweerde-and-vinoodh-matadin/', 'snippet': 'The fashion photography duo teamed with the cult jewelry brand on a new collection that’s all about affection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This fall, the fashion photography duo Inez van Lamsweerde and Vinoodh Matadin are turning their creative efforts to a collaboration with TenThousandThings, the cult jewelry brand known for its organic-looking designs. Based on a design that Matadin commissioned for van Lamsweerde last year — a chain strung with a pair of intertwined rings and a tiny star, symbolizing the couple’s love for each other and their 10-year-old son — the collection features rings, bangles and necklaces.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '104', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jewelry Forged by Love, From TenThousandThings and Inez van Lamsweerde and Vinoodh Matadin', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Perfect Pairing: A Labor of Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-14T19:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malina Joseph Gilchrist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malina', 'middlename': 'Joseph', 'lastname': 'Gilchrist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d60b5eaa-412b-5835-ae68-821cd183fd9b', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d60b5eaa-412b-5835-ae68-821cd183fd9b'}, {'abstract': 'The violence in Egypt has underscored how the Arab Spring revolutions have devolved into bitter political power struggles among competing groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/world/middleeast/egypt-bloodshed-may-be-ill-omen-for-broader-region.html', 'snippet': 'The violence in Egypt has underscored how the Arab Spring revolutions have devolved into bitter political power struggles among competing groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — In Libya, armed militias have filled a void left by a revolution that felled a dictator. In Syria, a popular uprising has morphed into a civil war that has left more than 100,000 dead and provided a haven for Islamic extremists. In Tunisia, increasingly bitter political divisions have delayed the drafting of a new constitution.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xla