 conference in Austin, Tex. Suddenly, Mr. Smith knew that Emma had to re-think its platform and its products.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Do You Do When What You Have Been Doing No Longer Works?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Clint', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nashville (Tenn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-14T20:04:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': "By You're the Boss Editors", 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdcbe7e5-1c33-5adc-abd2-d00da45d47ae', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdcbe7e5-1c33-5adc-abd2-d00da45d47ae'}, {'abstract': 'We apologize for the temporary lack of diatribes.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/lost-in-cyberspace/', 'snippet': 'We apologize for the temporary lack of diatribes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In case you’ve been wondering, Chinese Viagra salesmen gremlins have apparently attacked the New York Times. Blog access went down first, so my attempts to post this morning failed; the regular paper is now back up, but so far we can’t do images, which makes posts that included charts not worth doing for the moment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lost In Cyberspace', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'k