aid it could no longer endure the safety risks and would shut down all operations in the country after 22 years of working there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — One of the world’s most tenacious humanitarian groups said Wednesday that it could no longer endure the risks that come with operating in Somalia, in a move that underscored the continued violence in the country despite recent steps toward stability.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/15/world/somalia/somalia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/15/world/somalia/somalia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/15/world/somalia/somalia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/15/world/somalia/somalia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/15/world/somalia/somalia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/15/world/somalia/somalia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/15/world/somalia/somalia-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Doctors Without Borders to Pull Out of Somalia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Citing Risks, Aid Group Says It Will Pull Out of Somalia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kulish, Nicholas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Doctors Without Borders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-14T20:07:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ddc157b-88f8-5c24-b505-6280e56c1df4', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ddc157b-88f8-5c24-b505-6280e56c1df4'}, {'abstract': 'Unable to admit having been wrong.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/hawks-doves-and-ostriches/', 'snippet': 'Unable to admit having been wrong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than four years ago Allan Meltzer issued a dire prediction: the Fed’s policy of expanding its balance sheet will lead to high inflation. We’re still waiting for that to happen. So it might behoove Meltzer to admit that he was wrong and ask where his analysis went wrong.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawks, Doves, and Ostriches', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-14T20:10:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfa7e63c-a67e-5721-9744-b5888e9d5c50', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfa7e63c-a67e-5721-9744-b5888e9d5c50'}, {'abstract': 'A little sympathy for those who were wrong.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/the-great-recession-test/', 'snippet': 'A little sympathy for those who were wrong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A postscript to my Meltzer post: I actually feel some human sympathy for Meltzer (though not too much). After all, put yourself in his position: you’ve literally spent decades promoting yourself as an authority on monetary policy, co-founding the Shadow Open Market Committee to critique the Fed. And now comes your moment of glory. This time the Fed has really done it, adopting a policy you consider wildly irresponsible and inflationary. So you deliver your dire warnings of the doom ahead, and wait for vindication.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Great Recession Test', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-14T20:15:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f082973-93ff-5352-8a1c-6ceac4f57fc8', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f082973-93ff-5352-8a1c-6ceac4f57fc8'}, {'abstract': 'Josh Harris, the principal owner of the Philadelphia 76ers, is expected to 