humbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/14/world/middleeast/20130815-EGYPT-slide-I5X6/20130815-EGYPT-slide-I5X6-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bloody Crackdown in Egypt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-14T22:05:32+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/30fa5412-56b3-5b43-9e14-225521fd881f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/30fa5412-56b3-5b43-9e14-225521fd881f'}, {'abstract': 'The French chef Anne-Sophie Pic’s new collection of recipes features dishes that are meant to inspire more than instruct, like scallops topped with rose petals and crab topped with tea foam.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/food-matters-the-cookbook-not-meant-for-home-cooks/', 'snippet': 'The French chef Anne-Sophie Pic’s new collection of recipes features dishes that are meant to inspire more than instruct, like scallops topped with rose petals and crab topped with tea foam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Only the fourth woman in history to be awarded three Michelin stars, Anne-Sophie Pic is routinely described as the best female chef in the world. That her culinary achievements are often qualified by gender might irk another chef, but the 44-year-old embraces the softer side of cooking. At La Dame de Pic, her year-old restaurant in Paris, the dishes are light and delicate, and each menu comes with a perfume strip to evoke the various flavors of the meal. In her new cookbook, ‘‘Le Livre Blanc’’ (her first in English, available Sept. 1), she features recipes like Normandy scallops topped with a ‘‘sunset’’ of rose petals and radicchio and crab topped with Chinese white-jasmine tea foam, which are accompanied by lovely, spare photographs. It’s as much an art book as a practical guide; Pic explained that she doesn’t expect home cooks to replicate her recipes — after all, who has gariguette strawberries in the fridge? ‘‘But,” she added, “I will be very happy if they were inspired by my associations of taste.’’', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Food Matters | The Cookbook Not Meant for Home Cooks', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-14T22:07:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7929e929-6096-511c-8d32-27caa4d78285', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7929e929-6096-511c-8d32-27caa4d78285'}, {'abstract': 'An eco-friendly home that started one man’s career as a green architect evolves, like the chemical-free gardens outside.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/garden/in-pursuit-of-the-perfectly-passive.html', 'snippet': 'An eco-friendly home that started one man’s career as a green architect evolves, like the chemical-free gardens outside.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KINDERHOOK, N.Y. — The little passive-solar house that the architect Dennis Wedlick designed more than 25 years ago with his life partner, Curt DeVito, was state of the art back then. It has all the whimsical geometry of a Wedlick house: an acute isosceles triangle on top of a pillbox; four round white pillars on the narrow porch; floor-to-ceiling windows for the most effective solar gain.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/15/garden/15DENNIS1/15DENNIS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/15/garden/15DENNIS1/15DENNIS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 469}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/15/garden/15DENNIS1/15DENNIS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/15/garden/15DENNIS1/15DENNIS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1602, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/15/garden/15DENNIS1/15DENNIS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/15/garden/15DENNIS1/15DENNIS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subt