iddlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e5162df-6254-59a0-a141-6d079a8f89f6', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e5162df-6254-59a0-a141-6d079a8f89f6'}, {'abstract': 'Hannah Anderson, the 16-year-old California girl who was rescued last weekend after six days in captivity, answered dozens of questions about the ordeal on a now-closed social media account that family and friends said belonged to her.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/14/california-teenager-answers-questions-about-kidnapping/', 'snippet': 'Hannah Anderson, the 16-year-old California girl who was rescued last weekend after six days in captivity, answered dozens of questions about the ordeal on a now-closed social media account that family and friends said belonged to her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hannah Anderson, the 16-year-old California girl rescued last weekend in the Idaho wilderness after being held hostage for six days, shared extraordinary details of her ordeal as she fielded dozens of questions on a social media account, since deleted, that her family and friends say belonged to her.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California Teenager Answers Questions About Kidnapping', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hostages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Christina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-14T22:57:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3df594fc-dc6c-5ba4-b1eb-a9089783d32e', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3df594fc-dc6c-5ba4-b1eb-a9089783d32e'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Oh has played Dr. Cristina Yang since the show’s debut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/arts/television/sandra-oh-to-leave-greys-anatomy.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Oh has played Dr. Cristina Yang since the show’s debut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The future of ABC’s long-running prime-time medical soap, “Grey’s Anatomy,” got a little murkier this week when Sandra Oh, below, who has played Dr. Cristina Yang since the show’s debut, announced she was leaving the series (but not until the end of this season). Ms. Oh, who was nominated for five Emmy Awards as Dr. Yang, has played one of the show’s most consistently popular characters. Her decision to leave comes early, which should make it easier for the show’s creator, Shonda Rhimes, to write the character off the show. But there is a chance Ms. Oh will not be the only departure. Most of the show’s regulars, including Ellen Pompeo, Patrick Dempsey, Chandra Wilson and James Pickens Jr., have contracts that end after the coming season. ABC released a statement saying, “It’s our intention to have ‘Grey’s’ on the air for many years to come, with as many of the original cast as possible.” The network has good reason to push for further seasons: the series remains ABC’s highest-rated drama, though its numbers have fallen in recent years from its days as a prime-time phenomenon.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sandra Oh to Leave ‘Grey’s Anatomy’', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sandra Oh to Leave ‘Grey’s Anatomy’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'perso