ates would pull out of \xa0joint military exercises with the Egyptian army scheduled for September.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Military Madness in Cairo', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Military Madness in Cairo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sisi, Abdul-Fattah el-', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T01:20:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bd18617-854f-56a5-b8d9-567a70259aa4', 'word_count': 658, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bd18617-854f-56a5-b8d9-567a70259aa4'}, {'abstract': 'Civil unions in New Jersey deprive same-sex couples of important rights and benefits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/opinion/obvious-inequality.html', 'snippet': 'Civil unions in New Jersey deprive same-sex couples of important rights and benefits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite polls that show broad public support for allowing same-sex couples to marry, New Jersey, to its great shame, has refused to follow the example set by other states in the Northeast — Connecticut, Delaware, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Hampshire, New York, Rhode Island and Vermont — in granting marriage equality. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obvious Inequality', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obvious Inequality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoens, Helen E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobson, Mary C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T01:20:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff18493d-ee53-569b-8f96-b547de113e75', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff18493d-ee53-569b-8f96-b547de113e75'}, {'abstract': 'America’s largest wireless carriers finance a moving documentary on the perils of texting while driving.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/opinion/werner-herzog-says-dont-text-and-drive.html', 'snippet': 'America’s largest wireless carriers finance a moving documentary on the perils of texting while driving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Werner Herzog, the prolific German filmmaker behind “Fitzcarraldo,” “Rescue Dawn” and “Cave of Forgotten Dreams,” has directed a 35-minute documentary on the perils of texting while driving. America’s four largest wireless carriers financed the film, “From One Second to the Next,” and released it online last week. AT&T will take the lead in distributing it to more than 40,000 high schools. Maddening and moving, it may be the first example of a new genre: the arthouse public service announcement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Werner Herzog Says: Don’t Text and Drive', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Werner Herzog Says: Don&#8217;t Text and Drive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herzog, Werner', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Driver Distraction and Fatigue', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T01:20:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d1408e1-3a74-507f-af0f-347b0db0b5ae', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d1408e1-3a74-507f-af0f-347b0db0b5ae'}, {'abstract': 'The recent stop-and-frisk decision does nothing to disrupt the authority the Supreme Court has given police officers to target African-Americans and Latinos with little or no basis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/opinion/racial-profiling-lives-on.html', 'snippet': 'The recent stop-and-frisk decision does nothing to disrupt the authority the Supreme Court has given police officers to target African-Americans and Latinos with little or no basis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — THE historic ruling by Judge Shira A. Scheindlin that the stop-and-frisk practices of the New York Police Department violate the Constitution is being applauded as a major victory against unreasonable policing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Racial Profiling Lives On', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Racial Profiling Lives On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carbado, Devon W', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Cheryl I', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crenshaw, Kimberle W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scheindlin, Shira A', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T01:23:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Devon W. Carbado, Cheryl I Harris and Kimberle Williams Crenshaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Devon', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Carbado', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': 'I <missing Dot>', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Kimberle', 'middlename': 'Williams', 'lastname': 'Crenshaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0b93e74-9746-5c86-86aa-ef3d2d00bafc', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0b93e74-9746-5c86-86aa-ef3d2d00bafc'}, {'abstract': 'Vernon Wells is a constant presence at early batting practice, and perhaps that is what has brought about his recent resurgence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/sports/baseball/still-starting-his-days-early-the-yankees-wells-reawakens-his-bat.html', 'snippet': 'Vernon Wells is a constant presence at early batting practice, and perhaps that is what has brought about his recent resurgence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of hours before the official start of batting practice Tuesday, Vernon Wells was in the batting cage getting in a few early swings. He slapped line drives over the left-field fence, the balls struck so hard that stadium workers in the outfield grandstands had to move out of the way to avoid being hit. One worker jokingly yelled at Wells to be careful. Wells waved and laughed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Starting His Days Early, the Yankees’ Wells Reawakens His Bat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still Starting His Days Early, the Yankees&#8217; Wells Reawakens His Bat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wells, Vernon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hafner, Travis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T01:27:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jorge Arangure Jr', 'person': [{'firstname'