tion': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e26a2a32-1f63-52b7-85ca-ec203ee50c05', 'word_count': 658, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e26a2a32-1f63-52b7-85ca-ec203ee50c05'}, {'abstract': 'The Los Angeles-based design collective Commune has launched a rustic, eco-friendly furniture line that uses materials such as black walnut, white oak and copper.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/by-design-furnishings-that-are-made-to-age/', 'snippet': 'The Los Angeles-based design collective Commune has launched a rustic, eco-friendly furniture line that uses materials such as black walnut, white oak and copper.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Los Angeles-based collective Commune, responsible for hip projects like the Ace Swim Club in Palm Springs and the Opening Ceremony boutique in Tokyo, are starting a well-made, understated line of furniture in keeping with their rustic, minimalist style. “I want to make things that age well and are not disposable,” the Commune principal Roman Alonso said. The collection uses two types of wood — black walnut and white oak — and includes subtle metal cleats and brass or copper trim, which will acquire a patina over time. There are customizable options as well: a chair’s slipcover and a daybed’s bolster come in organic materials like linen and shearling. How do the partners make decisions collaboratively? “We only make it if we want it ourselves,” Alonso said.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '101', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'By Design | Furnishings That Are Made to Age', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Line: Made to Age', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T15:08:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T