ford-Stuyvesant section of Brooklyn, N.Y., on July 5, is documenting his painful recovery in a blog, How I Survived a Gunshot Wound to the Gut, in an effort to push for gun control. Struck by a stray bullet in a drive-by shooting, he still feels incredible pain in his stomach and bleeding from his chest, he told WABC. The writing is therapeutic because he suffers from post-traumatic stress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: August 15, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T15:35:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/222fecf4-814c-545c-acfb-f554a34838f8', 'word_count': 1439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/222fecf4-814c-545c-acfb-f554a34838f8'}, {'abstract': 'Despite signs of a reviving economy, several big retail chains said consumers were still limiting their spending to the essentials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/business/wal-mart-lowers-outlook-as-consumers-hold-back.html', 'snippet': 'Despite signs of a reviving economy, several big retail chains said consumers were still limiting their spending to the essentials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lot of Americans are still spending their money only on socks and other essentials, highlighting the disparity between younger and poorer consumers and those who are benefiting from the economic recovery. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/business/Shop/Shop-artic