 'nyt://article/78799f8a-23e7-5507-b0d9-2a7da840a867'}, {'abstract': 'A few more thoughts on the Washington Post’s missed opportunity.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/a-last-word-on-the-post-and-politico/', 'snippet': 'A few more thoughts on the Washington Post’s missed opportunity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m quite sure I’m hitting diminishing returns in my analysis of the Washington D.C. newspaper scene, but let me just reply to this piece in Buzzfeed, in which an ex-Politico staffer makes the case that it would be a tragedy if\xa0the Post took what he thinks was my Sunday column’s advice and tried to transform itself into Politico:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Last Word on the Post and Politico', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bezos, Jeffrey P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T17:09:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f00b81cc-9452-5ccf-985c-9328e50d7440', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f00b81cc-9452-5ccf-985c-9328e50d7440'}, {'abstract': 'The pilot said on Britain’s Channel 4 that the airline put pressure on pilots to reduce costs by limiting the amount of reserve fuel they carried.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/business/global/ryanair-fires-pilot-who-questioned-airlines-safety-on-tv.html', 'snippet': 'The pilot said on Britain’s Channel 4 that the airline put pressure on pilots to reduce costs by limiting the amount of reserve fuel they carried.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Ryanair, the Dublin-based budget airline, confirmed Thursday that it had fired one of its most senior pilots and was pursuing legal action against him after the pilot raised safety questions about the airline’s fuel policy in a British television interview.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryanair Fires Pilot Who Questioned Airline’s Safety on TV', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ryanair Fires Pilot Who Questioned Airline’s Safety on TV', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ryanair Holdings PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T17:28:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7191fe2-32fc-568e-8eb4-d450cb87b8c0', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7191fe2-32fc-568e-8eb4-d450cb87b8c0'}, {'abstract': 'I want to mention a few points that didn’t fit into the space or the story I wanted to tell.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/behind-the-southern-road-trip/', 'snippet': 'I want to mention a few points that didn’t fit into the space or the story I wanted to tell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I decided to write about L.C. King Manufacturing in Bristol, Tenn., I wasn’t really thinking about Made in America. Somehow, the marketing around American-made fogs the actual picture — the hows and whys a garment is made, as well as the problems. I marvel at the skills of people who make things, whether it’s jeans or a Paris couture dress. And, as I tried to say in today’s article, a factory like L.C. King can impart a specific difference — through its needle, its work-wear tradition and whatever is floating in the air of that 100-year-old facility.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Southern Road Trip', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T17:35:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55de723a-2728-5d77-9405-72619e90ba16', 'word_count': 1140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55de723a-2728-5d77-9405-72619e90ba16'}, {'abstract': 'How the pocket diary transformed the war experience for Union soldiers – and left a rich, but overlooked, historical record.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/dear-diary/', 'snippet': 'How the pocket diary transformed the war experience for Union soldiers – and left a rich, but overlooked, historical record.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On July 7, 1863, just three days after the fall of Vicksburg, Miss., Cpl. John White of the 20th Regiment, Wisconsin Volunteers, walked into the beleaguered city to pick up contraband and prisoners. Like many Union soldiers carrying diaries in their packs, White recorded the moment for posterity: “Today I went into the city of Vicksburgh. Had a good ramble. Very hot day. The prisoners are getting their paroles. Vicksburgh is quite a pretty place.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dear Diary', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T17:37:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Molly McCarthy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Molly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McCarthy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/667661ee-2c27-5518-a283-73ad99eca813', 'word_count': 1214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/667661ee-2c27-5518-a283-73ad99eca813'}, {'abstract': 'The latest test flight of Space Exploration Technologies Corporation’s Grasshopper vehicle demonstrated more pronounced steering maneuvers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/science/space/latest-spacex-rocket-test-successfully-goes-sideways.html', 'snippet': 'The latest test flight of Space Exploration Technologies Corporation’s Grasshopper vehicle demonstrated more pronounced steering maneuvers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine taking a 10-story building, launching it, angling it so that it shifts 330 feet to the side as it rises 820 feet into the air – and then landing it on the same spot it started.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Latest SpaceX Rocket Test Successfully Goes Sideways', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Space Exploration Technologies Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Musk, Elon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Spaceflight', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T17:42:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8355f03f-f524-5a8e-b7ee-2c6069b0c9ca', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8355f03f-f524-5a8e-b7ee-2c6069b0c9ca'}, {'abstract': 'Though a government shutdown seems relatively unlikely, President Obama and his Republican interlocutors face a challenge in bridging seemingly irreconcilable goals in a fiscal deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/us/politics/a-washington-puzzle-solving-3-fiscal-disputes.html', 'snippet': 'Though a government shutdown seems relatively unlikely, President Obama and his Republican interlocutors face a challenge in bridging seemingly irreconcilable goals in a fiscal deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — On the endgame for the budget showdown looming in Washington this fall, only this is clear: President Obama thinks Republicans cannot risk another debt crisis or government shutdown, and Republican leaders agree.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/us/MEMO/MEMO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/16/us/MEMO/MEMO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/us/MEMO/