ew York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Multiple Wildfires Raging in Western States', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Interagency Fire Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Idaho', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Western States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T20:14:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/225f3087-2949-5f88-9d25-7f0557376098', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/225f3087-2949-5f88-9d25-7f0557376098'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary “Cutie and the Boxer” tracks the tempestuous marriage and parallel careers of the New York-based Japanese artists Ushio and Noriko Shinohara.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/now-screening-forty-years-of-love-and-art-and-chaos/', 'snippet': 'The documentary “Cutie and the Boxer” tracks the tempestuous marriage and parallel careers of the New York-based Japanese artists Ushio and Noriko Shinohara.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Cutie and the Boxer,” the debut feature-length documentary from Zachary Heinzerling, chronicles the four-decade marriage and careers of the New York-via-Japan painters and sculptors Ushio and Noriko Shinohara. But it’s anything but a dewy-eyed love story. The film, which won the Directing Award for best United States documentary at Sundance this year, shifts its focus from Ushio’s career to Noriko’s as she emerges from her husband’s shadow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Screening | Forty Years of Love and Art and Chaos', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dumbo (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T20:15:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathan Reese', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reese', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d709e3f7-f41a-5184-93c9-6677fcb1ab44', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d709e3f7-f41a-5184-93c9-6677fcb1ab44'}, {'abstract': 'The limits of advice in marital strife, an apology full of crocodile tears and other pressing questions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/fashion/retiring-the-therapy-couch.html', 'snippet': 'The limits of advice in marital strife, an apology full of crocodile tears and other pressing questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My husband and I are close friends with another couple. After years of dissatisfaction, the husband began an affair. He moved out of the house, but still returns almost daily for meals and laundry and to see the children. His wife wants to save the marriage and see a counselor. But the husband told us (though not his wife) that he will never reconcile with her. For months, they have sought no professional help. Instead, they come to us, separately and together, to vent and for advice. I told the husband he had to tell his wife the truth. He became upset, but nothing changed. At what point does our advice become unproductive interference?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Retiring the Therapy Couch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Time to Step Aside', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T20:17:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e477a01-0744-535e-b1ce-c9da70d7d884', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e477a01-0744-535e-b1ce-c9da70d7d884'}, {'abstract': '“The feeling that you get from being in control of your health and the way you look is a feeling like no other,” says the Tony Award-winning “Pippin” actress Patina Miller.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/patina-millers-broadway-workout/', 'snippet': '“The feeling that you get from being in control of your health and the way you look is a feeling like no other,” says the Tony Award-winning “Pippin” actress Patina Miller.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks to Broadway, Patina Miller is in the best shape of her life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Patina Miller’s Broadway Workout', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Calories', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Patina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T20:20:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69fc5efa-0767-5561-9ffb-319cee8d357f', 'word_count': 1260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69fc5efa-0767-5561-9ffb-319cee8d357f'}, {'abstract': '“William Trost Richards: Visions of Land and Sea,” at the National Academy Museum, reclaims an American Pre-Raphaelite whose paintings were almost photorealistic in their detail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/arts/design/william-trost-richards-at-national-academy-museum.html', 'snippet': '“William Trost Richards: Visions of Land and Sea,” at the National Academy Museum, reclaims an American Pre-Raphaelite whose paintings were almost photorealistic in their detail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'William Trost Richards had a thing about ocean waves. He would wade in among them or stand on the beach, studying them for hours, “until people thought he was insane,” one of his children recalled. He was not crazy, though. He was an American Pre-Raphaelite, a follower of the English critic John Ruskin’s dictum of artistic truth to nature, the achievement of which should brook no compromise. The payoff for Richards’s observational extremism came in the form of landscape and maritime paintings and drawings of arresting, nearly photorealistic intensity, a selection of which can be seen in “William Trost Richards: Visions of Land and Sea,” at the National Academy Museum. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/16RICHARDS_SPAN/0816RICHARDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/16RICHARDS_SPAN/0816RICHARDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/16RICHARDS_SPAN/0816RICHARDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/16RICHARDS_SPAN/0816RICHARDS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1288, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/16RICHARDS_SPAN/0816RICHARDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/16RICHARDS_SPAN/0816RICHARDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/16RICHARDS_SPAN/0816RICHARDS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Magician of the Rolling Hills and Rocky Shore', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Magician of the Rolling Hills and Rocky Shore', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, William Trost', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Academy Museum and School of Fine Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T20:21:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1682dc64-737f-58d7-829e-cdb6cd2b