hy-by-jeff-guinn.html', 'snippet': 'How did a juvenile delinquent named Charles Manson become the notorious killer whose crimes still horrify us today?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve never met Charles Manson, although I did meet one of his former cellmates in the late 1980s, at an ill-\xadbegotten writers’ conference on the Oregon coast. He was the protégé of an elderly and naïve writing coach, and he leapt from her car, heading straight for me, probably because I was the only true-crime writer there. He waved a creased note and shouted: “Charlie gave this to me! See — there’s his signature. I know Charlie Manson personally!”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/books/review/18RULE/18RULE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 485, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/18/books/review/18RULE/18RULE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 485}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/books/review/18RULE/18RULE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 828, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/books/review/18RULE/18RULE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1602, 'width': 1981, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/books/review/18RULE/18RULE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/18/books/review/18RULE/18RULE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': No