, 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Gray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0aeca7ef-b49b-5ab2-9082-41a164ab53c0', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0aeca7ef-b49b-5ab2-9082-41a164ab53c0'}, {'abstract': 'One whole quarter of growth!', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/the-soft-bigotry-of-low-european-expectations/', 'snippet': 'One whole quarter of growth!', 'lead_paragraph': 'It really is kind of pathetic to see European leaders claiming vindication after one whole quarter of positive growth, at the thrilling annual rate of 1.2 percent. Just to say the obvious: when you’ve suffered a huge hit to output and employment, you’re supposed to have a long period of fast growth to make up the lost ground. Otherwise you’re making the definition of success way too easy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Soft Bigotry of Low European Expectations', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T21:26:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1952940b-09a6-5775-b3c0-0b9b0c14fe9c', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1952940b-09a6-5775-b3c0-0b9b0c14fe9c'}, {'abstract': 'This poignant exhibition presents 37 images from “Time of Change: Civil Rights Photographs, 1961-1965,” published in 2002.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytim