one, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9471533-4cc8-5c3b-ad8f-bf0f7932fcad', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9471533-4cc8-5c3b-ad8f-bf0f7932fcad'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for interesting and peculiar items. Thursday’s selections include a profile of the philosopher behind a data-mining start-up that helped find and kill Osama Bin Laden. Plus, new research showed that using Facebook erodes overall well-being.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/todays-scuttlebot-the-c-i-a-backed-start-up-and-facebook-blues/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for interesting and peculiar items. Thursday’s selections include a profile of the philosopher behind a data-mining start-up that helped find and kill Osama Bin Laden. Plus, new research showed that using ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day, The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for interesting and peculiar items. On Thursday, The Washington Post said its Web site had been breached by the Syrian Electronic Army, a hacker collective that supports the Syrian president, Bashar al-Assad. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: The C.I.A.-Backed Start-Up and Facebook Blues', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T22:38:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c968db00-0ee2-52c3-a24c-02815cd6860e', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c968db00-0ee2-52c3-a24c-02815cd6860e'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to walks, talks, exhibitions, readings, dance-offs and other cultural events in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/arts/spare-times-for-aug-16-22.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to walks, talks, exhibitions, readings, dance-offs and other cultural events in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Free Outdoor Yoga (Saturday, Sunday, and Tuesday through Thursday) As long as the weather cooperates, there are ample opportunities for yoga enthusiasts to practice their sun salutations under the sun. The setting for yoga on Tuesdays (at 10 a.m.) and Thursdays (at 6 p.m.), through Sept. 19, is Bryant Park, above, Avenue of the Americas, at 40th Street, (212) 768-4242, bryantpark.org. On Wednesday at 6:30 p.m., people will gather at Columbus Park, at Bayard, Baxter and Mulberry Streets in Chinatown, for a session sponsored by the city’s Department of Parks and Recreation; nycgovparks.org/programs/recreation/shape-up-nyc. Also on Wednesday, yoga is part of a lunchtime event at Lincoln Center, which next week includes music by the Dahka Band and Karikatura, from noon to 2 p.m. The series runs through Sept. 25; (212) 581-3774, lincolnsquarebid.org/news/views.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for Aug. 16-22', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-15T22:40:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Gaffney and Anne Mancuso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gaffney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mancuso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e1ee634-7d5e-57c1-9826-379adb3de457', 'word_count': 3185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e1ee634-7d5e-57c1-9826-379adb3de457'}, {'abstract': 'Giovanni’s Bistro, Bar and Catering in Berkeley Heights turns out what it calls “new American cuisine with Mediterranean and Italian influences.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/nyregion/a-review-of-giovannis-bistro-in-berkeley-heights.html', 'snippet': 'Giovanni’s Bistro, Bar and Catering in Berkeley Heights turns out what it calls “new American cuisine with Mediterranean and Italian influences.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'With fewer than 40 seats filling a storefront in a quiet patch of Berkeley Heights across the street from an abandoned movie theater, Giovanni’s Bistro, Bar and Catering is short on dazzle at first blush. Its pleasures creep up on you instead, starting with the warmth of the staff; the small, reasonably priced wine list; the fresh bread; the clean, crisp décor; and finally the polished cooking of Michael Metzner, the executive chef. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge',