cter on the popular Fox TV series, had struggled with substance abuse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lisa Robin Kelly, an actress best known for her recurring role on the hit sitcom “That ’70s Show,” died on Wednesday in Los Angeles. She was 43.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/kelly-obit/kelly-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 305, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/kelly-obit/kelly-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 305, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/kelly-obit/kelly-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/kelly-obit/kelly-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/kelly-obit/kelly-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lisa Robin Kelly, Actress on ‘That ’70s Show’ Sitcom, Dies at  43', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lisa Robin Kelly, 43, Actress On ‘That ’70s Show’ Sitcom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Lisa Robin (1970-2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T01:32:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/068192fe-e4e7-5a52-861e-af19dc8609c6', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/068192fe-e4e7-5a52-861e-af19dc8609c6'}, {'abstract': 'A scientific evaluation of the delisting plan for gray wolves has gotten tangled up in politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/opinion/wolves-under-review.html', 'snippet': 'A scientific evaluation of the delisting plan for gray wolves has gotten tangled up in politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In June, the Fish and Wildlife Service prematurely proposed to end federal protection for gray wolves in the lower 48 states in the belief that wolves had fully recovered from near eradication in the early 20th century. This was politics masquerading as science. The Fish and Wildlife Service would love to shed the responsibility of protecting large carnivores, like the wolf and the grizzly bear, and hunters and ranchers throughout the Rocky Mountains would love to see wolves eradicated all over again.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wolves Under Review', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wolves Under Review', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wolves', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fish and Wildlife Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T01:40:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a71cdd9-1ce0-5b16-9e5c-28eb2f4dc80d', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a71cdd9-1ce0-5b16-9e5c-28eb2f4dc80d'}, {'abstract': 'The Detroit bankruptcy case provides another example of how Wall Street wins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/opinion/no-banker-left-behind.html', 'snippet': 'The Detroit bankruptcy case provides another example of how Wall Street wins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Detroit bankruptcy case has been cast as a contest between bondholders and pensioners that can be resolved only by shared sacrifice.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Banker Left Behind', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Banker Left Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Derivatives (Financial Instruments)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UBS AG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T01:40:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d27adaea-d22a-5828-affd-1909d9fafa79', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d27adaea-d22a-5828-affd-1909d9fafa79'}, {'abstract': 'Voters in Virginia face a governor’s election muddled by ethical issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/opinion/insider-influence-in-the-commonwealth.html', 'snippet': 'Voters in Virginia face a governor’s election muddled by ethical issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For all the candidates’ pronouncements on the issues, the governor’s election in Virginia has morphed into a sorry lesson for voters in how political favoritism for insiders undermines public trust. After months of disclosures and controversy, Gov. Bob McDonnell is busy returning and repaying more than $150,000 in gifts and loans to a donor who enjoyed access to the statehouse and Mr. McDonnell’s support for his dietary supplement business.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Insider Influence in the Commonwealth', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Insider Influence in the Commonwealth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonnell, Robert F', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McAuliffe, Terry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuccinelli, Kenneth T II', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodham, Anthony', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GreenTech Automotive Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T01:40:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f17acaa-e99c-5911-b565-60bccebcf7d1', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f17acaa-e99c-5911-b565-60bccebcf7d1'}, {'abstract': 'An overdue standard from the Food and Drug Administration is good news for consumers with food allergies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/opinion/is-it-really-gluten-free.html', 'snippet': 'An overdue standard from the Food and Drug Administration is good news for consumers with food allergies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most consumers understand that “lite” or “low in carbs” on food packaging labels are marketing descriptions, nothing more. But the label “gluten free” is a promise that is critical for the health of about three million Americans who can get ill if they eat the proteins that occur naturally in wheat, barley or other related grains. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It Really Gluten Free?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is It Really Gluten Free?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gluten', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T01:40:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d9fbcc0-71ef-5410-b4c6-c0e43532bb79', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d9fbcc0-71ef-5410-b4c6-c0e43532bb79'}, {'abstract': 'The expansion of instant replay in baseball runs the risk of slowing down an already slow game in an effort to get every call correct.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/sports/baseball/pausing-to-consider-a-rules-change.html', 'snippet': 'The expansion of instant replay in baseball runs the risk of slowing down an already slow game in an effort to get every call correct.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Baseball, for many casual fans, has a problem with excitement. More specifically, the sport known as the national pastime has often been accused of being boring in comparison with the flashier National Football League.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/sports/subSCOREillo/subSCOREillo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/16/sports/subSCOREillo/subSCOREillo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 639}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/sports/subSCOREillo/subSCOREillo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 962, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/sports/subSCOREillo/subSCOREillo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1924, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/sports/subSCOREillo/subSCOREillo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/16/sports/subSCOREillo/subSCOREillo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ