 opened at Circle in the Square.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Broadway season has barely begun to shake off its summer slumber, but I think I can guarantee that the months to come will bring no odder musical than “Soul Doctor,” the true-life tale of the folk-singing Rabbi Shlomo Carlebach, which opened on Thursday night at the Circle in the Square. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/16SOULDOC_SPAN/16SOULDOC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/16SOULDOC_SPAN/16SOULDOC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/16SOULDOC_SPAN/16SOULDOC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/16SOULDOC_SPAN/16SOULDOC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/16SOULDOC_SPAN/16SOULDOC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/16SOULDOC_SPAN/16SOULDOC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/16SOULDOC_SPAN/16SOULDOC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rabbi With a Beat and Tie-Dyed Prayers', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rabbi With a Beat And Tie-Dyed Prayers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carlebach, Shlomo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, ERIC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wise, Daniel S', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schechter, David', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pouffer, Benoit-Swan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iman, Amber', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T02:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f847919-d860-5c23-ad5d-3e6a0987f57f', 'word_count': 1158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f847919-d860-5c23-ad5d-3e6a0987f57f'}, {'abstract': 'A judge ordered Hattiesburg on Thursday to stage a special mayoral election after accusations of fraud led to a protracted legal dispute.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/us/mississippi-a-do-over-in-hattiesburg.html', 'snippet': 'A judge ordered Hattiesburg on Thursday to stage a special mayoral election after accusations of fraud led to a protracted legal dispute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A judge ordered Hattiesburg on Thursday to stage a special mayoral election after accusations of fraud led to a protracted legal dispute. Mayor Johnny L. DuPree won the June 4 election by 37 votes, but lawyers for his challenger, Dave Ware, said that widespread misconduct had allowed Mr. DuPree to win. A jury considered Mr. Ware’s allegations last month, but the proceedings ended in a mistrial and Mr. DuPree stayed in office. Mr. Ware continued his courtroom fight, and Judge William F. Coleman agreed on Thursday to support his campaign’s motion for a special election. Gov. Phil Bryant will schedule the new vote for the city of about 47,000 people. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mississippi: A Do-Over in Hattiesburg', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mississippi: A Do-over In Hattiesburg', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blinder, Alan S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hattiesburg (Miss)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DuPree, Johnny L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ware, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coleman, William F', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryant, Phil', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T02:04:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e397df59-7f34-5276-9982-751afbde7c26', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e397df59-7f34-5276-9982-751afbde7c26'}, {'abstract': 'Four months after 8-year-old Martin Richard was killed in the Boston Marathon bombings, his family is inspired by their surviving daughter, who has made remarkable progress after losing a leg.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/15/boston-bombing-victims-family-is-inspired-by-injured-daughter/', 'snippet': 'Four months after 8-year-old Martin Richard was killed in the Boston Marathon bombings, his family is inspired by their surviving daughter, who has made remarkable progress after losing a leg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the four-month anniversary of the Boston Marathon bombings on Thursday, the family of 8-year-old Martin Richard, who was killed, published an update on their Tumblr blog. They discussed the constant pain they feel over the loss of their son and described the inspiration they are drawing from their daughter, Jane, 7, who lost a leg in the blasts but has made remarkable progress with a prosthetic leg.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boston Bombing Victim’s Family Is Inspired by Injured Daughter', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richard, Martin (2005-13)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T02:13:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5b69b51-2d47-5807-b0a7-90e75b2676d8', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5b69b51-2d47-5807-b0a7-90e75b2676d8'}, {'abstract': 'The Dream Defenders, a group of students who have been occupying the governor’s office since July 16, called it quits on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/us/florida-sit-in-ends-at-governors-office.html', 'snippet': 'The Dream Defenders, a group of students who have been occupying the governor’s office since July 16, called it quits on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Dream Defenders, a group of students who have been occupying the governor’s office since July 16, called it quits on Thursday. The group was pushing for changes to the Stand Your Ground provision in Florida’s self-defense laws and wanted to secure a special legislative session on the issue. The students were also hoping to cast light on the state’s racial profiling practices and zero-tolerance rules in schools, which have led to increases in suspensions and expulsions. This week, the group won enough petitions by Florida lawmakers to poll the Legislature on the need for a special session. But the group was unable to secure the required 96 legislative votes. Gov. Rick Scott, a Republican, also rejected the idea of a session. Republican legislative leaders said it was time for the students to clear out. The Dream Defenders did persuade the House speaker, Will Weatherford, to hold a hearing on Stand Your Ground next month. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida: Sit-In Ends at Governor’s Office', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida: Sit-In Ends at Governor’s Office', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alvarez, Lizette', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dream Defenders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Richard L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Self-Defense', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T02:15:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/202a285b-5c42-58f2-a1d6-9ad9ee0058e1', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/202a285b-5c42-58f2-a1d6-9ad9ee0058e1'}, {'abstract': 'Fran Weiner, Anthony D. Weiner’s mother, a retired math teacher, made her first appearance on the campaign trail on Thursday outside of Brooklyn Technical High School, Mr. Weiner’s alma mater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/nyregion/a-weiner-endorsement.html', 'snippet': 'Fran Weiner, Anthony D. Weiner’s mother, a retired math teacher, made her first appearance on the campaign trail on Thursday outside of Brooklyn Technical High School, Mr. Weiner’s alma mater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First, there was a flash of teal earrings and a floppy red hat. Then a car door swung open, cameras clicked away, and a pair of gel-padded sneakers hit the ground.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/nyregion/trailside/trailside-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/16/nyregion/trailside/trailside-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/nyregion/trailside/trailside-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/nyregion/trailside/trailside-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/nyregion/trailside/trailside-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/16/nyregion/trailside/trailside-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/nyregion/trailside/trailside-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Teacher Praises Weiner (She’s Hardly Impartial)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Teacher Praises Weiner (She’s Hardly Impartial)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Javier C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Fran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T02:18:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Javier C. Hernández', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hernández', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cdf7828-d7e0-52e2-9c71-2821a4225488', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cdf7828-d7e0-52e2-9c71-2821a4225488'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Pat McCrory vetoed a measure on Thursday that would have imposed a drug-testing mandate on some welfare applicants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/us/north-carolina-drug-testing-for-welfare-aid-vetoed.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Pat McCrory vetoed a measure on Thursday that would have imposed a drug-testing mandate on some welfare applicants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Pat McCrory vetoed a measure\xa0on Thursday\xa0that would have imposed a drug-testing mandate on some welfare applicants. The bill called for candidates to submit to screening if officials had “reasonable suspicion” of drug use. A recent arrest or conviction for a drug offense would have met that standard. Law enforcement agencies would not have received copies of test results. Governor McCrory, a Republican, described the proposal in a statement as “a recipe for government overreach and unnecessary government intrusion.” The legislature, which the G.O.P. controls, overwhelmingly approved the plan in July and could try to override the veto. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Carolina: Drug Testing for Welfare Aid Vetoed', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Carolina: Drug Testing For Welfare Aid Vetoed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blinder, Alan S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCrory, Pat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Drug Use)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T02:22:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3731ea0b-630f-5859-a339-46c4477406e7', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3731ea0b-630f-5859-a339-46c4477406e7'}, {'abstract': 'A new poll that showed Bill de Blasio, the public advocate, and Christine C. Quinn, the City Council speaker, each received support from 24 percent of voters who said they were likely to vote in the Sept. 10 primary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/nyregion/poll-shows-a-tight-race.html', 'snippet': 'A new poll that showed Bill de Blasio, the public advocate, and Christine C. Quinn, the City Council speaker, each received support from 24 percent of voters who said they were likely to vote in the Sept. 10 primary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a dead heat.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poll Shows a Tight Race', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Poll Shows A Tight Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T02:25:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33e8f8fb-c4e7-52de-9599-9d4790964418', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33e8f8fb-c4e7-52de-9599-9d4790964418'}, {'abstract': 'Of all the Solheim Cup parents, nobody has more wisdom to impart than Jessica Korda’s father, Petr Korda, who compiled a 29-13 record in Davis Cup competition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/sports/golf/kordas-father-knows-the-pressure-of-playing-for-country.html', 'snippet': 'Of all the Solheim Cup parents, nobody has more wisdom to impart than Jessica Korda’s father, Petr Korda, who compiled a 29-13 record in Davis Cup competition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARKER, Colo. — Lexi Thompson’s parents followed her inside the ropes at Colorado Golf Club on Thursday. So did Michelle Wie’s parents, who conferred with her occasionally about her putts and whatnot as she made her way around the front nine. It was the last practice before Friday’s start of the Solheim Cup, a biennial competition between the best women golfers from the United States and Europe, and Thompson and Wie were practicing with Jessica Korda, whose father, Petr, was nowhere to be seen. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/sports/CITY-SOLHEIM/CITY-SOLHEIM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/16/sports/CITY-SOLHEIM/CITY-SOLHEIM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/sports/CITY-SOLHEIM/CITY-SOLHEIM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/sports/CITY-SOLHEIM/CITY-SOLHEIM-superJumbo.j