 is unlikely that health care spending in the United States will grow more quickly than gross domestic product, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/controlling-health-care-spending-revisited/', 'snippet': 'It is unlikely that health care spending in the United States will grow more quickly than gross domestic product, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Uwe E. Reinhardt is an economics professor at Princeton. He has some financial interests in the health care field.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Controlling Health Care Spending, Revisited', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T04:01:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Uwe E. Reinhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Uwe', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Reinhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71180146-f52a-5338-822c-08c0bec28fda', 'word_count': 1221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71180146-f52a-5338-822c-08c0bec28fda'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 10 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/word-of-the-day-edify/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 10 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'edify •\\ˈe-də-ˌfi\\• verb', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | edify', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T04:06:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26d799f7-fe2c-523b-be65-4bb41759327c', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26d799f7-fe2c-523b-be65-4bb41759327c'}, {'abstract': 'The violations of privacy rules, which were often inadvertent, cast new light on the agency’s potential for intrusions on Americans’ communications.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/us/nsa-often-broke-rules-on-privacy-audit-shows.html', 'snippet': 'The violations of privacy rules, which were often inadvertent, cast new light on the agency’s potential for intrusions on Americans’ communications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The National Security Agency violated privacy rules protecting the communications of Americans and others on domestic soil 2,776 times over a one-year period, according to an internal audit leaked by the former N.S.A. contractor Edward J. Snowden and made public on Thursday night.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.S.A. Often Broke Rules on Privacy, Audit Shows', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.S.A. Often Broke Rules On Privacy, Audit Shows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act (FISA)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T04:24:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33ca5574-c31a-5fcc-8a83-eca3e9b50352', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33ca5574-c31a-5fcc-8a83-eca3e9b50352'}, {'abstract': 'The sudden retirement of the recent Wimbledon champion Marion Bartoli on Wednesday night was the talk of the Western & Southern Open the next day, with players from both tours expressing shock at her departure.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/players-react-to-bartolis-sudden-retirement/', 'snippet': 'The sudden retirement of the recent Wimbledon champion Marion Bartoli on Wednesday night was the talk of the Western & Southern Open the next day, with players from both tours expressing shock at her departure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MASON, Ohio — The sudden retirement of the recent Wimbledon champion Marion Bartoli on Wednesday night was the talk of the Western & Southern Open the next day, with players from both tours expressing shock at her departure. Below, a look at some players’ reactions:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Players React to Bartoli’s Sudden Retirement', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bartoli, Marion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T04:38:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bdf7739-8f11-54f4-8880-d5a376fb1dcc', 'word_count': 909, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bdf7739-8f11-54f4-8880-d5a376fb1dcc'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (13) PARSIFAL Jonas Kaufmann sings the title role in this new production of Wagner’s opera about the knights of the grail, staged in a postapocalyptic setting of sun-baked earth and swirling mists by the French Canadian director François Girard, in his Metropolitan Opera debut. René Pape plays the wise knight Gurnemanz; Katarina Dalayman (on the ground above, next to Mr. Kaufmann and in front of Mr. Pape) is the wayward temptress Kundry; Peter Mattei is the wounded king Amfortas; and Evgeny Nikitin is the evil wizard Klingsor. Daniele Gatti conducts this coproduction with Opéra National de Lyon and the Canadian Opera Company, presented in two parts by “Great Performances at the Met.” “The gloominess of this production can become oppressive,” Anthony Tommasini wrote in a New York Times review in February. Still, “there is much to admire in Mr. Girard’s thoughtful and intrepid staging, full of striking imagery.” The Met, he added, “has assembled about the best ‘Parsifal’ cast available today,” while Mr. Gatti “draws diaphanous playing from the great Met orchestra and captures the shifting currents of this richly chromatic and complex score.” Part 2 will be broadcast next Friday at 9.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e459f309-7607-5c53-892b-737dd39c480b', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e459f309-7607-5c53-892b-737dd39c480b'}, {'abstract': 'Zack Wheeler pitched six impressive innings, and the Mets took the lead on Marlon Byrd’s double in the eighth to end a three-game skid.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/sports/baseball/wheeler-and-byrd-help-mets-end-skid.html', 'snippet': 'Zack Wheeler pitched six impressive innings, and the Mets took the lead on Marlon Byrd’s double in the eighth to end a three-game skid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — After each outing, the learning experiences take hold, the lessons crystallize, and the end result is that Zack Wheeler gets even more devastating.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheeler Rears Back and Strikes Out 12 in Mets’ Win', 'kicker': 'Mets 4, Padres 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wheeler Rears Back and Strikes Out 12 in Mets&#8217; Win ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Diego Padres', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheeler, Zack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byrd, Marlon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T05:47:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55422f87-e685-5f27-9ab5-ae2d9bee5c1b', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55422f87-e685-5f27-9ab5-ae2d9bee5c1b'}, {'abstract': 'The friendship of two survivors of the Partition offers hope for India and Pakistan.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/stepping-across-the-line-at-wagah-border/', 'snippet': 'The friendship of two survivors of the Partition offers hope for India and Pakistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last time I crossed the India-Pakistan border was in January. Crossing the border on foot has a strange way of defying the received wisdom about border crossings, and indeed about India and Pakistan. Travelers with visas and the requisite clearances can walk across the border post at Wagah in the northern state of Punjab until about 3:30 or 4 in the afternoon. After the immigration counters close, the border post at Wagah turns into a site for unabashed chauvinism as the gates are closed between the two countries.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/world/asia/16-indiapak-IndiaInk/16-indiapak-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/16/world/asia/16-indiapak-IndiaInk/16-indiapak-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/world/asia/16-indiapak-IndiaInk/16-indiapak-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 623, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/world/asia/16-indiapak-IndiaInk/16-indiapak-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1247, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/world/asia/16-indiapak-IndiaInk/16-indiapak-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/16/world/asia/16-indiapak-IndiaInk/16-indiapak-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/world/asia/16-indiapak-IndiaInk/16-indiapak-IndiaInk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stepping Across the Line at Wagah Border', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T06:56:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Urvashi Butalia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Urvashi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Butalia', 'qualifier': None, 'title