'}, {'abstract': 'We’re adding a week to our Summer Reading Contest to accommodate the many students who still want to post. We will not be formally judging this week’s entries, but we will be posting our favorites to our “Comments of the Moment.”', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/summer-reading-contest-what-interested-you-most-in-the-times-this-week-9/', 'snippet': 'We’re adding a week to our Summer Reading Contest to accommodate the many students who still want to post. We will not be formally judging this week’s entries, but we will be posting our favorites to our “Comments of the Moment.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In The Times this week: Thousands were injured and hundreds killed in Egypt, where a new outbreak of violence underscored how the Arab Spring has devolved into bitter political power struggles. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Reading Contest | What Interested You Most in The Times This Week?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T11:46:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b324a5d-2ff5-56cb-bd3c-1f317076b2c7', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b324a5d-2ff5-56cb-bd3c-1f317076b2c7'}, {'abstract': 'Carl C. Icahn is heading to the Delaware Court of Chancery in his effort to stop a buyout of Dell. | Two private equity investors agreed on Thursday to buy the New Jersey Devils hockey team. | In the wake of scandals, India is aiming to overhaul its corporate oversight laws.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/morning-agenda-icahns-fight-over-dell-heads-to-court/', 'snippet': 'Carl C. Icahn is heading to the Delaware Court of Chancery in his effort to stop a buyout of Dell. | Two private equity investors agreed on Thursday to buy the New Jersey Devils hockey team. | In the wake of scandals, India is aiming to overhaul i...', 'lead_paragraph': 'ICAHN’S FIGHT OVER DELL HEADS TO COURT \xa0|\xa0 Carl C. Icahn is heading to the Delaware Court of Chancery in his effort to stop a buyout of Dell by its founder. On Friday, the court is scheduled to consider whether to expedite Mr. Icahn’s lawsuit against the board of the computer maker. (The hearing had originally been planned for earlier this week.) Mr. Icahn is seeking to have the court schedule a hearing to consider his claims that two meetings planned for Dell — to vote on the buyout and to elect directors — should be held on the same date. Steven M. Davidoff wrote in DealBook about the case this month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Icahn’s Fight Over Dell Heads to Court', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T11:57:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d47a3c33-1de7-5a72-8163-b3d94297ef67', 'word_count': 1377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d47a3c33-1de7-5a72-8163-b3d94297ef67'}, {'abstract': 'Yelena Isinbayeva, one of Russia’s most prominent athletes, said she supported a measure that has been criticized in the West as being antigay.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/sports/global/russian-pole-vaulter-defends-law-on-homosexuality.html', 'snippet':