}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87c391a9-c660-5ee9-ab27-f9d24c9a11c7', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87c391a9-c660-5ee9-ab27-f9d24c9a11c7'}, {'abstract': 'This week, James McBride and Jeff Guinn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/08/16/books/review/18books_pod-blog.html', 'snippet': 'This week, James McBride and Jeff Guinn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, James McBride and Jeff Guinn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside The New York Times Book Review: James McBride’s ‘Good Lord Bird’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T15:27:23+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/29a3caa1-c009-5cf2-9721-df0bd01e0805', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/29a3caa1-c009-5cf2-9721-df0bd01e0805'}, {'abstract': 'After the financial crisis, real estate was generally shunned. But global demand and other factors caused farmland prices to surge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/your-money/despite-drop-in-commodity-prices-farmland-values-rise.html', 'snippet': 'After the financial crisis, real estate was generally shunned. But global demand and other factors caused farmland prices to surge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAN LINDSTROM remembers looking at a piece of Nebraska farmland six or seven years ago that cost $3,300 an acre. Raised on a farm, he ran the numbers with his brother who is farming the family land and concluded that it was too expensive. He figured that with a 2 to 3 percent return, it made more sense to put the money into a dividend-paying stock and have his brother lease additional land.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/business/17wealth-span/17wealth-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/17/business/17wealth-span/17wealth-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/business/17wealth-span/17wealth-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/business/17wealth-span/17wealth-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/business/17wealth-span/17wealth-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/17/business/17wealth-span/17wealth-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/business/17wealth-span/17wealth-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Drop in Commodity Prices, Farmland Values Rise', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Drop in Commodity Prices, Farmland Values Rise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T15:37:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/251c8451-abd2-5d90-9daa-35c39159db54', 'word_count': 1311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/251c8451-abd2-5d90-9daa-35c39159db54'}, {'abstract': 'It doesn’t matter whether the banks hold reserves.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/banks-and-the-monetary-base-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'It doesn’t matter whether the banks hold reserves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cullen Roche is unhappy with the way I treat monetary expansion in my old Japan paper (pdf); or actually he’s unhappy with the way I talk about it. I’m actually kind of reluctant to even get into this, because any discussion of these issue brings out the people who believe that they have discovered the hidden secrets of the monetary universe, somehow missed by generations of economists. But here goes anyway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Banks and the Monetary Base (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T15:39:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7017638d-0319-5f7e-aa34-0a318cba0978', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7017638d-0319-5f7e-aa34-0a318cba0978'}, {'abstract': 'Three airline mergers had gained approval since 2008, but the Justice Department has hardened its stance with a proposed union between American and US Airways.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/business/for-airlines-it-may-be-one-merger-too-many.html', 'snippet': 'Three airline mergers had gained approval since 2008, but the Justice Department has hardened its stance with a proposed union between American and US Airways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shareholders and employees of American Airlines and US Airways may well be wondering: why us?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/business/17stewart-span/18stewart-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/17/business/17stewart-span/18stewart-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/business/17stewart-span/18stewart-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 622, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/business/17stewart-span/18stewart-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1245, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/business/17stewart-span/17stewart-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legac