e, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/092c498b-4d79-5f7e-bd6f-2419af133b72', 'word_count': 1173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/092c498b-4d79-5f7e-bd6f-2419af133b72'}, {'abstract': 'We chart the success of Renzo Rosso, the co-founder of Diesel. Rosso, now worth an estimated $3 billion, was a farmer’s son who made his first pair on jeans on his mother’s sewing machine.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/by-the-numbers-king-of-the-jean-pool/', 'snippet': 'We chart the success of Renzo Rosso, the co-founder of Diesel. Rosso, now worth an estimated $3 billion, was a farmer’s son who made his first pair on jeans on his mother’s sewing machine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thirty-five years ago, Renzo Rosso co-founded Diesel, the company that almost single-handedly incited the premium denim craze. Now 57 and worth an estimated $3 billion, the farmer’s son who created his first pair of jeans on his mother’s sewing machine has expanded his empire to include fashion brands like Maison Martin Margiela, Marni and Viktor & Rolf, all under the umbrella of his parent company OTB (short for his personal motto, Only the Brave). Despite these successes, Rosso’s life is in many ways very small. Case in point: the Italian businessman owns only one home, an 18th-century Palladian villa just an hour drive from his hometown of Brugine. Of course when he wants to go further, there’s always the private jet.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '118', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'King of the Jean Pool', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'King of the Jean Pool', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jeans (Apparel)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosso, Renzo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Diesel Jeans Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T16:18:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Colman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Colman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a9306a1-1596-5716-a456-95221de49c8f', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a9306a1-1596-5716-a456-95221de49c8f'}, {'abstract': 'A. O. Scott’s review of “Lee Daniels’ The Butler.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/100000002392037/movie-review-lee-daniels-the-butler.html', 'snippet': 'A. O. Scott’s review of “Lee Daniels’ The Butler.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A. O. Scott’s review of “Lee Daniels’ The Butler.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/video-movies-thebutler-081513/video-movies-thebutler-081513-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/video-movies-thebutler-081513/video-movies-thebutler-081513-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/video-movies-thebutler-081513/video-movies-thebutler-081513-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/video-movies-thebutler-081513/video-movies-thebutler-081513-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/16/arts/video-movies-thebutler-081513/video-movies-thebutler-081513-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': "Movie Review: 'Lee Daniels' The Butler'", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Lee Daniels' The Butler (Movie)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T16:23:48+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Vijai Singh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vijai', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/20629d22-10e6-594b-a59a-721818641a6b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/20629d22-10e6-594b-a59a-721818641a6b'}, {'abstract': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/books/review/paperback-row.html', 'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IRON CURTAIN: The Crushing of Eastern Europe, 1944-1956,  by Anne Applebaum. (Anchor, $17.95.) In her Pulitzer Prize-winning “Gulag” (2003), Applebaum documented the horror of Stalin’s Soviet terror machine. Now this remarkable sequel, drawn from newly opened archives and survivor interviews, shows how the Soviet Union imposed its totalitarian will upon Eastern European nations ravaged by World War II.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paperback Row', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T16:28:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'B