and Tobago in the Port of Spain suburb of St. James, resemble how it would have looked in the late 1940s, when it was acquired by the Naipaul family. Many original furnishings and items, some described in the 1961 novel, will be on display.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calendar: Coming Events in Trinidad and Tobago; Lucas, Ohio; Charlottesville, Va.', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T17:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2cd6af3-493a-511c-bee6-f4b7e5f0a9e7', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2cd6af3-493a-511c-bee6-f4b7e5f0a9e7'}, {'abstract': 'The move clears the way for UBS to buy back a portfolio of distressed assets that were moved off the UBS books during the financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/ubs-repays-loan-it-received-during-bailout/', 'snippet': 'The move clears the way for UBS to buy back a portfolio of distressed assets that were moved off the UBS books during the financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The Swiss National Bank said Friday that a fund set up as part of UBS’s bailout five years ago had fully repaid a loan it received as part the rescue. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fund Set Up for UBS Bailout Repays Loan', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'UBS Finishes Repaying Swiss Government For Bailout', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam