'Pelengaris, Angel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Viand Cafe (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T19:06:53+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/0ee6fedb-486a-5e17-bba3-1546f28572c4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/0ee6fedb-486a-5e17-bba3-1546f28572c4'}, {'abstract': 'The Charlie Parker Jazz Festival, now in its 21st year, doesn’t always genuflect directly to its namesake.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/arts/music/spirit-of-parker-freely-inhaled.html', 'snippet': 'The Charlie Parker Jazz Festival, now in its 21st year, doesn’t always genuflect directly to its namesake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Charlie Parker Jazz Festival, now in its 21st year, doesn’t always genuflect directly to its namesake, the alto saxophonist and bebop paragon commonly known as Bird. But this year the lineage is clear. Two anchors of the lineup are Jimmy Heath, who earned the sobriquet “Little Bird” early in his career, and Lee Konitz, who became known in the same era for his stubborn independence from the Parker style. Mr. Heath, 86, will lead his big band in the premiere of a suite called “Bird Is the Word” on Friday night; Mr. Konitz, 85, will work with a quartet on Sunday afternoon. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/arts/18GUIDE2/18GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/18/arts/18GUIDE2/18GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 902}}, {'r