 son-in-law gave her a camera for Christmas. The British-born Cameron was a mother of six and religious. She was also a friend of many Victorian artists, poets and thinkers, many of whom she photographed in a dreamy, soft-focused manner that was often condemned by her contemporaries for its lack of craftsmanship. “From the first moment I handled my lens with a tender ardor,” she wrote, “and it has become to me as a living thing, with voice and memory and creative vigor.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Photographer’s ‘Tender Ardor’', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Photographer’s ‘Tender Ardor’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, Julia Margaret', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T19:15:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07fea435-58e8-58cd-ba7f-fc2851a0f9b5', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07fea435-58e8-58cd-ba7f-fc2851a0f9b5'}, {'abstract': 'Martha Graham’s 1984 version of “Le Sacre du Printemps (The Rite of Spring),” Stravinsky’s disquieting ballet, is being revived by the Martha Graham Dance Company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/arts/dance/a-classic-outrageous-still.html', 'snippet': 'Martha Graham’s 1984 version of “Le Sacre du Printemps (The Rite of Spring),” Stravinsky’s disquieting ballet, is being revived by the Martha Graham Dance Company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year marks a century of ominous springtime shudders. “Le Sacre du Printemps (The Rite of Spring),” Stravinsky’s disquieting ballet about an ancient tribe’s spring sacrifice of a young woman to appease the gods, had its premiere in 1913. Many choreographers have tackled this score, among them Martha Graham, whose 1984 version is being revived by the Martha Graham Dance Company. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/arts/18GUIDE9/18GUIDE9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/18/arts/18GUIDE9/18GUIDE9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/arts/18GUIDE9/18GUIDE9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/arts/18GUIDE9/18GUIDE9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1357, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/arts/18GUIDE9/18GUIDE9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/18/arts/18GUIDE9/18GUIDE9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/arts/18GUIDE9/18GUIDE9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Classic, Outrageous Still', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Dance', 'content_kicker': None,