ne': {'main': 'Veiled Group Shows Ease of Using Web for Attack Ads', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Veiled Group Shows Ease\r\nOf Using Web for Attacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corasaniti, Nick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citizen Truth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T21:22:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34e2a807-a544-5981-b13e-dd4ec66caaf7', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34e2a807-a544-5981-b13e-dd4ec66caaf7'}, {'abstract': 'Sgt. Kimberly D. Munley, who as a civilian police officer shot Maj. Nidal Malik Hasan during his 2009 rampage, confronted him in court on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/us/sergeant-who-shot-fort-hood-gunman-testifies-in-trial.html', 'snippet': 'Sgt. Kimberly D. Munley, who as a civilian police officer shot Maj. Nidal Malik Hasan during his 2009 rampage, confronted him in court on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KILLEEN, Tex. — The last time Sgt. Kimberly D. Munley faced Maj. Nidal Malik Hasan, they stood about eight feet apart, and each of them was holding a gun. It was shortly after 1 p.m. on Nov. 5, 2009, outside the building on the Fort Hood Army base where Major Hasan had waged a brief but deadly shooting rampage with a laser-equipped semiautomatic pistol.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sergeant Who Confronted Fort Hood Gunman Faces Him in Court', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sergeant Who Confronted Fort Hood Gunman Faces Him in Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fernandez, Manny', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hasan, Nidal Malik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Hood (Tex)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts-Martial', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Munley, Kimberly D', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T21:25:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7350803-1672-5c41-bb02-2828b53dddd5', 'word_count': 996, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7350803-1672-5c41-bb02-2828b53dddd5'}, {'abstract': '“Last Tango in Berlin,” Ute Lemper’s new show at 54 Below, uses “The Threepenny Opera” as a starting and ending point.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/arts/music/ute-lemper-in-cabaret-at-54-below.html', 'snippet': '“Last Tango in Berlin,” Ute Lemper’s new show at 54 Below, uses “The Threepenny Opera” as a starting and ending point.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Last Tango in Berlin,” the title of Ute Lemper’s, dense, fiery new show at 54 Below, refers to the disappearance of European cabaret traditions under the relentless onslaught of pop. Berlin may be the cultural capital of Europe, observed Ms. Lemper, who was born in Germany in 1963, but today it is “almost without any memory.” Genres like the caustic, cynical cabaret of Germany’s Weimar period and the more romantic French chanson are all but forgotten. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/arts/17UTE/17UTE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/17/arts/17UTE/17UTE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 698}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/arts/17UTE/17UTE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 881, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/arts/17UTE/17UTE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1762, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/arts/17UTE/17UTE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/17/arts/17UTE/17UTE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/arts/17UTE/17UTE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Corrupt World of Then, So Similar to Now', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Corrupt World of Then, So Similar to Now', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lemper, Ute', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '54 Below (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T21:25:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/29b6b9e3-63fa-517d-9493-095eca1acace', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29b6b9e3-63fa-517d-9493-095eca1acace'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for interesting and peculiar items. Friday’s selections include a review of the Steve Jobs movie and a glam profile of Marissa Mayer as the “it” chief executive.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/todays-scuttlebot-a-review-of-jobs-and-marissa-mayer-in-vogue/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for interesting and peculiar items. Friday’s selections include a review of the Steve Jobs movie and a glam profile of Marissa Mayer as the “it” chief executive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day, The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for interesting and peculiar items. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cre