{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Correa, Rafael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T21:53:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56657328-4531-579d-b334-84219203b43c', 'word_count': 591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56657328-4531-579d-b334-84219203b43c'}, {'abstract': 'The upstart company Hedley & Bennett is outfitting L.A.’s top chefs (and other leading creative professionals) with smart new smocks.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/16/by-design-the-kitchen-apron-gets-a-stylish-upgrade/', 'snippet': 'The upstart company Hedley & Bennett is outfitting L.A.’s top chefs (and other leading creative professionals) with smart new smocks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you ate only at the Los Angeles restaurants whose chefs sport Hedley & Bennett aprons, you’d be eating at some of the finest places the city has to offer. Jon Shook, Vinny Dotolo and Ludo Lefebvre use them at Trois Mec, the toughest reservation in town. Michael Voltaggio places a new order every week for Ink. Nancy Silverton sells a version of the one she uses at Mozza. And Michael Cimarusti proudly sports them at Providence, where Ellen Bennett, the aprons’ creator, works two days a week. (“I shucked 85 oysters yesterday!” she says.)', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'By Design | The Kitchen Apron Gets a Stylish Upgrade', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'By Design: Beyond The Stove: Aprons on Parade', 'name': None, 'seo': No