': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Comment on ‘Modern Mothers’ Turn to Scratch an Itch’', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T23:48:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00858b0a-180e-5ee3-b96d-8a16c9c764c4', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00858b0a-180e-5ee3-b96d-8a16c9c764c4'}, {'abstract': 'About 575 people were rescued by government vessels and small fishing boats by early Saturday morning, an official said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/world/asia/philippines-17-killed-as-ferry-and-cargo-ship-collide.html', 'snippet': 'About 575 people were rescued by government vessels and small fishing boats by early Saturday morning, an official said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' At least 24 people were killed when a passenger ferry carrying nearly 700 people collided with a cargo ship and sank in the central Philippines on Friday night, officials said. About 575 people were rescued by government vessels and small fishing boats by early Saturday, Petty Officer Joy Villegas of the Philippine Coast Guard said in a phone interview. Hundreds of people were still thought to be missing. The ferry, St. Thomas of Aquinas, was not far from shore off the island of Cebu when it collided with the cargo boat Sulpicio Express 7. “The incident was visible from the shoreline, so it was easier to respond and conduct search and rescue,” Petty Officer Villegas said. Survivors interviewed on local television said that when the ferry began listing, panicked passengers raced to the deck and leapt into the ocean as it sank. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Philippines: 24 Killed as Cargo Ship and Passenger Ferry Collide Off Coast', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Philippines: 24 Killed as Cargo Ship And Passenger Ferry Collide Off Coast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-16T23:51:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Whaley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Whaley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/846820fa-6f62-5010-b03e-0938edd09f32', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/846820fa-6f62-5010-b03e-0938edd09f32'}, {'abstract': 'Sixteen seconds before a U.P.S. cargo plane crashed on approach to the Birmingham airport, a system in the cockpit warned that the plane was descending too fast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/us/alabama-automatic-system-warned-pilots-before-ups-crash.html', 'snippet': 'Sixteen seconds before a U.P.S. cargo plane crashed on approach to the Birmingham airport, a system in the cockpit warned that the plane was descending too fast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Sixteen seconds before a U.P.S. cargo plane crashed on approach to the airport in Birmingham, Ala., on Wednesday morning, an automated system in the cockpit warned that the aircraft, an Airbus A300, was descending too fast, a member of the National Transportation Safety Board said Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Automatic System Warned Pilots Before Alabama Crash', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, '