job as Manhattan borough president and would make a fine New York City comptroller. He is not a flashy candidate and he has no measurable notoriety. But in this turbulent election season, we don’t need another celebrity office seeker.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For New York City Comptroller', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For New York City Comptroller', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stringer, Scott M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spitzer, Eliot L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Comptrollers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of the Comptroller (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T02:01:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b0fcf5d-0030-572d-8f52-3e33f8c8b4d5', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b0fcf5d-0030-572d-8f52-3e33f8c8b4d5'}, {'abstract': 'The sport’s most influential group has introduced a reform to repair racing’s much-damaged credibility.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/opinion/handicapping-dopers-at-the-racetrack.html', 'snippet': 'The sport’s most influential group has introduced a reform to repair racing’s much-damaged credibility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It turns out that the destructive and widespread doping of racehorses has become as much a concern for the $2 bettor as it is for the Jockey Club, the sport’s most influential group, which is urging far stronger safeguards to repair racing’s credibility. The club’s new opinion poll finds that as bettors handicap their choices, nearly four out of five ponder the possibility of illegal drug use, much the way they factor in a muddy track. Bettors are also making smaller wagers because of their suspicions. This a red flag from the sport’s customer base.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Handicapping Dopers at the Racetrack', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Handicapping Dopers at the Racetrack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Drug Use)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jockey Club, The', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T02:01:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a790cda-4afa-5003-aceb-7648f09e0f9e', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a790cda-4afa-5003-aceb-7648f09e0f9e'}, {'abstract': 'The government should make public its official guidance on the use of location-tracking devices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/opinion/gps-tracking-and-secret-policies.html', 'snippet': 'The government should make public its official guidance on the use of location-tracking devices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week brought fresh revelations about the National Security Agency’s sloppy and invasive collection of phone data on Americans and others, as reported first by The Washington Post. In another realm of surveillance — the government’s broad use of location tracking devices — the Justice Department was in federal court on Thursday defending its refusal to release memos containing information about its policies governing the use of GPS and other potentially invasive technologies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'GPS Tracking and Secret Policies', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'GPS Tracking and Secret Policies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weissmann, Andrew', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T02:02:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/56651540-1385-566d-b785-1ea65648d07b', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56651540-1385-566d-b785-1ea65648d07b'}, {'abstract': 'The European squad came into this week as the decided underdogs in the biennial Solheim Cup with no victories on American soil, but they took the lead by the end of the afternoon Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/sports/golf/cheers-calm-nerves-as-europe-takes-lead-in-the-solheim-cup.html', 'snippet': 'The European squad came into this week as the decided underdogs in the biennial Solheim Cup with no victories on American soil, but they took the lead by the end of the afternoon Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARKER, Colo. — Before she hit her first shot in her Solheim Cup debut, the teenager Lexi Thompson glanced up in the stands behind the tee box and made eye contact with her teammate Morgan Pressel. They exchanged nods, and shortly after — as Thompson prepared to hit — Pressel exhorted the crowd to make more noise.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/sports/Y-SOLHEIM-1/Y-SOLHEIM-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/17/sports/Y-SOLHEIM-1/Y-SOLHEIM-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/sports/Y-SOLHEIM-1/Y-SOLHEIM-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/sports/Y-SOLHEIM-1/Y-SOLHEIM-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/sports/Y-SOLHEIM-1/Y-SOLHEIM-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/17/sports/Y-SOLHEIM-1/Y-SOLHEIM-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/sports/Y-SOLHEIM-1/Y-SOLHEIM-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cheers Calm Nerves as Europe Takes Lead in the Solheim Cup', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cheers Ease Nerves, But Ruling Sours Mood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solheim Cup (Golf)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wie, Michelle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Lexi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pressel, Morgan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nordqvist, Anna', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sergas, Giulia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettersen, Suzann', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T02:03:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94caf868-4066-5010-9515-512b44e195d1', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94caf868-4066-5010-9515-512b44e195d1'}, {'abstract': 'One Republican member of the Federal Election Commission is maneuvering to keep the agency from doing its job.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/opinion/a-new-danger-to-campaign-law.html', 'snippet': 'One Republican member of the Federal Election Commission is maneuvering to keep the agency from doing its job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republican operatives are charging forward with their efforts to sabotage the Federal Election Commission in its lawful obligation to police campaign abuses. The six-member commission is evenly divided between the two parties, but the Republican vice chairman, Donald McGahn, has spent his tenure as a partisan obstructionist, adroitly engineering 3-to-3 standoff votes to block penalties and other recommendations by staff investigators who uncover abuses by big-money campaigners. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Danger to Campaign Law', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Danger to Campaign Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGahn, Donald', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Election Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T02:16:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f4c6fa9-f32a-5822-9d3c-94456d4cb170', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f4c6fa9-f32a-5822-9d3c-94456d4cb170'}, {'abstract': 'Dozens of people were killed across Egypt on Friday as supporters of the ousted President Mohamed Morsi clashed with police.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/08/16/world/middleeast/unrest-in-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'Dozens of people were killed across Egypt on Friday as supporters of the ousted President Mohamed Morsi clashed with police.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dozens of people were killed across Egypt on Friday as supporters of the ousted President Mohamed Morsi clashed with police.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/world/17egypt/17eg