rs-a-response/', 'snippet': 'It’s worthwhile to question our ardent desire to increase instrumental control over the world and ourselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I would like to thank the readers of The Stone for their insightful feedback on my recent post, “Bursting the Neuro-Utopian Bubble.” There seemed to be a few questions about my basic argument, which I will do my best to clarify here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brain Changers: A Response', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain Activity Map Project', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T03:13:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Y. Fong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': 'Y.', 'lastname': 'Fong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3408f287-4026-5b31-89e3-929fbe3c5087', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3408f287-4026-5b31-89e3-929fbe3c5087'}, {'abstract': 'The Democratic candidate William C. Thompson Jr. made a return visit to the Lincoln Houses, a public housing complex in Harlem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/nyregion/back-for-dinner-at-housing-project.html', 'snippet': 'The Democratic candidate William C. Thompson Jr. made a return visit to the Lincoln Houses, a public housing complex in Harlem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, the leading Democratic candidates for mayor expressed shock at some of the conditions at Lincoln Houses, a public housing complex in Harlem, after staying there overnight with residents at the invitation of the Rev. Al S