s in Mason, Ohio. After his win, Isner pretended to tear open his shirt to reveal a Superman logo, a celebration move he has borrowed from Cam Newton, the quarterback of the Carolina Panthers. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Djokovic and Murray Fall at the Western & Southern Open Quarterfinals', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Tennis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Isner Upsets Djokovic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rothenberg, Ben', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berdych, Tomas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isner, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy (1987- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T03:23:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1fff95a-a388-5e11-b619-515ed6de3f87', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1fff95a-a388-5e11-b619-515ed6de3f87'}, {'abstract': 'Pei-Shen Qian, a 73-year-old immigrant, is believed to have produced more than 60 works that were attributed to Modernist masters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/nyregion/struggling-immigrant-artist-tied-to-80-million-new-york-fraud.html', 'snippet': 'Pei-Shen Qian, a 73-year-old immigrant, is believed to have produced more than 60 works that were attributed to Modernist masters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pei-Shen Qian’s neighbors on 95th Street in Woodhaven, Queens, knew he scratched out a living as an artist: he often dried his paintings in the sun, propping them up on the weathered white siding of his modest house.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/nyregion/PAINTER/PAINTER-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 198, 'width': 300, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/nyregion/PAINTER/PAINTER-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 198, 'width': 300, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/nyregion/PAINTER/PAINTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/17/nyregion/PAINTER/PAINTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Struggling Immigrant Artist Tied to $80 Million New York Fraud', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Struggling Immigrant Artist Tied To $80 Million New York Fraud', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nir, Sarah Maslin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qian, Pei-Shen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forgery', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosales, Glafira', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knoedler & Co', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value