icker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isner, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T03:52:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/250a0d53-24d1-5199-8e55-0484ac5ca126', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/250a0d53-24d1-5199-8e55-0484ac5ca126'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees’ Alex Rodriguez made his first appearance in Boston this season, and the reception by Red Sox fans was loud and fierce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/sports/baseball/back-at-fenway-rodriguez-is-met-with-fervent-booing.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees’ Alex Rodriguez made his first appearance in Boston this season, and the reception by Red Sox fans was loud and fierce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — As Alex Rodriguez stepped into the batter’s box Friday night, he seemed unfazed by the crowd’s jeers. The boos were low-pitched and from the gut, as if the louder the crowd booed, the more it would hurt. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Back at Fenway, Rodriguez Is Met With Fervent Booing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back at Fenway, Rodriguez Is Met With Fervent Booing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T04:50:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0677c63d-0289-59a1-91be-42752676c778', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0677c63d-0289-59a1-91be-42752676c778'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:30 P.M. (HBO) ANNA KARENINA (2012) Keira Knightley, above, stars as Anna, the bored wife of a virtuous government official (Jude Law) in mid-19th-century Imperial Russia, who travels from St. Petersburg to Moscow to calm a marital storm in the household of her philandering brother (Matthew Macfadyen) in Joe Wright’s stagy adaptation of the Tolstoy novel. Aaron Taylor-Johnson plays the man who captures her heart: Count Vronsky, a young military officer with the eyes of a poet and a domineering mother (Olivia Williams). And Alicia Vikander is Kitty, a lovely young woman adored by Levin, the gloomy rural landowner (Domhnall Gleeson) widely understood to be Tolstoy’s alter ego, with his idea of love — an ennobling union of souls — serving as a rebuke to the amorality festering in cities. “I assume you know that it ends badly, but Mr. Wright’s real interest, like Tolstoy’s, is in everything that happens in between Anna’s first meeting with Vronsky and her final encounter with the wheels of a train,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. And while Mr. Wright’s screen versions of Jane Austen’s “Pride and Prejudice” and Ian McEwan’s “Atonement” “remain trapped in literariness,” he added, “Mr. Wright’s ‘Anna Karenina’ is different. It is risky and ambitious enough to count as an act of artistic hubris, and confident enough to triumph on its own slightly — wonderfully — crazy terms. Pious Tolstoyans may knit their brows about the stylistic liberties Mr. Wright and the screenwriter, Tom Stoppard, have taken, but surely Tolstoy can withstand (and may indeed benefit from) their playful, passionate rendering of his masterpiece.” Jacqueline Durran won an Oscar for costume design.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/df5aa440-b8ab-534b-a0ac-328c1a0a2d42', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df5aa440-b8ab-534b-a0ac-328c1a0a2d42'}, {'abstract': 'Marlon Byrd, Ike Davis and Daniel Murphy each homered, and Jon Niese allowed only one run in a Mets victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/sports/baseball/niese-limits-padres-as-mets-flash-power.html', 'snippet': 'Marlon Byrd, Ike Davis and Daniel Murphy each homered, and Jon Niese allowed only one run in a Mets victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — Week after week, the frustrating outings piled up, the fastball velocity dipped and the earned run average ticked upward. It was not the Jon Niese that the Mets were accustomed to seeing, the one they hoped to see in the future. Something was not right. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Resurgent Niese Limits Padres as Mets Flash Power', 'kicker': 'Mets 5, Padres 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Resurgent Niese Limits Padres as Mets Flash Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Diego Padres', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Ike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byrd, Marlon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Niese, Jon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Daniel (1985- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T05:53:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0a3aa11-e396-5763-9107-39a7502117bc', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0a3aa11-e396-5763-9107-39a7502117bc'}, {'abstract': 'Programming pitches for the first channel for dogs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/opinion/sunday/tv-for-dogs.html', 'snippet': 'Programming pitches for the first channel for dogs.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The first channel for dogs, available through DirectTV and online, entertains dogs home alone with scientifically developed behavior patterns, movements, and sounds from a dog’s perspective.”  ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TV for Dogs', 'kicker': 'Loose Ends', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'TV for Dogs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DogTV', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T06:17:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Freeman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Freeman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/73154cbc-acc3-549e-8eb1-bd2aaabaad12', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73154cbc-acc3-549e-8eb1-bd2aaabaad12'}, {'abstract': 'Yang Maodong, better known by his pen name, Guo Feixiong, is the second well-known member of China’s “rights defense” movement to be arrested in recent weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/world/asia/well-known-dissident-is-detained-in-southern-china.html', 'snippet': 'Yang Maodong, better known by his pen name, Guo Feixiong, is the second well-known member of China’s “rights defense” movement to be arrested in recent weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The police in southern China have detained an outspoken advocate of democratic rights on charges of disrupting public order, his lawyer and human rights groups said Saturday. They called his detention another step in a government effort to stifle dissidents who have challenged the Communist Party over censorship and officials’ wealth.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prominent Advocate Held in Southern China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prominent Advocate Held in Southern China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yang Maodong', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chinese Human Rights Defenders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T08:21:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09dd82a1-4322-5055-b75f-a0ceb69ab10e', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09dd82a1-4322-5055-b75f-a0ceb69ab10e'}, {'abstract': 'The Amazon founder has often faced doubts about his strategy and the company’s prospects. As a companion to a major profile this weekend, some previous articles trace his achievements and his image through the years.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/jeff-bezos-a-brief-anthology/', 'snippet': 'The Amazon founder has often faced doubts about his strategy and the company’s prospects. As a companion to a major profile this weekend, some previous articles trace his achievements and his image through the years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the years since Amazon.com sold its first book online in 1995, JeffBezos has often faced doubts about his strategy and the company’s prospects — even as it became a giant force in retailing and Mr. Bezos built a personal fortune. As a companion to a major profile this weekend by David Streitfeld and Christine Haughney, here is a sampler of previous articles tracing what he has accomplished and how he has been perceived.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/technology/17bits-bezos-1998/17bits-bezos-1998-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/17/technology/17bits-bezos-1998/17bits-bezos-1998-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/technology/17bits-bezos-1998/17bits-bezos-1998-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/technology/17bits-bezos-1998/17bits-bezos-1998-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/technology/17bits-bezos-1998/17bits-bezos-1998-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/17/technology/17bits-bezos-1998/17bits-bezos-1998-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/17/technology/17bits-bezos-1998/17bits-bezos-1998-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeff Bezos: A Brief Anthology', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bezos, Jeffrey P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T09:17:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d855cd8d-90c5-533c-968d-01f6f576b10d', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d855cd8d-90c5-533c-968d-01f6f576b10d'}, {'abstract': 'A standoff between supporters of the ousted president, Mohamed Morsi, and soldiers at a mosque ended with no reports of casualties, but it was emblematic of Egypt’s wider chaos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/world/middleeast/standoff-in-cairo-as-security-forces-surround-mosque.html', 'snippet': 'A standoff between supporters of the ousted president, Mohamed Morsi, and soldiers at a mosque ended with no reports of casualties, but it was emblematic of Egypt’s wider chaos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Soldiers fired on a Cairo mosque on Saturday where supporters of the ousted president, Mohamed Morsi, had taken shelter, briefly turning a central thoroughfare into a war zone in a further sign that Egypt’s new military rulers are struggling to impose order days after security forces killed hundreds of antigovernment Islamists.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/world/sub-cairo1/sub-cairo1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/18/world/sub-cairo1/sub-cairo1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/world/sub-cairo1/sub-cairo1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/world/sub-cairo1/sub-cairo1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1357, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/world/sub-cairo1/sub-cairo1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/18/world/sub-cairo1/sub-cairo1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/world/sub-cairo1/sub-cairo1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Soldiers Storm a Mosque in Cairo, as Egyptian Leaders Struggle for Order', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Soldiers Storm a Mosque in Cairo, as Egyptian Leaders Struggle for Order', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahim, Kareem', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheikh, Mayy El', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T10:43:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim and Mayy El Sheikh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mayy', 'middlename': 'El', 'lastname': 'Sheikh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c67d1900-87f1-500c-8f30-724ba053ef37', 'word_count': 990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c67d1900-87f1-500c-8f30-724ba053ef37'}, {'abstract': 'At City Winery in New York City, June celebrated the release of her album “Pushin’ Against a Stone,” announcing it was time “do the dadgum song already!”', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/valerie-june-follows-the-mississippi-from-memphis-to-manhattan/', 'snippet': 'At City Winery in New York City, June celebrated the release of her album “Pushin’ Against a Stone,” announcing it was time “do the dadgum song already!”', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are few people in the world today who could get away with saying “dadgum.” Fewer still who could get away with saying it onstage at a wine bar in SoHo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Valerie June Follows the Mississippi from Memphis to Manhattan', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T12:02:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Vecsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vecsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd95744e-9479-5a02-978a-c127404f4e0f', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd95744e-9479-5a02-978a-c127404f4e0f'}, {'abstract': 'Proust called the vanished past “lost time,” but what would he make of a world where everything is stored forever? Without thinking about it, as we record everything we lose some things, too.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/whats-lost-when-everything-is-recorded/', 'snippet': 'Proust called the vanished past “lost time,” but what would he make of a world where everything is stored forever? Without thinking about it, as we record everything we lose some things, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While we fret about losing privacy and other dangers of the digital revolution, one sad change is happening with little notice: Our technology is stealing the romance of old conversations, that quaint notion that some things are best forgotten.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/business/17bits-memory/17bits-memory-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/18/business/17bits-memory/17bits-memory-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/business/17bits-memory/17bits-memory-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/business/17bits-memory/17bits-memory-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1382, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/business/17bits-memory/17bits-memory-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandar