aec6629-4cb7-5a68-b840-70b95bbb112f'}, {'abstract': 'Nurse understaffing is a growing problem in America’s hospitals.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/17/when-no-one-is-on-call/', 'snippet': 'Nurse understaffing is a growing problem in America’s hospitals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We nurses all have stories — if we’re lucky, it’s just one — about the time we failed a patient. It’s usually a problem of being too busy: too many cases, too many procedures to keep track of until one critical step, just one, slips through our frenetic fingers and someone gets hurt.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When No One Is on Call', 'kicker': 'Bedside', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When No One Is on Call', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T18:27:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Theresa Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Theresa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4931615-4e63-5e20-ad1f-e328b4993a85', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4931615-4e63-5e20-ad1f-e328b4993a85'}, {'abstract': 'An economist says his own experience in starting a business has helped shape his thinking on the subject of capitalism and culture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/business/why-innovation-is-still-capitalisms-star.html', 'snippet': 'An economist says his own experience in starting a business has helped shape his thinking on the subject of capitalism and culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAPITALISM is culture. To sustain it, laws and institutions are important, but the more fundamental role is played by the basic human spirit of independence and initiative.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/business/18-VIEW/18-VIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/18/business/18-VIEW/18-VIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 452}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/business/18-VIEW/18-VIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 772, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/business/18-VIEW/18-VIEW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1468, 'width': 1947, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/business/18-VIEW/18-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/18/business/18-VIEW/18-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/business/18-VIEW/18-VIEW-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Innovation Is Still Capitalism’s Star', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Innovation Is Still Capitalism’s Star', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shiller, Robert J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phelps, Edmund S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crowdfunding (Internet)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capitalism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T18:29:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert J. Shiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Shiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3c34421-50ca-560f-8cce-581d0c5e0374', 'word_count': 1256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3c34421-50ca-560f-8cce-581d0c5e0374'}, {'abstract': 'Returning to the States after living in Britain for 17 years, a Times correspondent reflects on changes here and there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/opinion/sunday/ta-ta-london-hello-awesome.html', 'snippet': 'Returning to the States after living in Britain for 17 years, a Times correspondent reflects on changes here and there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVEN after 18 years, I never really knew where I stood with the English. Why did they keep apologizing? (Were they truly sorry?) Why were they so unenthusiastic about enthusiasm? Why was their Parliament full of classically educated grown-ups masquerading as unruly schoolchildren? ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/sunday-review/18LYALL/18LYALL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 911, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/18/sunday-review/18LYALL/18LYALL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 911}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/sunday-review/18LYALL/18LYALL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 675, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/sunday-review/18LYALL/18LYALL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1661, 'width': 1094, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/sunday-review/18LYALL/18LYALL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/18/sunday-review/18LYALL/18LYALL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/sunday-review/18LYALL/18LYALL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ta-Ta, London. Hello, Awesome.', 'kicker': 'Dispatch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ta-Ta, London. Hello, Awesome.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyall, Sarah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Americans Abroad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T18:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/35e3f73d-2859-5fc9-94e2-4b10d26c6c13', 'word_count': 1588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35e3f73d-2859-5fc9-94e2-4b10d26c6c13'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Christie, Ted Cruz and Rand Paul may be grabbing headlines, but Jeb Bush shouldn’t be forgotten, least of all by Republicans concerned about the party’s health.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/opinion/sunday/bruni-the-pasts-future-republican.html', 'snippet': 'Chris Christie, Ted Cruz and Rand Paul may be grabbing headlines, but Jeb Bush shouldn’t be forgotten, least of all by Republicans concerned about the party’s health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LET Rand Paul have his epic filibuster and Ted Cruz his scowling threats to shut down the government. Let Chris Christie thunder to a second term as the governor of New Jersey, his hubris flowering as his ultimate designs on the White House take shape.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'