ch a step would have struck financial analysts and consumers as outlandish — as outlandish, say, as the idea that people might stop using Google or Facebook.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tech Love Isn’t Forever', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tech Love Isn’t Forever', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bajaj, Vikas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BlackBerry (Handheld Device)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BlackBerry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T19:02:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae59883d-ffc8-5228-8011-7a28f481824d', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae59883d-ffc8-5228-8011-7a28f481824d'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers are lining up for a chance to take money from the banks — and do their bidding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/opinion/sunday/the-cash-committee.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers are lining up for a chance to take money from the banks — and do their bidding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The House Financial Services Committee has grown so large that a highly unusual fourth row of seats had to be installed in the committee room. Every term, scores of members, particularly freshmen, demand a seat on the panel — not because they have a burning interest in regulating banks and Wall Street, but because they know that they will be able raise much more money if one of the 61 seats has their name on it.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cash Committee', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cash Committee', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Financial Services Committee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotton, Tom', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barr, Andy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T19:04:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/fde145d2-797d-5140-9c83-dfa72d035ca7', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fde145d2-797d-5140-9c83-dfa72d035ca7'}, {'abstract': 'Proposed changes could help revive Mexico’s energy sector and give its economy a much-needed lift.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/opinion/sunday/foreign-investment-in-mexican-oil.html', 'snippet': 'Proposed changes could help revive Mexico’s energy sector and give its economy a much-needed lift.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Enrique Peña Nieto of Mexico proposed ambitious constitutional reforms last week that would allow foreigners to invest in Mexico’s nationalized oil industry for the first time in 75 years. Such a change could help revive the country’s energy sector and give its economy a much-needed lift.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Foreign Investment in Mexican Oil', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Foreign Investment in Mexican Oil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pena Nieto, Enrique', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pemex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T19:04:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d23a1603-0014-53be-8944-b9e1c5e8f454', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d23a1603-0014-53be-8944-b9e1c5e8f454'}, {'abstract': 'Tampa Bay Rays Manager Joe Maddon allows his players vast freedom in the clubhouse, which Luke Scott uses to decorate his locker in an unusual fashion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/18/sports/baseball/where-spear-and-boar-meet-bat-and-glove-in-rays-clubhouse.html', 'snippet': 'Tampa Bay Rays Manager Joe Maddon allows his players vast freedom in the clubhouse, which Luke Scott uses to decorate his locker in an unusual fashion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. — Most baseball players use their lockers for gear: mitts, bats and jerseys. Luke Scott, an outfielder and designated hitter with the Tampa Bay Rays, uses his to display a mounted boar’s head.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/sports/dogLUKE2/dogLUKE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/18/sports/dogLUKE2/dogLUKE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/sports/dogLUKE2/dogLUKE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/sports/dogLUKE2/dogLUKE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/sports/dogLUKE2/dogLUKE2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/18/sports/dogLUKE2/dogLUKE2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/18/sports/dogLUKE2/dogLUKE2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Spear and Boar Meet Bat and Glove', 'kicker': None, 'con