aph': 'MOGADISHU, Somalia — A technician for the state-run broadcaster Radio Mogadishu was murdered on Saturday, the sixth media employee killed so far this year in Somalia. Separately, in the first such execution in Somalia, a man found guilty of killing a journalist last year was executed by firing squad.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Radio Station Employee Is Shot Dead in Somalia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Radio Station Employee Is Shot Dead in Somalia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kulish, Nicholas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radio Mogadishu', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-17T22:24:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mohamed Ibrahim and Nicholas Kulish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mohamed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ibrahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf468dcd-578b-5612-b48d-9013caf6040b', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf468dcd-578b-5612-b48d-9013caf6040b'}, {'abstract': 'A Texas law requiring DNA analysis of all biological evidence in death penalty cases could add t