n today’s puzzle, constructor Jean O’Conor riffs on the many meanings of one common English word by demonstrating the myriad ways it can be used. For a single four-letter word with only three unique letters, it’s got plenty of versatility – my edition of Webster’s spouts off 51 definitions – and the six examples that Jean uses show its diverse denotations in action. After all, it’s not readily apparent that there’s a verbal link between POPPY SEEDS and WALLPAPER. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off to a Good Start', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-18T22:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Gaffney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gaffney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1418897-ac7c-5471-b1ad-534ad9350ae2', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1418897-ac7c-5471-b1ad-534ad9350ae2'}, {'abstract': 'Genteel towns in the Litchfield Hills of Connecticut are shocked by charges against Jasper Johns’s assistant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/arts/design/community-shock-at-accusations-against-jasper-johnss-aide.html', 'snippet': 'Genteel towns in the Litchfield Hills of Connecticut are shocked by charges against Jasper Johns’s assistant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For 16 years, William Morrison has watched the passing parade at his airy, contemporary Morrison Gallery in Kent, in northwestern Connecticut, where luminaries like Meryl Streep, Sam Waterston, Kevin Bacon and Kate Winslet, and far-flung artists great and small live the understated good life of the Litchfield Hills.'