ank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0eaacd77-18cf-55db-92f1-8742caefdab4', 'word_count': 1515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0eaacd77-18cf-55db-92f1-8742caefdab4'}, {'abstract': 'Kasper Konig, a Berlin curator who has defended art against censorship by conservatives, has been named chief curator of the 10th edition of Manifesta, the roving European contemporary art biennial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/arts/design/manifesta-curator-named.html', 'snippet': 'Kasper Konig, a Berlin curator who has defended art against censorship by conservatives, has been named chief curator of the 10th edition of Manifesta, the roving European contemporary art biennial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kasper Konig, a Berlin curator who has defended art against censorship by conservatives, has been named chief curator of the 10th edition of Manifesta, the roving European contemporary art biennial. This year the event is to be held in Russia for the first time, just as the country’s treatment of gay men and women is being criticized internationally. Manifesta 10 is to be held in St. Petersburg from June 28 to Oct. 31, 2014, with activities centered in the restored contemporary art wing of the State Hermitage, Russia’s most important museum, which is in the former Winter Palace of the czars. The museum will be celebrating its 250th anniversary, and Manifesta will be recognizing its 20th as a post-cold-war platform for cultural dialogue.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Manifesta Curator Named', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Manifesta Curator Named', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kishkovsky, Sophia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Konig, Kasper', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-18T22:18:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sophia Kishkovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sophia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kishkovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d29a88c2-05cc-579a-bdf0-621d502ec00a', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d29a88c2-05cc-579a-bdf0-621d502ec00a'}, {'abstract': 'The British architect Norman Foster has resigned from a proposed expansion of the Pushkin Museum of Fine Arts in Moscow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/arts/design/project-in-moscow-loses-norman-foster.html', 'snippet': 'The British architect Norman Foster has resigned from a proposed expansion of the Pushkin Museum of Fine Arts in Moscow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British architect Norman Foster has resigned from a proposed expansion of the Pushkin Museum of Fine Arts in Moscow. The plan was to expand and modernize the 101-year-old institution and had an estimated cost of $670 million. The project was approved by the Russian government in 2009, but it stalled over disputes between Russian officials and preservationists, according to The Art Newspaper. The architecture firm Foster & Partners released a statement last week that said Mr. Foster, above, had sent a resignation letter in June to Irina Antonova, the former director of the Pushkin. “Foster & Partners took this action because the museum, for the last three years, has not involved us in the development of the project, which was being carried out by others,” the statement said. Ms. Antonova resigned in July as museum director, a post she held for more than 50 years. She was said to have supported Mr. Foster’s involvement.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Project in Moscow Loses Norman Foster', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Project in Moscow Loses Norman Foster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foster, Norman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pushkin Museum of Fine Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-18T22:20:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/86814f4c-c146-506b-9af3-a7394ec40518', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86814f4c-c146-506b-9af3-a7394ec40518'}, {'abstract': 'The Fishbein Trophy is presented to the player who wins the most master points at the Summer North American Championships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/crosswords/bridge/mark-itabashi-wins-fishbein-trophy-in-atlanta.html', 'snippet': 'The Fishbein Trophy is presented to the player who wins the most master points at the Summer North American Championships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — The Fishbein Trophy is presented to the player who wins the most master points at the Summer North American Championships. This year’s was awarded to Mark Itabashi of Murrieta, Calif. He won two major national championships, the von Zedtwitz Life Master Pairs and the Truscott/United States Playing Card Senior Swiss Teams to finish 45.69 points head of Jacek Kalita and Michal Nowosadzki from Poland. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/19/crosswords/bridge/19card/19card-jumbo.gif', 'height': 500, 'width': 246, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/19/crosswords/bridge/19card/19card-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 500, 'width': 246, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/19/crosswords/bridge/19card/19card-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/19/crosswords/bridge/19card/19card-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/19/crosswords/bridge/19card/19card-thumbLarge.gif', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mark Itabashi Wins Fishbein Trophy in Atlanta', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-18T22:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_o