section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Heller-Roazen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heller-Roazen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c68e770-bfdf-5753-827a-4a6f55c81d3c', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c68e770-bfdf-5753-827a-4a6f55c81d3c'}, {'abstract': 'Xu Zhiyong’s fight made him one of China’s best-known human rights advocates, and it has now landed him in prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/opinion/misrule-of-law.html', 'snippet': 'Xu Zhiyong’s fight made him one of China’s best-known human rights advocates, and it has now landed him in prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'XU ZHIYONG, a lawyer for the underprivileged, knew he risked his freedom by challenging the Chinese Communist Party to fulfill its vows to fight corruption and promote the rule of law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Misrule of Law', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Misrule Of Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xu Zhiyong', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hua Ze', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T01:03:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hua Ze', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ze', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7acd146e-34b5-5a04-aa3f-91e75bcb6109', 'word_count': 862, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7acd146e-34b5-5a04-aa3f-91e75bcb6109'}, {'abstract': 'The F.B.I. needs to be held to a higher standard when reporting on criminal histories in work-related background checks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/opinion/a-flawed-background-check-system.html', 'snippet': 'The F.B.I. needs to be held to a higher standard when reporting on criminal histories in work-related background checks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Federal Trade Commission has rightly intensified scrutiny of the companies that provide the criminal background checks used by most firms and corporations to screen job applicants. In too many cases, the reports are out of date and incomplete, causing job seekers who may have been arrested but never charged — or who have had their cases expunged or even dismissed — to be unfairly locked out of the job market. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Flawed Background-Check System', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Flawed Background-Check System', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Employment Law Project', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T01:05:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/98fa1ad1-93a8-51a8-96ba-c455c3234500', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98fa1ad1-93a8-51a8-96ba-c455c3234500'}, {'abstract': 'The families of those killed in the building collapse are still waiting for adequate compensation from the government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/opinion/bangladeshs-workers-deserve-better.html', 'snippet': 'The families of those killed in the building collapse are still waiting for adequate compensation from the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four months after a building collapse killed more than 1,100 factory workers in Bangladesh, their families are still waiting for adequate — and in some cases, any — compensation. This is a shocking lapse by Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina and her government. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bangladesh’s Workers Deserve Better', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bangladesh’s Workers Deserve Better', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hasina, Sheikh', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rana Plaza Building Collapse, Bangladesh (2013)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reparations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T01:06:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a123032-b2bc-5889-ab03-9702b3297215', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a123032-b2bc-5889-ab03-9702b3297215'}, {'abstract': 'Candidates for mayor should promise to extend Bloomberg’s environmental record.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/opinion/wanted-another-green-mayor.html', 'snippet': 'Candidates for mayor should promise to extend Bloomberg’s environmental record.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York has been a dirty, gritty city practically forever, but it has also had farsighted leaders who qualify as green visionaries, going back to the 19th century. They preserved valuable real estate as irreplaceable public parkland; dreamed up an astonishing system of aqueducts to carry clean mountain water, unpumped and unfiltered, to city taps; and built a walkable, ridable, electric-train metropolis generations before “smart growth” and “transit-oriented development” were buzzwords.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wanted: Another Green Mayor', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wanted: Another Green Mayor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, William C Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T01:06:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/48daec8d-1043-56ea-8772-df1cd7638956', 'word_count': 644, 