.com/2013/08/19/when-you-promote-someone-and-it-doesnt-work-out/', 'snippet': 'Can you return someone to their old job?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I recently received the following question from a reader. It came in response to a post I had written about what I called the difference between human resources happy (a focus on superficial things like Ping Pong tables) and high-performance happy (a focus on the mission).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When You Promote Someone and It Doesn’t Work Out', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T11:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cliff Oxford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cliff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oxford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/475a7367-407a-585d-8391-f039c9520552', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/475a7367-407a-585d-8391-f039c9520552'}, {'abstract': 'An inquiry examines whether JPMorgan Chase hired the children of Chinese officials to help win business. | Some public funds are moving to reduce their reliance on the Wall Street. | SAC Capital Advisors is preparing to become leaner. | The latest deal by Alibaba may raise some eyebrows.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/morning-agenda-jpmorgan-faces-bribery-inquiry-over-china/', 'snippet': 'An inquiry examines whether JPMorgan Chase hired the children of Chinese officials to help win business. | Some public funds are moving to reduce their reliance on the Wall Street. | SAC Capital Advisors is preparing to become leaner. | The latest...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal authorities have opened a bribery investigation into whether JPMorgan Chase hired the children of Chinese officials to help the bank win business, Jessica Silver-Greenberg, Ben Protess and David Barboza report in DealBook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan Faces Bribery Inquiry Over China', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T11:36:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40344c71-9efd-5e8e-a9b3-683e02a70d6d', 'word_count': 1661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40344c71-9efd-5e8e-a9b3-683e02a70d6d'}, {'abstract': 'The commission said it would send inspectors, and it warned Spain not to start charging people for crossing into the British territory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/world/europe/british-warship-arrives-in-gibraltar.html', 'snippet': 'The commission said it would send inspectors, and it warned Spain not to start charging people for crossing into the British territory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — The European Commission on Monday stepped into a dispute between Britain and Spain over Gibraltar, the British territory at the tip of the Iberian Peninsula, saying that it would soon send inspectors there and warning Madrid not to raise tensions further by charging people for crossing into the territory.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/world/20gibraltar/20gibraltar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, '