ks by Joel and Ethan Coen, Hayao Miyazaki, Richard Curtis, J. C. Chandor and James Franco are among the features that will be presented in the main slate of the New York Film Festival, the Film Society of Lincoln Center said on Monday. That roster includes “Inside Llewyn Davis,” the Coen brothers’ look at a fictional folk singer in 1960s New York; “The Wind Rises,” the first animated feature directed by Mr. Miyazaki in five years; “About Time,” a romantic comedy that Mr. Curtis (“Four Weddings and a Funeral”) says will be his swan song; “All Is Lost,” Mr. Chandor’s film starring Robert Redford as a yachtsman adrift in the Indian Ocean; and “Child of God,” Mr. Franco’s adaptation of the Cormac McCarthy novel.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/cannes2/cannes2-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/cannes2/cannes2-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/cannes2/cannes2-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/cannes2/cannes2-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/cannes2/cannes2-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/05/20/arts/cannes2/cannes2-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumb