nnipeg. In a statement, Stephen Tobin, owner of Drop Entertainment Group, which is producing the events, said the decision was made “in light of the performer’s recent personal and health-related issues.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chris Brown Cancels Concerts After Probation Ruling', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T18:23:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel McDermon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDermon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e63b2d2a-d2c1-59a9-9dc8-c59c42f34d01', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e63b2d2a-d2c1-59a9-9dc8-c59c42f34d01'}, {'abstract': 'The panel found that human activity is almost certainly behind most temperature increases in recent decades.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/science/earth/extremely-likely-that-human-activity-is-driving-climate-change-panel-finds.html', 'snippet': 'The panel found that human activity is almost certainly behind most temperature increases in recent decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An international panel of scientists has found with near certainty that human activity is the cause of most of the temperature increases of recent decades, and warns that sea levels could conceivably rise by more than three feet by the end of the century if emissions continue at a runaway pace.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20