 of other women,” according to Erin Thornton, its executive director, who happens to be expecting right now herself. “To this day, hundreds of thousands of women will die in pregnancy and childbirth, but 90 percent of those could be prevented just with basic, simple access to health care.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Christy Turlington Burns and Citizens of Humanity Promote Maternal Health', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, Christy Turlington', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Every Mother Counts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T19:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca80523a-9f69-5bde-bde1-6f0725df38ce', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca80523a-9f69-5bde-bde1-6f0725df38ce'}, {'abstract': 'The mayor of the Brazilian city is offering to fully finance a Woody Allen film, if production takes place there.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/rio-de-janeiro-makes-woody-allen-an-offer/', 'snippet': 'The mayor of the Brazilian city is offering to fully finance a Woody Allen film, if production takes place there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apparently Rio de Janeiro is not satisfied with being chosen as the site of the 2016 Summer Olympics and the host of the championship game of next year’s World Cup of soccer. Now Brazil’s most effervescent city also wants Woody Allen to make a movie there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rio de Janeiro Makes Wo