ing beds are widely believed to have played a large role in the increasing rates of skin cancer in recent decades. The most serious type,\xa0melanoma, has risen sharply among young white women in particular.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/health/well_awareness/well_awareness-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 217, 'width': 219, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/health/well_awareness/well_awareness-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 217, 'width': 219, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/health/well_awareness/well_awareness-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/07/health/well_awareness/well_awareness-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/07/health/well_awareness/well_awareness-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Indoor Tanning Remains Popular, Despite Risks', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Awareness: Studentsu2019 Use of Tanning Beds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Melanomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suntan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T20:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fcd8470-91d6-51cc-8aeb-5f213a33a1e6', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fcd8470-91d6-51cc-8aeb-5f213a33a1e6'}, {'abstract': 'The Egyptian government has acknowledged killing 36 Islamists in its custody on Sunday, and an attack by suspected militants in the Sinai peninsula left at least 24 police officers dead.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/video-and-images-of-killings-in-egypt/', 'snippet': 'The Egyptian government has acknowledged killing 36 Islamists in its custody on Sunday, and an attack by suspected militants in the Sinai peninsula left at least 24 police officers dead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, 5:38 p.m. | As our colleagues David Kirkpatrick and Rod Nordland report from Cairo, Egypt has seen two grisly mass killings in the last 24 hours. The government has acknowledged killing 36 Islamist prisoners in its custody under circumstances that remain unclear, and an attack by suspected militants in a remote corner of the Sinai peninsula left at least 24 police officers dead and 3 injured. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egyptians Share Gruesome Images of Dead Prisoners and Soldiers', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T20:04:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack and Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1bb3794-96f4-5928-bbe9-5a7ea1061726', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1bb3794-96f4-5928-bbe9-5a7ea1061726'}, {'abstract': 'With rare exceptions, it is hard to think of a single truly novel psychotropic drug that has emerged in the last 30 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/health/a-dry-pipeline-for-psychiatric-drugs.html', 'snippet': 'With rare exceptions, it is hard to think of a single truly novel psychotropic drug that has emerged in the last 30 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fully 1 in 5 Americans take at least one psychiatric medication. Yet when it comes to mental health, we are facing a crisis in drug innovation.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/science/20MIND_SPAN/20MIND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/20/science/20MIND_SPAN/20MIND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/science/20MIND_SPAN/20MIND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/science/20MIND_SPAN/20MIND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1620, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's