o teams of researchers devised a method for teleporting small bits of information. And a wounded $600 million telescope is like a shopping cart with a broken wheel, says NASA. Onward and upward.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Progress in Quest for a Reusable Rocket, and Teleporting Data', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quenqua, Douglas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rocket Science and Propulsion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Holes (Space)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Spaceflight', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Space Exploration Technologies Corp', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kepler Space Telescope', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T20:28:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Quenqua', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quenqua', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54de076a-6f97-5048-9e99-a1e5e83c6079', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54de076a-6f97-5048-9e99-a1e5e83c6079'}, {'abstract': 'The party’s soul-searching phase is over. Republicans are back to denouncing every utterance that strays from right-wing orthodoxy.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/g-o-p-purity-control/', 'snippet': 'The party’s soul-searching phase is over. Republicans are back to denouncing every utterance that strays from right-wing orthodoxy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After losing the 2012 election the G.O.P. engaged in a bit of soul-searching, and talked publicly about changing their image, if not their policies. That phase is definitively over. The Republicans are back to denouncing every utterance that strays from an absolutely rigid right-wing orthodoxy, and even ones that really don’t.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Purity Control', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Ted', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Priebus, Reince R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T20:31:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfc3563b-b8dc-5297-acd0-c93746fa0b8f', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfc3563b-b8dc-5297-acd0-c93746fa0b8f'}, {'abstract': 'Defense Secretary Chuck Hagel speaks about the United States’ relationship with Egypt after days of intense violence there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/100000002395628/hagel-on-egypt-at-the-pentagon.html', 'snippet': 'Defense Secretary Chuck Hagel speaks about the United States’ relationship with Egypt after days of intense violence there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Defense Secretary Chuck Hagel speaks about the United States’ relationship with Egypt after days of intense violence there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/19/world/video-hagel-china/video-hagel-china-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/19/world/video-hagel-china/video-hagel-china-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/19/world/video-hagel-china/video-hagel-china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/19/world/video-hagel-china/video-hagel-china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/19/world/video-hagel-china/video-hagel-china-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hagel on Egypt at the Pentagon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagel, Chuck', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T20:34:44+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/f06c25e4-1f00-594a-85e5-3e20a5fb405f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/f06c25e4-1f00-594a-85e5-3e20a5fb405f'}, {'abstract': 'Defense lawyers said Pfc. Bradley Manning, who awaits sentencing for his role in disclosing government documents to WikiLeaks, could once again be a productive member of society.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/us/mannings-lawyers-urge-a-lenient-sentence.html', 'snippet': 'Defense lawyers said Pfc. Bradley Manning, who awaits sentencing for his role in disclosing government documents to WikiLeaks, could once again be a productive member of society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT MEADE, Md. — Pfc. Bradley Manning’s defense lawyers on Monday made a last-minute personal plea to the military judge hearing his court-martial, asking her to be lenient in sentencing and to allow Private Manning a chance to rehabilitate himself. A prosecutor in the case urged a 60-year sentence for disclosing hundreds of thousands of documents to WikiLeaks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Sentencing Hearing, Lawyers for Manning Urge Leniency', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Sentencing Hearing, Lawyers For Manning Urge Leniency', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Bradley E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huetteman, Emmarie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coombs, David E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank