ter over how much it was willing to pay for books.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/business/media/simon-schuster-and-barnes-noble-reach-a-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Barnes & Noble, the nation’s largest book chain, had been locked in a disagreement with Simon & Schuster over how much it was willing to pay for books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a dispute over terms that stretched for most of the year, Simon & Schuster and Barnes & Noble said in a joint statement on Monday that they had “resolved their outstanding business issues.” Both parties “look forward to promoting great books by Simon & Schuster authors,” they said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Simon & Schuster and Barnes & Noble Reach a Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Simon & Schuster Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barnes & Noble Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T20:55:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0245ddc8-59aa-57fc-88dc-ade1f0c5360e', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0245ddc8-59aa-57fc-88dc-ade1f0c5360e'}, {'abstract': 'The Petersen Automotive Museum announced that its building would get a striking new facade by early 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/petersen-automotive-museum-announces-exterior-redesign/', 'snippet': 'The Petersen Automotive Museum announced that its building would get a striking new facade by early 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PEBBLE BEACH, Calif. – Not long after it began liquidating nearly a third of the 400 cars in its collection, the Petersen Automotive Museum in Los Angeles announced a major exterior redesign of the museum Sunday at a news conference held here at the Pebble Beach Concours d’Élégance.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Petersen Automotive Museum Announces Exterior Redesign', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Petersen Auto Museum\r\nTo Redesign Its Building', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Pebble Beach Concours D'Elegance (Car Show)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mullin, Peter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Petersen Automotive Museum', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pebble Beach (Calif)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T20:56:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Sass', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sass', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6928920a-3b0a-51eb-995f-07360fbb4439', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6928920a-3b0a-51eb-995f-07360fbb4439'}, {'abstract': 'William C. Thompson Jr., who did not make a strong appeal to Caribbean-Americans in his last run for mayor, addressed 300 on Monday, following up on a TV ad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/nyregion/thompson-tries-to-turn-caribbean-ties-into-votes.html', 'snippet': 'William C. Thompson Jr., who did not make a strong appeal to Caribbean-Americans in his last run for mayor, addressed 300 on Monday, following up on a TV ad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A steel drum band welcoming the guest of honor? Check. The flags of Grenada, Barbados, Trinidad and Tobago, and other Caribbean island nations adorning the mirrored walls? Check.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/20thompson-1/20thompson-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/20thompson-1/20thompson-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/20thompson-1/20thompson-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/20thompson-1/20thompson-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/20thompson-1/20thompson-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/20thompson-1/20thompson-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/20thompson-1/20thompson-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thompson Tries to Turn Caribbean Ties Into Votes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thompson Works\r\nHis Caribbean Ties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen, David W', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, William C Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Caribbean Area', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T20:57:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0937c46-d194-5fde-a473-2cb14d966259', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0937c46-d194-5fde-a473-2cb14d966259'}, {'abstract': 'The officials failed to alert residents amid a deluge of rain last summer that left more than 170 people dead, a judge found.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/world/europe/4-officials-convicted-of-negligence-over-russia-flooding.html', 'snippet': 'The officials failed to alert residents amid a deluge of rain last summer that left more than 170 people dead, a judge found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — A court in southern Russia convicted four local officials of criminal negligence on Monday for failing to alert residents to flash flooding in the city of Krymsk last summer that killed more than 170 people. The verdict came as Russia was coping with disastrous flooding again, this time in the country’s Far East.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '4 Officials Convicted of Negligence Over Russia Flooding', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: 4 Officials Found Negligent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Krymsk (Russia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T20:57:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a1ad5e8-c160-5c6c-a5e4-605da55b279a', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a1ad5e8-c160-5c6c-a5e4-605da55b279a'}, {'abstract': 'The Nashville duo’s chart-topping second album came out last week amid rumors of their breakup. This exclusive behind-the-scenes video shows a happier time, and offers hope for the future.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/listen-up-all-is-not-lost-for-the-civil-wars/', 'snippet': 'The Nashville duo’s chart-topping second album came out last week amid rumors of their breakup. This exclusive behind-the-scenes video shows a happier time, and offers hope for the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Civil Wars’ self-titled sophomore album, which was No. 1 on the Billboard 200 chart last week, tells the story of a duo in turmoil. Recorded earlier this year amid building tension between the bandmates Joy Williams and John Paul White (they abruptly halted a European tour last November because of “internal discord and irreconcilable differences of ambition”), the album is rife with allusions to heartache and regret, providing subtext for the two singer-songwriters’ own conflict.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Listen Up | All Is Not Lost for the Civil Wars', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, John Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Joy (1944- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Civil Wars, The (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T21:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Oloizia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oloizia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/286b170e-1f84-5cc4-b31b-c1e2e85548d0', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/286b170e-1f84-5cc4-b31b-c1e2e85548d0'}, {'abstract': 'Under the label Project Rushmore, Harley-Davidson unveiled eight new motorcycles for 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/harley-davidson-unveils-project-rushmore-bikes/', 'snippet': 'Under the label Project Rushmore, Harley-Davidson unveiled eight new motorcycles for 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harley-Davidson unveiled eight new 2014 motorcycles on Monday that were developed under Project Rushmore