19/oversight-board-faults-broker-dealer-audits/', 'snippet': 'The Public Company Accounting Oversight Board found deficiencies in some audits of brokerage firms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Auditors performed complete and correct audits of at least three brokerage firms last year, the Public Company Accounting Oversight Board said Monday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oversight Board Faults Broker-Dealer Audits', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oversight Board Faults Broker-Dealer Audits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Brokers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Company Accounting Oversight Board', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T21:43:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/963178db-ecbd-50fd-a9ae-7301dc36792b', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/963178db-ecbd-50fd-a9ae-7301dc36792b'}, {'abstract': 'Pastiche, Cusco and Camille are the winning choices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/garden/the-results-of-the-baby-llama-naming-contest.html', 'snippet': 'Pastiche, Cusco and Camille are the winning choices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you’ve raised as many llamas as Richard Snyder has — hundreds, over several decades — naming the new babies can be a chore. This year Mr. Snyder, who was featured in a recent article about llama enthusiasts, invited Times readers to help name the three crias, or baby llamas, born on his farm in Milford, Pa., in May. There were two males and a female, and their parents’ names were given as inspiration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04LLAMABABY_SPAN/04LLAMABABY_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04LLAMABABY_SPAN/04LLAMABABY_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04LLAMABABY_SPAN/04LLAMABABY_SPAN-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04LLAMABABY_SPAN/04LLAMABABY_SPAN-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04LLAMABABY_SPAN/04LLAMABABY_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04LLAMABABY_SPAN/04LLAMABABY_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/04/garden/04LLAMABABY_SPAN/04LLAMABABY_SPAN-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Results of the Baby-Llama Naming Contest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Results of the Baby-Llama Naming Contest ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Llamas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Personal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T21:44:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer A. Kingson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Kingson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13b960d5-e6d3-59f0-ae39-0a370cca5a73', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13b960d5-e6d3-59f0-ae39-0a370cca5a73'}, {'abstract': 'Monteverdi’s final opera, “L’Incoronazione di Poppea,” is a story of romantic intrigue in Nero’s court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/arts/music/monteverdis-incoronazione-di-poppea-by-dellarte-opera.html', 'snippet': 'Monteverdi’s final opera, “L’Incoronazione di Poppea,” is a story of romantic intrigue in Nero’s court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It did not take long for the medium of opera, as it coalesced in Italy in the first half of the 17th century, to discover the heady combination of glorious music put to the service of venality and vice. Monteverdi, a founding father, certainly had it down by the time of his final opera, “L’Incoronazione di Poppea,” which appeared in Venice in 1643.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/arts/POPPEA/POPPEA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/20/arts/POPPEA/POPPEA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 640}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'