 a rare Amazon service hiccup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — On occasion, I visit a small store in my neighborhood only to find a sign saying the store is closed for an hour or so. It’s mildly irritating, but it has never occurred to me that those moments are worth freaking out over.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/19/technology/19bits-amazonoutage/19bits-amazonoutage-articleLarge.png', 'height': 208, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/19/technology/19bits-amazonoutage/19bits-amazonoutage-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 208}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/19/technology/19bits-amazonoutage/19bits-amazonoutage-jumbo.png', 'height': 289, 'width': 832, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/19/technology/19bits-amazonoutage/19bits-amazonoutage-superJumbo.png', 'height': 289, 'width': 832, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/19/technology/19bits-amazonoutage/19bits-amazonoutage-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/19/technology/19bits-amazonoutage/19bits-amazonoutage-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Web Site Down? How Dare You!', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Web Site Down?\r\nHow Dare You!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Network Outages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T22:49:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd7c7bf5-bc1e-5c25-91a8-1fb1b3a33fb3', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd7c7bf5-bc1e-5c25-91a8-1fb1b3a33fb3'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for interesting and peculiar items. Monday’s selections include an attack on Mark Zuckerberg’s Facebook page to focus attention on privacy and security issues. Plus, McAfee, the Internet security firm, expressed concern over trying to quantify the total financial loss of cybercrime.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/todays-scuttlebot-zuckerbergs-faceboook-page-hacked-and-mcafees-regrets/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for interesting and peculiar items. Monday’s selections include an attack on Mark Zuckerberg’s Facebook page to focus attention on privacy and security issues. Plus, McAfee, the Internet security firm, exp...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day, The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for interesting and peculiar items. Earlier in the afternoon, Amazon.com went down. It came, as Nick Wingfield noted, after a week in which several of the Internet’s biggest companies went dark for a time. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Zuckerberg’s Facebook Page Hacked and McAfee’s Regrets', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T22:51:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82dcbb92-e6f6-5903-95ea-4e60f77f3dbf', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82dcbb92-e6f6-5903-95ea-4e60f77f3dbf'}, {'abstract': 'In his first televised policy speech since taking office, Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif also maintained the option of military action against militants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/world/asia/pakistans-leader-says-hes-open-to-talks-with-taliban.html', 'snippet': 'In his first televised policy speech since taking office, Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif also maintained the option of military action against militants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — In his first televised policy speech to the country since assuming office in June, Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif on Monday hinted at his government’s inclination to hold talks with Taliban militants even while maintaining the option of military action against them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prime Minister of Pakistan Open to Talks With Taliban', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prime Minister Of Pakistan Open to Talks With Taliban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharif, Nawaz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T23:23:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/847b6478-a1a6-566b-9722-fd00b44f24d7', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/847b6478-a1a6-566b-9722-fd00b44f24d7'}, {'abstract': 'Chancellor Angela Merkel canceled a campaign appearance in the Bavarian town of Ingolstadt after a man armed with a knife and replica of a pistol took three hostages in the local city hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/world/europe/germany-police-foil-hostage-taker.html', 'snippet': 'Chancellor Angela Merkel canceled a campaign appearance in the Bavarian town of Ingolstadt after a man armed with a knife and replica of a pistol took three hostages in the local city hall.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Chancellor Angela Merkel canceled a campaign appearance in the northern Bavarian town of Ingolstadt on Monday after a 24-year-old man armed with a knife and a realistic plastic replica of a pistol took three hostages in the local city hall. The police later stormed the building, freeing the hostages and wounding the suspect. It was unclear whether the episode had any connection with Ms. Merkel’s plans for an appearance in a nearby square. She was to proceed with a planned appearance in the nearby city of Regensburg later Monday. Ms. Merkel is seeking a third term in federal elections on\xa0Sept. 22. All three hostages were unharmed, said Günther Beck, a police spokesman. The suspect suffered a gunshot wound and was being treated by doctors, but he was expected to appear in a local court on Tuesday, Mr. Beck said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany: Police Foil Hostage Taker', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany: Police Foil Hostage Taker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ingolstadt (Germany)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hostages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T23:38:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b43335c0-7a06-5f77-bd88-78cbc5a4b511', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b43335c0-7a06-5f77-bd88-78cbc5a4b511'}, {'abstract': 'More than 250 weapons were recovered on their way into the city from North and South Carolina, which have looser firearms laws.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/nyregion/gun-seizure-exposes-pipeline-from-south.html', 'snippet': 'More than 250 weapons were recovered on their way into the city from North and South Carolina, which have looser firearms laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The guns often arrived by Chinatown bus, packed into patterned bags and destined for sale in a Brooklyn rap studio or in the backs of cars on the Lower East Side.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/y-GUNS/y-GUNS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/y-GUNS/y-GUNS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/y-GUNS/y-GUNS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/y-GUNS/y-GUNS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/y-GUNS/y-GUNS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/y-GUNS/y-GUNS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/y-GUNS/y-GUNS-thumbLarge.