ern Iraq since Thursday, which the United Nations says is one of the largest cross-border migrations since the Syrian conflict began in 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': ' At least 29,000 Syrians have flooded into northern Iraq since Thursday, the United Nations refugee agency said Monday, calling it one of the largest cross-border migrations since the Syrian conflict began in 2011. Officials said 20,000 crossed over on Thursday alone. More than 1.9 million Syrians have already sought refuge in neighboring countries; more than 180,000 are now in Iraq. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria: Thousands Flee to Iraq', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria: Thousands Flee to Iraq', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-19T23:59:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b81e36b-8cfd-59eb-b4a2-34a336e3e75a', 'word_count': 60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b81e36b-8cfd-59eb-b4a2-34a336e3e75a'}, {'abstract': 'South Korea and the United States began another round of military drills on Monday, but North Korea remained uncharacteristically silent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/world/asia/south-korea-us-joins-war-drills.html', 'snippet': 'South Korea and the United States began another round of military drills on Monday, but North Korea remained uncharacteristically silent.', 'lead_paragraph': ' South Korea and the United States began another round of military drills on Monday. In the past, North Korea denounced the drills as a rehearsal for an invasion, but on Tuesday its criticism was less harsh, which analysts said was a sign of the North’s interest in continuing diplomacy. The drills, which continue until Aug. 30, involve 30,000 American and 50,000 South Korean troops in computer-simulated war exercises. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Korea: U.S. Joins War Drills', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Korea: U.S. Joins War Drills', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T00:11:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/60df7db2-04b4-59a0-b72a-b1d9b0c405b7', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60df7db2-04b4-59a0-b72a-b1d9b0c405b7'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department is expected to name Leslie R. Caldwell, the former lead prosecutor in the Enron case, as the next head of its criminal division, according to people briefed on the decision.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/19/former-enron-prosecutor-expected-to-be-named-to-justice-dept-post/', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department is expected to name Leslie R. Caldwell, the former lead prosecutor in the Enron case, as the next head of its criminal division, according to people briefed on the decision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department is expected to name Leslie R. Caldwell, the former lead prosecutor in the Enron case, as the next head of its criminal division, according to people briefed on the decision.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prosecutor in Enron Case Expected to Be Named to Justice Dept. Post', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Prosecutor In Enron Case Coming Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caldwell, Leslie R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Enron Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T00:13:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman and Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a7135e8-96f8-5f94-8057-8b532b25b3de', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a7135e8-96f8-5f94-8057-8b532b25b3de'}, {'abstract': 'The commemoration of the bombing of the United Nations Baghdad offices was overshadowed by staff members who said internal labor practices had compromised their safety and security.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/world/at-un-labor-tensions-mar-10th-anniversary-of-bombing.html', 'snippet': 'The commemoration of the bombing of the United Nations Baghdad offices was overshadowed by staff members who said internal labor practices had compromised their safety and security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United Nations commemorated the 10th anniversary of the single deadliest assault in the organization’s history on Monday, the bombing of its Baghdad offices that killed 22 people, with Secretary General Ban Ki-moon warning in a speech that since then “the attackers who target us have grown more sophisticated, more brazen and better armed.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At U.N., Labor Tensions Mar 10th Anniversary of Bombing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At U.N., Labor Tensions Mar 10th Anniversary of Bombing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baghdad (Iraq)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T00:20:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffeb7243-308a-5198-9644-5cd02c17d2a6', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffeb7243-308a-5198-9644-5cd02c17d2a6'}, {'abstract': 'About 100 objections to Detroit’s eligibility for bankruptcy were filed in federal court before a midnight deadline on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/us/michigan-many-object-to-bankruptcy.html', 'snippet': 'About 100 objections to Detroit’s eligibility for bankruptcy were filed in federal court before a midnight deadline on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': '\ufeffAbout 100 objections to Detroit’s eligibility for bankruptcy were filed in federal court before a\xa0midnight deadline on Monday. The challenges, most from individual city retirees or residents, contend that city officials did not prove insolvency or negotiate enough with creditors before seeking Chapter 9 protection last month. Unions also argued that the case should be dismissed because it will violate pension protections under the State Constitution. The state attorney general, Bill Schuette, who will defend pensioners in later bankruptcy proceedings, did not protest the city’s eligibility.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan: Many Object to Bankruptcy', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michigan: 100 Object to Bankruptcy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yaccino, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T00:24:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Yaccino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/50f047fe-6d94-5162-a768-90e58d5d4572', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50f047fe-6d94-5162-a768-90e58d5d4572'}, {'abstract': 'In a nation used to 6 percent annual expansion, something closer to 5 percent, which would be a reason for celebration elsewhere, is producing angst.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/world/americas/as-a-boom-slows-peru-grows-uneasy.html', 'snippet': 'In a nation used to 6 percent annual expansion, something closer to 5 percent, which would be a reason for celebration elsewhere, is producing angst.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIMA, Peru — From his office window, Henrik Kristensen, the chief executive of the company that runs Peru’s main port, can still look out at rows of newly arrived, shiny Kia automobiles from South Korea and shipping containers stacked four high, full of imported items like television sets and brand-name clothing bound for the growing number of malls that serve this country’s burgeoning middle class.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/world/PERU-1/PERU-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/20/world/PERU-1/PERU-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/world/PERU-1/PERU-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/world/PERU-1/PERU-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/world/PERU-1/PERU-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 