 trial of his father, Bo Xilai, in which he expressed concerns for his imprisoned mother.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Bo Guagua, the younger son of a fallen Communist Party leader scheduled to go on trial this week, made a rare public comment on the case on Monday, saying in a statement that he had been unable to communicate with his father or mother for a year and a half and drawing attention to their “clandestine detention.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/world/SUB-PRINCELING/SUB-PRINCELING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/20/world/SUB-PRINCELING/SUB-PRINCELING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/world/SUB-PRINCELING/SUB-PRINCELING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/world/SUB-PRINCELING/SUB-PRINCELING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/world/SUB-PRINCELING/SUB-PRINCELING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/20/world/SUB-PRINCELING/SUB-PRINCELING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/world/SUB-PRINCELING/SUB-PRINCELING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fallen Chinese Official’s Son Is ‘Denied Contact’ With Parents', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fallen Chinese Official’s Son Is ‘Denied Contact’ With Parents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bo Guagua', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bo Xilai', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gu Kailai', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chongqing (China)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T01:04:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/228bdb8f-bad7-596c-a6b2-f03f21be61fa', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/228bdb8f-bad7-596c-a6b2-f03f21be61fa'}, {'abstract': 'A billion dollars won’t buy democracy. It never has.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/opinion/america-has-no-leverage-in-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'A billion dollars won’t buy democracy. It never has.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — EGYPT has entered a dark tunnel, and it is difficult to say when, and in what condition, it will emerge. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/opinion/0820OPEDthibault/082