le East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T01:05:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Simon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/eac5dc32-df1b-562a-b8b7-ee87dd3ff07a', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eac5dc32-df1b-562a-b8b7-ee87dd3ff07a'}, {'abstract': 'Taxpayers should understand that stop-and-frisk reforms will cost millions of dollars and may ultimately not be needed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/opinion/the-real-costs-of-policing-the-police.html', 'snippet': 'Taxpayers should understand that stop-and-frisk reforms will cost millions of dollars and may ultimately not be needed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANAMA, Bahrain — SETTING aside the legal wisdom of the recent decision by a federal judge against the New York Police Department and its stop-and-frisk policy, one thing seems clear: the judge’s remedy will be enormously expensive and time-consuming to implement, and at a time when the number of stops is falling dramatically. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/opinion/0820OPEDmenchin/0820OPEDmenchin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/20/opinion/0820OPEDmenchin/0820OPEDmenchin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'