guez’s drug-testing history, Major League Baseball agreed to waive the clause.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees were off on Monday, but there was no letup in an increasingly contentious battle between the team’s highest-paid player, Alex Rodriguez, and seemingly the rest of the baseball world.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rodriguez’s Lawyer Calls Baseball’s Offer a ‘Trap’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rodriguez’s Lawyer Calls Baseball’s Offer a ‘Trap’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tacopina, Joseph', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T01:14:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Eder and David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c417f5ff-2949-5202-ac15-2736b3211ef3', 'word_count': 1083, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c417f5ff-2949-5202-ac15-2736b3211ef3'}, {'abstract': 'The United States and the rest of the world cannot acquiesce to the military’s brutality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/opinion/false-choices-on-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'The United States and the rest of the world cannot acquiesce to the military’s brutality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A surprising number of world leaders and foreign policy experts have effectively acquiesced in the continued brutality of Egypt’s generals, arguing that support for the military is the only way to restore stability in the Arab world’s most populous state and limit wider regional turmoil. But this is just one of several false choices misinforming the debate and one that is certain to ensure more unrest, not less.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'False Choices on Egypt', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'False Choices on Egypt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T01:14:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e35a3924-8212-54c6-bcab-f11d74b0b637', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e35a3924-8212-54c6-bcab-f11d74b0b637'}, {'abstract': 'Vital endowment agencies are struggling to operate because of Washington’s inaction and severe budget cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/opinion/trifling-with-the-arts-and-humanities.html', 'snippet': 'Vital endowment agencies are struggling to operate because of Washington’s inaction and severe budget cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than eight months ago, the high-wattage Broadway producer Rocco Landesman announced his departure as chairman of the National Endowment for the Arts. Mr. Landesman, who took the job in 2009, will be hard to replace but not impossible. The White House has taken too long to nominate a successor. It also needs a new leader for the National Endowment for the Humanities, which has been missing a permanent chief since May.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trifling With the Arts and Humanities', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trifling With the Arts and Humanities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Endowment for the Arts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Endowment for the Humanities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landesman, Rocco', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T01:14:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/440b32c6-9630-54b8-b14a-f25315015031', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/440b32c6-9630-54b8-b14a-f25315015031'}, {'abstract': 'Federal agents raided 16 carwashes in Arizona and accused managers of intentionally hiring immigrants in the United States illegally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/us/carwash-managers-held-in-immigration-raids.html', 'snippet': 'Federal agents raided 16 carwashes in Arizona and accused managers of intentionally hiring immigrants in the United States illegally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — Federal agents arrested 11 managers and supervisors of a local car-washing chain on immigration fraud and other charges in weekend raids that brought in more than 200 people, setting off fear among immigrants already on edge by years of relentless enforcement in a state at the core of the debate over illegal immigration. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/us/sub-IMMIG/sub-IMMIG-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/20/us/sub-IMMIG/sub-IMMIG-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/us/sub-IMMIG/sub-IMMIG-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/us/sub-IMMIG/sub-IMMIG-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/us/sub-IMMIG/sub-IMMIG-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subTyp