izona and accused managers of intentionally hiring immigrants in the United States illegally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/08/19/us/20immig.html', 'snippet': 'Federal agents raided 16 carwashes in Arizona and accused managers of intentionally hiring immigrants in the United States illegally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal agents raided 16 carwashes in Arizona and accused managers of intentionally hiring immigrants in the United States illegally.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indictment in Immigration Raids at Arizona Carwashes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Immigration and Customs Enforcement (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T01:32:38+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/e7dad071-8fef-5042-8daf-e9c4ab8b800b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/e7dad071-8fef-5042-8daf-e9c4ab8b800b'}, {'abstract': 'In four short years, BlackBerry went from dominance to being an also-ran.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/opinion/nocera-how-not-to-stay-on-top.html', 'snippet': 'In four short years, BlackBerry went from dominance to being an also-ran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the late 1970s and early 1980s, the dominant computing device used in corporate America was a word processor made by Wang Laboratories. The company’s founder and chief executive was An Wang, a brilliant Chinese immigrant who was widely hailed as a visionary entrepreneur