ed States military aid to Egypt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ll be featuring a history question on Test Yourself every Tuesday this school year. Some, like the one below, will relate current events around the world to history, while others will test students’ knowledge of important past events. Let us know what you think! ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | History, Aug. 20, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T08:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/395e68d5-15a7-5e5f-9aa5-a6798881cecd', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/395e68d5-15a7-5e5f-9aa5-a6798881cecd'}, {'abstract': 'What changes to New York City’s physical landscape do you think are most important? Do you believe these charges are mostly positive or negative? Why?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/6-qs-about-the-news-how-mayor-bloomberg-reshaped-new-york-city/', 'snippet': 'What changes to New York City’s physical landscape do you think are most important? Do you believe these charges are mostly positive or negative? Why?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The interactive feature “Reshaping New York” provides a tour of the ways New York City’s physical landscape has changed in the last 12 years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/19/learning/reshapenewyorkLN/reshapenewyorkLN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleL