w for Tuesday: Local Egyptians react to the violence back home, a new television network begins broadcasting and hundreds of illegal guns are seized.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The unrest in Egypt may feel far-off for many New Yorkers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/20NYTODAY/20NYTODAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/20NYTODAY/20NYTODAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/20NYTODAY/20NYTODAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/20NYTODAY/20NYTODAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/20NYTODAY/20NYTODAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/20NYTODAY/20NYTODAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/20NYTODAY/20NYTODAY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Today: A Struggle Far From Home', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T09:56:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b626c3aa-9ec7-5ce9-a456-5665816d209b', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b626c3aa-9ec7-5ce9-a456-5665816d209b'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s weather was great, attracting all sorts of interesting cars that showed up along Woodward Avenue in Detroit for this year’s Dream Cruise.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/the-2013-woodward-dream-cruise-a-perfect-day-for-cruising/', 'snippet': 'This year’s weather was great, attracting all sorts of interesting cars that showed up along Woodward Avenue in Detroit for this year’s Dream Cruise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — The Woodward Dream Cruise, an annual automotive celebration along the famous avenue that bisects the Detroit metropolitan area, attracted tens of thousands of interesting cars and more than a million spectators to its 19th edition on a perfect summer Saturday. The event, now a weeklong street festival, also drew more police officers than a law-enforcement convention, as units from all over Michigan pitched in to help control the cars and the crowds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 2013 Woodward Dream Cruise: A Perfect Day for Cruising', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruises', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T10:00:03+0000', 'document