ent attempt to reduce risk and wean the economy off easy credit; it will, among other things, coordinate monetary regulatory policies, information-sharing and statistics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The Chinese authorities said on Tuesday that they would set up a group to coordinate financial regulation, in an apparent attempt to reduce risk and wean the economy off easy credit and steer it toward a slower, more sustainable expansion.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Chinese Agency to Increase Financial Coordination', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Chinese Agency to Increase Financial Coordination', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T11:38:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bettina Wassener and Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bettina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wassener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92b6bfd9-c0e6-5eaa-9e8a-111fb6424ba9', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92b6bfd9-c0e6-5eaa-9e8a-111fb6424ba9'}, {'abstract': 'The Carlyle Group has hired Matthew J. O’Connor from General Electric as a new co-head of its power investments group, the latest move to expand its energy practice.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/carlyle-hires-g-e-executive-for-power-investment-team/', 'snippet': 'The Carlyle Group has hired Matthew J. O’Connor from General Electric as a new co-head of its power investments group, the latest move to expand its energy practice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Carlyle Group said on Tuesday that it had hired Matthew J. O’Connor from General Electric as a new co-head of its power investments group.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carlyle Hires G.E. Executive for Power Investment Team', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carlyle Group LP', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T11:50:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d80e61b6-2143-5d66-8a6e-01e2aa548c03', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d80e61b6-2143-5d66-8a6e-01e2aa548c03'}, {'abstract': 'The S.E.C. extracts its first admission of wrongdoing under a new policy. | Hiring the children of the elite is a time-tested practice in the United States. | President Obama urges regulators to move faster on rules for Wall Street. | The Fed identifies shortcomings in banks’ responses to stress tests.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/morning-agenda-the-s-e-c-s-tougher-stance/', 'snippet': 'The S.E.C. extracts its first admission of wrongdoing under a new policy. | Hiring the children of the elite is a time-tested practice in the United States. | President Obama urges regulators to move faster on rules for Wall Street. | The Fed iden...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission has signaled that it was now taking a harder line on securities settlements, as it extracted its first admission of wrongdoing under a new policy, DealBook’s Alexandra Stevenson reports. The S.E.C. said on Monday that the hedge fund manager Philip A. Falcone had agreed to admit wrongdoing and to be barred from the securities industry for at least five years to settle accusations of market manipulation. He and his fund, Harbinger Capital Partners, must also pay more than $18 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The S.E.C.’s Tougher Stance', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T11:56:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5085a317-5e0d-5d97-b3f2-0d5414fe4757', 'word_count': 1589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5085a317-5e0d-5d97-b3f2-0d5414fe4757'}, {'abstract': 'Legal options can be pursued regarding estate issues, and as for manners, turn your focus to those who love you, not those who have abandoned you.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/booming/gay-widower-finds-himself-opposed-by-partners-family.html', 'snippet': 'Legal options can be pursued regarding estate issues, and as for manners, turn your focus to those who love you, not those who have abandoned you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every other Tuesday, Steven Petrow, the author of “Steven Petrow’s Complete Gay & Lesbian Manners” (Workman, 2011), addresses questions about gay and straight etiquette for a boomer-age audience. Send