stname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/37597bbf-ba5b-5a29-9ea1-f7ba64ec4f7c', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37597bbf-ba5b-5a29-9ea1-f7ba64ec4f7c'}, {'abstract': 'With three weeks until the Democratic mayoral primary, William C. Thompson Jr. is hoping to pivot the conversation to New York City’s schools with a new television advertisement.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/20/the-ad-campaign-thompson-turns-attention-to-education/', 'snippet': 'With three weeks until the Democratic mayoral primary, William C. Thompson Jr. is hoping to pivot the conversation to New York City’s schools with a new television advertisement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With three weeks until the Democratic mayoral primary, William C. Thompson Jr. is hoping to pivot the conversation to New York City’s schools, a topic he believes will allow him to rise above his rivals. In a 30-second advertisement, “Mother Teacher,” which began being broadcast on Tuesday, he uses the story of his mother, Elaine Thompson, a public-school teacher, to indirectly attack Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s record on education.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ad Campaign: Thompson Turns Attention to Education', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thompson Turns Attention to Education', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, William C Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-20T21:55:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'secti