o return the Fed to dullness and its chairman to obscurity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/21/opinion/wanted-a-boring-leader-for-the-fed.html', 'snippet': 'Instead of casting about for a new maestro, we need to return the Fed to dullness and its chairman to obscurity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEDFORD, Mass. — THE debate over who should succeed Ben S. Bernanke, the chairman of the Federal Reserve, has been exceptionally personality-driven. Supporters and opponents of the two leading contenders — Lawrence H. Summers, a former Treasury secretary and adviser to President Obama, and Janet L. Yellen, a Clinton administration veteran like Mr. Summers, and now the Fed’s vice chairwoman — have been feuding in public. Mr. Obama has called the decision, which is expected soon, one of the most important of his presidency.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wanted: A Boring Leader for the Fed', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wanted: A Boring Leader for the Fed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bhide, Amar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenspan, Alan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quantitative Easing', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-21T01:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amar Bhidé', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bhidé', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0c1f6a7-3470-5534-914a-c43b3c824ce8', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0c1f6a7-3470-5534-914a-c43b3c824ce8'}, {'abstract': 'With the money New York City spends fighting lawsuits with scorched-earth tactics, it could repave 65 miles of streets, or pay for 80 police officers or 159 teachers, or 887 seats in Head Start.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/21/nyregion/high-costs-of-citys-litigation-add-up-to-a-grim-tally-of-missed-opportunities.html', 'snippet': 'With the money New York City spends fighting lawsuits with scorched-earth tactics, it could repave 65 miles of streets, or pay for 80 police officers or 159 teachers, or 887 seats in Head Start.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Suppose you were in charge of New York City and had $10 million to spend. That’s enough money to repave 65 miles of streets, or pay for 80 police officers or 159 teachers, or cover the cost of 887 seats in Head Start.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In High Costs of City’s Litigation, a Litany of Missed Opportunities ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In High Costs of City’s Litigation, a Litany of Missed Opportunities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cardozo, Michael A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-21T01:02:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byli