 the witness stand inside a military courtroom on Tuesday to tell of a night of gunfire, bloodshed and horror a world away.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/21/us/BALES/BALES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 175, 'width': 234, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/21/us/BALES/BALES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 175, 'width': 234, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/21/us/BALES/BALES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/21/us/BALES/BALES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/21/us/BALES/BALES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Villagers Tell of Slaughter by a Soldier in Kandahar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Villagers Tell Of Slaughter By a Soldier In Kandahar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bales, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-21T01:09:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ba9e3a8-af81-575a-818c-2452b1baa0ac', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ba9e3a8-af81-575a-818c-2452b1baa0ac'}, {'abstract': 'Some members of Congress instead are threatening a devastating government default over the new health care reform.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/21/opinion/republicans-retreat-from-a-shutdown.html', 'snippet': 'Some members of Congress instead are threatening a devastating government default over the new health care reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether out of pure self-preservation or a sudden attack of common sense, a growing group of Republicans is saying no to the strident extremists who want to shut down the government this fall if health care reform is allowed to proceed. “I think it’s the dumbest idea I’ve ever heard of,” Senator Richard Burr, a Republican of North Carolina, said recently.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Retreat From a Shutdown', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republicans Retreat From a Shutdown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-21T01:10:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/034e1355-7e9f-5ad3-8827-452049542cb7', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/034e1355-7e9f-5ad3-8827-452049542cb7'}, {'abstract': 'Even though decades have passed and billions of dollars have been spent, the fight over Yucca Mountain continues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/21/opinion/time-to-stop-stalling-on-nuclear-waste.html', 'snippet': 'Even though decades have passed and billions of dollars have been spent, the fight over Yucca Mountain continues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal appeals court has given the Nuclear Regulatory Commission a well-justified rebuke for “flouting the law” when it stopped analyzing the safety of the proposed nuclear waste site at Yucca Mountain in Nevada, some 100 miles northwest of Las Vegas. The commission engaged in some questionable maneuvers aimed at preventing the Yucca site from ever opening, thus carrying out pledges to scuttle the facility made by President Obama, while campaigning for the presidency in 2008, and Senator Harry Reid, a Democrat of Nevada and the majority leader, who has ferociously opposed the site for years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Time to Stop Stalling on Nuclear Waste', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Time to Stop Stalling on Nuclear Waste', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Wastes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yucca Mountain (Nev)', 'rank': 