'firstname': 'Saritha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cacd9ec-138e-5fdc-883b-ecd60198adcb', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cacd9ec-138e-5fdc-883b-ecd60198adcb'}, {'abstract': 'Do not even think of pulling into that Dunkin’ Donuts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/21/booming/wanted-a-bare-knuckled-gps.html', 'snippet': 'Do not even think of pulling into that Dunkin’ Donuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m getting ready for a summer road trip. I had hoped to update my GPS device, but that requires a degree from M.I.T.: download a program onto the computer, get in the car with the computer and encourage the two systems to talk. That update, which I am pretty sure was some manual writer’s idea of a joke, would have turned down the volume of the iPod when directions were given instead of the current program in which the GPS Lady cannot be heard over Dion and the Belmonts, while I’m yelling: “What? What?” Then I miss the exit, and the GPS Lady, a condescending shrew who — believe me —I would never be friends with in real life, says, “Recalculating, you nitwit.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/21/booming/21wadler-booming-roadtrip1/21wadler-booming-roadtrip1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/21/booming/21wadler-booming-roadtrip1/21wadler-booming-roadtrip1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 709}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/21/booming/21wadler-booming-roadtrip1/21wadler-booming-roadtrip1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 868, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'lega