os in Chelsea. The restaurant, which will stay at 313 Church Street, will be redesigned.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/21/dining/Canvasmorimoto/Canvasmorimoto-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/21/dining/Canvasmorimoto/Canvasmorimoto-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 426}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/21/dining/Canvasmorimoto/Canvasmorimoto-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/21/dining/Canvasmorimoto/Canvasmorimoto-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1456, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/21/dining/Canvasmorimoto/Canvasmorimoto-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/21/dining/Canvasmorimoto/Canvasmorimoto-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/21/dining/Canvasmorimoto/Canvasmorimoto-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Masaharu Morimoto’s Tribeca Canvas Is Closing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morimoto, Masaharu', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'TriBeCa (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-21T15:18:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53a557b0-4d42-52c2-9b57-218aeaa1f7a0', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53a557b0-4d42-52c2-9b57-218aeaa1f7a0'}, {'abstract': 'This you consider a success story?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/21/2009-and-all-that/', 'snippet': 'This you consider a success story?', 'lead_paragraph': 'There has been a lot of commentary on Neil Irwin’s report on why the White House doesn’t want Janet Yellen to chair the Fed, with good reason. The merits of Yellen versus Summers aside, it sounds as if the WH wants Summers, and doesn’t want Yellen, for all the wrong reasons. They want a team player — and consider Yellen’s somewhat independent stance as a liability, even though she has been consistently right. They consider Yellen diminished because she wasn’t part of the team making policy in 2009 — when most people outside the WH don’t consider 2009 anything like a policy triumph.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2009 And All That', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-21T15:23:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d77415e4-ab3d-570e-a39d-fd7080fba99e', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d77415e4-ab3d-570e-a39d-fd7080fba99e'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a clarifying device.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/21/the-point-of-economath/', 'snippet': 'It’s a clarifying device.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Noah Smith has a fairly caustic meditation on the role of math in economics, in which he says that it’s nothing like the role of math in physics — and suggests that it’s mainly about doing hard stuff to prove that you’re smart.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Point of Economath', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-21T15:41:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0522f6d-2ca5-5023-9455-089a585d9006', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0522f6d-2ca5-5023-9455-089a585d9006'}, {'abstract': 'Notable New Yorkers reflect on Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s accomplishments as he gets ready to leave office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000002397593/weighing-in-on-bloombergs-legacy.html', 'snippet': 'Notable New Yorkers reflect on Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s accomplishments as he gets ready to leave office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Notable New Yorkers reflect on Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s accomplishments as he gets ready to leave office.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/20/nyregion/video-bloomberg-mashup/video-bloomberg-mashu