s', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28a1a0c2-1c42-51dc-a61e-ec9e51d66ec2', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28a1a0c2-1c42-51dc-a61e-ec9e51d66ec2'}, {'abstract': 'The Spanish artist transformed the brand’s Rem Koolhaas-designed SoHo store, a process captured in this exclusive time-lapse video.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/21/in-store-at-prada-a-provocative-mural-by-santi-moix/', 'snippet': 'The Spanish artist transformed the brand’s Rem Koolhaas-designed SoHo store, a process captured in this exclusive time-lapse video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We live in an era of increased security, but still the Spanish painter Santi Moix was stunned by the number of men in black who circled him during the 48 hours he recently spent inside the Prada Epicenter store in SoHo. “Tons of them, looking like secret agents” kept tabs on him, he said, as he temporarily transformed the Rem Koolhaas-designed space. “Now you can go to Gagosian, they have security everywhere,” he added, “but Prada was the first to have protection for the bags and the shoes.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Store | At Prada, a Provocative Mural by Santi Moix', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moix, Santi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prada SpA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-21T16:30:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b29a5530-edaf-5a29-8f6c-46a57f1fc473', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b29a5530-edaf-5a29-8f6c-46a57f1fc473'}, {'abstract': 'Even when he couldn’t do it in person, Lincoln understood the importance of addressing the concerns of the electorate.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/21/read-it-very-slowly/', 'snippet': 'Even when he couldn’t do it in person, Lincoln understood the importance of addressing the concerns of the electorate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Aug. 14, 1863, James C. Conkling invited President Abraham Lincoln to Springfield to attend a mass rally of “Unconditional Union men” on Sept. 3. Conkling was a former mayor of Springfield and a member of the Illinois House of Representatives. In a letter of introduction earlier that year, the president called him “my personal friend of long standing.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Read It Very Slowly’', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Letters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-21T16:30:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Louis P. Masur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Louis', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Masur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ec5add0-7990-54f2-9504-e425df48769e', 'word_count': 1906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ec5add0-7990-54f2-9504-e425df48769e'}, {'abstract': 'For Charles Isherwood, “The Poseidon Adventure” awakened his critical sensibilities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/theater/a-ship-sinks-and-a-boy-is-enthralled.html', 'snippet': 'For Charles Isherwood, “The Poseidon Adventure” awakened his critical sensibilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nobody is born with good taste. Or bad taste, either. A sensibility is developed only over many years. Innate sympathies are cultivated or coarsened by contact with whatever aspects of culture you happen to come across, or later search out, as your worldview opens up beyond the realms of immediate need — food, drink, toys! — to the more complicated constructs that, at their best, we call art.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/22/arts/22FIRSTCRUSH/22FIRSTCRUSH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/22/arts/22FIRSTCRUSH/22FIRSTCRUSH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 693}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/22/arts/22FIRSTCRUSH/22FIRSTCRUSH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 887, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/22/arts/22FIRSTCRUSH/22FIRSTCRUSH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1773, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/22/arts/22FIRSTCRUSH/22FIRSTCRUSH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/22/arts/22FIRSTCRUSH/22FIRSTCRUSH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbn