, 'type_of_material': 'An Appraisal', '_id': 'nyt://article/b868d79a-013d-5fd6-bc68-e841d1017696', 'word_count': 881, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b868d79a-013d-5fd6-bc68-e841d1017696'}, {'abstract': 'The brand that originated in 2009 as a popular source for handmade eyewear is releasing its first line of handmade bags.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/21/in-store-illesteva-totes-out-new-line-of-handbags/', 'snippet': 'The brand that originated in 2009 as a popular source for handmade eyewear is releasing its first line of handmade bags.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Handbags are the latest offering from Illesteva, the accessories brand that first drew a celebrity following with eyewear in 2009 and has since added umbrellas and collaborations with the likes of Zac Posen and Dasha Zhukova to its repertory. Alina Silberman, who founded the line along with her brother Daniel Silberman and their friend Justin Salguero, came up with the idea. “It wasn’t planned, to be honest,” she said. “I just really wanted to do it. I thought it was too expensive, what was out there, and I thought we could do it better.” The collection, which includes chic clutches and round purses, isn’t just for women. Daniel said he has been traveling the past month with the backpack, one of the four designs that are available at illesteva.com, some of which will be for sale at Barneys New York early next month. Since the team often flies between New York, where the boys live, and Germany, Italy and France, where their glasses are manufactured, travel was a big inspiration for the project.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Store | Illesteva Totes Out New Line of Handbags', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Store: New to Tote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-21T21:34:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'sect