Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/30899a14-d2ee-5560-a89e-d16e7c110b91', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30899a14-d2ee-5560-a89e-d16e7c110b91'}, {'abstract': 'A new report finds that incomes are down since the recovery began, especially for the young and those nearing retirement. These groups have suffered from the recession in other ways, too.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/21/gen-y-and-boomers-suffering-the-most/', 'snippet': 'A new report finds that incomes are down since the recovery began, especially for the young and those nearing retirement. These groups have suffered from the recession in other ways, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Robert Pear reports, a new study from Sentier Research finds that four years after the start of the economic recovery, the median American household income is still down 4.4 percent. Incomes have risen a little since their recent trough in August 2011, but not enough to make up for the losses sustained earlier.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gen Y and Boomers, Suffering the Most', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sentier Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-21T21:41:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_ma