nyt://article/dea616f7-afe9-5f69-a21d-82bea3c79bb0'}, {'abstract': 'Next month, the Dallas Arboretum will open an eight-acre, $62 million children’s garden complete with a plant petting zoo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/garden/please-pet-the-geranium.html', 'snippet': 'Next month, the Dallas Arboretum will open an eight-acre, $62 million children’s garden complete with a plant petting zoo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Next month, the Dallas Arboretum will open the Rory Meyers Children’s Adventure Garden, an eight-acre, $62 million, mostly open-air learning center. The 150 interactive exhibits include an edible garden, a treetop walkway, a native wetlands ecosystem, and a lab for solving nature mysteries “CSI”-style. Designed to teach children the life and earth sciences, the garden has been a 17-year project of Maria Conroy, the arboretum’s vice president for education and a former elementary school teacher.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/22/garden/22QNA_SPAN/22QNA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/22/garden/22QNA_SPAN/22QNA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/22/garden/22QNA_SPAN/22QNA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/22/garden/22QNA_SPAN/22QNA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/22/garden/22QNA_SPAN/22QNA_