yrian-rebels/', 'snippet': 'Journalists for the French newspaper Le Monde reported in May that they had witnessed repeated chemical attacks on Syrian rebel forces in the Damascus suburbs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In light of claims that forces loyal to President Bashar al-Assad carried out deadly chemical attacks on rebel-held areas outside Damascus on Wednesday, it is worth noting that journalists for the French newspaper Le Monde reported in May that they had witnessed repeated chemical attacks on rebel forces in that same region.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'French Journalists Previously Reported Chemical Attacks in Damascus Suburbs', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T00:26:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bce5b8ad-acf3-5b46-813b-6356b631dc8b', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bce5b8ad-acf3-5b46-813b-6356b631dc8b'}, {'abstract': 'Adel Borghei, an Iranian umpire and referee, was selected to work at the United States Open — and then he wasn’t.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/sports/tennis/us-sanctions-mean-iranian-referee-cant-work-at-the-us-open.html', 'snippet': 'Adel Borghei, an Iranian umpire and referee, was selected to work at the United States Open — and then he wasn’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In May, the Iranian tennis referee Adel Borghei received confirmation that he had secured a coveted slot at the United States Open. “Congratulations,” the letter started.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sanctions Against Iran Mean a Tennis Referee Can’t Work at the Open', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sanctions Against Iran Mean a Tennis Referee Can’t Work at the Open', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T00:28:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52da5530-f352-59e8-bcc1-2040f70edc22', 'word_count': 659, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52da5530-f352-59e8-bcc1-2040f70edc22'}, {'abstract': 'My mother named me after Kris Kristofferson. Could I saddle my son with a famous name?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/21/a-star-is-born/', 'snippet': 'My mother named me after Kris Kristofferson. Could I saddle my son with a famous name?', 'lead_paragraph': 'My wife gave birth to our first child this April. When you tell people that you’re expecting, the second question they ask (after the gender) is, “Do you have a name picked out?” Because we make a living working with books, my wife and I take t