ies whose communities the police targeted. The Democratic candidates running to succeed Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg, who is appealing the decision, have vowed to overhaul the stop-and-frisk approach and end the city’s appeal. Because the plaintiffs in the lawsuit, Floyd v. City of New York, requested only an injunction and not monetary damages, in all likelihood there will be no case left after Inauguration Day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Imagining the Court', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalia, Antonin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scheindlin, Shira A', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T01:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edcbf485-584c-59a9-9a1e-8e7d6750f868', 'word_count': 1768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edcbf485-584c-59a9-9a1e-8e7