emptions to political lobbying groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/opinion/shadowy-inauguration-for-sunshine-law.html', 'snippet': 'New York state’s ethics commission should not grant blanket exemptions to political lobbying groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York state ethics commission voted behind closed doors last June to exempt a leading abortion-rights group, Naral Pro-Choice New York, from a new ethics law requiring tax-exempt organizations to disclose their major donors as they lobby in public forums. The action is causing understandable controversy and cries of liberal bias. It should be reconsidered — out in the open and in the spirit of the law’s goal to shed more sunshine, not less, on the entwined workings of government and political lobbying. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shadowy Inauguration for Sunshine Law', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shadowy Inauguration for Sunshine Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Naral Pro-Choice America', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T01:18:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/607d0ce3-6276-5358-bd7c-ae3847c10213', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/607d0ce3-6276-5358-bd7c-ae3847c10213'}, {'abstract': 'Even if prosecutors were trying to discourage other potential leakers, the 35-year sentence is far too long.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/opinion/bradley-mannings-sentence-is-excessive.html', 'snippet': 'Even if prosecutors were trying to discourage other potential leakers, the 35-year sentence is far too long.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 35-year sentence a military judge imposed on Pfc. Bradley Manning Wednesday morning was in some sense a vindication of his defense: following his conviction last month on charges of violating the Espionage Act, Private Manning faced up to 90 years in prison. He had previously pleaded guilty to lesser versions of those crimes that exposed him to 20 years behind bars. For a defense lawyer, a sentence of one-third the potential maximum is usually not a bad outcome. But from where we sit, it is still too much, given his stated desire not to betray his country but to encourage debate on American aims and shed light on the “day to day” realities of the American war effort.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bradley Manning’s Excessive Sentence', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Happened to Clemency?: Bradley Manning’s sentence is excessive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Bradley E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T01:18:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d31d06bf-0586-5bf1-aa7d-33e7bd689441', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d31d06bf-0586-5bf1-aa7d-33e7bd689441'}, {'abstract': 'Despite promises to reform the criminal justice system, President Obama’s use of the pardon power remains low.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/opinion/what-happened-to-clemency.html', 'snippet': 'Despite promises to reform the criminal justice system, President Obama’s use of the pardon power remains low.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Attorney General Eric Holder said many encouraging things in his important speech on the future of sentencing reform, but the most striking thing may have been what he did not say. In all his 4,000 words on America’s “broken” legal system — and particularly on its outlandishly harsh and ineffective sentencing laws — there was not one mention of executive clemency.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pardon Rates Remain Low', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Happened to Clemency?: Despite justice-reform promise, pardon rate remains low', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodgers, Ronald L', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T01:18:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/933bbf8b-2257-5432-9c3e-fbcb6f05621b', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/933bbf8b-2257-5432-9c3e-fbcb6f05621b'}, {'abstract': 'Naloxone, which is widely used in hospitals, is slowly getting into the hands of emergency medical technicians and nonmedical personnel across New York State.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/nyregion/training-to-apply-a-drug-is-urged-in-overdose-cases.html', 'snippet': 'Naloxone, which is widely used in hospitals, is slowly getting into the hands of emergency medical technicians and nonmedical personnel across New York State.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Samantha Dittmeier was the youngest of Karen Allar’s four children. “She was very loving, very compassionate,” said Ms. Allar, 51, an employment counselor who lives on Long Island. “Unfortunately, the addiction got to her.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/22/nyregion/Y-Overdose/Y-Overdose-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/22/nyregion/Y-Overdose/Y-Overdose-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/22/nyregion/Y-Overdose/Y-Overdose-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/22/nyregion/Y-Overdose/Y-Overdose-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '