, '_id': 'nyt://article/32782396-9cfc-57a6-999d-203cc78f567f', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32782396-9cfc-57a6-999d-203cc78f567f'}, {'abstract': 'Because Terry McAuliffe, the Democratic candidate for governor of Virginia, is running for a state office, federal regulations that prevent “super PACs” from contributing directly to Congressional or presidential campaigns do not apply.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/21/how-a-super-pac-can-give-1-2-million-to-mcauliffe/', 'snippet': 'Because Terry McAuliffe, the Democratic candidate for governor of Virginia, is running for a state office, federal regulations that prevent “super PACs” from contributing directly to Congressional or presidential campaigns do not apply.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Democratic Governors Association’s “super PAC” has given $1.2 million to the party’s nominee for governor of Virginia, one of the larger single political donations in recent history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McAuliffe Gets $1.2 Million Donation From ‘Super PAC’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuccinelli, Kenneth T II', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McAuliffe, Terry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Governors Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T01:27:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Derek Willis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6060624a-459f-5e88-ad3d-88cca59fb08a', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6060624a-459f-5e88-ad3d-88cca59fb08a'}, {'abstract': 'Michael B. Hill, accused of firing shots outside a Decatur elementary school, was carrying 498 rounds of ammunition and a stolen  AK-47, the police said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/us/georgia-suspect-in-school-scare-was-heavily-armed-police-say.html', 'snippet': 'Michael B. Hill, accused of firing shots outside a Decatur elementary school, was carrying 498 rounds of ammunition and a stolen  AK-47, the police said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The man accused of exchanging gunfire with the police at a Decatur elementary school was held without bond Wednesday \xa0on charges that included aggravated assault on a police officer and terroristic threats. Investigators were trying to determine whether the man, Michael B. Hill, 20, had stolen the AK-47 they say he used in trying to seize control of the Ronald E. McNair Discovery Learning Academy\xa0on Tuesday. The police said the weapon belonged to an acquaintance of Mr. Hill, who was carrying 498 rounds of ammunition. No one was injured. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia: Suspect in School Scare Was Heavily Armed, Police Say', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia: Suspect In School Scare Was Heavily Armed, Police Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Michael B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'},