058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e3aa983-a4ae-5020-b083-e8a80272584f'}, {'abstract': 'Iran’s longtime ambassador to the International Atomic Energy Agency will become the third senior Iranian nuclear official to be replaced under President Hassan Rouhani.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/world/middleeast/iran-another-nuclear-official-to-be-replaced.html', 'snippet': 'Iran’s longtime ambassador to the International Atomic Energy Agency will become the third senior Iranian nuclear official to be replaced under President Hassan Rouhani.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Iran’s longtime ambassador to the International Atomic Energy Agency will leave in September, news agencies reported Wednesday, making him the third senior Iranian nuclear official to be replaced under the new administration of President Hassan Rouhani. The ambassador, Ali Asghar Soltanieh, frequently criticized the agency, the nuclear monitoring arm of the United Nations, as well as what he views as Western bias against Iran. Mr. Rouhani, who took office this month, has vowed to pursue a more flexible approach toward resolving the dispute over Iran’s nuclear program, which many countries suspect is aimed at giving it the capability to produce nuclear weapons, despite Iranian denials. Last Friday Mr. Rouhani replaced the head of Iran’s Atomic Energy Organization, which runs the country’s nuclear facilities. On Tuesday state news media signaled that negotiations over the nuclear program would now be handled by Mr. Rouhani’s foreign minister, Mohammad Javad Zarif, an American-educated diplomat.  ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran: Another Nuclear Official to Be Replaced', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran: Another Nuclear Official to Be Replaced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Atomic Energy Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rouhani, Hassan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soltanieh, Ali Asghar', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T01:37:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/38db5320-7f63-518b-8bb0-332d5b19f98d', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38db5320-7f63-518b-8bb0-332d5b19f98d'}, {'abstract': 'A team physician has recommended elbow surgery to repair a partly torn medial collateral ligament for pitcher Jeremy Hefner, who was a key member of the Mets’ rotation earlier this season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/sports/baseball/mets-hefner-appears-headed-for-tommy-john-surgery.html', 'snippet': 'A team physician has recommended elbow surgery to repair a partly torn medial collateral ligament for pitcher Jeremy Hefner, who was a key member of the Mets’ rotation earlier this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeremy Hefner traveled a circuitous route before becoming a key member of the Mets’ starting rotation this season. This week, his professional path presented another sharp, perilous turn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/22/sports/baseball/22hefner-1/22hefner-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarg