rgency in the coverage of the N.S.A.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, Friday, Aug. 23, 1:41 p.m. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Well Has The Times Advanced a Story That It Didn’t Break?', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T14:21:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc5a7ff3-afe7-53fa-8411-06ea7880fbc5', 'word_count': 1328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc5a7ff3-afe7-53fa-8411-06ea7880fbc5'}, {'abstract': 'Former President Hosni Mubarak’s release ended more than two years of incarceration but stopped short of granting him full freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/world/middleeast/mubarak-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'Former President Hosni Mubarak’s release ended more than two years of incarceration but stopped short of granting him full freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Egypt’s new rulers on Thursday moved former President Hosni Mubarak from a prison cell to house arrest at a military hospital, ending more than two years of incarceration but stopping short of granting him full freedom.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mubarak Is Moved From Prison to House Arrest, Stoking Anger of Islamists', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mubarak Is Moved From Prison to House Arrest, Stoking Anger of Islamists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value