, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T15:55:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1c3152c-fd54-5a7f-b4a3-31e24a306b48', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1c3152c-fd54-5a7f-b4a3-31e24a306b48'}, {'abstract': 'Fewer than one in three black Americans and not even half of whites say the United States has made “a lot” of progress toward the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.’s goal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/us/americans-see-racial-equality-as-a-work-in-progress-pew-poll-finds.html', 'snippet': 'Fewer than one in three black Americans and not even half of whites say the United States has made “a lot” of progress toward the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.’s goal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fewer than one in three black Americans and not even half of whites say the United States has made “a lot” of progress toward achieving racial equality in the half-century since the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. declared he had “a dream” that one day freedom, justice and brotherhood would prevail and that his children would “not be judged by the color of their skin but by the content of their character.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Race Equality Is Still a Work in Progress, Survey Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Race Equality Is Still a Work In Progress, Survey Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T16:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bb34f5f-f7d6-594a-9c0d-e50ec113605a', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bb34f5f-f7d6-594a-9c0d-e50ec113605a'}, {'abstract': 'Times editors have been discussing how to handle Pfc. Bradley Manning’s change-of-gender preference in copy.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/the-soldier-formerly-known-as-bradley-manning/', 'snippet': 'Times editors have been discussing how to handle Pfc. Bradley Manning’s change-of-gender preference in copy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, Monday, Aug. 26 | The soldier who was sentenced as Pfc. Bradley Manning told the world Thursday that she\xa0wishes to be known from now on as Chelsea Manning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Soldier Formerly Known as Bradley Manning', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T16:15:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b766039-89af-5fc9-ad68-ed84afc48e89', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b766039-89af-5fc9-ad68-ed84afc48e89'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s first choice is for college performance data to help determine federal aid. The alternative is to publish the data and let parents and students use it to decide where to enroll.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/obamas-backup-plan-on-colleges/', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s first choice is for college performance data to help determine federal aid. The alternative is to publish the data and let parents and students use it to decide where to enroll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'White House officials are well aware that their plan to link federal financial aid to college performance faces hurdles. College presidents have generally resisted attempts to measure outcomes, and Congressional Republicans have generally resisted any domestic-policy proposal from President Obama.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Backup Plan on Colleges', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduation Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T16:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/286d132d-5918-5a91-8a98-5209d6f27d17', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/286d132d-5918-5a91-8a98-5209d6f27d17'}, {'abstract': 'Egypt has broken down. The question is whether it can again find its voice, its wits, its hopes.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/on-a-flight-back-to-cairo/', 'snippet': 'Egypt has broken down. The question is whether it can again find its voice, its wits, its hopes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — The man across the aisle was reading an article headlined: “No Turning Back and No Surrender Before the Forces of Darkness.” As our plane descended over night-time Cairo, the streets were blurry in the weak city lights, and eerily empty because of a military curfew. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On a Flight Back to Cairo', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ElBaradei, Mohamed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T16:32:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ursula Lindsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ursula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8674a05-e302-501c-8ddc-ee8b54698277', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8674a05-e302-501c-8ddc-ee8b54698277'}, {'abstract': 'While circumcision rates in the United States remained stable elsewhere, they plummeted in the 13 Western states. Why?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/circumcision-rates-in-u-s-drop-drastically-in-western-states/', 'snippet': 'While circumcision rates in the United States remained stable elsewhere, they plummeted in the 13 Western states. Why?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The percentage of male newborns who are circumcised in United States hospitals has dropped drastically. Over a 32-year period, the number of male newborns circumcised in the hospital decreased nationally to 58.3 percent in 2010 from 64.5 percent in 1979, according to new data from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Circumcision Rates in U.S. Drop Drastically in Western States', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circumcision', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T16:43:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hope Reeves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hope', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reeves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7aa7392c-fabf-5ff7-be22-aac0cef12955', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7aa7392c-fabf-5ff7-be22-aac0cef12955'}, {'abstract': 'A problem at the Nasdaq stock market halted trading in all Nasdaq-listed stocks on Thursday. Nasdaq began reopening stocks for trading soon after 3 p.m.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/nasdaq-market-halts-trading/', 'snippet': 'A problem at the Nasdaq stock market halted trading in all Nasdaq-listed stocks on Thursday. Nasdaq began reopening stocks for trading soon after 3 p.m.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 9:39 p.m. | The United States stock market showed again on Thursday that it remained vulnerable to technological breakdowns even as regulators and market operators work to keep up with trading that is increasingly electronic and driven by speed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pricing Problem Suspends Nasdaq for Three Hours', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pricing Problem Suspends NASDAQ For Three Hours', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nasdaq Composite Index', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NASDAQ OMX Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Stock Exchange', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T16:52:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathaniel Popper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 