und, but the school has recovered a tape of a Q. and A. session that followed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are hundreds of thousands of carefully preserved manuscripts and recordings that chronicle every speech, interview and public appearance made by one of America’s greatest orators, the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. At least one of his appearances, however, seems to have slipped through the cracks of time, only to be discovered nearly 50 years later in the archives of the New School.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/nyregion/22cityroom-king1/22cityroom-king1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 878, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/23/nyregion/22cityroom-king1/22cityroom-king1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 878}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/nyregion/22cityroom-king1/22cityroom-king1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 700, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/nyregion/22cityroom-king1/22cityroom-king1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1959, 'width': 1338, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/nyregion/22cityroom-king1/22cityroom-king1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/23/nyregion/22cityroom-king1/22cityroom-king1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/nyregion/22cityroom-king1/22cityroom-king1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Found After Decades, a Forgotten Tape of King ‘Thinking on His Feet’', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Found After Decades, a Forgotten Tape of Dr. King', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFFIRMATIVE ACTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New School', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T17:22:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mona el Naggar', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1447b5e3-1669-55ea-8434-f8dc64b743f6', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1447b5e3-1669-55ea-8434-f8dc64b743f6'}, {'abstract': 'Whom should you ask if you have tech problems or complaints?', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/problems-with-your-gadgets-you-need-a-consumer-advocate/', 'snippet': 'Whom should you ask if you have tech problems or complaints?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I get lots and lots of e-mail. I reply to as much as I can — but certain categories, I’ll tell you right now, I can’t answer. “What should I buy?”