tment said it would become a co-plaintiff in a case against a Texas redistricting plan, and would sue the state over a law requiring voters to show photo identification.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/us/politics/justice-dept-moves-to-protect-minority-voters-in-texas.html', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department said it would become a co-plaintiff in a case against a Texas redistricting plan, and would sue the state over a law requiring voters to show photo identification.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration on Thursday escalated its efforts to restore a stronger federal role in protecting minority voters in Texas, announcing that the Justice Department would become a plaintiff in two lawsuits against the state.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Is Suing in Texas Cases Over Voting by Minorities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Is Suing In Texas Cases Over Voting By Minorities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identification Devices', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T18:32:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None,