g to those who recall that its evocative words — “Congress shall make no law . . . abridging the freedom of speech, or of the press” — were ratified 222 years ago. But for a century and a quarter those words were essentially dead letters — until 1919, when Justice Oliver Wendell Holmes resuscitated them with a shocking dissenting opinion that ultimately became the theory of our Constitution and the law of the land. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/books/review/25DERSHOWITZ/25DERSHOWITZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/25/books/review/25DERSHOWITZ/25DERSHOWITZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 742}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/books/review/25DERSHOWITZ/25DERSHOWITZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 828, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/books/review/25DERSHOWITZ/25DERSHOWITZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1656, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/books/review/25DERSHOWITZ/25DERSHOWITZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/25/books/review/25DERSHOWITZ/25DERSHOWITZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/books/review/25DERSHOWITZ/25DERSHOWITZ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'wi