ns', 'value': 'Fort Hood (Tex)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts-Martial', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T20:15:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/931544b6-3353-59f1-ba07-2f22d1b7d776', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/931544b6-3353-59f1-ba07-2f22d1b7d776'}, {'abstract': 'A guessing game with Miranda July.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/can-you-guess-what-this-is-13/', 'snippet': 'A guessing game with Miranda July.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RULES1. Player has not seen the photo beforehand.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can You Guess What This Is?', 'kicker': 'Summer Game', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can You Guess What This Is?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T20:18:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamara Shopsin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shopsin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ecf654e-1296-52f4-bad9-cd8a2437371c', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ecf654e-1296-52f4-bad9-cd8a2437371c'}, {'abstract': 'The violinist Joshua Bell performed Tchaikovsky’s flamboyant showpiece, the songful Violin Concerto in D, with the Mostly Mozart Festival Orchestra on Wednesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/arts/music/joshua-bell-teams-up-with-the-mostly-mozart-orchestra.html', 'snippet': 'The violinist Joshua Bell performed Tchaikovsky’s flamboyant showpiece, the songful Violin Concerto in D, with the Mostly Mozart Festival Orchestra on Wednesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Familiarity, they say, breeds contempt. But that maxim, however hoary, is not unassailable. Audiences for concerts of mainstream orchestral repertory have not yet grown tired of Tchaikovsky’s showy, songful Violin Concerto in D, composed in 1878 and now almost surely played somewhere on the planet every week of the year. New evidence came on Wednesday night in the boisterous applause that followed the work’s first movement, as the violinist Joshua Bell played the concerto with the Mostly Mozart Festival Orchestra at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/0823BELL/0823BELL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/0823BELL/0823BELL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/0823BELL/0823BELL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/0823BELL/0823BELL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/0823BELL/0823BELL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/0823BELL/0823BELL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/0823BELL/0823BELL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tchaikovsky’s Showpiece, Performed by a Showman', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tchaikovsky’s Showpiece, Performed by a Showman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mostly Mozart Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bell, Joshua', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T20:22:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f923354-a1a3-5fe2-8ba0-38aa3bfea8f9', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f923354-a1a3-5fe2-8ba0-38aa3bfea8f9'}, {'abstract': 'The challenge of writing regulations that put the Affordable Care Act’s requirements for employers into practice, and then getting computer systems to carry them out, proved too much, too soon.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/employer-mandate-delayed-by-paperwork-and-efforts-to-reduce-it/', 'snippet': 'The challenge of writing regulations that put the Affordable Care Act’s requirements for employers into practice, and then getting computer systems to carry them out, proved too much, too soon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last several weeks, we’ve taken a close look at the Affordable Care Act’s employer mandate, which requires companies with at least 50 employees to provide affordable health insurance to workers or pay a penalty. We’ve examined, among other issues, how the mandate defines affordable, how it treats workers whose hours vary — even whether it could be used as catalyst for hiring formerly undocumented immigrants. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Employer Mandate, Delayed by Paperwork (and Efforts to Reduce It)', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Restaurant Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Retail Federation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Chamber of Commerce', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T20:29:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0bca723-42a9-59c2-bbc5-d7740f8ab277', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0bca723-42a9-59c2-bbc5-d7740f8ab277'}, {'abstract': 'A simple chicken dish and salad is a great accompaniment for German riesling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/dining/a-salad-with-farm-stand-allure.html', 'snippet': 'A simple chicken dish and salad is a great accompaniment for German riesling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The calendar is leaning into Labor Day, but that does not mean summer is over. There is still much at the greenmarket to recommend for a bottle of dry German riesling. Consider leafy herbs, the whisper of sweetness in fresh corn and summer squash and a ripe tomato, all brought together with a splash of lemon.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/dining/28PAIR_SPAN/28PAIR_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/28/dining/28PAIR_SPAN/28PAIR_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/dining/28PAIR_SPAN/28PAIR_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/dining/28PAIR_SPAN/28PAIR_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/dining/28PAIR_SPAN/28PAIR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/28/dining/28PAIR_SPAN/28PAIR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/dining/28PAIR_SPAN/28PAIR_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Salad With Farm-Stand Allure', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T20:32:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/584b09df-93cc-563f-bdda-f914a1c7b39d', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/584b09df-93cc-563f-bdda-f914a1c7b39d'}, {'abstract': 'What city kid can resist the siren song of bowling alleys and Dairy Queens?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/magazine/the-summer-i-discovered-suburbia.html', 'snippet': 'What city kid can resist the siren song of bowling alleys and Dairy Queens?', 'lead_paragraph': 'One preteen summer, I was sent by my parents to Kent, Ohio, to spend a few days with my cousins, Jessica and Anna. They were close to my age and looked like me: Norwegian, with blond hair and blue eyes. They, and their parents, a dental hygienist and geographer, were warm and easygoing. And yet, when I arrived at their cozy two-story house, it felt like touching down on an alien planet. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '62', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/magazine/25lives/mag-25Lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 258, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/25/magazine/25lives/mag-25Lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 258}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/magazine/25lives/mag-25Lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 276, 'width': 643, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/magazine/25lives/mag-25Lives-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 276, 'width': 643, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/magazine/25lives/25lives-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/25/magazine/25lives/25lives-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/magazine/25lives/25lives-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Summer I Discovered Suburbia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Falling for Sprawl', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suburbs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T20:33:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ada Calhoun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calhoun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/113f4de7-c914-5458-85ae-a886495d5f4b', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/113f4de7-c914-5458-85ae-a886495d5f4b'}, {'abstract': 'The thoughtfully designed menu at Trattoria 632 shifts with availability.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/nyregion/a-review-of-trattoria-632-in-purchase.html', 'snippet': 'The thoughtfully designed menu at Trattoria 632 shifts with availability.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That Trattoria 632 looks like someone’s expanded residence is not surprising. This roomy restaurant, bar and lounge was cobbled together from two adjoining homes. Although the many walls that sheltered a few generations have been removed and the space repurposed for the building’s new life, this merging wasn’t a redo, it was a make-do, on what might have been a limited budget. The resulting layout is a tad awkward, and homey touches remain, but the mismatching sets the tone for informality and adds a bit of country charm. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/nyregion/25DINEWE2/25DINEWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/25/nyregion/25DINEWE2/25DINEWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/nyregion/25DINEWE2/25DINEWE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'l