urday-tv-is-ladies-night.html', 'snippet': 'Saturday night is increasingly known for TV movies with women in prominent roles, like the coming “Escape From Polygamy” and “After All These Years.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were television movies before “Sharknado,” and there continue to be television movies after “Sharknado.” Witness this Saturday night, when Lifetime offers a topical drama, “Escape From Polygamy”; Hallmark Channel provides a frothy romantic mystery, “After All These Years”; and Nickelodeon kicks in “Swindle,” a children’s caper movie modeled on the “Ocean’s” films.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23ACTRESSES_SPAN/23ACTRESSES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23ACTRESSES_SPAN/23ACTRESSES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23ACTRESSES_SPAN/23ACTRESSES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23ACTRESSES_SPAN/23ACTRESSES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23ACTRESSES_SPAN/23ACTRESSES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23ACTRESSES_SPAN/23ACTRESSES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23ACTRESSES_SPAN/23ACTRESSES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Oh, Yes, Saturday TV Is Ladies Night', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oh, Yes, It’s Ladies Night', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T20:35:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c9e0024-b2c9-59ad-a38f-89d26102b1b8', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c9e0024-b2c9-59ad-a38f-89d26102b1b8'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time since 2011, Yahoo had more unique visitors in a month than any other Web property, but why that happened remains unclear.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/yahoo-surpasses-google-to-take-top-spot/', 'snippet': 'For the first time since 2011, Yahoo had more unique visitors in a month than any other Web property, but why that happened remains unclear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Without question, it has been a good month for Marissa Mayer, the chief executive of Yahoo. She was featured in a fancy fashion spread in Vogue magazine, Yahoo’s stock has continued to climb, and now, like a big cherry on top, the company beat Google to become the most visited Web property in America.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '