 'nyt://article/59efe272-4d98-53b5-b796-369ae58fcc5b'}, {'abstract': 'In Renny Harlin’s “Devil’s Pass,” American students investigate a Russian skiing disaster shrouded in mystery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/movies/devils-pass-wrings-laughs-from-the-found-footage-genre.html', 'snippet': 'In Renny Harlin’s “Devil’s Pass,” American students investigate a Russian skiing disaster shrouded in mystery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Opens on Friday in Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fools Rush In, With Camera', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Devil’s Pass', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harlin, Renny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T20:47:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Miriam Bale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Miriam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/319ba22a-ec58-585f-8d32-2f09a6ccf88a', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/319ba22a-ec58-585f-8d32-2f09a6ccf88a'}, {'abstract': 'Classical music critics choose their favorite recordings of Wagner, including selected performances of “Tristan und Isolde” and “Lohengrin,” as well as parts of the “Ring”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/arts/music/critics-name-their-favorite-wagner-recordings.html', 'snippet': 'Classical music critics choose their favorite recordings of Wagner, including selected performances of “Tristan und Isolde” and “Lohengrin,” as well as parts of the “Ring”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Love his music or hate his personality, the one thing you can’t do with Wagner is ignore him, especially this year, as the music world celebrates his bicentenary. However petty and malicious the man could be, his artistic achievement was huge, not only in sheer physical bulk but also in ambition, imagination and invention.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23WAGNER1/23WAGNER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 759, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23WAGNER1/23WAGNER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 759}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23WAGNER1/23WAGNER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 810, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23WAGNER1/23WAGNER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1620, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23WAGNER1/23WAGNER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23WAGNER1/23WAGNER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23WAGNER1/23WAGNER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Wagner’s Birthday, but We Get the Gifts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wagner’s Birthday, But We Get the Gifts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wagner, Richard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T20:50:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich, Anthony Tommasini, Zachary Woolfe, Vivien Schweitzer and Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}, {'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 5}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a18f386-8b39-59e3-ad05-88fc806f0139', 'word_count': 2462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a18f386-8b39-59e3-ad05-88fc806f0139'}, {'abstract': 'Joe Swanberg’s new romance, “Drinking Buddies,” reveals, among other things, that passive-aggression is nowadays less a personal trait than a cultural norm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/movies/in-joe-swanbergs-drinking-buddies-couples-face-tests.html', 'snippet': 'Joe Swanberg’s new romance, “Drinking Buddies,” reveals, among other things, that passive-aggression is nowadays less a personal trait than a cultural norm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A conventional way to describe Kate and Luke’s relationship would be to say they’re just friends. But “just” hardly captures the intensity of the bond between them. Co-workers at a thriving Chicago microbrewery, Kate (Olivia Wilde) and Luke (Jake Johnson) have an effortless, comfortable intimacy. They get each other’s jokes and never tire of each other’s company. Daily lunch companions, they often extend the nightly busman’s holiday of after-work beer-drinking until closing time. They snuggle up in booths and couches, sometimes dozing off, but more like puppies in a box than lovers in bed. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/0823DRINKING_SPAN/0823DRINKING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 293, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/0823DRINKING_SPAN/0823DRINKING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 293}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/0823DRINKING_SPAN/0823DRINKING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 501, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/0823DRINKING_SPAN/0823DRINKING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1001, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/0823DRINKING_SPAN/0823DRINKING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/0823DRINKING_SPAN/0823D