{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McCall Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T21:56:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard G. Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e92a917-ad01-57cd-a8cd-48344fb05bdd', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e92a917-ad01-57cd-a8cd-48344fb05bdd'}, {'abstract': 'A critical guide to the visual arts in New York and the region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/arts/design/museum-and-gallery-listings-for-aug-23-29.html', 'snippet': 'A critical guide to the visual arts in New York and the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Museums and galleries are in Manhattan unless otherwise noted. Full reviews of recent art shows: nytimes.com/art. A searchable guide to these and many other art shows is at nytimes.com/events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum and Gallery Listings for Aug. 23-29', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T21:58:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8190cc3-4088-5678-9c5d-b6b752e22e54', 'word_count': 4913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8190cc3-4088-5678-9c5d-b6b752e22e54'}, {'abstract': 'For early fall, designers introduce statement pieces laced with Yves Klein’s iconic shade of blue.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/market-report-blue-gets-the-black-and-gray-treatment/', 'snippet': 'For early fall, designers introduce statement pieces laced with Yves Klein’s iconic shade of blue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Designers have embraced Yves Klein’s iconic shade of blue in standout pieces for early fall. From tops (Victoria Beckham’s prim calf-hair coat and Jil Sander’s artistic turtleneck sweater) to bottoms (Roger Vivier’s flocked leather bootie and Manolo Blahnik’s signature stiletto) and everything in between (Christopher Kane’s color-blocked velvet dress and a calf-hair bag from Michael Kors), this deep indigo hue is being paired, accented and trimmed with black and gray to prove that the similar shades can, and should, be worn together. The pièce de résistance: Dior’s ladylike watch with baguette sapphires and bright diamonds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Market Report | Blue Gets the Black and Gray Treatment', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckham, Victoria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blahnik, Manolo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kane, Christopher (1982- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kors, Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Dior SA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roger Vivier', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T22:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87cbf1a8-fe18-58de-950d-ffcf7ee650c1', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87cbf1a8-fe18-58de-950d-ffcf7ee650c1'}, {'abstract': 'In Noah Buschel’s “Sparrows Dance,” an agoraphobic actress is forced to call upon the assistance of a poetry-writing handyman.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/movies/sparrows-dance-starring-marin-ireland-and-paul-sparks.html', 'snippet': 'In Noah Buschel’s “Sparrows Dance,” an agoraphobic actress is forced to call upon the assistance of a poetry-writing handyman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To describe the setup of “Sparrows Dance,” Noah Buschel’s disarmingly offbeat romance, is to risk alienating audiences fatigued by too-quirky characters and low-budget contrivance. In one corner, we have an unnamed, severely agoraphobic actress (Marin Ireland); in the other, a saxophone-playing, poetry-writing plumber (Paul Sparks). Between them lies a tiny New York City apartment and a mental-health problem as vast as a football field.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23RDP_SPARROWS_SPAN/0823FILMRDP01sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23RDP_SPARROWS_SPAN/0823FILMRDP01sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23RDP_SPARROWS_SPAN/0823FILMRDP01sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23RDP_SPARROWS_SPAN/0823FILMRDP01sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1150, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23RDP_SPARROWS_SPAN/0823FILMRDP01sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23RDP_SPARROWS_SPAN/0823FILMRDP01sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23RDP_SPARROWS_SPAN/0823FILMRDP01sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Plumber Lends a Sympathetic Ear', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sparrows Dance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buschel, Noah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ireland, Marin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sparks, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T22:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c246747-49c7-5532-afd8-e3902e009fb3', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c246747-49c7-5532-afd8-e3902e009fb3'}, {'abstract': 'Playful sculptures abound in “Lightness of Being,” a group show at City Hall Park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/arts/design/lightness-of-being-group-show-at-city-hall-park.html', 'snippet': 'Playful sculptures abound in “Lightness of Being,” a group show at City Hall Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A certain pants-making company promoted its denim three years ago with the imperative “Be stupid.” This was an attempt at irony. It really meant, “If you are smart, you will buy our jeans.” Variations on that tag line explained: “Stupid might fail. Smart doesn’t even try”; and “Stupid creates. Smart critiques.” In other words, to be original and creative, you might have to be willfully ignorant of what passes for conventional intelligence — or, at least, appear to be so. Think of the seemingly naïve TV detective Columbo. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23SCULPTURE_SPAN/23SCULPTURE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23SCULPTURE_SPAN/23SCULPTURE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23SCULPTURE_SPAN/23SCULPTURE_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23SCULPTURE_SPAN/23SCULPTURE_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23SCULPTURE_SPAN/23SCULPTURE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23SCU