ern: Hopper to O’Keeffe” the Museum of Modern Art tries to show that the museum did not ignore American artists during its early decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s sad. When the Museum of Modern Art isn’t jumping the shark with celebrity-performance art featuring the likes of Tilda Swinton, it can often be found paddling about in the lukewarm waters of the shallow end.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23MODERNJP01_SPAN/23MODERNJP01_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23MODERNJP01_SPAN/23MODERNJP01_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23MODERNJP01_SPAN/23MODERNJP01_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23MODERNJP01_SPAN/23MODERNJP01_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23MODERNJP01_SPAN/23MODERNJP01_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23MODERNJP01_SPAN/23MODERNJP01_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23MODERNJP01_SPAN/23MODERNJP01_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Comfortable Old Friends', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Comfortable Old Friends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T22:04:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d096b97-62ee-561b-a9f5-328a71e302ec', 'word_count': 1331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d096b97-62ee-561b-a9f5-328a71e302ec'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to walking tours, street fairs, parades and other cultural events in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/arts/spare-times-for-aug-23-29.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to walking tours, street fairs, parades and other cultural events in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Battle of Brooklyn Commemoration (Sunday) It was a Revolutionary War battle that George Washington and his troops would probably have liked to forget — they lost — but the Battle of Brooklyn, on Aug. 27, 1776, was the colonists’ first major confrontation with the British after declaring independence, giving the occasion a special place in history. Its 237th anniversary will be celebrated on Sunday, from 10 a.m. to 3 p.m., with events at one of the sites involved, what is now Green-Wood Cemetery, Fifth Avenue and 25th Street, Greenwood Heights, Brooklyn.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for Aug. 23-29', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-22T22:07:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Mancuso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mancuso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/b36431ed-2f4d-534f-9130-f88e2a6ae001', 'word_count': 3208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b36431ed-2f4d-534f-9130-f88e2a6ae001'}, {'abstract': '“Savannah” tells the story of a well-born Southerner who turns his back on privilege to hunt ducks with a former slave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/movies/savannah-a-true-story-from-the-south-of-long-ago.html', 'snippet': '“Savannah” tells the story of a well-born Southerner who turns his back on privilege to hunt ducks with a former slave.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Savannah,” a picturesque film based on a true story from the early-20th-century South, has a tone that leaves you expecting an outsize character to emerge and carry you to an ending that is the stuff of legends. But the man at the center of the story, Ward Allen (Jim Caviezel), turns out to be something less than that. He’s an interesting fellow but not particularly larger than life, at least as portrayed here.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23savannah1/23savannah1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/23/arts/23savannah1/23savannah1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargehei