raph': 'In 2003, Gov. Rick Perry signed the Move Over Act. It gave Texas drivers a new rule of the road when they came across a police car or other emergency vehicle parked on a shoulder with its lights flashing: slow down or move one lane over while passing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/us/23ttRoadsafety/23ttRoadsafety-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 244, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/23/us/23ttRoadsafety/23ttRoadsafety-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 244}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/us/23ttRoadsafety/23ttRoadsafety-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/us/23ttRoadsafety/23ttRoadsafety-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/us/23ttRoadsafety/23ttRoadsafety-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/23/us/23ttRoadsafety/23ttRoadsafety-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/us/23ttRoadsafety/23ttRoadsafety-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Law Updated to Protect Some Who Do Roadwork', 'kicker': 'Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'prin