dy’s Investors Service threatened on Thursday to downgrade the credit ratings of several big financial firms.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moody’s Threatens to Cut Credit Ratings of Banks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moody’s Threatens to Cut Credit Ratings of Banks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Ratings and Credit Rating Agencies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Investors Service Inc", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T00:26:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12d02eb4-63fd-528c-831d-9aabfd1aa617', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12d02eb4-63fd-528c-831d-9aabfd1aa617'}, {'abstract': 'Some are questioning whether Catherine M. Russell, ambassador at large for global women’s issues, will see a less prominent role under Secretary of State John Kerry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/us/politics/a-question-of-how-womens-issues-will-fare-in-washington-and-overseas.html', 'snippet': 'Some are questioning whether Catherine M. Russell, ambassador at large for global women’s issues, will see a less prominent role under Secretary of State John Kerry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Catherine M. Russell’s portfolio includes half the population of the planet, roughly 3.5 billion women. But working with the 70,000 employees of the State Department to make women’s issues a permanent priority, she said, may be the “harder slog” in a difficult new job.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/world/russell/russell-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/23/world/russell/russell-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/world/russell/russell-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/world/russell/russell-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/world/russell/russell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/23/world/russell/russell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/world/russell/russell-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Question of How Women’s Issues Will Fare, in Washington and Overseas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Question of How Women’s Issues Will Fare, in Washington and Overseas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheaton, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Russell, Catherine M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T00:32:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c5f0703-14eb-5ce4-a863-2a9a8a77fedd', 'word_count': 1326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c5f0703-14eb-5ce4-a863-2a9a8a77fedd'}, {'abstract': 'Today’s automated stock exchanges are fast and efficient, so long as the computers are working. When things go awry, chaos can emerge quickly.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/in-markets-tuned-up-machinery-stubborn-ghosts-remain/', 'snippet': 'Today’s automated stock exchanges are fast and efficient, so long as the computers are working. When things go awry, chaos can emerge quickly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A generation ago, when the stock market crashed on Oct. 19, 1987, the Nasdaq stock market appeared to have done much better than the New York Stock Exchange. While the Dow Jones industrial average fell 23 percent that day, the Nasdaq composite index was off just 11 percent.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Markets’ Tuned-Up Machinery, Stubborn Ghosts Remain', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Markets’ Tuned-Up Machinery, Stubborn Ghosts Remain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Futures and Options Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High-Frequency and Flash Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nasdaq Composite Index', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Stock Exchange', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T00:38:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5143b7c7-23fb-5dfb-bae5-e53db57af494', 'word_count': 1212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5143b7c7-23fb-5dfb-bae5-e53db57af494'}, {'abstract': 'A parliamentary study found that prejudices played a role in the police’s failure to detect a neo-Nazi cell that carried out a string of attacks on immigrants for more than a decade.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/world/europe/german-officers-biases-seen-as-enabling-neo-nazis.html', 'snippet': 'A parliamentary study found that prejudices played a role in the police’s failure to detect a neo-Nazi cell that carried out a string of attacks on immigrants for more than a decade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Germany’s police and security services suffered from deeply rooted prejudices and a lack of cultural diversity, which allowed a neo-Nazi cell to carry out violent attacks against immigrants for more than a decade without being detected, according to a parliamentary committee report issued Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1