': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d04245f-9137-5235-b5fd-e80c97dc1398', 'word_count': 862, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d04245f-9137-5235-b5fd-e80c97dc1398'}, {'abstract': 'The protests are creating awkward dilemmas for Obama administration officials who are pressing the House of Representatives to pass broad immigration legislation this fall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/us/young-immigrants-protest-deportations.html', 'snippet': 'The protests are creating awkward dilemmas for Obama administration officials who are pressing the House of Representatives to pass broad immigration legislation this fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Young immigrants in the country illegally have escalated their protests against deportations this week, creating awkward dilemmas for Obama administration officials who are pressing the House of Representatives to pass broad immigration legislation this fall.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Young Immigrants Protest Deportations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Young Immigrants Protest Deportations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Julia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T01:07:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72c4efb2-bfb2-5bc7-8ef8-6a2aef777fff', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72c4efb2-bfb2-5bc7-8ef8-6a2aef777fff'}, {'abstract': 'Why do markets keep going wild? The answer is a variant on the same old story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/opinion/krugman-this-age-of-bubbles.html', 'snippet': 'Why do markets keep going wild? The answer is a variant on the same old story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So, another BRIC hits the wall. Actually, I’ve never much liked the whole “BRIC” — Brazil, Russia, India, and China — concept: Russia, which is basically a petro-economy, doesn’t belong there at all, and there are large differences among the other three. Still, it’s hard to deny that India, Brazil, and a number of other countries are now experiencing similar problems. And those shared problems define the economic crisis du jour.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Age of Bubbles', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Age Of Bubbles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krugman, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T01:08:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/160a513f-0635-52dc-a267-682a42f05224', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/160a513f-0635-52dc-a267-682a42f05224'}, {'abstract': 'The New Mexico Supreme Court said Thursday that the First Amendment did not permit a photography studio to reject a same-sex couple’s commitment ceremony.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/us/studio-has-no-right-to-bias-court-rules.html', 'snippet': 'The New Mexico Supreme Court said Thursday that the First Amendment did not permit a photography studio to reject a same-sex couple’s commitment ceremony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New Mexico Supreme Court on Thursday affirmed a decision against a photography studio that was sued after refusing to photograph a same-sex couple’s commitment ceremony in 2006, saying the First Amendment does not permit businesses that offer services for a profit to choose whom to serve.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Studio Has No Right to Bias, Court Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Studio Has No Right to Bias, Court Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santos, Fernanda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T01:12:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c83a5ca2-1c13-5963-97bf-5f27fd4cc836', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c83a5ca2-1c13-5963-97bf-5f27fd4cc836'}, {'abstract': 'A promising junior, Andy Fitzpatrick has been forced to put his career on hold on several occasions for financial reasons. Now he earns a living as part of Sloane Stephens’s team.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/22/british-player-finds-a-home-as-stephenss-hitting-partner/', 'snippet': 'A promising junior, Andy Fitzpatrick has been forced to put his career on hold on several occasions for financial reasons. Now he earns a living as part of Sloane Stephens’s team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Fitzpatrick is not used to such plush surroundings. Fitzpatrick, a British player ranked 620th, acknowledged that he felt a little out of place in the pampered environment of a high-level WTA tournament as he assisted Sloane Stephens with her United States Open preparations at the New Haven Open this week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Player Finds a Home as Stephens’s Hitting Partner', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stephens, Sloane', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T01:13:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69521b53-589e-5b64-b393-70f2e4861f89', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69521b53-589e-5b64-b393-70f2e4861f89'}, {'abstract': 'The trial of the fallen Chinese official Bo Xilai highlights the urgent issue of whether China’s leaders will revive the disastrous tactics and policies of Chairman Mao.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/opinion/its-all-about-mao.html', 'snippet': 'The trial of the fallen Chinese official Bo Xilai highlights the urgent issue of whether China’s leaders will revive the disastrous tactics and policies of Chairman Mao.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The trial of Bo Xilai, the fallen Chinese Communist Party official and former member of the ruling Politburo, is attracting the world’s attention with its tales of corruption, sex, murder and political intrigue. But while such details are riveting, they divert attention from the real meaning of the case.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s All About Mao', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s All About Mao', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bo Xilai', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mao Zedong', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cultural Revolution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T01:14:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zheng Wang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zheng', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9525631-7c47-5fe7-817f-a1e27b155e6b', 'word_count': 921, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9525631-7c47-5fe7-817f-a1e27b155e6b'}, {'abstract': 'Responding to an Op-Ed article about the merits of boycotting Russian vodka, readers examine ways to change Russia’s antigay policies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/opinion/will-a-boycott-help-russias-gays.html', 'snippet': 'Responding to an Op-Ed article about the merits of boycotting Russian