{'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (Flix) WET HOT AMERICAN SUMMER (2001) On the last day of the summer in 1981, Coop (Michael Showalter), a teenage counselor at Camp Firewood, outside Waterville, Me., decides that he will finally declare his love for his lifelong crush, Katie (Marguerite Moreau). Meanwhile, the camp’s director, Beth (Janeane Garofalo), has romantic designs of her own on Associate Professor Newman (David Hyde Pierce). This comedy — directed by David Wain, written by Mr. Showalter and Mr. Wain, and with an ensemble cast including Amy Poehler, Bradley Cooper, Paul Rudd and Christopher Meloni (above, center, with Mr. Showalter, left, and A. D. Miles) — is “at its best when it jettisons parody for off-the-cuff zaniness,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. He also singled out Mr. Rudd, who “not only steals Coop’s girl, but suavely walks off with Mr. Showalter’s movie as well.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/8089e1fb-a94a-570b-b494-17acfff24a56', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8089e1fb-a94a-570b-b494-17acfff24a56'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/news-quiz-august-23-2013/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | August 23, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T05:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aea9e7ff-f29b-579b-ae6e-02a712165097', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aea9e7ff-f29b-579b-ae6e-02a712165097'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors at the trial of Bo Xilai, the disgraced Communist Party official, asserted on Friday that he knew about a French villa bought for his family by a tycoon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/world/asia/bo-xilai-trial-china.html', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors at the trial of Bo Xilai, the disgraced Communist Party official, asserted on Friday that he knew about a French villa bought for his family by a tycoon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JINAN, China — Prosecutors in the trial of Bo Xilai, the former Communist Party star, presented testimony on Friday asserting that he knew about a villa on the French Riviera bought for his family by a tycoon and about demands for compensation from a British businessman managing the villa who was later murdered by Mr. Bo’s wife.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/24/world