jor': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T13:20:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d687a28-7639-5cc8-9abe-9ab2e33b83e3', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d687a28-7639-5cc8-9abe-9ab2e33b83e3'}, {'abstract': 'Steven A. Ballmer’s departure paves the way for a generational change at Microsoft and gives it an opportunity to adapt to a world dominated by technologies that have eluded its influence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/technology/ballmer-announces-retirement-from-microsoft.html', 'snippet': 'Steven A. Ballmer’s departure paves the way for a generational change at Microsoft and gives it an opportunity to adapt to a world dominated by technologies that have eluded its influence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — Steven A. Ballmer announced on Friday that he was leaving the top job at Microsoft, paving the way for a generational change at the once-dominant technology company and giving it an opportunity to reinvent itself for a world dominated by mobile devices, social media and other technologies that have eluded its influence.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ballmer Exit Brings Microsoft a Chance for Reinvention', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Exit at Microsoft, a Chance for Reinvention', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ballmer, Steven A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T13:22:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15e458d8-fe83-5db1-bddb-1d795b3e3f1c', 'word_count': 1205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15e458d8-fe83-5db1-bddb-1d795b3e3f1c'}, {'abstract': 'Five vegetable and grain salads that make for perfect dishes on hot summer days.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/health/in-these-salads-grains-sometimes-play-a-supporting-role.html', 'snippet': 'Five vegetable and grain salads that make for perfect dishes on hot summer days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m taking stock of my pantry as I do every summer, and I’ve found a number of jars, boxes and bags of grains with small amounts left in them – a half cup here, a quarter cup there, at most a cup. I put them all on my worktable last week and devised a salad for each of them. Some of the salads were more about vegetables and herbs than grains; it just depended on how much of the grain I had to work with.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/science/26recipehealth/26recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/23/science/26recipehealth/26recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/science/26recipehealth/26recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/science/26recipehealth/26recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1369, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/science/26recipehealth/26recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/23/science/26recipehealth/26recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/science/26recipehealth/26recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In These Salads, Grains Sometimes Play a Supporting Role', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T14:02:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/76710ce8-9e36-534f-9606-80cf15310d6f', 'word_count': 671, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76710ce8-9e36-534f-9606-80cf15310d6f'}, {'abstract': 'As my baby’s nighttime cry becomes a throaty scream, I have felt my lungs fill with air in preparation to yell back at her. To make her feel as terrible as I do.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/the-sound-of-the-crying-baby-and-the-fury-of-the-exhausted-parent/', 'snippet': 'As my baby’s nighttime cry becomes a throaty scream, I have felt my lungs fill with air in preparation to yell back at her. To make her feel as terrible as I do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I don’t think of myself as someone who is easily angered. In my capacity as a mental health provider, I have been called every name in the book, spat at and nearly assaulted. Although these experiences are never pleasant, I can intellectualize away my feelings about patients’ hostile behavior: this is just a part of their illness. While I have certainly felt frustrated after a long night on call, I would not describe myself as feeling genuinely angry toward these patients. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sound (of the Crying Baby) and the Fury (of the Exhausted Parent)', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANGER (EMOTION)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crying', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T14:08:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arjune Rama, M. D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arjune', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rama', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d401b63-1045-5b12-9399-1d1b61b4180c', 'word_count': 646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d401b63-1045-5b12-9399-1d1b61b4180c'}, {'abstract': 'Actually, we aren’t having an argument.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/the-monetary-base-is-lm-and-all-that-very-nerdy/', 'snippet': 'Actually, we aren’t having an argument.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cullen Roche weighs in on my arguments about the usefulness of IS-LM — and I think we’ve reached a moment of impressive clarity. Basically, we aren’t having a real argument about the economic substance, on which we appear to agree. Instead, Roche and others are misunderstanding both what I mean by IS-LM and my reasons for invoking it in our current predicament. And much of the blame probably rests with yours truly: I probably haven’t been explicit enough about what I’m doing and why.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Monetary Base, IS-LM, And All That (Very Nerdy)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T14:13:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d75a946-66ec-5769-a51f-ca83c6bcee03',