n was focused on national security and social issues — as I like to say, he ran as America’s defender against gay married terrorists — but as soon as the returns were in, he declared that he had a mandate to … privatize Social Security.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Singapore Is The New Chile', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T14:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7706dd1-02be-53a5-9e42-2109b25f37ab', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7706dd1-02be-53a5-9e42-2109b25f37ab'}, {'abstract': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/books/review/editors-choice.html', 'snippet': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': ' THE GOOD LORD BIRD,  by James McBride (Riverhead, $27.95.) McBride’s romp of a novel, narrated by a freed slave boy who passes as a girl, is a risky portrait of the radical abolitionist John Brown in which irreverence becomes a new form of homage. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editors’ Choice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Editors’ Choice | Recent books of particular interest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T14:50:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1f908da-72cf-5b6c-ba13-484419232b66', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1f908da-72cf-5b6c-ba13-484419232b66'}, {'abstract': 'Upgrading from Windows XP before security support ends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/technology/personaltech/beyond-windows-xp.html', 'snippet': 'Upgrading from Windows XP before security support ends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. I keep reading warnings about Windows XP getting retired next year with no more security updates. I don’t like the look of Windows 8, but if I upgrade to Windows 7, how long will that system be supported?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyond Windows XP', 'kicker': 'Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Windows (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T14:52:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. D. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8e348d4-9268-5c49-990c-45f570b78401', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8e348d4-9268-5c49-990c-45f570b78401'}, {'abstract': 'Johnny Manziel’s style, rooted in improvisation and individualism, is challenging a tradition of institutional dominance valued by Nick Saban and Alabama.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/sport