ported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2eaeaa2c-ae4e-5cfa-b44d-0097e83f2855', 'word_count': 1356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2eaeaa2c-ae4e-5cfa-b44d-0097e83f2855'}, {'abstract': 'A memoir of living with autism, by Naoki Higashida, a Japanese 13-year-old.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/books/review/the-reason-i-jump-by-naoki-higashida.html', 'snippet': 'A memoir of living with autism, by Naoki Higashida, a Japanese 13-year-old.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Autism is an endless mystery, largely unknowable by its nature, yet there are dozens of books by or about autistic people determined to explain the lives of those affected. The newest is “The Reason I Jump,” popular in Japan since it was published in 2007. The author, Naoki Higashida, was 13 years old at the time he wrote the memoir, and nonverbal. He wrote by spelling out words on a Japanese alphabet letter board. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Voice of the Voiceless', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Voice of the Voiceless', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tisdale, Sallie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mitchell, David Stephen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Higashida, Naoki', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T15:19:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sallie Tisdale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sallie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tisdale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': No