'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T15:20:03+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Books', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By SARAH HARRISON SMITH', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Harrison', 'lastname': 'SMITH', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/cd47db37-1d5a-50e7-86b8-1a19a67403e9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/cd47db37-1d5a-50e7-86b8-1a19a67403e9'}, {'abstract': 'In four picture books, a menagerie of creatures teaches lessons on making friends and getting along.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/books/review/bully-by-laura-vaccaro-seeger-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'In four picture books, a menagerie of creatures teaches lessons on making friends and getting along.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No child (except yours and mine) is nice all the time. But we don’t look the other way anymore when children are mean. Four new picture books about bullying substitute animals for children. This charming menagerie lightens things up, allows us to laugh, and sometimes sneaks in — or rams through — a valuable lesson.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/books/review/0825-bks-Zerkin1/0825-bks-Zerkin1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/25/books/review/0825-bks-Zerkin1/0825-bks-Zerkin1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/books/review/0825-bks-Zerkin1/0825-bks-Zerkin1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo