egall switches from a raucous mood to the gently psychedelic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s pretty easy to spot Ty Segall’s influences. This singer-songwriter, raised in Laguna Beach, Calif., has Neil Young’s name tattooed on his right arm and the logo from Black Sabbath’s 1972 album “Vol. 4” inked on his left. His music is likewise a recognizable combination of disparate sources, displaying a remarkable ability to synthesize different elements of pre-1980s rock — heavy ’60s garage-rock riffs, harmonies that evoke the Beatles or early Tyrannosaurus Rex, and a punk velocity — into fresh and catchy pop nuggets.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25SNAPSHOT/25SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25SNAPSHOT/25SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25SNAPSHOT/25SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 443, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25SNAPSHOT/25SNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 886, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25SNAPSHOT/25SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25SNAPSHOT/25SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': No