 — badly. Already stretched thin, she strategically overloads on cases that could bolster her reputation and tutors an ambitious if occasionally bumbling pupil (Tom Hughes). ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25GUIDE2/25GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25GUIDE2/25GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25GUIDE2/25GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25GUIDE2/25GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25GUIDE2/25GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25GUIDE2/25GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25GUIDE2/25GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharp Lawyers, Willing to Cut', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sharp Lawyers, Willing to Cut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T17:52:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12baba83-b152-5924-99bb-91b6f69fceef', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12baba83-b152-5924-99bb-91b6f69fceef'}, {'abstract': 'For such a populist, accessible and at times interactive artist, Red Grooms doesn’t get much respect or exposure these days.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/arts/design/living-large-at-yale-gallery.html', 'snippet': 'For such a populist, accessible and at times interactive artist, Red Grooms doesn’t get much respect or exposure these days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For such a populist, accessible and at times interactive artist, Red Grooms doesn’t get much respect or exposure these days. His place in history rests mostly on his role in the invention of Happenings, less on his contribution as deviant, satirical Pop artist and latter-day American (art) Scene painter. Starting\xa0Friday, “Red Grooms: Larger Than Life” at the Yale University Art Gallery will feature Mr. Grooms’s forays into the history of modernism with a group of oversize paintings and drawings. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25GUIDE3/25GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 224, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25GUIDE3/25GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 224}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/arts/25GUIDE3/25GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'hei