e, 'lastname': 'Milioti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf298a5d-9286-501f-b35c-bba81473ebc0', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf298a5d-9286-501f-b35c-bba81473ebc0'}, {'abstract': 'Three weeks before the primary, John A. Catsimatidis has released two ads criticizing his main Republican rival, Joseph J. Lhota.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/the-ad-campaign-catsimatidis-turns-attention-to-lhota/', 'snippet': 'Three weeks before the primary, John A. Catsimatidis has released two ads criticizing his main Republican rival, Joseph J. Lhota.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks to his considerable fortune, John A. Catsimatidis has been a steady presence on television as he seeks the Republican nomination for mayor. His advertisements so far have touted his rags-to-riches biography and his commitment to public safety. Now, three weeks before the primary, he is going on the attack against his main Republican rival, Joseph J. Lhota. Mr. Lhota is the focus of a 30-second commercial, “3 Things,” that began airing Friday. A second new commercial, “Cares About Us,” also criticizes Mr. Lhota.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ad Campaign: Catsimatidis Goes on the Attack', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Catsimatidis Attacks Lhota on Tolls, Fares and ‘Mall Cops’ Comment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catsimatidis, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lhota, Joseph J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T18:19:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan and Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10168f61-0220-56b8-86e0-e80c57c9eb20', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10168f61-0220-56b8-86e0-e80c57c9eb20'}, {'abstract': 'Casamista, a portable humidifier, is made of molded satin-textured plastic, has a purifying filter and will fit on top of any water bottle or glass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/garden/play-misty-for-me.html', 'snippet': 'Casamista, a portable humidifier, is made of molded satin-textured plastic, has a purifying filter and will fit on top of any water bottle or glass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When designing Casamista, a portable humidifier produced by Umbra, Alan Wisniewski said he began with the idea of things that smoke: tugboat funnels, automobile tailpipes and rooftop chimneys. He settled on the last. “I thought that a traveling house with a functional chimney was a little reminder of a home away from home,” he said. The humidifier, made of molded satin-textured plastic, has a purifying filter and will fit on top of any water bottle or glass. It can also be used with water-soluble essential oils. The device comes with a USB cable and can run on AAA batteries, which are not included. Available in avocado or black for $25. Information: (800) 387-5122 or umbra.com. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/23/dining/23goods/23goods-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarg