jor': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T20:36:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Landon Thomas Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Landon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ab87074-05d9-585e-b890-a6f9596f7d19', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ab87074-05d9-585e-b890-a6f9596f7d19'}, {'abstract': 'A weekly capsule of events around the globe curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/calendar-coming-events-in-hawaii-kentucky-munich/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of events around the globe curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aloha Festivals, Oahu, Hawaii\xa0A celebration of Hawaiian culture and history through music, dance, cuisine and art will take place at various locations on Oahu during the 2013 Aloha Festivals from Sept. 12 to 28. Highlights include an opening ceremony featuring traditional chants and hula dancing, concerts, demonstrations, activities, displays of crafts, food booths, block parties and a parade with marching bands, floats with cascades of Hawaiian flowers, and pa’u riders (women on horseback), above. Many of this year’s events pay tribute to the ocean-voyaging culture of the islands’ ancestors. All events are free and open to the public.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calendar: Coming Events in Hawaii; Kentucky; Munich', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T20:36:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34d1e914-44ec-5e7d-856d-1194654e15a2', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34d1e914-44ec-5e7d-856d-1194654e15a2'}, {'abstract': 'The jewelry designer has a ceramic figure passed down from her grandfather that reflects its multifaceted owner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/fashion/jewlery-designer-betony-vernons-guardian-angel.html', 'snippet': 'The jewelry designer has a ceramic figure passed down from her grandfather that reflects its multifaceted owner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Success is, of course, a beautiful thing, a gift of affirmation from the world that comes in a neat little box. The only problem is that if you want to keep this gift, you usually have to get into the box and stay there. In other words, the good news is that you get a niche. That’s also the bad news. If you don’t fit easily in your assigned compartment, you may get uncomfortable.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/fashion/25POSSESSED1/25POSSESSED1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/25/fashion/25POSSESSED1/25POSSESSED1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 899}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/fashion/25POSSESSED1/25POSSESSED1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/fashion/25POSSESSED1/25POSSESSED1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1367