d_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/409cbb3e-30c4-5035-8f75-2c5ee4f2ebbb'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Clancy’s Splinter Cell: Blacklist seems to be on the brink of saying something challenging about the war on terror. And then it appears to retreat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/arts/video-games/tom-clancys-splinter-cell-blacklist-goes-undercover.html', 'snippet': 'Tom Clancy’s Splinter Cell: Blacklist seems to be on the brink of saying something challenging about the war on terror. And then it appears to retreat.', 'lead_paragraph': '“If you want to keep your hands, I want names,” an American spy growls at one point in the new video game Tom Clancy’s Splinter Cell: Blacklist. The man he is yelling at is on the ground, arms stretched, wrists trapped between the nearly closed legs of a folding chair. Our hero, the spy, whom we control in most of the game, is torturing this other man for information. He’s worried about another terrorist attack in the United States, which would be the second one in Blacklist.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/24/arts/24SPLINTER/24SPLINTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/24/arts/24SPLINTER/24SPLINTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/24/arts/24SPLINTER/24SPLINTER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/24/arts/24SPLINTER/24SPLINTER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '