the issue off with a short note about books. Well, about physical objects really. We photographed writers with forthcoming books — Jonathan Lethem, Edwidge Danticat, Richard Dawkins, Jhumpa Lahiri and Julian Barnes — at home in their work spaces. Quite frankly, none of the spaces look that remarkable; there are no bursts of design genius or eccentric collections. Just what one might expect: wood tables, crowded bookshelves, laptops, messy desks. But as you read each writer’s essay about their space, you understand the resonance these ordinary, simple things convey to each of them. Value is something we bestow upon objects — whether a picture tacked on the wall, a mess of papers, an old typewriter. We animate the inanimate through our memories, associations and desires.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editor’s Letter', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-23T23:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deborah Needleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deborah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Needleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00651425-a8f9-5e97-afda-25984c36d425', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00651425-a8f9-5e97-afda-25984c36d425'}, {'abstract': 'Readers discuss the Justice Department’s opposition to a proposed merger between American Airlines and USAirways.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/opinion/whats-ailing-the-airlines-and-us.html', 'snippet': 'Readers discuss the Justice Department’s opposition to a proposed merger between American Airlines and USAirways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [