eadline': {'main': 'At a Fed Conference, Views Differ Sharply on Stimulus’s Effect', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At a Fed Conference, Views Differ Sharply On Stimulus’s Effect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appelbaum, Binyamin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve Bank of Kansas City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jackson Hole (Wyo)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quantitative Easing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bullard, James B', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lagarde, Christine', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T00:53:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f886770e-0287-566f-b9fc-6e6c6e44476a', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f886770e-0287-566f-b9fc-6e6c6e44476a'}, {'abstract': 'Seeing Sandy as a sign of calamities that await, a presidential task force wants federal money directed to preparing for the worst.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/opinion/the-next-hurricane-and-the-next.html', 'snippet': 'Seeing Sandy as a sign of calamities that await, a presidential task force wants federal money directed to preparing for the worst.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hurricane Sandy, the monster storm that hit the Atlantic Seaboard on Oct. 29, left at least 159 dead and caused $65 billion in damages. But as a presidential task force made clear this week, Sandy cannot be considered a seasonal disaster or regional fluke but as yet another harbinger of the calamities that await in an era of climate change. With that in mind, the report says that individuals, local governments and states that expect federal help cannot simply restore what was there but must adopt new standards and harden community structures to withstand the next flood or hurricane. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Next Hurricane, and the Next', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Next Hurricane, and the Next...', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Flood Insurance Program', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T00:54:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/fff3714a-6ec4-5fef-b55b-0dd1907fb301', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fff3714a-6ec4-5fef-b55b-0dd1907fb301'}, {'abstract': 'Ecuadorean back-tracking on an oil drilling moratorium dashes hopes for a model for protecting regional biodiversity hot spots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/opinion/a-good-deal-gone-bad.html', 'snippet': 'Ecuadorean back-tracking on an oil drilling moratorium dashes hopes for a model for protecting regional biodiversity hot spots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2007, the president of Ecuador, Rafael Correa, offered the world a deal: find $3.6 billion and he would institute a permanent moratorium on oil drilling in the Amazon’s Yasuni National Park, one of the most biologically diverse places on the planet. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Good Deal Gone Bad', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Good Deal Gone Bad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yasuni National Park (Ecuador)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drilling and Boring', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Correa, Rafael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMAZON JUNGLE', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ecuador', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T01:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd2966f1-343d-5cb3-86dd-b0e404dda513', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd2966f1-343d-5cb3-86dd-b0e404dda513'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Harrison, once hailed as the next American tennis idol, has stumbled over the past year. But with a new coach and a new attitude, he hopes to rise again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/sports/tennis/a-potential-star-finds-lessons-in-his-stumbles.html', 'snippet': 'Ryan Harrison, once hailed as the next American tennis idol, has stumbled over the past year. But with a new coach and a new attitude, he hopes to rise again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the draw for the United States Open was made Thursday, Ryan Harrison’s name again appeared next to that of one of the biggest stars in the sport. This time, it was Rafael Nadal, the No. 2 seed, who comes to New York with a 10-match winning streak and a 15-0 record on hardcourts.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/24/sports/HARRISON/HARRISON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/24/sports/HARRISON/HARRISON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/24/sports/HARRISON/HARRISON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/24/sports/HARRISON/HARRISON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/24/sports/HARRISON/HARRISON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'c