 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/world/americas/mexico-bodies-linked-to-abduction.html', 'snippet': 'The remains of five bodies pulled from a mass grave in Tlalmanalco have been identified as members of a group of young people who vanished from a bar in May.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The remains of five bodies pulled from a mass grave discovered this week in Tlalmanalco have been identified as members of a group of young people who vanished from a bar in May, the attorney general said Friday. Twelve people disappeared from the Heaven nightclub in a bustling neighborhood in Mexico City, where residents are not accustomed to the brazen acts of violence that have convulsed other regions of the country. Relatives of the victims have complained about the investigation’s slow progress. The mass grave, 30 miles east of Mexico City, contained 13 craniums, the attorney general’s office said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Bodies Linked to Abduction', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Bodies Linked to Abduction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico City (Mexico)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T01:45:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Zabludovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zabludovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa096522-d371-567e-a627-feeba