'_id': 'nyt://article/14cc463b-b0ad-5976-9abf-f4afb565df63', 'word_count': 1104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14cc463b-b0ad-5976-9abf-f4afb565df63'}, {'abstract': 'General Order No. 11 and the horrific bush war on the nation’s western border.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/23/tom-ewings-dirty-war/', 'snippet': 'General Order No. 11 and the horrific bush war on the nation’s western border.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thomas Ewing Jr. was a conscientious man. Though never as flamboyant as his foster brother, William Tecumseh Sherman, Ewing was ambitious for political fame and fortune, as befitted the son of one of Ohio’s leading Whig politicians. His father had served both in the United States Senate and in the cabinets of Presidents William Henry Harrison and Zachary Taylor. Thomas Ewing Jr., or Tom, was his father’s personal secretary when the elder Ewing ran Taylor’s Department of the Interior. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tom Ewing’s Dirty War', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T02:11:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Etcheson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Etcheson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/befc2430-ade6-56b2-b4e5-a57b21aa6229', 'word_count': 1895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/befc2430-ade6-56b2-b4e5-a57b21aa6229'}, {'abstract': 'New York City’s Transportation Department issued a “request for expressions of interest” in a bid to find potential private partners that could install and maintain the service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/nyregion/staten-island-ferry-exploring-free-wi-fi-onboard-and-in-terminals.html', 'snippet': 'New York City’s Transportation Department issued a “request for expressions of interest” in a bid to find potential private partners that could install and maintain the service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Staten Island Ferry, known for its free rides and inexpensive beer, may soon add another amenity: Internet access.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Staten Island Ferry Exploring Free Wi-Fi Onboard and in Terminals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Staten Island Ferry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T02:12:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0da2d49-1cf6-59c0-849b-af639f9cc0fa', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0da2d49-1cf6-59c0-849b-af639f9cc0fa'}, {'abstract': 'The Times makes recommendations for the Democratic primary, for the public advocate and for the Manhattan and Queens borough presidents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/opinion/new-york-city-election-choices.html', 'snippet': 'The Times makes recommendations for the Democratic primary, for the public advocate and for the Manhattan and Queens borough presidents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Public AdvocateThe job of public advocate is little more than a bullhorn, and sometimes not even that. The original purpose of this position was to give citizens a voice in City Hall and serve as a watchdog on the mayor and the city government. But the job’s influence has been whittled away by a succession of mayors, and its budget is a mere $2.2 million, barely enough to pay the electric bills and a few modest salaries. Its only real power comes if the mayor dies or resigns; the public advocate takes over until an election can be held in a few months.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York City Election Choices', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York City Election Choices', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Public Advocate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Squadron, Daniel L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Letitia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saujani, Reshma', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Borough Presidents', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brewer, Gale A', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Katz, Melinda R', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T02:19:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Th