tigators that he had assumed that the vehicle’s guard had been knocking, having finished his pickup at the check-cashing store. But the man who entered the armored truck was not his partner. It was a gunman with a scarf wrapped around his head. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside Job Is Considered in Armored-Car Robbery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside Job Is Considered In Armored-Car Robbery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMORED CAR SERVICES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pay-O-Matic Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T02:25:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5e95610-3abc-5322-b11e-df37d7520273', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5e95610-3abc-5322-b11e-df37d7520273'}, {'abstract': 'Giants fans reflected on their decisions to wait in an endless string of brake lights for an inconsequential preseason game at MetLife Stadium.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/sports/football/weighing-pain-of-traffic-for-preseason-games.html', 'snippet': 'Giants fans reflected on their decisions to wait in an endless string of brake lights for an inconsequential preseason game at MetLife Stadium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Traffic is as much a part of the modern sports experience as the game itself, but not all event congestion is crea