, 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T12:56:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f55c7bba-3f4b-5dcc-927a-b265b862669a', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f55c7bba-3f4b-5dcc-927a-b265b862669a'}, {'abstract': 'The company that helped bring in cloud computing will — within the next few years — become a tired relic or lead big business customers to a whole new kind of computing. On the eve of a meeting with 21,000 customers, VMware’s chief executive lays out his plan.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/vmware-killed-the-past-can-it-claim-the-future/', 'snippet': 'The company that helped bring in cloud computing will — within the next few years — become a tired relic or lead big business customers to a whole new kind of computing. On the eve of a meeting with 21,000 customers, VMware’s chief executive lays ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'VMware is a 15-year-old tech company with a market capitalization of $36 billion. Next week, it will host 21,000 customers in San Francisco and will start to find out if that means it is young or old.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/24/business/bits-vmware/bits-vmware-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 878, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/24/business/bits-vmware/bits-vmware-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 878}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/24/business/bits-vmware/bits-vmware-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 700, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/24/business/bits-vmware/bits-vmware-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1400, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/24/business/bits-vmware/bits-vmware-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/24/business/bits-vmware/bits-vmware-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/24/business/bits-vmware/bits-vmware-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'VMware Killed the Past. Can It Claim the Future?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'VMware Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T13:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba532d34-62e4-5247-889f-c1a6d1542a4b', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba532d34-62e4-5247-889f-c1a6d1542a4b'}, {'abstract': 'From the point of view of a tech critic, Steven A. Ballmer’s 13-year reign as head of Microsoft is baffling.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/how-ballmer-missed-the-tidal-shifts-in-tech/', 'snippet': 'From the point of view of a tech critic, Steven A. Ballmer’s 13-year reign as head of Microsoft is baffling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By now, you’ve probably heard: Steven A. Ballmer will soon be stepping down as chief executive of Microsoft.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Ballmer Missed the Tidal Shifts in Tech', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ballmer, Steven A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T13:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0d34a99-6a09-5a9c-bba3-384a068f06ae', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0d34a99-6a09-5a9c-bba3-384a068f06ae'}, {'abstract': 'Network externalities, then and now.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/on-the-symmetry-between-microsoft-and-apple/', 'snippet': 'Network externalities, then and now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am not a tech industry maven, so I am busy coming up to speed on the implications of the Ballmer resignation. And what I’m about to say may be obvious to many. Still, I think it’s worth saying: there is, once you look past the surface, a remarkable symmetry between Microsoft’s strategy in its heyday and Apple’s strategy today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On The Symmetry Between Microsoft And Apple', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T13:38:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d6c8a3c-f529-55e5-8d9b-657733eec99d', 'word_count': 689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d6c8a3c-f529-55e5-8d9b-657733eec99d'}, {'abstract': 'The anniversary of the 1963 March on Washington is less a commemoration, organizers say, than an effort to inject fresh energy into issues of economics and justice that still leave racial gaps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/us/following-in-the-footsteps-of-king-and-looking-to-galvanize-a-new-generation.html', 'snippet': 'The anniversary of the 1963 March on Washington is less a commemoration, organizers say, than an effort to inject fresh energy into issues of economics and justice that still leave racial gaps.', 'lead_paragraph': "WASHINGTON — Half a century after the emotional apex of the civil rights movement, Martin Luther King Jr.'s “I Have a Dream” speech, tens of thousands of people retraced his footsteps on Saturday, and his successors in the movement spoke of the still-unmet promise of America, as he did, at the Lincoln Memorial.", 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trying to Inspire a New Generation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Following King’s Path, and Trying to Galvanize a New Generation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gabriel, Trip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharpton, Al', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, John R', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fulton, Sybrina', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T13:42:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7d7cfd2-c157-5101-b003-a942373ee2d7', 'word_count': 1263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7d7cfd2-c157-5101-b003-a942373ee2d7'}, {'abstract': 'A government program, hidden in plain sight.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/maybe-theyll-never-figure-it-out/', 'snippet': 'A government program, hidden in plain sight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kathleen Geier points to some polling I’d missed: 39 percent of Americans agree that the government should stay out of Medicare, while only 46 percent disagree; the rest aren’t sure. She also points to the Suzanne Mettler work showing that many beneficiaries of Social Security and Medicare believe that they have never benefited from a government program.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maybe They’ll Never Figure It Out', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T14:27:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3289d64a-1704-5345-bcbd-c4b903fef041', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3289d64a-1704-5345-bcbd-c4b903fef041'}, {'abstract': 'Video, images and voices of people who participated in the Saturday’s event commemorating the 50th anniversary of the March on Washington for Jobs and Freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/scenes-from-the-50th-anniversary-of-the-march-on-washington/', 'snippet': 'Video, images and voices of people who participated in the Saturday’s event commemorating the 50th anniversary of the March on Washington for Jobs and Freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated | 9:24 p.m. As my colleagues reported, tens of thousands of people from across the country streamed onto the National Mall on Saturday for a daylong commemoration of the approaching 50th anniversary of the March on Washington for Jobs and Freedom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/24/us/20130825_MARCH-slide-VLWX/20130825_MARCH-slide-VLWX-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/24/us/20130825_MARCH-slide-VLWX/20130825