ing the tournament from her home in Belgium, where she is expecting her second child, a boy, with her husband, the retired basketball player Brian Lynch. She has spent the year as a fan, particularly of her friend and fellow Belgian Kirsten Flipkens, who reached the semifinals of Wimbledon. She remains involved in tennis as a WTA ambassador for USANA Health Sciences, and is renovating and developing a tennis club and academy in her hometown, Bree. This interview was edited and condensed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thrill of Family Replaces Thrill of Game for Clijsters', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clijsters, Kim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T18:12:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Naila-Jean Meyers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Naila-jean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meyers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ec65c3a-086c-531a-8d3a-bd7d58045e43', 'word_count': 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ec65c3a-086c-531a-8d3a-bd7d58045e43'}, {'abstract': 'We cannot rely on the makers of new technology to think about the moral and privacy implications.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/sunday-review/addicted-to-apps.html', 'snippet': 'We cannot rely on the makers of new technology to think about the moral and privacy implications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — IN Silicon Valley, that fairy-tale land of robots and driverless cars, a deeply held belief motivates all: If you build it, they w