t': 'A founder and the director of Random International on depressing books, world music and raising tadpoles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/opinion/sunday/florian-ortkrass.html', 'snippet': 'A founder and the director of Random International on depressing books, world music and raising tadpoles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Florian Ortkrass is a founder and director of Random International, a group of London-based artists who combine technology and natural elements to create temporary, interactive installations, including the recent “Rain Room” at the Musuem of Modern Art. Another work, “Tower,” an appearing and disappearing water structure, opened on Friday at the Ruhrtriennale international arts festival in Germany. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/sunday-review/25DOWNLOAD/25download-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 288, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/sunday-review/25DOWNLOAD/25download-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 562, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/sunday-review/25DOWNLOAD/25download-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/25/sunday-review/25DOWNLOAD/25download-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/sunday-review/25DOWNLOAD/25download-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Florian Ortkrass', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florian Ortkrass', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Random International', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Kate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ortkrass, Florian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T18:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0ea2e02-3889-568c-8095-ca9e9d727821', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0ea2e02-3889-568c-8095-ca9e9d727821'}, {'abstract': 'In Egypt and the broader Middle East, the United States can only do so much without the support of the people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/opinion/sunday/friedman-foreign-policy-by-whisper-and-nudge.html', 'snippet': 'In Egypt and the broader Middle East, the United States can only do so much without the support of the people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF you follow the commentary on American foreign policy toward Egypt and the broader Middle East today, several themes stand out: People in the region argue: “Whatever went wrong, the United States is to blame.” Foreign policy experts argue: “Whatever President Obama did, he got it wrong.” And the American public is saying: “We’re totally fed up with that part of the world and can’t wait for the start of the N.F.L. season. How do you like those 49ers?” ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinio