 but at the upper and lower ends of the spectrum. The outlook for the middle class may rely on “new artisans” who combine technical and interpersonal skills.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the four years since the Great Recession officially ended, the productivity of American workers — those lucky enough to have jobs — has risen smartly. But the United States still has two million fewer jobs than before the downturn, the unemployment rate is stuck at levels not seen since the early 1990s and the proportion of adults who are working is four percentage points off its peak in 2000.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Technology Wrecks the Middle Class', 'kicker': 'The Great Divide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Technology Wrecks the Middle Class', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T18:35:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David H. Autor And David Dorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Autor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48d97238-8c74-548e-8506-6d4bdaeabaf3', 'word_count': 1634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48d97238-8c74-548e-8506-6d4bdaeabaf3'}, {'abstract': 'A new White House initiative is intended to involve social and behavioral scientists in policy making.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/business/public-policies-made-to-fit-people.html', 'snippet': 'A new White House initiative is intended to involve social and behavioral scientists in policy making.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I HAVE written here before about the potential gains to government from involving social and behavioral scientists in designing public policies. My enthusiasm comes in part from my experiences as an academic adviser to the Behavioral Insights Team created in Britain by Prime Minister David Cameron.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Public Policies, Made to Fit People', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Public Policies, Made to Fit People', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thaler, Richard H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of Science and Technology Policy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reading and Writing Skills (Education)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T18:35:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard H. Thaler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Thaler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'ny