45, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f927b0cb-d95b-50a5-a08a-c41ead4fbe73'}, {'abstract': 'Want to lose a friend who’s a writer? Ask her, a month in, how it’s going.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/dont-ask-what-im-writing/', 'snippet': 'Want to lose a friend who’s a writer? Ask her, a month in, how it’s going.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No stage of the writing process — not the editor’s first response to the manuscript, not the review gauntlet — is as fraught for writers as those first few months of uncertainty: that miserable time when we think, believe, know with absolute assurance that we’ve found the key to the novel in our heads, though maybe, probably, definitely not.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Ask What I’m Writing', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Ask What I’m Writing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T19:06:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Slouka', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slouka', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/048d3d19-1e61-5b7a-bdb3-c22f353f6998', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/048d3d19-1e61-5b7a-bdb3-c22f353f6998'}, {'abstract': 'A Fed leader has to know that economics is not yet a science, and may never be.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/what-is-economics-good-for/', 'snippet': 'A Fed leader has to know that economics is not yet a science, and may never be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recent debates over who is most qualified to serve as the next chairman of the Federal Reserve have focused on more than just the candidates’ theory-driven economic expertise. They have touched on matters of personality and character as well. This is as it should be. Given the nature of economies, and our ability to understand them, the task of the Fed’s next leader will be more a matter of craft and wisdom than of science.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Is Economics Good For?', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Is Economics Good For?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T19:09:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Rosenberg and Tyler Curtain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Curtain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b86bbce-eea3-51ce-8a5f-1fdaa68edeb0', 'word_count': 1274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b86bbce-eea3-51ce-8a5f-1fdaa68edeb0'}, {'abstract': 'Notable quotes from business articles that appeared in The New York Times last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/business/the-chatter-for-sunday-august-25.html', 'snippet': 'Notable quotes from business articles that appeared in The New York Times last week.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There will be less opinion, less yelling and fewer celebrity sightings.