e Federal Reserve and the central banks of Europe and Japan, by depressing domestic interest rates, have helped to push trillions of dollars into developing markets in recent years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Central Bankers Say Emerging Economies Will Be Ready for Fed Exit', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T20:28:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6a9ab0d-7ad5-57be-a791-130cda3d90ec', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6a9ab0d-7ad5-57be-a791-130cda3d90ec'}, {'abstract': 'A gem from James Tobin.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/24/commercial-banks-as-creators-of-money/', 'snippet': 'A gem from James Tobin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thank you, Matthew Klein! In the course of critiquing Robert Hall’s paper for Jackson Hole, he mentions and links to another half-century-old paper by James Tobin, Commercial Banks as Creators of “Money” (pdf), that I had forgotten about, and is even more precisely on point than the Tobin-Brainard piece I’ve been citing. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Commercial Banks As Creators of “Money”', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-24T20:31:13+0000', 'document_ty