ww.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/us/politics/iowas-gop-fears-its-role-in-presidential-selection-is-diminishing.html', 'snippet': 'In Iowa, which prides itself on its pivotal role in presidential campaigns, Republicans worry that the growing dominance of the conservative wing could render it less relevant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMES, Iowa — On the surface, Iowa’s Republican presidential caucuses seem healthier than ever: would-be candidates are flocking here mere months after the last White House race ended, drawing sizable crowds and ample news coverage. Senator Ted Cruz of Texas and former Senator Rick Santorum of Pennsylvania were in this central Iowa college town for a Christian conservative conference this month, and Senator Rand Paul of Kentucky has come to the state twice since May. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iowa’s G.O.P. Fears Its Role in Presidential Selection Is Diminishing', 'kicker': 'Political Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iowa’s G.O.P. Fears Its Role in Presidential Selection Is Diminishing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Jonathan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Branstad, Terry E', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-