giving the homeless three options: accept help at a shelter, go to jail or leave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLUMBIA, S.C. — In South Carolina’s capital, officials declare that their tree-lined Main Street, clogged with shops, banks, restaurants and hotels, is evidence that a long-sought economic revival has arrived.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/us/COLUMBIA-1/COLUMBIA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/25/us/COLUMBIA-1/COLUMBIA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/us/COLUMBIA-1/COLUMBIA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/us/COLUMBIA-1/COLUMBIA-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1205, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/us/COLUMBIA-1/COLUMBIA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/25/us/COLUMBIA-1/COLUMBIA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/us/COLUMBIA-1/COLUMBIA-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'South Carolina City Takes Steps to Evict Homeless From Downtown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Southern Capital Seeks Limits on the Homeless', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Columbia (SC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blinder, Alan S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'City Councils', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-25T19:16:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44731a61-2198-5186-915d-49825aff53a4', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44731a61-2198-5186-915d-49825aff53a4'}, {'abstract': 'Rangers goaltender Henrik Lundqvist said he did not agree with a new law in Russia that has been criticized as antigay, but he said he thought sports and politics should be kept separate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/sports/hockey/lundqvist-clarifies-stance-on-russian-law.html', 'snippet': 'Rangers goaltender Henrik Lundqvist said he did not agree with a new law in Russia that has been criticized as antigay, but he said he thought sports and politics should be kept separate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last season, Rangers goalie Henrik Lundqvist was one of the first professional athletes to participate in the You Can Play campaign, promoting respect for all athletes without regard to sexual orientation. That was why some were surprised when Lundqvist, in Stockholm earlier this month to prepare for the Sochi Olympics, declined to comment on a new law in Russia that has been criticized in the West as antigay. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lundqvist Disagrees With Russian Law, but Supports Games', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lundqvist Disagrees With Russian Law, But Supports Games', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lundqvist, Henrik', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeff Z', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Hockey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burke, Brian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-25T19:24:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e860672-b48a-558e-aae0-352c2e212099', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e860672-b48a-558e-aae0-352c2e212099'}, {'abstract': 'Mozart had the spotlight to himself on Friday, the final night of the monthlong Mostly Mozart Festival at Lincoln Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/arts/music/louis-langree-leads-mostly-mozart-festivals-grand-finale.html', 'snippet': 'Mozart had the spotlight to himself on Friday, the final night of the monthlong Mostly Mozart Festival at Lincoln Center.', 'lead_paragraph'