me': None, 'lastname': 'Rapold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb61e4b3-fa6c-5df5-951e-b4aa05b1547e', 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb61e4b3-fa6c-5df5-951e-b4aa05b1547e'}, {'abstract': 'NBC is developing a half-hour television series based on the 1994 coming-of-age film “Reality Bites,” according to Variety’s Web site.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/arts/television/reality-bites-tv-series.html', 'snippet': 'NBC is developing a half-hour television series based on the 1994 coming-of-age film “Reality Bites,” according to Variety’s Web site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NBC is developing a half-hour television series based on the 1994 coming-of-age film “Reality Bites,” according to Variety’s Web site. This single-camera comedy will follow the continuing romantic and professional misadventures of the movie’s heroine, Lelaina Pierce (originally played by Winona Ryder), and her group of 20-something slacker friends living in Houston during the 1990s. Helen Childress, who wrote the film’s screenplay, will also write the pilot script, and Ben Stiller, who starred in and directed the movie, will be an executive producer on the show. Casting has not been announced.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Reality Bites’ TV Series', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Reality Bites’ TV Series', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Reality Bites (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-25T22:07:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a32fb6ad-491f-5409-a1ed-1708dcc235e6', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a32fb6ad-491f-5409-a1ed-1708dcc235e6'}, {'abstract': 'The singer Linda Ronstadt has revealed in an interview with AARP Magazine that she has Parkinson’s disease and that she is no longer able to sing as a result.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/arts/music/linda-ronstadt-is-ill.html', 'snippet': 'The singer Linda Ronstadt has revealed in an interview with AARP Magazine that she has Parkinson’s disease and that she is no longer able to sing as a result.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The singer Linda Ronstadt has revealed in an interview with AARP Magazine that she has Parkinson’s disease and that she is no longer able to sing as a result. Ms. Ronstadt, 67, received her official diagnosis eight months ago, although she had symptoms for the past eight years. “I couldn’t sing,” she said in the interview, “and I couldn’t figure out why. I knew it was mechanical. I knew it had to do with the muscles.” Her hands also began to shake, but she attributed that symptom to a shoulder operation. A neurologist then diagnosed Parkinson’s. “I wouldn’t have suspected that in a million, billion years,” she said. Ms. Ronstadt’s memoir, “Simple Dreams,” is to be released on Sept. 17 and chronicles her life and musical career. She has won 11 Grammy Awards and sold over 100 million records worldwide. But according to AARP’s Web site, the book does not discuss her diagnosis or the loss of her voice.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/arts/arts3/arts3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 553, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/26/arts/arts3/arts3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 553}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/arts/arts3/arts3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 944, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/arts/arts3/arts3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 1476, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/arts/arts3/arts3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/26/arts/arts3/arts3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/arts/arts3/arts3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Linda Ronstadt Is Ill', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Linda Ronstadt Is Ill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ronstadt, Linda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Parkinson's Disease", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-25T22:08:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bad790b-0b90-5d1c-8f34-88f0603e3a16', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bad790b-0b90-5d1c-8f34-88f0603e3a16'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Leonard, a son of the author Elmore Leonard, who died last week at 87, hopes to complete his father’s last novel, BBC News reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/books/a-final-book-is-planned-from-elmore-leonard.html', 'snippet': 'Peter Leonard, a son of the author Elmore Leonard, who died last week at 87, hopes to complete his father’s last novel, BBC News reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter Leonard, a son of the author Elmore Leonard, who died last week at 87, hopes to complete his father’s last novel, BBC News reported. In an interview on the BBC Radio news program “Broadcasting House” on Sunday, Mr. Leonard, who is also a published author, said that the matter had “been discussed among family members and I’ve talked to Greg Sutter, Elmore’s longtime researcher.” He added that he did not know how many pages his father had already written. The book, which has the working title “Blue Dreams,” was originally conceived to feature a rogue Immigration and Customs Enforcement agent, bull riding and Mr. Leonard’s popular federal marshal character, Raylan Givens.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Final Book Is Planned From Elmore Leonard', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Final Book Is Planned From Elmore Leonard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leonard, Elmore (1925-2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-25T22:09:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6da9f95a-adb3-5880-becb-47cfc9bbac64', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6da9f95a-adb3-5880-becb-47cfc9bbac64'}, {'abstract': 'After the pair events at the 3rd World Youth Open Championships came the junior (under 26) and youngsters (under 21) knockout teams.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/crosswords/bridge/australia-vs-turkey-at-3rd-world-youth-open-championships.html', 'snippet': 'After the pair events at the 3rd World Youth Open Championships came the junior (under 26) and youngsters (under 21) knockout teams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — After the pair events at the 3rd World Youth Open Championships came the junior (under 26) and youngsters (under 21) knockout teams. (There were too few entries for a separate women’s competition. They competed in the appropriate age brackets.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/crosswords/bridge/26card/26card-jumbo.gif', 'height': 500, 'width': 247, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/crosswords/bridge/26card/26card-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 500, 'width': 247, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/crosswords/bridge/26card/26card-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy