ew York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Series', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca871906-9367-5531-98b6-9ebee13b88c0', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca871906-9367-5531-98b6-9ebee13b88c0'}, {'abstract': 'Joseph J. Lhota’s new ad uses former Mayor Rudolph W. Giuliani to respond to an attack ad by John A. Catsimitadis, his major opponent.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/the-ad-campaign-lhota-brings-in-a-big-gun/', 'snippet': 'Joseph J. Lhota’s new ad uses former Mayor Rudolph W. Giuliani to respond to an attack ad by John A. Catsimitadis, his major opponent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joseph J. Lhota jumped into the Republican race for mayor with the support of his former boss, Rudolph W. Giuliani, and now, a little more than two weeks before Primary Day, he is deploying Mr. Giuliani in a new 30-second advertisement, titled “Wrongly Attacked.” The ad is a response to a new attack ad by his major opponent in the Republican primary, the billionaire John A. Catsimatidis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ad Campaign: Lhota Brings In a Big Gun', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catsimatidis, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lhota, Joseph J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T02:33:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e360ee52-9b6d-5755-a908-7c7be26eef7c', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e360ee52-9b6d-5755-a908-7c7be26eef7c'}, {'abstract': 'The most recent ad from the Thompson campaign features the candidate speaking directly to the camera on stop-and-frisk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000002405489/lived-it.html', 'snippet': 'The most recent ad from the Thompson campaign features the candidate speaking directly to the camera on stop-and-frisk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most recent ad from the Thompson campaign features the candidate speaking directly to the camera on stop-and-frisk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/multimedia/video-lived-adcampaign/video-lived-adcampaign-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/25/multimedia/video-lived-adcampaign/video-lived-adcampaign-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/multimedia/video-lived-adcampaign/video-lived-adcampaign-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/25/multimedia/video-lived-adcampaign/video-lived-adcampaign-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/multimedia/video-lived-adcampaign/video-lived-adcampaign-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': "'Lived It'", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T02:34:31+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'YouTube', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Youtube', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/6a913994-3343-5dca-8e33-ec35e3d9a9bc', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/6a913994-3343-5dca-8e33-ec35e3d9a9bc'}, {'abstract': 'William C. Thompson Jr., in the first ad attacking a rival in the Democratic primary, said Bill de Blasio had lied.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/25/the-ad-campaign-thompson-counterattacks/', 'snippet': 'William C. Thompson Jr., in the first ad attacking a rival in the Democratic primary, said Bill de Blasio had lied.', 'lead_paragraph': 'William C. Thompson Jr., a Democratic candidate for mayor, spent much of the previous week arguing that Bill de Blasio, one of his rivals, was stretching the truth in his latest ad, which claims that Mr. de Blasio would be “the only candidate to end a stop-and-frisk era that targets minorities.” On Sunday, Mr. Thompson intensified the debate by attacking Mr. de Blasio directly in his own 30-second television advertisement, called “Lived It.” The ad marks the first time that a Democratic candidate has gone after a rival in a television ad, and comes just over two weeks before a primary vote that appears to be a tight race among Mr. Thompson, Mr. de Blasio and Christine C. Quinn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ad Campaign: Thompson Counterattacks', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, William C Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T02:40:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f6fd64e-016b-5292-9e68-51f9fff86a85', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f6fd64e-016b-5292-9e68-51f9fff86a85'}, {'abstract': 'Bill de Blasio was the campaign manager for Hillary Rodham Clinton’s 2000 Senate race, and his leadership style, easygoing but indecisive, could be inefficient, aides said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/nyregion/in-2000-a-clinton-war-room-didnt-fit-de-blasios-style.html', 'snippet': 'Bill de Blasio was the campaign manager for Hillary Rodham Clinton’s 2000 Senate race, and his leadership style, easygoing but indecisive, could be inefficient, aides said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the middle of the 2000 Senate race, Hillary Rodham Clinton’s advisers found themselves on a conference call about what seemed a small-bore subject: campaign signs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/nyregion/Y-DEBLASIO/Y-DEBLASIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/26/nyregion/Y-DEBLASIO/Y-DEBLASIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/