mall town in Alabama to defend his cousin Bill (Ralph Macchio) in a murder trial. Marisa Tomei, above with Mr. Pesci, in an Oscar-winning performance, is Mona Lisa Vito, Vinny’s fiancée, researcher, expert witness and conscience. In The New York Times, Vincent Canby wrote that this comedy “is easily the most inventive and enjoyable American film farce in a long time, even during those extended patches when it seems to be marking time or when it continues with a running gag that can’t stay the distance.” He added that Mr. Pesci “is a puzzled delight as he attempts to gather his wits, being helped not at all by Mona Lisa’s loudly articulated common sense and her ability to read law books and retain their contents.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T04:17:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e63a5f0-2b54-583b-9379-656ff74a6c79', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e63a5f0-2b54-583b-9379-656ff74a6c79'}, {'abstract': 'Arguments about equal pay for an unequal product miss the point. The games on the two tours are fundamentally different, and the biggest difference is the serve.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/celebrating-difference-between-mens-and-womens-tennis/', 'snippet': 'Arguments about equal pay for an unequal product miss the point. The games on the two tours are fundamentally different, and the biggest difference is the serve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is always noise at the United States Open comparing men and women in terms of prize money.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating Difference Between Men’s and Women’s Tennis', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Women's Tennis Assn", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T04:41:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': "By Craig O'Shannessy", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Shannessy", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54e8c038-2227-5480-8ec4-00586381d907', 'word_count': 831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54e8c038-2227-5480-8ec4-00586381d907'}, {'abstract': 'ONGC Videsh, a unit of the India’s state-run Oil and Natural Gas Corporation, says it will acquire a 10 percent stake in a natural gas project in Mozambique from Anadarko Petroleum in an all-cash deal.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/indian-firm-to-pay-2-6-billion-to-build-its-stake-in-african-gas-project/', 'snippet': 'ONGC Videsh, a unit of the India’s state-run Oil and Natural Gas Corporation, says it will acquire a 10 percent stake in a natural gas project in Mozambique from Anadarko Petroleum in an all-cash deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG – A unit of India’s state-run Oil and Natural Gas Corporation said on Monday that it would pay $2.64 billion in cash for a minority stake in a natural gas project in Mozambique, the latest example of how Asia’s biggest emerging economies are zeroing in on Mozambique’s vast offshore energy resources. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian Firm to Pay $2.6 Billion to Build Its Stake in African Gas Project', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANADARKO PETROLEUM CORP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ONGC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mozambique', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T04:45:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Gough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9544b247-e02f-5518-b015-1dd74bd8c6f4', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9544b247-e02f-5518-b015-1dd74bd8c6f4'}, {'abstract': 'The 2013 MTV Video Music Awards were a tribute to the stubborn persistence of pop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/arts/music/mtv-video-music-awards-review.html', 'snippet': 'The 2013 MTV Video Music Awards were a tribute to the stubborn persistence of pop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We experience things via reactions now, rather than head-on. As has become the norm, the best way to engage with the 2013 MTV Video Music Awards, broadcast on MTV on Sunday night from the Barclays Center in Brooklyn, was to follow on Twitter the slanderous jokes and instantly available GIFs of memorable moments.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1