 who has over the past four decades explored expansive themes through 11 feature films and 22 documentaries, many of which have won awards.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/being-adoor-gopalakrishnan/', 'snippet': 'Profile of the Indian film director who has over the past four decades explored expansive themes through 11 feature films and 22 documentaries, many of which have won awards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Adoor Gopalakrishnan had his way, India would celebrate the centenary of Indian cinema not this year, exactly 100 years after “Raja Harishchandra,” the first feature film made in India, but in 2055. For Mr. Gopalakrishnan, 72, one of India’s finest film directors, the birth of Indian cinema began in 1955 because it was the year that Satyajit Ray made “Pather Panchali” (“Song of the Little Road”).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/world/asia/26-gopalakrishnan-IndiaInk/26-gopalakrishnan-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/26/world/asia/26-gopalakrishnan-IndiaInk/26-gopalakrishnan-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/world/asia/26-gopalakrishnan-IndiaInk/26-gopalakrishnan-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/world/asia/26-gopalakrishnan-IndiaInk/26-gopalakrishnan-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/