ould you put these sentences in order?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Note: As we explained last week, we’ll be publishing a new type of Test Yourself question, one just for English-Language Learners, each Monday morning this school year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | E.L.L. Practice', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T08:40:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Ferlazzo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ferlazzo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7565a4c6-75a7-5696-bbd0-ade45c56951f', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7565a4c6-75a7-5696-bbd0-ade45c56951f'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibit opening in Boston explores “complexities of identity,” showcasing works of art by female photographers in Iran and the Arab world.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/a-show-of-strength-by-middle-eastern-women-photographers/', 'snippet': 'An exhibit opening in Boston explores “complexities of identity,” showcasing works of art by female photographers in Iran and the Arab world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite the cultural limitations many have faced, women have been at the forefront of photography in Iran and the Arab world. In societies dominated by men, female photographers are using images to raise questions and explore issues of identity. They’re telling stories\xa0— often their own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Show of Strength by Middle Eastern Women Photographers', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject',