hange operator in the United States, as the industry continues to face pressure to consolidate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several weeks ago, William O’Brien, the chief executive of the trading platform Direct Edge, and several of his senior managers flew discreetly to Kansas City, Mo. Waiting for them at the Charles B. Wheeler Downtown Airport there were Joe Ratterman, head of the rival BATS Global Markets, and his team.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BATS and Direct Edge to Merge, Taking On Older Rivals', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Exchanges to Merge, Taking On Larger Rivals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Brien, William", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratterman, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BATS Global Markets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Direct Edge', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NASDAQ OMX Group Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T13:02:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced and Nathaniel Popper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Popper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77a196a2-8baf-5172-8e5c-bdbf520e7e5b', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77a196a2-8baf-5172-8e5c-bdbf520e7e5b'}, {'abstract': 'As the school year nears, experts urge us to prepare our children for new schedules well ahead of the first day. But what if we don’t?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/when-school-starts-tomorrow-and-your-child-is-still-on-a-summer-schedule/', 'snippet': 'As the school year nears, experts urge us to prepare our children for new schedules well ahead of the first day. But what if we don’t?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I know I should have, but I didn’t. How many times a day does that phrase run through a parent’s head? I know I should have cooked them a vegetable for dinner. I know I should have enforced that timeout threat. I know I should have made them change out of their PJs before camp; brush their teeth for the full two minutes; turn off the television after an hour; stop using the word “idiot” when referring to their brothers (I suspect the last two are related … thank you Snotty Boy of “Back to the Barnyard”).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/style/motherlode-alarm-clock/motherlode-alarm-clock-jumbo.png', 'height': 369, 'width': 372, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/style/motherlode-alarm-clock/motherlode-alarm-clock-superJumbo.png', 'height': 369, 'width': 372, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/style/motherlode-alarm-clock/motherlode-alarm-clock-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/25/style/motherlode-alarm-clock/motherlode-alarm-clock-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailhe