 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/science/a-molten-planet-and-meteorite-jewelry.html', 'snippet': 'Recent developments in health and science news. This week: A bog mummy’s remains are dated to 2000 B.C., and a United Nations warning on global warming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid the big and alarming news — a United Nations report confirming that human-made greenhouse emissions were significantly warming the planet and leading to much higher sea levels — were some diverting discoveries. Astronomers spotted a planet that circles its star in a little more than eight hours, a well-preserved bog mummy found in Ireland is at least 4,000 years old, and marine scientists discovered a new species of clam that lives among the spines of sea urchins in the Pacific Ocean.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/science/sub27WEEK/sub27WEEK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/27/science/sub27WEEK/sub27WEEK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/science/sub27WEEK/sub27WEEK-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/science/sub27WEEK/sub27WEEK-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1247, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/science/sub27WEEK/sub27WEEK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbna