ell. The food stands have the usual sporting event fare, but they also teem with quality items that go beyond hot dogs and nachos. The bad news is, you’ll pay dearly for them. The good news is, the prices do not seem to have gone up from last year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Open Food Review: An Incredibly Shrinking Lunch', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T19:46:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c78c705-7efd-5944-8b02-4140c703a5e0', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c78c705-7efd-5944-8b02-4140c703a5e0'}, {'abstract': 'Given Donald Trump’s financial achievements, and lack of modesty, it is no surprise he opened a school to pass on the secrets of his success, but Trump University always seemed liked a dubious enterprise, the author contends.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/trump-further-sullies-for-profit-schools/', 'snippet': 'Given Donald Trump’s financial achievements, and lack of modesty, it is no surprise he opened a school to pass on the secrets of his success, but Trump University always seemed liked a dubious enterprise, the author contends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leave it to the real estate mogul Donald Trump to give the for-profit education industry an even worse rap than it already has. Schools looking to make a buck have come under scrutiny recently for taking students’ money but providing lackluster job results. New York State’s $40 million lawsuit over Mr. Trump’s foray into the industry underscores the need for these institutions to make credentials clear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Further Sullies For-Profit Schools', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'For-Profit Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T19:54:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Indiviglio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Indiviglio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9402eb21-0ceb-5a15-89eb-58c10353acea', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9402eb21-0ceb-5a15-89eb-58c10353acea'}, {'abstract': 'Three series will focus on documentary films at this year’s New York Film Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/new-york-film-festival-to-showcase-documentaries-on-science-and-democracy/', 'snippet': 'Three series will focus on documentary films at this year’s New York Film Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Movies\xa0 about science and democracy and a series devoted to cinematic portraiture will anchor the documentary portion of the New York Film Festival, the Film Society of Lincoln Center said on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Film Festival to Showcase Documentaries on Science and Democracy', 'kicker': 'Arts