y Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1bc16a2-e040-5df6-bad5-de2749798a2e', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1bc16a2-e040-5df6-bad5-de2749798a2e'}, {'abstract': 'Photos from the West Bank, Iraq, Syria and Myanmar.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/pictures-of-the-day-west-bank-and-elsewhere-14/', 'snippet': 'Photos from the West Bank, Iraq, Syria and Myanmar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from the West Bank, Iraq, Syria and Myanmar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: West Bank and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T20:43:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee2f0677-0120-54b5-96a2-8378dbd3a07d', 'word_count': 42, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee2f0677-0120-54b5-96a2-8378dbd3a07d'}, {'abstract': 'Put your predictive skills to the test each week of the baseball season.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/triple-play-week-21-results/', 'snippet': 'Put your predictive skills to the test each week of the baseball season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a close call on Question 1, with just over 33 percent of you picking the Tampa Bay Rays to come out of the week leading the American League wild-card race and just under 32 percent going with the Oakland A’s. At 74-54, the Rays have a two and a half game edge over the A’s in the wild-card standings. (Tampa Bay trails Boston by a game in the A.L. East, and Oakland is second to Texas by two and a half games in the A.L. West.) Nice work, prognosticators. The Rays took two out of three games at Baltimore, then two out of three at home against the Yankees, while the A’s lost four of six over all, including two of three over the weekend at Baltimore.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Triple Play: Week 21 Results', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kershaw, Clayton', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Votto, Joey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN LEAGUE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oakland Athletics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Rays', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T20:48:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roger van der Horst', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5086fbf4-ba4f-5a2b-8a59-8478f7c53432', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5086fbf4-ba4f-5a2b-8a59-8478f7c53432'}, {'abstract': 'Served cool, the traditional Japanese beverage can be the perfect rejoinder to hot, stifling nights.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/feeling-for-a-sake-thats-perfect-for-summer-sipping/', 'snippet': 'Served cool, the traditional Japanese beverage can be the perfect rejoinder to hot, stifling nights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the uninitiated, drinking sake probably only means throwing back porcelain thimbles of scalding liquid that turns tepid before you know it. But the traditional Japanese beverage served cold can be a pleasant answer to less-than-comfortable summer nights. A particularly delicious variety that has been popping up at many of New York’s izakayas (the Japanese equivalent to a gastropub) and sake bars recently is the Tokubetsu Junmai from the gourmet sake brewery Nanbu Bijin. Its name translates to “southern beauty,” but Nanbu Bijin is actually located in northern Japan, in a region once controlled by the Nanbu clan of samurai. This junmai — a pure, full-bodied class of premium sake — has a bright, floral bouquet, almost like a lily blossom, and starts crisp before offering a sweet finish almost like honeydew. New Yorkers can find it at Decibel, in the East Village, and Sakagura, near Grand Central Terminal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling For | A Sake That’s Perfect for Summer Sipping', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T20:53:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Nichols', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nichols', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/746198c1-0416-5127-b1ba-1f7450004513', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/746198c1-0416-5127-b1ba-1f7450004513'}, {'abstract': 'A conversation with Lloyd Simmonds, creative director of Yves Saint Laurent Makeup, about how to interpret fall’s grungy beauty look for the professional woman.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/heroin-chic-beauty-for-the-office/', 'snippet': 'A conversation with Lloyd Simmonds, creative director of Yves Saint Laurent Makeup, about how to interpret fall’s grungy beauty look for the professional woman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having always had a soft spot for grunge (for nostalgia reasons, including junior high years spent in a Seattle suburb) and spinoffs thereof, like “heroin chic,” the fall runways with their disgruntled ’90s air felt as familiar as a fuzzy mohair cardigan. In beauty, lip colors were jam-black at some shows (perhaps riffing on Drew Barrymore’s plummy lips during her wild child days), while others interpreted the bare-faced era more literally (slightly greasy skin and stringy hair like Kate Moss’s in the old Calvin Klein ads). But considering that the first time around I was a jobless teenager and that a shiny complexion and unwashed hair is probably not the best combination for the office, I looked to Lloyd Simmonds, creative director of Yves Saint Laurent Makeup, for a few pointers. After all, he had to interpret the very grungy Saint Laurent clothing designed by Hedi Slimane into a viable makeup collection. Here are some snippets from our conversation. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Heroin Chic’ Beauty for the Office?', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Black Lips: Makeup for a Grunge Revival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yves Saint Laurent', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T21:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bee Shapiro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shapiro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b705b3d-b1b1-55db-ab25-bf8ff2d38884', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b705b3d-b1b1-55db-ab25-bf8ff2d38884'}, {'abstract': 'A new study sheds more light on how Salmonella typhi, the bacteria that cause typhoid fever, hide in the body.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/health/bacteria-study-offers-clues-to-typhoid-mary-mystery.html', 'snippet': 'A new study sheds more light on how Salmonella typhi, the bacteria that cause typhoid fever, hide in the body.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scientists are one step closer to explaining how Typhoid Mary could have infected dozens of New Yorkers over a 12-year career as a cook, killing at least three of them, without having ever been sick herself.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bacteria Study Offers Clues to Typhoid Mary Mystery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clues to Typhoid Mary Mystery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mallon, Mary (1869-1938)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salmonella (Bacteria)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cell Host & Microbe (Journal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T21:01:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ada07783-4f9f-5c18-a6f9-65452fd78654', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ada07783-4f9f-5c18-a6f9-65452fd78654'}, {'abstract': 'A snow leopard was born in April to Maya and Leo, who was brought to New York from Pakistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/nyregion/baby-snow-leopard-born-at-bronx-zoo-is-now-on-display.html', 'snippet': 'A snow leopard was born in April to Maya and Leo, who was brought to New York from Pakistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 17-pound snow leopard, born this spring at the Bronx Zoo, is now on display, the first son of an orphaned snow leopard from Pakistan. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Almost 5 Months Old, Bronx Native Makes Zoo Debut', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bronx Native, Still a Baby,\r\nIs Making His Zoo Debut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foderaro, Lisa W', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx Zoo Wildlife Conservation Park', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Leopards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breeding of Animals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T21:01:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa W. Foderaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Foderaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10519b8f-e918-5ee7-a7d5-9bb0c336e519', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10519b8f-e918-5ee7-a7d5-9bb0c336e519'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Siebert’s pragmatic approach to effecting change on Wall Street characterized many of her accomplishments, her admirers said.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/remembering-muriel-siebert-an-icon-for-women-2/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Siebert’s pragmatic approach to effecting change on Wall Street characterized many of her accomplishments, her admirers said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a generation of women on Wall Street, Muriel F. Siebert was more than just a leader in finance; she was their point of reference.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering Muriel Siebert, an ‘Icon’ for Women', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Siebert, Muriel F (1928-2013)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '85 Broads Unlimited LLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Stock Exchange', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T21:03:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69eda4d4-9d56-54c8-bc6e-8eedb1bb89de', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69eda4d4-9d56-54c8-bc6e-8eedb1bb89de'}, {'abstract': 'Somehow one of our oldest and sanest traditions has become a laughingstock: it’s not hip to pack a work lunch. Let’s try to fix that.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/dining/bring-your-lunch-to-work.html', 'snippet': 'Somehow one of our oldest and sanest traditions has become a laughingstock: it’s not hip to pack a work lunch. Let’s try to fix that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are few brown-baggers in the building where I work. This is not because the food in the neighborhood is so great (it isn’t), or because the cafeteria is Google-like (it isn’t), but because many people are either “too busy” or too embarrassed to bring their lunch. Somehow one of our oldest and sanest traditions has become a laughingstock: it’s not hip to bring lunch. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/dining/28JPFLEX_SPAN/28JPFLEX_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/28/dining/28JPFLEX_SPAN/28JPFLEX_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/dining/28JPFLEX_SPAN/28JPFLEX_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/dining/28JPFLEX_SPAN/28JPFLEX_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/dining/28JPFLEX_SPAN/28JPFLEX_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/28/dining/28JPFLEX_SPAN/28JPFLEX_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/dining/28JPFLEX_SPAN/28JPFLEX_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bring Your Lunch to Work', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thinking Inside the Bag', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bittman, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microwave Ovens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lunch Boxes and Bags', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T21:07:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76d866c7-1eee-5eaf-8ca7-d602e3411024', 'word_count': 911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76d866c7-1eee-5eaf-8ca7-d602e3411024'}, {'abstract': 'Treasury Secretary Jacob J. Lew informed House Speaker John A. Boehner that the government is likely to reach its borrowing limit in mid-October.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/08/27/us/politics/27debt-limit-letter.html', 'snippet': 'Treasury Secretary Jacob J. Lew informed House Speaker John A. Boehner that the government is likely to reach its borrowing limit in mid-October.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Treasury Secretary Jacob J. Lew informed House Speaker John A. Boehner that the government is likely to reach its borrowing limit in mid-October.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lew’s Letter to Congress About the Debt Limit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lew, Jacob J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T21:12:57+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/b06989df-44b5-54fb-bb8f-a49ada07f953', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/b06989df-44b5-54fb-bb8f-a49ada07f953'}, {'abstract': 'In Fraser Grace’s “Breakfast With Mugabe,” the president of Zimbabwe, Robert Mugabe, sees a psychotherapist, and colonialism is put on the couch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/theater/reviews/breakfast-with-mugabe-by-fraser-grace.html', 'snippet': 'In Fraser Grace’s “Breakfast With Mugabe,” the president of Zimbabwe, Robert Mugabe, sees a psychotherapist, and colonialism is put on the couch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To his critics in the West, Robert Mugabe, president of the politically and economically troubled Zimbabwe, is a tyrant, an election rigger, a thug who uses past victimhood to justify further oppression.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/BREAKFAST/BREAKFAST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/BREAKFAST/BREAKFAST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/BREAKFAST/BREAKFAST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1017, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/BREAKFAST/BREAKFAST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1017, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/BREAKFAST/BREAKFAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/BREAKFAST/BREAKFAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/BREAKFAST/BREAKFAST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Oppressed Becomes Oppressor', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oppressed Becomes Oppressor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grace, Fraser', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mugabe, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coleman, Rosalyn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barnes, Ezra', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T21:14:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4be7f755-d0f1-51bc-b133-6eff41acfac2', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4be7f755-d0f1-51bc-b133-6eff41acfac2'}, {'abstract': 'A spokesman for the production linked the drop in sales to the recent injury of one of the performers.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/weekly-ticket-sales-drop-under-1-million-for-broadways-spider-man/', 'snippet': 'A spokesman for the production linked the drop in sales to the recent injury of one of the performers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time since performances began in November 2010, the Broadway musical “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark” took in less than $1 million for a standard eight-performance playing week, with last week’s gross totaling $966,952. While ticket sales have been softening since last fall for the $75 million musical, the most expensive in Broadway history, a spokesman on Monday linked last week’s total to “fallout” from a well-publicized foot injury suffered by the cast member Daniel Curry during the Aug. 15 performance.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/theater/26spider/26spider-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/26/theater/26spider/26spider-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 426}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/theater/26spider/26spider-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/theater/26spider/26spider-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1453, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/26/theater/26spider/26spider-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/26/theater/26spider/26spider-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 