llion, saddling him with a loss of about $473 million.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'His Links Severed, Ackman Sells Stake in J.C. Penney', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'His Links Severed, Ackman Moves to Sell Stake in J.C. Penney', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ackman, William A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ullman, Myron E III', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JC Penney Company Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pershing Square Capital Management', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T21:22:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4917e3b-e404-5686-beec-3faad75bdd9d', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4917e3b-e404-5686-beec-3faad75bdd9d'}, {'abstract': 'This tender dish with a fruity North African accompaniment requires something soft and not very tannic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/dining/a-syrah-to-pair-with-lamb-shanks.html', 'snippet': 'This tender dish with a fruity North African accompaniment requires something soft and not very tannic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bordeaux is the classic pairing for lamb, but that would be true of a simpler Western dish: chops or a roast, for example. This dish of meltingly tender lamb shanks with a fruity North African accompaniment requires something softer and less tannic. I would reach for a syrah from the northern Rhône Valley, like a St.-Joseph, a Crozes-Hermitage or even those rare syrah-based Côtes du Rhônes, like Éric Texier’s Brézème.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Syrah to Pair With Lamb Shanks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'And to Drink...', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asimov, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T21:22:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ebd1803-9570-5953-b824-77bf1000ee58', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ebd1803-9570-5953-b824-77bf1000ee58'}, {'abstract': 'The publication of a complete collection of short stories by James Purdy has refocused attention on his unflinching and wildly original style.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/books/james-purdy-neglected-writer-continues-to-fascinate.html', 'snippet': 'The publication of a complete collection of short stories by James Purdy has refocused attention on his unflinching and wildly original style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When he died in 2009, at 94, James Purdy was a forgotten man. He had always been a cult writer, held in almost worshipful regard for his wildly original, sometimes shocking novels and stories that worked the margins of American society, fringe territory populated by small-town folk, failed artists and tormented gay men. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/PURDY/PURDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/PURDY/PURDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 767}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/PURDY/PURDY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/PURDY/PURDY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1546, 'width': 1210, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/PURDY/PURDY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/PURDY/PURDY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/PURDY/PURDY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'James Purdy, a Fabulist Haunting the Fringes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fabulist Haunting The Fringes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Purdy, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T21:23:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf8bb586-b004-5945-b91d-52053d1f621a', 'word_count': 1244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf8bb586-b004-5945-b91d-52053d1f621a'}, {'abstract': 'In his revival of “Anna Christie” at the Berkshire Theater Group, the director David Auburn finesses Eugene O’Neills creaky plot with a calm, persuasive production.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/theater/reviews/david-auburn-stages-anna-christie-in-the-berkshires.html', 'snippet': 'In his revival of “Anna Christie” at the Berkshire Theater Group, the director David Auburn finesses Eugene O’Neills creaky plot with a calm, persuasive production.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STOCKBRIDGE, Mass. — As perhaps suits a tale of the sea, Eugene O’Neill’s “Anna Christie” is encrusted with layer upon layer of barnacles. The last, daring word in modern theater and modern subject matter when it opened on Broadway in 1921, this Pulitzer Prize-winning drama of a prostitute’s redemption now seems all but buried in quaintness, myth and exotica. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/27ANNA/27ANNA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/27ANNA/27ANNA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/27ANNA/27ANNA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank':