cked elements of the prosecution’s case on Monday and said his former top deputy and his wife, both of whom provided evidence against him, had a passionate relationship.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/world/asia/27china-bo/27china-bo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/27/world/asia/27china-bo/27china-bo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/world/asia/27china-bo/27china-bo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/world/asia/27china-bo/27china-bo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1533, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/world/asia/27china-bo/27china-bo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/27/world/asia/27china-bo/27china-bo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/world/asia/27china-bo/27china-bo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dollop of Romance Is Added to Intrigue at Former Chinese Politician’s Trial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dollop of Romance Is Added to Intrigue at Former Chinese Politician’s Trial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ansfield, Jonathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bo Xilai', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gu Kailai', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang Lijun', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T21:37:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong and Jonathan Ansfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ansfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd00d83a-428e-5d59-b9f2-453d8a1139a0', 'word_count': 1240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd00d83a-428e-5d59-b9f2-453d8a1139a0'}, {'abstract': 'On the conservative Catholic’s case for same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/what-joseph-bottum-wants/', 'snippet': 'On the conservative Catholic’s case for same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joseph Bottum’s essay in Commonweal making what’s advertised (and what the Times has covered) as “a conservative Catholic’s case for same-sex marriage” is so deliberately discursive — to the point of obscuring, at times, exactly what kind of argument the former First Things editor is making\xa0— that it’s hard to know exactly where a response would best begin. But I thought I would pluck out the following passage, which is an aside in the essay but a suggestive one, I think, in terms of understanding both Bottum’s personal motivations in writing this piece and some of the larger issues in play as well. He’s writing here about anti-Catholicism in American life, and he pauses to note how surprising it would be, from the vantage point of earlier eras and debates, that the church’s attitude toward homosexuality would have ended up giving fuel to an anti-Catholic fire:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Joseph Bottum Wants', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Protestant Churches', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Andrew', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilde, Oscar', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T21:43:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f0808f9-8ad7-507e-aaaa-abe8d2d47a5d', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f0808f9-8ad7-507e-aaaa-abe8d2d47a5d'}, {'abstract': 'Antigovernment activists posted video to YouTube that showed United Nations inspectors in blue helmets and body armor arriving at a cramped rebel clinic, where they interviewed witnesses and survivors of a suspected chemical attack.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/26/video-shows-u-n-inspectors-interviewing-survivors-of-suspected-syrian-chemical-attack/', 'snippet': 'Antigovernment activists posted video to YouTube that showed United Nations inspectors in blue helmets and body armor arriving at a cramped rebel clinic, where they interviewed witnesses and survivors of a suspected chemical attack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleagues Michael Gordon, Alan Cowell and Rick Gladstone report, United Nations weapons inspectors visited two hospitals in the Syrian countryside outside of Damascus on Monday to interview survivors of last week’s suspected chemical weapons attack and collect patient samples, despite a volley of sniper fire that disabled the lead vehicle in their convoy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Shows U.N. Inspectors in Syria Interviewing Survivors of Suspected Chemical Attack', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T21:44:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8cd9a79-7bb3-5f2f-94f7-2f56087bafcd', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8cd9a79-7bb3-5f2f-94f7-2f56087bafcd'}, {'abstract': 'Mohammad Javad Zarif seems near certain to lead Iran’s delegation in nuclear talks — further indications, analysts say, that the new leadership is serious about a new policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/world/middleeast/irans-pick-for-nuclear-talks-carries-hope-of-eased-tensions.html', 'snippet': 'Mohammad Javad Zarif seems near certain to lead Iran’s delegation in nuclear talks — further indications, analysts say, that the new leadership is serious about a new policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Until this summer, Mohammad Javad Zarif, one of Iran’s most accomplished diplomats, was an outcast, exiled from the government by ultraconservatives for working too closely with the West. Rather than presenting the Iranian case to the world, as he had done so effectively throughout a 35-year diplomatic career, he was spending his days teaching at the Foreign Ministry’s training center on a quiet, leafy campus in North Tehran.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/world/IRAN/IRAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 464, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/27/world/IRAN/IRAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 464}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/world/IRAN/IRAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 792, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/world/IRAN/IRAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1584, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/world/IRAN/IRAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType':