learly visible, the “Today” team explained how a debut novel by a 21-year-old unknown had snagged this distinction. Not one bit of the five-minute segment concerned exactly what Ms. Shannon has written.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/BOOK/BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 914, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/BOOK/BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 914}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/BOOK/BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 673, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/BOOK/BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1345, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hunger Muggles’ Occult Dystopia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hunger Muggles’ Occult Dystopia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T22:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9d76e9c-14e3-5145-81be-30292d8c3dc6', 'word_count': 1104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9d76e9c-14e3-5145-81be-30292d8c3dc6'}, {'abstract': 'The release of the 25th-anniversary edition of Madden NFL prompts a question: can sports video games count as sports?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/arts/video-games/madden-nfl-25-portrays-real-football.html', 'snippet': 'The release of the 25th-anniversary edition of Madden NFL prompts a question: can sports video games count as sports?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The habit of insisting that the virtual life is somehow not part of real life has diminished with time. Few people regard, say, online magazines as fake magazines anymore. And more than one politician has been felled by a scandal involving sex that was purely digital. So even though it wasn’t physical, it must have been real. Right?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/submadden/submadden-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/submadden/submadden-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/submadden/submadden-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/submadden/submadden-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1273, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/submadden/submadden-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/submadden/submadden-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/arts/submadden/submadden-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Examined, the Virtual Life Is Worth Living', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Examined, the Virtual Life Is Worth Living', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suellentrop, Chris', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Electronic Arts Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T22:06:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Video Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Suellentrop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suellentrop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c340346-8ae2-5e8f-a529-e409a010ccc2', 'word_count': 940, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c340346-8ae2-5e8f-a529-e409a010ccc2'}, {'abstract': 'Fred Richards, global creative director at the Brand Union, has passport stamps, a birth place and a legal name that make security people uneasy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/business/a-world-traveler-is-harmless-yet-suspect.html', 'snippet': 'Fred Richards, global creative director at the Brand Union, has passport stamps, a birth place and a legal name that make security people uneasy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I THINK I’m a friendly person, but once I get on an airplane I barely speak to anyone. I’m traveling so much, predominantly throughout the United States, Asia and Europe, that sometimes I’m not even quite sure of my itinerary.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/business/Flier/Flier-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/27/business/Flier/Flier-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/business/Flier/Flier-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/business/Flier/Flier-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1475, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/business/Flier/Flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/27/business/Flier/Flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/business/Flier/Flier-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A World Traveler Is Harmless, Yet Suspect', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A World Traveler Is Harmless, Yet Suspect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Fred', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brand Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-26T22:06:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fred Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fred', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ec926ad-7332-5641-8f5c-61baa22aac4d', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ec926ad-7332-5641-8f5c-61baa22aac4d'}, {'abstract': 'Archea architects of Florence have built a new headquarters for Antinori winemakers in Tuscany.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/arts/design/archea-architects-headquarters-for-antinori-winemakers.html', 'snippet': 'Archea architects of Florence have built a new headquarters for Antinori winemakers in Tuscany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BARGINO, Italy — For all its beauty, Italy has suffered reckless development. Travel outside any big city, and you’ll come across aging sprawl: unplanned wastelands of shopping malls, factories and housing projects, many from the 1960s and ’70s. Florence, a dozen or so miles from here, is no exception. The city started devolving into a mess of shabby suburbs years ago; nearby towns like Tavarnelle and Pogg