:51:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7d125c7-215c-5432-a31f-b7215687cf67', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7d125c7-215c-5432-a31f-b7215687cf67'}, {'abstract': 'Giants defensive end Jason Pierre-Paul was taken off the physically unable to perform list Monday, and safety Antrel Rolle joined him at practice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/sports/football/nfl-roundup.html', 'snippet': 'Giants defensive end Jason Pierre-Paul was taken off the physically unable to perform list Monday, and safety Antrel Rolle joined him at practice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A day after the Giants’ defense took a major step backward when safety Stevie Brown was placed on injured reserve, the unit took two major steps forward. Jason Pierre-Paul, a defensive end who was nearly unstoppable when he recorded 16 ½ sacks and helped the Giants win the Super Bowl two years ago, was taken off the physically unable to perform list Monday. He was joined in practice by safety Antrel Rolle, who had been sidelined since Aug. 12 with a sprained ankle. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pierre-Paul and Rolle Join Practice', 'kicker': 'N.F.L. Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pierre-Paul And Rolle Join Practice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pedulla, Tom', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodson, Mike', '