y to ever learn how to get things right.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/opinion/the-risk-pool.html', 'snippet': 'At the start of another school year, parents, remember: if we never give our children permission to get things wrong, they’re unlikely to ever learn how to get things right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BELGRADE LAKES, Me. — THIRTY-SEVEN years ago this week my friend Pearce Bunting was at the wheel of my Volkswagen and I was in the passenger seat when he drove the car off a road in suburban Philadelphia. It bounced off a fire hydrant and then plunged into a small ravine. I remember thinking, as we flew through the air, that I was about to find out whether there was life after death. I heard the crash as if from a distant room. Then a vague blue blob spoke. “Are you all right?” it wanted to know, and then said, more reassuringly, “You’re going to be all right.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/04/opinion/BOYLAN_NEW/BOYLAN_NEW-articleLarge-v6.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/08/04/opinion/BOYLAN_NEW/BOYLAN_NEW-articleLarge-v6.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/04/opinion/BOYLAN_NEW/BOYLAN_NEW-jumbo-v7.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/04/opinion/BOYLAN_NEW/BOYLAN_NEW-superJumbo-v6.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/04/opinion/BOYLAN_NEW/BOYLAN_N