 '2013-08-27T02:48:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/130753b0-e3bb-5336-a6b4-f50431494976', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/130753b0-e3bb-5336-a6b4-f50431494976'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department on Monday asked a full federal appeals court not to hear arguments from lawyers for a New York Times reporter, who has been subpoenaed to testify in a leak case against a former C.I.A. officer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/us/prosecutors-press-subpoena-for-times-reporter-in-leak-case.html', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department on Monday asked a full federal appeals court not to hear arguments from lawyers for a New York Times reporter, who has been subpoenaed to testify in a leak case against a former C.I.A. officer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department on Monday asked a full federal appeals court not to hear arguments from lawyers for a New York Times reporter, James Risen, whom prosecutors have subpoenaed to testify in a criminal leak case against a former C.I.A. officer, Jeffrey Sterling. A three-judge panel of the appeals court in Richmond, Va., ruled in July that reporters have no special privilege to avoid testifying about their sources and that Mr. Risen, who prosecutors say used Mr. Sterling as a source for a 2006 book on the C.I.A., would have to testify. Mr. Risen’s lawyers asked the full 15-judge court to reconsider the case, but the Justice Department argued in Monday’s filing that the ruling was correct and that no further hearing was justified. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prosecutors Press Subpoena for Times Reporter in Leak Case', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prosecutors Press Subpoena For Reporter In Leak Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Risen, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sterling, Jeffrey Alexander', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News Sources, Confidential Status of', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-27T02:54:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7493d4b-c3c8-568b-98df-8513237d7e4d', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7493d4b-c3c8-568b-98df-8513237d7e4d'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Huttenlocher counted synapses, observing how much of the information coming to the brain was discarded as the mind became more efficient.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/us/peter-huttenlocher-explorer-of-the-brains-development-dies-at-82.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Huttenlocher counted synapses, observing how much of the information coming to the brain was discarded as the mind became more efficient.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Peter Huttenlocher, a pediatric neurologist and neuroscientist whose innovative research counting billions of brain synapses — the microscopic information highways of the mind — revealed that brains develop rapidly in young children and later “prune” themselves as they mature, died on Aug. 15 in Chicago. He was 82. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/us/HUTTENLOCHER-obit/HUTTENLOCHER-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 893, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/27/us/HUTTENLOCHER-obit/HUTTENLOCHER-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 893}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/us/HUTTENLOCHER-obit/HUTTENLOCHER-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/us/HUTTENLOCHER-obit/HUTTENLOCHER-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1376, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/us/HUTTENLOCHER-obit/HUTTENLOCHER-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/27/us/HUTTENLOCHER-obit/HUTTENLOCHER-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/us/HUTTENLOCHER-obit/HUTTENLOCHER-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter Huttenlocher, Explorer of the Brain, Dies at 82', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peter Huttenlocher, Explorer of the Brain, Dies at 82', 'name': None, 's