(4), 6-4.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ernests Gulbis was one of the more surprising upset losses on Day 1 at the United States Open, falling to 88th-ranked Andreas Haider-Maurer, 3-6, 6-3, 1-6, 7-6 (4), 6-4.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gulbis, With a Favorable Draw, Cannot Capitalize', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gulbis, Ernests', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-27T03:02:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0023dfa-966a-5014-b0ea-27733db38b09', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0023dfa-966a-5014-b0ea-27733db38b09'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets’ Matt Harvey has had a way of keeping fans on the edge of their seats, wondering if he would throw a no-hitter. Now, they are left wondering if he will be back.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/sports/baseball/with-harvey-fans-still-waiting-to-exhale.html', 'snippet': 'The Mets’ Matt Harvey has had a way of keeping fans on the edge of their seats, wondering if he would throw a no-hitter. Now, they are left wondering if he will be back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The great thing about being a fan is that no matter how much a team lets you down — through its own fault or bad luck — you never stop dreaming. Be skeptical, be wary, but unless you believe that someday, somehow, your team could reward you, what is the point of caring?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times