rell, above, and Brendan Gleeson) struggle to keep a low profile in Belgium after they are ordered to stay put by their boss (Ralph Fiennes) as punishment for a botched assignment in this dark comedy, written and directed by Martin McDonagh. “Much of the pleasure of Mr. McDonagh’s dialogue comes from intonation and repetition,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “His characters tend to repeat their own and one another’s words, a device that forces you to heed both the musicality of the language and all that lies beneath those words — the oblique hopes, the implied fears, the unarticulated relationships.” She added, “He talks a blue streak beautifully, but he has yet to find the nuance and poetry that make his red images signify with commensurate sizzle and pop.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-27T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7adacd9-085e-5695-a4d3-88b030fa081d', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7adacd9-085e-5695-a4d3-88b030fa081d'}, {'abstract': 'On Monday night the lower house of Parliament passed the bill that guarantees a legal right to food to 70 percent of the Indian population.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/lower-house-gives-nod-to-food-security-bill/', 'snippet': 'On Monday night the lower house of Parliament passed the bill that guarantees a legal right to food to 70 percent of the Indi