name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bachi Karkaria', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bachi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Karkaria', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0dcb283-123f-5fed-bbc1-d1c7edb52625', 'word_count': 901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0dcb283-123f-5fed-bbc1-d1c7edb52625'}, {'abstract': 'Answer this question about the March on Washington, which took place 50 years ago this week.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/test-yourself-history-aug-27-2013/', 'snippet': 'Answer this question about the March on Washington, which took place 50 years ago this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ll be featuring a history question on Test Yourself every Tuesday this school year. Some will relate current events around the world to history, while others will test students’ knowledge of important past events. Let us know what you think! ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | History, Aug. 27, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-27T08:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/170f04f3-bf0c-5d84-88dd-649b50c521e2', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/170f04f3-bf0c-5d84-88dd-649b50c521e2'}, {'abstract': 'How do you think the United States should respond if United Nations inspectors determine that the Syrian government used chemical weapons?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/6-qs-about-the-news-u-s-accuses-syria-of-using-chemical-weapons/', 'snippet': 'How do you think the United States should respond if United Nations inspectors determine that the Syrian government used chemical weapons?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the article “Kerry Says Chemical Arms Attack in Syria Is ‘Undeniable,’” Michael R. Gordon, Alan Cowell and Rick Gladstone write about the Obama administration’s accusations against the Syrian government.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '6 Q’s About the News | U.S. Accuses Syria of Using Chemical Weapons', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-27T08:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e246420d-170d-58f7-8aa8-cc40262c4f97', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e246420d-170d-58f7-8aa8-cc40262c4f97'}, {'abstract': 'Why the reinsurance industry wants to change the way we think about climate change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/magazine/mutually-insured-destruction.html', 'snippet': 'Why the reinsurance industry wants to change the way we think about climate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In March 1947, a winter of heavy snowfall followed by a quick thaw and torrents of rain swelled rivers throughout England and Wales. Over the course of just 13 days, at least 27,000 homes and businesses were flooded. It was one of the worst natural disasters in British history. But thanks to climate change, which can prevent the thick snowpack from which spring floods draw their strength, that sort of flood may be less likely to happen today.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/magazine/01eureka/mag-01Eureka-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/09/01/magazine/01eureka/mag-01Eureka-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/magazine/01eureka/mag-01Eureka-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/magazine/01eureka/mag-01Eureka-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1839, 'width': 1379, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/magazine/01eureka/mag-01Eureka-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/09/01/magazine/01eureka/mag-01Eureka-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/magazine/01eureka/mag-01Eureka-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mutually Insured Destruction', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mutually Insured Destruction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koerth-Baker, Maggie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {