0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aron Pilhofer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pilhofer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce985d55-22dc-5725-971a-4f01d55288ed', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce985d55-22dc-5725-971a-4f01d55288ed'}, {'abstract': 'Experts assigned to examine accusations of human rights abuses in North Korea urged the government on Tuesday to allow them access to prison camps and other sites where violations have been reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/world/asia/un-rights-panel-presses-for-access-to-north-korea.html', 'snippet': 'Experts assigned to examine accusations of human rights abuses in North Korea urged the government on Tuesday to allow them access to prison camps and other sites where violations have been reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — The first United Nations panel of experts assigned to investigate North Korean human rights abuses urged the government in Pyongyang on Tuesday to allow them to visit, even as the North called their work slanderous.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Investigators Press North Koreans to Allow a Visit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Investigators Press North Koreans to Allow a Visit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'gl