address a man in Mandarin, but it is also used to address women held in high esteem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — “Have you noticed how woman opinion leaders are being called ‘Mr.’ on Weibo?” asked my sharp-eyed friend Mei Zhang, referring to the influential Twitter-like microblogs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Moniker Only a Mister Could Like', 'kicker': 'Letter from China', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In China, a Respected Ms. May Be Labeled Mr.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tatlow, Didi Kirsten', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-27T11:27:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a0ab7ca-a28e-530d-9e0b-891a8e0f909a', 'word_count': 1060, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a0ab7ca-a28e-530d-9e0b-891a8e0f909a'}, {'abstract': 'Frederick Wiseman’s movie, “At Berkeley,” shows aspects of life at a university that is receiving less and less public funding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/movies/moviesspecial/film-chronicles-the-inner-workings-of-berkeley.html', 'snippet': 'Frederick Wiseman’s movie, “At Berkeley,” shows aspects of life at a university that is receiving less and less public funding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has taken Frederick Wiseman 45 years to get from high school to college. The master filmmaker’s latest portrait of an institution, “At Berkeley,” centers on the University of California in Berkeley and joins an extraordinary résumé that stretches back to “High School” in 1968 and his controversial debut, “Titicut Follies,” in 1967. In between, Mr. Wiseman has established himself as one of America’s greatest chroniclers in any medium.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/movies/28iht-venicewiseman28-picA/28iht-venicewiseman28-picA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 310, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/28/movies/28iht-venicewiseman28-picA/28iht-venicewiseman28-picA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 310}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/movies/28iht-venicewiseman28-picA/28iht-venicewiseman28-picA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 529, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/movies/28iht-venicewiseman28-picA/28iht-venicewiseman28-picA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 992, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/movies/28iht-venicewiseman28-picA/28iht-venicewiseman28-picA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/28/movies/28iht-venicewiseman28-picA/28iht-venicewiseman28-picA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/movies/28iht-venicewisem