h Carolina beach. While the film leaves the viewer with a powerful image of the sacrifice of African-American soldiers and their white officers, it does not address the fate of those members of the 54th Massachusetts who were captured that July day in 1863. The entrance of black troops into the Civil War following the Emancipation Proclamation placed the Confederate authorities in a difficult dilemma: what to do with African-Americans in Union blues taken prisoner on the battlefield? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Plight of the Black P.O.W.', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisoners of War', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Jefferson F', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-27T15:46:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas J. Ward Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Ward', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eec7760e-994f-5767-8bec-8077ccee7050', 'word_count': 1281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eec7760e-994f-5767-8bec-8077ccee7050'}, {'abstract': 'Christian Wulff, a onetime ally of Chancellor Angela Merkel, faces charges of accepting f