cDermon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDermon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ec624b7-8d8f-5e93-9033-4bb84f700b20', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ec624b7-8d8f-5e93-9033-4bb84f700b20'}, {'abstract': 'Nearing the end of his summer road trip, the Frugal Traveler stops in Minnesota where he sits runway-side for a fashion show and catches his first demolition derby.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/travel/from-fashion-to-crashing-at-county-fairs.html', 'snippet': 'Nearing the end of his summer road trip, the Frugal Traveler stops in Minnesota where he sits runway-side for a fashion show and catches his first demolition derby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York’s fall Fashion Week starts in a few days, but you won’t find me staking out Lincoln Center to steal a glimpse of a model or designer. I’ve already had my fill of runway glamour this summer, at the Cloverbud division of the 4-H Fashion Revue at the Becker County Fair in Detroit Lakes, Minn. Better yet, I didn’t have to flash press credentials: there was no security at the red-and-white striped tent. And there were plenty of places to sit — comfy bales of hay instead of chairs crammed onto risers — and watch the kids (kindergartners through third graders) show off the ensembles they’ve put together (that is, bought at the mall).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/27/travel/27-frugal-span/27-frugal-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/27/travel/27-frugal-span/27-frugal-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': '