nd riven by partisanship that it has done little legislating on even the most important issues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Legitimize Intervention in Syria', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-27T20:50:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Giacomo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giacomo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abdf5035-9a7b-5605-b1bf-60338eb21369', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abdf5035-9a7b-5605-b1bf-60338eb21369'}, {'abstract': 'Sales had been suspended in France since July in a dispute over the German carmaker’s decision not to equip certain models with a new, more environmentally friendly refrigerant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/business/global/french-court-lifts-ban-on-mercedes-benz-autos.html', 'snippet': 'Sales had been suspended in France since July in a dispute over the German carmaker’s decision not to equip certain models with a new, more environmentally friendly refrigerant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Daimler, the German maker of Mercedes-Benz cars, may resume sales in France after the country’s highest administrative court temporarily lifted a ban on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/business/EUCars1/EUCars1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge'