', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Club of New York', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-27T22:16:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15709962-749e-51ba-ac6a-ed3d0cbe9bc9', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15709962-749e-51ba-ac6a-ed3d0cbe9bc9'}, {'abstract': 'The mass wedding was held in Albuquerque’s Civic Plaza after a ruling that the county clerk could issue same-sex marriage licenses.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/gay-and-lesbian-mass-wedding-held-in-new-mexico/', 'snippet': 'The mass wedding was held in Albuquerque’s Civic Plaza after a ruling that the county clerk could issue same-sex marriage licenses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 100 people lined up outside the county clerk’s office in Albuquerque to get marriage licenses Tuesday morning, the day after a state district judge ruled that same-sex marriage was legal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gay and Lesbian Mass Wedding Held in New Mexico', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBUQUERQUE (NM)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-27T22:17:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a74bcee-a4e9-53a7-b183-a8134863fc49', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a74bcee-a4e9-53a7-b183-a8134863fc49'}, {'abstract': 'Luciano Benetton, the father of the Italian sportswear label, displays 200 of his commissioned works, each the size of a business card, at the Venice Biennale.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/collected-the-united-colors-of-benetton-and-the-world/', 'snippet': 'Luciano Benetton, the father of the Italian sportswear label, displays 200 of his commissioned works, each the size of a business card, at the Venice Biennale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Luciano Benetton, the father of the Italian sportswear label the United Colors of Benetton, embraces and encourages a multi-culti global perspective through his company’s clothes and ad campaigns, and, now, through art. “I have always been a strong believer that people may not speak to each other because of economic or political issues, but I’m pretty sure that even those countries which aren’t speaking to each other can through art,” said Benetton, who recently curated the exhibition “Imago Mundi” (“Images of the World”) at the Querini Stampalia Foundation in Venice. The show is an extension of the Venice Biennale and includes over 1,000 works from his personal collection, by artists from Australia, India, Japan, South Korea and the United States.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The United Colors of Benetton, and the World', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On View: Tiny Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': []