e to deter further massacres and to punish President Bashar al-Assad. But there is widespread confusion over the legal basis for the use of force in these terrible circumstances. As a legal matter, the Syrian government’s use of chemical weapons does not automatically justify armed intervention by the United States. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bomb Syria, Even if It Is Illegal', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bomb Syria, Even if It Is Illegal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hurd, Ian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kosovo', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-27T23:55:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Hurd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hurd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d0bb782-608c-543e-9533-99160634763b', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d0bb782-608c-543e-9533-99160634763b'}, {'abstract': 'A pitch from the Blue Jays starter J. A. Happ hit Robinson Cano on the left hand in the first inning. He stayed in to run the bases, before leaving the game.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/27/cano-leaves-game-after-taking-a-pitch-off-his-hand/', 'snippet': 'A pitch from the Blue Jays starter J. A. Happ hit Robinson Cano on the left hand in the first inning. He stayed in to run the bases, before leaving the game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TORONTO — Through all the Yankees injuries this year, the only good news was that Robinson Cano did not get caught in the unrelenting storm. But that may have changed Tuesday after Cano was struck on the left hand by a pitch from J. A. Happ of the Toronto Blue Jays in the first inning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cano Leaves Game After Taking a Pitch Off His Hand', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cano, Robinson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Happ, J A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Blue Jays', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T00:08:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/250e4e32-a0cb-5ad5-9c47-bb9d9ab3cd12', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/250e4e32-a0cb-5ad5-9c47-bb9d9ab3cd12'}, {'abstract': 'Our Web site was unavailable to some users for a time on Tuesday. We regret if this has caused you any inconvenience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/business/media/to-our-readers.html', 'snippet': 'Our Web site was unavailable to some users for a time on Tuesday. We regret if this has caused you any inconvenience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our Web site was unavailable to some users for a time on Tuesday. The disruption was the result of an external attack on our domain name registrar, and we are at work on fully restoring service. We regret if this has caused you any inconvenience.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Our Readers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T00:15:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dce67999-6540-564a-bcb6-d8e71e21cdea', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dce67999-6540-564a-bcb6-d8e71e21cdea'}, {'abstract': 'The early release from prison of the killer of Enrique Camarena had D.E.A. officials asking, “Who dropped the ball?”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/world/americas/us-officials-return-to-pursuit-of-1985-killer-of-american-agent.html', 'snippet': 'The early release from prison of the killer of Enrique Camarena had D.E.A. officials asking, “Who dropped the ball?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY — The last time Ralph Villarruel, an American drug agent, saw the notorious drug lord, he said he watched in dismay as the suspect raised a bottle of Champagne from inside a Lear jet, as if to mock the American investigators pursuing him as the plane revved up to flee Mexico.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/world/MEXICO-1/MEXICO-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 911,