.html', 'snippet': 'The number dropped to levels not seen in nearly a decade, and city lawyers cited the data in a letter requesting that a judge delay ordering any changes until an appeal is heard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The number of police stops in New York City over recent months plummeted to levels not seen in nearly a decade, back when the Bloomberg administration was just beginning to turn to stop-and-frisk tactics, according to new data.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Stop-and-Frisk Encounters Plunged in Second Quarter of 2013, Data Show', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Police Stop-and-Frisk Encounters Plunged in Second Quarter of 2013, Data Show', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scheindlin, Shira A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T01:03:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8f29c69-1061-5d01-8930-3a7f9da9748f', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8f29c69-1061-5d01-8930-3a7f9da9748f'}, {'abstract': 'The March on Washington was so successful that we often forget, 50 years later, that it occurred in a political environment not so different from our own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/opinion/what-happened-to-jobs-and-justice.html', 'snippet': 'The March on Washington was so successful that we often forget, 50 years later, that it occurred in a political environment not so different from our own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADISON, Wis. — ON Aug. 28, 1963, nearly a quarter of a million people thronged the nation’s capital for the March on Washington for Jobs and Freedom, the largest civil rights demonstration in American history. Its impact on American politics was tremendous: in addition to building support to pass the civil rights bill that President John F. Kennedy had recently proposed, marchers succeeded in strengthening and expanding the scope of the bill far beyond what the president had envisioned. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/opinion/0828OPEDburrill/0828OPEDburrill-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 847, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/28/opinion/0828OPEDburrill/0828OPEDburrill-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 847}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/opinion/0828OPEDburrill/0828OPEDburrill-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/opinion/0828OPEDburrill/0828OPEDburrill-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/opinion/0828OPEDburrill/0828OPEDburrill-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/28/opinion/0828OPEDburrill/0828OPEDburrill-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/opinion/0828OPEDburrill/0828OPEDburrill-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happened to Jobs and Justice?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Happened to Jobs and Justice?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Randolph, A Philip', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T01:07:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By William P. Jones', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Jones', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/23fb59d4-8d45-5c6a-a1cf-a58dce6678f1', 'word_count': 861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23fb59d4-8d45-5c6a-a1cf-a58dce6678f1'}, {'abstract': 'Crucial lessons from the March on Washington still need to be learned.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/opinion/the-fight-for-voting-rights-50-years-later.html', 'snippet': 'Crucial lessons from the March on Washington still need to be learned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the 50th anniversary of the March on Washington, the country can take pride in progress made toward the guarantee of equal rights for all. Yet it is disheartening to watch the continuing battles over the right to vote, a core goal of the civil rights movement and the foundation of any functioning democracy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fight for Voting Rights, 50 Years Later', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Fight for Voting Rights, 50 Years Later', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identification Devices', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T01:08:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c06175d-fd44-5f4d-95ab-0efc73a051bf', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c06175d-fd44-5f4d-95ab-0efc73a051bf'}, {'abstract': 'Nelson L. Castro pleaded guilty on Tuesday to one count of making false statements after denying that he had given an interview on YouTube about his informer activities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/nyregion/legislator-who-informed-on-others-admits-lying-to-authorities.html', 'snippet': 'Nelson L. Castro pleaded guilty on Tuesday to one count of making false statements after denying that he had given an interview on YouTube about his informer activities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nelson L. Castro, the former Democratic state assemblyman from the Bronx who became a government informer and secretly recorded conversations in a corruption investigation, is in trouble because of another recording — this one quite public.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/nyregion/CASTRO/CASTRO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 492, 'width': 370, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/nyregion/CASTRO/CASTRO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 492, 'width': 370, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/nyregion/CASTRO/CASTRO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/28/nyregion/CASTRO/CASTRO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/nyregion/CASTRO/CASTRO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Legislator Who Informed on Others Admits Lying to Authorities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Legislator Who Informed on Others Pleads Guilty to Lying to Authorities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro, Nelson L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Informers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevenson, Eric A', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Engelmayer, Paul A', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Perjury', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T01:08:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de3bf32c-6766-5a7d-beb8-c2b18dee5b85', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de3bf32c-6766-5a7d-beb8-c2b18dee5b85'}, {'abstract': 'On Aug. 28, 1963, Americans were not the only ones marching on Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/opinion/the-global-march-on-washington.html', 'snippet': 'On Aug. 28, 1963, Americans were not the only ones marching on Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — AN important but little-known episode in the story of the March on Washington unfolded on Aug. 17, 1963, in a Paris nightclub called the Living Room.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mult