}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41254f7d-ac20-5a22-ac00-7f26449455fc', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41254f7d-ac20-5a22-ac00-7f26449455fc'}, {'abstract': 'Victoria Duval, a 17-year-old qualifier, rallied from two games down in the second set to beat Samantha Stosur, the world’s 11th-ranked player and 2011 United States Open champion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/sports/tennis/duval-charges-back-to-beat-stosur-winning-fans-along-the-way.html', 'snippet': 'Victoria Duval, a 17-year-old qualifier, rallied from two games down in the second set to beat Samantha Stosur, the world’s 11th-ranked player and 2011 United States Open champion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the dusk descended, and Victoria Duval continued her comeback, the crowd at Louis Armstrong Stadium seemed to evolve along with her. She began as a relative unknown facing Samantha Stosur, the world’s 11th-ranked player and the 2011 United States Open champion. By the third set, she was “Vicky” — the United States Open’s new fresh-faced darling, a 17-year-old qualifier from Haiti with the lightning quick forehands that belied her thin, goggles-wearing appearance.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/sports/NIGHT/NIGHT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 476, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/28/sports/NIGHT/NIGHT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 476}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/sports/NIGHT/NIGHT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/sports/NIGHT/NIGHT-superJumbo.jpg', 'he