'Catsimatidis, John A', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sliwa, Curtis', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALBANESE, SAL F', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salgado, Erick J', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T03:29:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0fd348b-3757-5681-a644-a02038c17c6f', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0fd348b-3757-5681-a644-a02038c17c6f'}, {'abstract': 'Unidentified assailants killed a prominent security official on Tuesday in the troubled North Caucasus region, which has a simmering Islamic insurgency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/world/europe/russia-security-official-killed-on-highway-in-ingushetia.html', 'snippet': 'Unidentified assailants killed a prominent security official on Tuesday in the troubled North Caucasus region, which has a simmering Islamic insurgency.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Unidentified assailants killed a prominent security official on Tuesday in the troubled North Caucasus region, which has a simmering Islamic insurgency. Akhmed Kotiyev, the head of the regional Security Council for the Ingushetia Republic, and his driver were killed by automatic fire from a passing car on a highway near Nazran, the republic’s capital, Russian state television reported. Yunus-Bek Yevkurov, the leader of Ingushetia, said that Mr. Kotiyev was known for negotiating with rebel fighters to abandon the insurgency, and that he was probably killed for that reason. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Security Official Killed on Highway in Ingushetia', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Security Official Killed On Highway in Ingushetia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Caucasus (Russia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ingushetia (Russian Republic)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yevkurov, Yunus-Bek', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T03:31:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d08fe64-76e6-5f59-a166-42e6b33b2a52', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d08fe64-76e6-5f59-a166-42e6b33b2a52'}, {'abstract': 'President François Hollande announced the outlines of a pension reform bill, aimed at preserving an underfunded system but which is likely to be seen by some as insufficient.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/world/europe/france-government-proposes-changes-in-pension-system.html', 'snippet': 'President François Hollande announced the outlines of a pension reform bill, aimed at preserving an underfunded system but which is likely to be seen by some as insufficient.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The government of President François Hollande announced Tuesday the broad outlines of a much anticipated pension reform bill, aimed at preserving a generous but underfunded system but which is likely to be seen by some European officials as insufficient. The bill will seek to stem a $28 billion deficit with increases in withholdings from workers and employers and, beginning in 2020, a gradual increase in the pay-in time required to receive a full pension. A reform in 2010 raised the minimum retirement age from 60 to 62 and increased the pay-in time to 41.5 years; the new bill would raise the pay-in time to 43 years by 2035. Unions and company representatives said they were disappointed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Government Proposes Changes in Pension System', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Government Proposes Changes in Pension System', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T03:57:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d670f936-b049-50fd-9a46-8313b8b9cc6e', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d670f936-b049-50fd-9a46-8313b8b9cc6e'}, {'abstract': 'Tears to the anterior cruciate ligament sideline more athletes for longer periods of time than almost any other acute injury. Researchers are