tes Open girls’ event at Flushing Meadows but she has never paid much attention to the junior tour. There are far bigger prizes in her sights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At 17, Croatia’s Vekic Handles Herself Like a Seasoned Player', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duque-Marino, Mariana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vekic, Donna', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T04:12:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c062af14-d467-590f-b862-acac95c19c90', 'word_count': 648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c062af14-d467-590f-b862-acac95c19c90'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (Discovery, Velocity) PATRICK DEMPSEY: RACING LE MANS Like Paul Newman, Steve McQueen and James Garner before him, the actor Patrick Dempsey, above, has a thing for speed, hitting the racetrack when he’s not on the set. This four-part mini-series, filmed in June, follows Mr. Dempsey and his Porsche 911 GT3 RSR team, which he owns with the Italian soccer star Alessandro Del Piero, in the 24 Hours of Le Mans, the grueling endurance race in France. In this premiere episode, Mr. Dempsey tries to strike a balance between work and what he calls his true passion while rustling up sponsorship.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T04:16:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c0835f4-11ce-5236-80c0-6162a3e25301', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c0835f4-11ce-5236-80c0-6162a3e25301'}, {'abstract': 'Robert King, a special envoy, will visit North Korea to help free Kenneth Bae, an American missionary detained last year and sentenced to 15 years hard labor for proselytizing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/world/asia/us-sends-envoy-to-north-korea-to-seek-americans-release.html', 'snippet': 'Robert King, a special envoy, will visit North Korea to help free Kenneth Bae, an American missionary detained last year and sentenced to 15 years hard labor for proselytizing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — Washington’s special envoy on North Korean human rights issues will visit that country on Friday to try to secure the release of an American imprisoned there on charges of plotting to harm the socialist country through his Christian missionary activities, the State Department said on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Sends Envoy to North Korea to Seek American’s Release', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Korea: U.S. Sends Envoy\r\nTo Seek American’s Release', '