k': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jaafari, Bashar', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T10:28:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle, Steven Erlanger and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd17be06-d42c-591d-96a2-c11f94fa93fa', 'word_count': 1172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd17be06-d42c-591d-96a2-c11f94fa93fa'}, {'abstract': 'Flush with frequent-flier miles? Maybe you can buy some nice Detroit municipal bonds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/booming/how-many-miles-do-i-need-to-murder-the-head-of-the-airline.html', 'snippet': 'Flush with frequent-flier miles? Maybe you can buy some nice Detroit municipal bonds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was 20 and knocking around Europe, I could sleep anywhere and get up feeling great. Hostels with a one-inch-thick mattress, a beach, a railroad seat, it didn’t matter — my college roommate and I, traveling on a Eurail pass in 1968, sought out night trains because that saved us the cost of a hotel room.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/booming/28wadler-booming/28wadler-booming-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 389, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/booming/28wadler-booming/28wadler-booming-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 389, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/booming/28wadler-booming/28wadler-booming-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/28/booming/28wadler-booming/28wadler-booming-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/booming/28wadler-booming/28wadler-booming-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Many Miles Do I Need to Murder the Head of the Airline?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frequent Flier Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Wadler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wadler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48996e47-51ae-55f7-83b2-3f0d879716b5', 'word_count': 964, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48996e47-51ae-55f7-83b2-3f0d879716b5'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Murray’s affection for the United States Open dates to his days in junior tennis, when the trip to Queens struck him as something special.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/murrays-affection-for-the-open-goes-way-back/', 'snippet': 'Andy Murray’s affection for the United States Open dates to his days in junior tennis, when the trip to Queens struck him as something special.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early in his career, Andy Murray frequently named the United States Open as his favorite tournament. His choice of something other than Wimbledon seemed to have a certain pointedness. Because Murray is Scottish, it was easy to wonder if there was a nationalist edge to his choice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Murray’s Affection for the Open Goes Way Back', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T11:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Asad Raza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Asad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22886d96-682c-5c38-8e66-ce8a465d041a', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22886d96-682c-5c38-8e66-ce8a465d041a'}, {'abstract': 'Does this site have the right approach? And what do you think of responsive design?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/a-web-site-tries-to-convince-mattress-shoppers-to-buy-online/', 'snippet': 'Does this site have the right approach? And what do you think of responsive design?', 'lead_paragraph': 'While most people might guess that mattresses would be among the hardest products to sell online, Firas Kittaneh concluded otherwise. In 2006, he closed his mall retail store because it was distracting him from selling online.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Web Site Tries to Convince Mattress Shoppers to Buy Online', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mattresses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T11:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Demb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Demb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/436cb685-7c99-5589-9f45-5ebd4132c85a', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/436cb685-7c99-5589-9f45-5ebd4132c85a'}, {'abstract': 'Learn more about classic poems by playing our crossword, either online or in print.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013