e, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d8cf73d-bc90-5e7b-a3c1-72b62ec5353f', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d8cf73d-bc90-5e7b-a3c1-72b62ec5353f'}, {'abstract': 'A number of private equity groups have been knocked out of the running to acquire ParknShop, the Hong Kong supermarket chain that is considering selling itself in a deal that could command $3 billion to $4 billion, according to people with knowledge of the matter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/private-equity-said-to-be-out-of-running-for-hong-kong-supermarket-chain/', 'snippet': 'A number of private equity groups have been knocked out of the running to acquire ParknShop, the Hong Kong supermarket chain that is considering selling itself in a deal that could command $3 billion to $4 billion, according to people with knowled...', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG – A number of private equity groups have been knocked out of the running to acquire ParknShop, the Hong Kong supermarket chain owned by the billionaire Li Ka-shing that is considering selling itself in a deal that could command $3 billion to $4 billion, according to people with knowledge of the matter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Private Equity Said to Be Out of Running for Hong Kong Chain', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets and Grocery Stores', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T11:15:36+0000', 'docum