’s Formula One movie, “Rush,” is the first film he as made without America as the primary audience, and it shows: it’s darker, sexier, moodier than any of his previous pictures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/movies/making-a-pit-stop-in-formula-one-with-rush.html', 'snippet': 'The director’s Formula One movie, “Rush,” is the first film he as made without America as the primary audience, and it shows: it’s darker, sexier, moodier than any of his previous pictures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ron Howard likes to think of himself as one of those chameleon directors, like Billy Wilder and Mike Nichols, who are known not for any one thing, but rather for doing lots of things well. He has made so many different kinds of movies that he sometimes seems to be working from a checklist: a pair of whimsical comedies (“Cocoon” and “Splash”), a fairy tale (“Willow”), a holiday film (“How the Grinch Stole Christmas”), a firefighting movie (“Backdraft”), a space epic (“Apollo 13”), a biopic (“A Beautiful Mind”), a western (“The Missing”), a boxing film (“Cinderella Man”), a buddy flick (“The Dilemma”) and two Dan Brown thrillers (“The Da Vinci Code” and “Angels & Demons”).', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/movies/rush-image-1/rush-images-slide-V5TO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/09/01/movies/rush-image-1/rush-images-slide-V5TO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/movies/rush-image-1/rush-images-slide-V5TO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/movies/rush-image-1/rush-images-slide-V5TO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/movies/rush-image-1/rush-image-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/09/01/movies/rush-image-1/rush-image-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/movies/rush-image-1/rush-images-slide-V5TO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ron Howard Switches Gears, Again', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ron Howard Switches Gears, Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGrath, Charles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lauda, Niki', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rush (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T12:16:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0af49e37-30aa-5c22-9bdb-2e9a71d64c13', 'word_count': 1662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0af49e37-30aa-5c22-9bdb-2e9a71d64c13'}, {'abstract': 'Merrill Lynch will pay $160 million to settle a racial bias lawsuit. | Two regulators are preparing enforcement actions and fines against JPMorgan Chase. | An effort to increase disclosure on executive pay may have created more murkiness.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/morning-agenda-a-record-payout-in-bias-case/', 'snippet': 'Merrill Lynch will pay $160 million to settle a racial bias lawsuit. | Two regulators are preparing enforcement actions and fines against JPMorgan Chase. | An effort to increase disclosure on executive pay may have created more murkiness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Merrill Lynch has agreed to pay $160 million to settle a racial bias lawsuit that wound through the federal courts for eight years, Patrick McGeehan reports in DealBook. The payout in the suit, which was filed on behalf of 700 black brokers who worked for Merrill, would be the largest amount ever distributed to plaintiffs in a racial discrimination suit against an American employer, Mr. McGeehan writes. Merrill, which is now owned by Bank of America, also agreed to take advice from black employees on how to improve their chances of success as brokers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Record Payout in Bias Case', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T12:20:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c62a4133-4ecf-53c3-af5f-26e4a1e33fb2', 'word_count': 1458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c62a4133-4ecf-53c3-af5f-26e4a1e33fb2'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: From da