': 'Assessing the Costs of Caring for an Aging Relative', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Health Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Leaves', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T15:39:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dfc46a0-dd29-5320-8053-2e617408f395', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dfc46a0-dd29-5320-8053-2e617408f395'}, {'abstract': 'An invisible epidemic of malnutrition-related deaths is killing hundreds of thousands of India’s children.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/malnutrition-ravages-indias-children/', 'snippet': 'An invisible epidemic of malnutrition-related deaths is killing hundreds of thousands of India’s children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANDRICHIWADI, India — On the morning of July 23, Shakuntala Kirkire, a housewife in Bandrachiwadi village in the western state of Maharashtra, carried her 10-month-old daughter in her arms and walked in rain down the slope of a hill on which her village stands. Her husband, Ajay Kirkire, walked close to her, holding up an umbrella to protect their sick child as they tried to reach the government-run clinic in a neighboring village.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/world/asia/28-shakuntala-malnutrit