y when that advances its goals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEL AVIV — Israel likes children and it wants more of them. It has high fertility rates — the highest, in fact, of all the states in the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development: almost 3 children per household, compared with an O.E.C.D. average of just over 1.7. It invests a lot of money in making fertility clinics and treatments accessible to its citizens. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Children of Israel', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arabs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zionism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lapid, Yair', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meridor, Dan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tel Aviv (Israel)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T16:39:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/926e139b-55e1-5107-86db-8db6520e6795', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/926e139b-55e1-5107-86db-8db6520e6795'}, {'abstract':