would probably require Swiss banks to pay fines totaling more than a billion dollars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 7:38 p.m. |  Switzerland and the United States are close to announcing an agreement to end their long dispute over how to punish banks that helped Americans evade taxes, banking and government officials said on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. and Switzerland Are Close to Deal on Penalizing Banks in Tax Case', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. and Switzerland Are Close to Deal on Penalizing Banks in Tax Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Widmer-Schlumpf, Eveline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Swiss Cantonal Banks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T16:59:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly and Lynnley Browning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Lynnley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b2f2e9b-24b0-5713-88a4-576e73eeab35', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b2f2e9b-24b0-5713-88a4-576e73eeab35'}, {'abstract': 'Live updates on the 50th anniversary of the March on Washington for Jobs and Freedom, where the civil rights leader Martin Luther King Jr. delivered his iconic “I Have a Dream” speech.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/live-updates-on-the-50th-anniversary-of-martin-luther-kings-i-have-a-dream-speech/', 'snippet': 'Live updates on the 50th anniversary of the March on Washington for Jobs and Freedom, where the civil rights leader Martin Luther King Jr. delivered his iconic “I Have a Dream” speech.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the 50th anniversary of the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.’s iconic “I Have a Dream” speech, thousands of people descended on the Lincoln Memorial on Wednesday. Joined by the former presidents Bill Clinton and Jimmy Carter, President Obama paid homage to Dr. King and others involved in the civil rights era. “And because they kept marching, America changed,” the president said. “Because they marched, the civil rights law was passed. Because they marched, the voting rights law was signed.” More coverage from the day’s events.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Updates on the 50th Anniversary of Martin Luther King’s ‘I Have a Dream’ Speech', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T16:59:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1faa9fa-4159-516b-83da-f2339562f904', 'word_count': 2835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1faa9fa-4159-516b-83da-f2339562f904'}, {'abstract': 'Although Coach Tom Coughlin intends to limit Eli Manning and the rest of the first-team offense to 12 to 15 snaps in Thursday’s preseason finale against the Patriots, he is pushing for results.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/29/sports/football/giants-offense-still-lacking-consistency-as-opener-nears.html', 'snippet': 'Although Coach Tom Coughlin intends to limit Eli Manning and the rest of the first-team offense to 12 to 15 snaps in Thursday’s preseason finale against the Patriots, he is pushing for results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — The Giants faced fourth-and-goal at the 2-yard line late in the opening half of Saturday night’s preseason game against the Jets when Eli Manning looked for Hakeem Nicks on a fade pattern. He later estimated that he underthrew the ball by a foot, the difference between allowing Nicks to snag it for a touchdown and having safety Dawan Landry render the pass incomplete.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/29/sports/29giants1/29giants1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/29/sports/29giants1/29giants1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/29/sports/29giants1/29giants1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/29/sports/29giants1/29giants1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1334, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/29/sports/29giants1/29giants1-thumbStanda