b': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T17:10:53+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/619059e8-c8dd-589c-bac7-62710c319c8d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/619059e8-c8dd-589c-bac7-62710c319c8d'}, {'abstract': 'Three new picture books about the Jewish holidays Rosh Hashana, Yom Kippur and Sukkot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/books/what-a-way-to-start-a-new-year-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Three new picture books about the Jewish holidays Rosh Hashana, Yom Kippur and Sukkot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the start of the school year come three Jewish holidays: Rosh Hashana, Yom Kippur and Sukkot. In “What a Way to Start a New Year!” Jacqueline Jules imagines what Rosh Hashana might be like for a young family whose new year is starting in a new house in a new town. Dina, who is about 7, finds nothing is as it should be: the friends she liked to visit for the holiday are now hours away, and her home is a mess of packing boxes. “It doesn’t feel like Rosh Hashana here,” she complains. “We don’t even have a round challah.” A series of mishaps makes the phrase “What a way to start a new year!” a common refrain in the house, until a colleague of Dina’s father suggests the family join him at the temple he attends. Though the holidays are different than Dina remembers, she learns something about making friends and embracing change. Judy Stead’s illustrations, rich with festive pinks, greens and purples, are attractive and cheerful even when her characters’\xa0expressive faces register disappointment or impatience. “What a Way to Start a New Year!” is notable in that Jules assumes a basic understanding of the holiday; making this amusing and less obviously didactic book a pleasure to read.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/books/28childrens-span/28childrens-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 310, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/28/books/28childrens-span/28childrens-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 310}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/books/28childrens-span/28childrens-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 528, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/books/28childrens-span/28childrens-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1277, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/books/28childrens-span/28childrens-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/28/books/28childrens-span/28childrens-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/books/28childrens-span/28childrens-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Holidays, High and Low', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name'