url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/28/the-ad-campaign-speaking-in-support-of-weiner/', 'snippet': 'A new ad from Anthony D. Weiner features the first time he has deployed surrogates — not himself — to make his campaign pitch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After soaring to the top of the Democratic mayoral primary field in some polls earlier this summer, former Representative Anthony D. Weiner is now struggling, and viewed as a long shot to make it to a runoff. But one asset he still has is a robust campaign war chest, so this week, he released three more television commercials. Perhaps the most notable one is “Choices,” because it represents the first time he has deployed surrogates — not himself — to make his campaign pitch.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ad Campaign: Speaking in Support of Weiner', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Speaking in Support of Weiner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-28T21:44:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f42ee3d-107b-5413-988f-c92344ac363e', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f42ee3d-107b-5413-988f-c92344ac363e'}, {'abstract': 'For actors like Daniel Brühl, the new globalism in film has brought opportunities that were almost unimaginab