956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fec5714-ab38-5176-941a-a4ae9a3a5d33'}, {'abstract': 'With Roger Federer slipping down the rankings, there is a possibility that Stanislas Wawrinka could become Switzerland’s No. 1 player in the next year.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/29/wawrinka-learning-to-banish-doubts/', 'snippet': 'With Roger Federer slipping down the rankings, there is a possibility that Stanislas Wawrinka could become Switzerland’s No. 1 player in the next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As one Swiss player is faltering, another is realizing his full potential. With Roger Federer slipping down the rankings, there is a possibility that Stanislas Wawrinka could become Switzerland’s No. 1 player in the next year or so, unless Federer halts his decline.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wawrinka Learning to Banish Doubts', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wawrinka, Stanislas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-29T05:10:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bb204f1-3e8d-542d-9991-3f01c83ff149', 'word_count': 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bb204f1-3e8d-542d-9991-3f01c83ff149'}, {'abstract': 'San Jose State University announced results Wednesday in its pilot partnership with Udacity, a for-profit provider of online courses, to offer introductory classes online for credit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/29/education/success-of-online-courses-weighed.html', 'snippet': 'San Jose State University announced results Wednesday in its pilot partnership with Udacity, a for-profit provider of online courses, to offer introductory classes online for credit.', 'lead_paragraph': ' San Jose State University announced results\xa0Wednesday\xa0in its closely watched pilot partnership with Udacity, a for-profit provider of online courses, to offer low-cost introductory classes online for credit. \xa0In three \xa0classes — \xa0elementary statistics, college algebra and introduction to programming — \xa0 a higher share of\xa0 online students than on-campus students passed with a C or better.\xa0 In two — entry-level math and general psychology — the on-campus students did better. This summer, \xa071 percent of the online students were from out of state or from foreign countries. The courses resume in the winter semester.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Success of Online Courses Weighed', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Education', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Success Of Online Courses Weighed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Jose State University', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Udacity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-29T05:16:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b955e6e-d819-5320-8289-3f3cbba3e580', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b955e6e-d819-5320-8289-3f3cbba3e580'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/29/news-quiz-august-29-2013/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | August 29, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-29T05:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23367892-188f-57f3-a9a4-bff30f913466', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23367892-188f-57f3-a9a4-bff30f913466'}, {'abstract': 'Matt Damon helps poor Indians get micro-finance for clean water and toilets.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/29/matt-damon-tries-to-get-clean-water-and-toilets-for-indias-poor/', 'snippet': 'Matt Damon helps poor Indians get micro-finance for clean water and toilets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matt Damon finds it a challenge to get people to care about water. It’s why he was in India from Aug. 23 to 26 on a four-day tour. Not to promote his latest film Elysium, a sci-fi dystopia with a socialist underpinning, but to help the rural and urban poor in India get access to clean water and sanitation by investing in tube wells, hand pumps and toilets with proper drainage facilities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank