cessful, Verizon would be able to shift from receiving dividends to being able to fully incorporate all of its profit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 8:27 p.m. |  With nearly 100 million Americans using Verizon Wireless for their cellphone service, it may not seem obvious that almost half of Verizon is owned by a company overseas.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Talks With Vodafone, Verizon Banks on Wireless Future', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Verizon Seeks Rest of Its Wireless Unit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vodafone Group Plc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-29T07:19:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen and Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63d606a2-3083-5420-a1c0-811c3d38289f', 'word_count': 1282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63d606a2-3083-5420-a1c0-811c3d38289f'}, {'abstract': 'The police in Pune detained a member of a right-wing Hindu group in the death last week of Narenda Dabholkar, who often debunked village mystics and wanted “black magic” outlawed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/30/world/asia/suspect-detained-in-killing-of-mysticism-foe-in-india.html', 'snippet': 'The police in Pune detained a member of a right-wing Hindu group in the death last week of Narenda Dabholkar, who often debunked village mystics and wanted “black magic” outlawed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — The police on Wednesday detained a member of Sanatan Sanstha, a right-wing Hindu organization, in  the killing last week of an activist who often debunked village mystics and had campaigned for a law banning “black magic.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspect Held in Killing of Anti-Mystic Activist in India', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suspect Held in Killing of Anti-Mystic Activist in India', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dabholkar, Narendra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pune (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Goa (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shinde, Sandeep', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sanatan Sanstha', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-29T07:42:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b31569bf-b711-5c95-813a-522a474cab7a', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b31569bf-b711-5c95-813a-522a474cab7a'}, {'abstract': 'Can you choose the word pair that correctly completes the sentences from the article?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/29/test-yourself-english-aug-29-2013/', 'snippet': 'Can you choose the word pair that correctly completes the sentences from the article?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the Opinionator blog post “Don’t Ask What I’m Writing.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Aug. 29, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-29T08:16:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbd1ccc6-6d46-5acf-a868-9c90040ebb99', 'word_count': 39, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbd1ccc6-6d46-5acf-a868-9c90040ebb99'}, {'abstract': 'Have you ever marched, protested or campaigned to help ensure that all people are treated fairly and without prejudice? If so, when?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/29/6-qs-about-the-news-thousands-gather-to-celebrate-a-dream-continue-a-struggle/', 'snippet': 'Have you ever marched, protested or campaigned to help ensure that all people are treated fairly and without prejudice? If so, when?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the article “Where King Stood, Obama Reframes a Dream for a New Era,” Peter Baker and Sheryl Gay Stolberg write about Wednesday’s commemoration of the 50th anniversary of the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.’s historic “I Have a Dream” speech.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '6 Q’s About the News | Thousands Gather to Celebrate a Dream and Continue a Struggle', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-29T08:30:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bd37bea-a3fe-5e95-a6b3-96a2fda8b41a', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bd37bea-a3fe-5e95-a6b3-96a2fda8b41a'}, {'abstract': 'He swore to his wife that his next novel would be short and fast. He lied.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/magazine/norman-rushs-brilliantly-broken-promise.html', 'snippet': 'He swore to his wife that his next novel would be short and fast. He lied.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One afternoon at the end of the summer of 2011, on the shady porch of a little red farmhouse near High Tor, in Rockland County, N.Y., the novelist Norman Rush, vigorous at 77, revealed himself as a man of great frankness. “I completely betrayed her,” Rush told me, astonishment in his voice over what he’d done to the woman sitting across from him, Elsa Rush, 76, his wife of 56 years.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/magazine/01rush1/mag-01Rush-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/09/01/magazine/01rush1/mag-01Rush-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/magazine/01rush1/mag-01Rush-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ