y announces $150 million in new financing, which it will use to build a worldwide sales and support organization. That could be the most serious challenge yet to EMC, but also takes Pure into new territory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pure Storage, an upstart maker of data storage equipment, hopes that $150 million is enough to take on a multibillion-dollar competitor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/technology/bits-purestorage/bits-purestorage-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/technology/bits-purestorage/bits-purestorage-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/technology/bits-purestorage/bits-purestorage-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/28/technology/bits-purestorage/bits-purestorage-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pure Storage Goes Global', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data Storage', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EMC Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pure Storage Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-29T11:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55f11f26-b161-58ea-bdaa-0061082ba467', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55f11f26-b161-58ea-bdaa-0061082ba467'}, {'abstract': 'One of my clients started planning the sale of his business six months before he wanted to sell. Another client started planning 10 years before he wanted to sell. Guess which one did better.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/29/the-right-and-wrong-way-to-sell-a-business/', 'snippet': 'One of my clients started planning the sale of his business six months before he wanted to sell. Another client started planning 10 years before he wanted to sell. Guess which one did better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year, I used to get together with a client who was a business owner, and every year I would ask him, “Bruce, have you told your guys that you want them to buy the business?” He had a plan that he would eventually sell his contracting business to his senior executives, but he had yet to inform them of this fact.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wrong Way to Sell a Business', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-29T11:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Patrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fed5b05-7b41-5ccf-a757-01d317c0cca