 her to a grueling workout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Li Na hired Carlos Rodriguez a year ago to coach her late-career drive to the top of women’s tennis — demoting her husband once again in the process — she had one prerequisite. “I needed someone really tough,” she told me. Even at \xa031, five years after “flying solo” from China’s state sports system, Li still possesses the punishing work ethic inculcated by her Chinese coaches. Two years ago, she fired a foreign coach because, she said with a laugh, “he was way too nice.” Rodriguez is gentle on the outside, too. But the wiry Rodriguez, an Argentine, who coached the former world No. 1 Justine Henin for 15 years, is renowned for his insistence on peak physical and psychological fitness. With “Kaluosi,” as she calls him (a transliteration of “Carlos”), Li knew she was signing up for pain. She just didn’t know how much.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/magazine/28-li-na-weights/28-li-na-weights-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/28/magazine/28-li-na-weights/28-li-na-weights-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/magazine/28-li-na-weights/28-li-na-weights-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 560, 'width': 841, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/magazine/28-li-na-weights/28-li-na-weights-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 560, 'width': 841, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/28/magazine/28-li-na-weights/28-li-na-weights