aseball cap. If you’re angling for membership in the honor society, slip on these striped leather loafers from Dries Van Noten or tote about town with a punchy pouchette from Tommy Hilfiger.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Market Report | Styles That’ll Put You at the Head of the Class', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Market Report: Top of the Class', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hilfiger, Tommy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Noten, Dries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watanabe, Junya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BALENCIAGA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gucci', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'J Crew Group', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-29T19:06:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26badd4d-4859-5803-8e25-def868860812', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26badd4d-4859-5803-8e25-def868860812'}, {'abstract': 'A guessing game with Michael McKean.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/29/can-you-guess-what-this-is-14/', 'snippet': 'A guessing game with Michael McKean.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RULES1. Player has not seen the photo beforehand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can You Guess What This Is?', 'kicker': 'Summer Game', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-29T19:07:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamara Shopsin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shopsin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01555a2d-c422-567f-bd32-8ca874c5da0d', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01555a2d-c422-567f-bd32-8ca874c5da0d'}, {'abstract': 'A city where the local food movement got a jump start is going further, and applying it to the space itself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/travel/portland-me-locavore-in-menu-and-decor.html', 'snippet': 'A city where the local food movement got a jump start is going further, and applying it to the space itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hardly a secret that Portland, Me., is a food-lover’s paradise. Stroll down the sloping streets and cobbled lanes in the heart of this small maritime city, and you can’t miss the evidence: bakeries fragrant with just-baked sour cherry pies; indie coffee shops selling wood-roasted beans; bars where cocktails might be infused with local rhubarb or kale or blueberries; and, of course, restaurants of seemingly every ethnic and gastronomic stripe.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/travel/01CHOICE4/01CHOICE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/09/01/travel/01CHOICE4/01CHOICE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/travel/01CHOICE4/01CHOICE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/travel/01CHOICE4/01CHOICE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2001, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/travel/01CHOICE4/01CHOICE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/09/01/travel/01CHOICE4/01CHOICE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/travel/01CHOICE4/01CHOICE4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Portland, Me.: Locavore in Menu and Décor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Locavore in Menu and Décor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MacNeille, Suzanne', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Me)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Local Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-29T19:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Suzanne MacNeille', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Suzanne', 'midd