 and a news conference on Thursday exemplified the mixed success Anthony D. Weiner is having drawing reporters, who just weeks ago mobbed his events.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/30/nyregion/for-weiner-these-days-crowds-arent-easy-to-find.html', 'snippet': 'A rally and a news conference on Thursday exemplified the mixed success Anthony D. Weiner is having drawing reporters, who just weeks ago mobbed his events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few short weeks ago, Anthony D. Weiner stood at the pinnacle of political celebrity, his every voter handshake chronicled by a voracious mob of reporters.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Weiner These Days, Crowds Aren’t Easy to Find', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tiny Crowd Hears Weiner’s Tax Plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T00:52:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40886b55-d9f1-5373-b60d-5e9260d16d6c', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40886b55-d9f1-5373-b60d-5e9260d16d6c'}, {'abstract': 'Taylor Farms, a giant supplier of produce and other food products, has a recent record of recalls that industry experts call high.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/30/business/taylor-farms-big-food-supplier-grapples-with-frequent-recalls.html', 'snippet': 'Taylor Farms, a giant supplier of produce and other food products, has a recent record of recalls that industry experts call high.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Taylor Farms, the large vegetable producer whose salad mix is being investigated in connection with an outbreak of illness involving hundreds of people in 22 states, has had an unusual number of voluntary recalls for potentially tainted products in the last three years.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/30/business/foodjumpsub/foodjumpsub-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/30/business/foodjumpsub/foodjumpsub-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/30/business/foodjumpsub/foodjumpsub-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/30/business/foodjumpsub/foodjumpsub-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/30/business/foodjumpsub/foodjumpsub-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/30/business/foodjumpsub/foodjumpsub-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/30/business/foodjumpsub/foodjumpsub-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taylor Farms, Big Food Supplier, Grapples With Frequent Recalls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Food Supplier Grapples With Frequent Recalls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strom, Stephanie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taylor Farms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T00:54:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Strom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6b0688f-d290-51e1-8d9e-91a0af20e4a7', 'word_count': 891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6b0688f-d290-51e1-8d9e-91a0af20e4a7'}, {'abstract': 'According to the United States Department of Agriculture, Taylor Farms has conducted ten recalls since February of 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/30/business/recalls-by-taylor-farms.html', 'snippet': 'According to the United States Department of Agriculture, Taylor Farms has conducted ten recalls since February of 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUNE 2013 Salad greens used in restaurants. Tainted with bacteria sickening more than 600 people. A little more than 200 of those cases were linked to greens supplied by Taylor.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recalls by Taylor Farms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recalls by Taylor Farms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taylor Farms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T00:57:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bfe45d7-8677-5589-821b-9a28ad0e0f81', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bfe45d7-8677-5589-821b-9a28ad0e0f81'}, {'abstract': 'The digital village square is the marketplace of ideas. But what if that marketplace looks like the “Star Wars” bar — or worse?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/29/toxic-populi/', 'snippet': 'The digital village square is the marketplace of ideas. But what if that marketplace looks like the “Star Wars” bar — or worse?', 'lead_paragraph': 'By now, most people have heard something about Delbert Belton, known as Shorty, the World War II veteran beaten to death last week in a parking lot of the town where I grew up, Spokane, Wash. At age 88, Belton was the Greatest Generation in a five-foot frame: he survived the Battle of Okinawa and worked 30 years in the cauldron of the local aluminum plant, only to get his head bashed in by couple of thugs in search of his wallet, as police reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toxic Populi', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spokane (Wash)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T01:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01f20f15-4046-59b5-83c4-e0fc870dc100', 'word_count': 1001, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01f20f15-4046-59b5-83c4-e0fc870dc100'}, {'abstract': 'The military strategy that the Obama administration is considering is not linked to its larger diplomatic strategy of persuading President Bashar al-Assad of Syria to yield power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/30/world/middleeast/aim-of-a-us-attack-on-syria-sharpening-a-blurred-red-line.html', 'snippet': 'The military strategy that the Obama administration is considering is not linked to its larger diplomatic strategy of persuading President Bashar al-Assad of Syria to yield power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The goal of the cruise missile strikes the United States is planning to carry out in Syria is to restore the smudged “red line” that President Obama drew a year ago against the use of poison gas.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aim of U.S. Attack: Restore a ‘Red Line’ That Became Blurred', 'kicker': 'Military Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aim of U.S. Attack: Restore a ‘Red Line’ That Became Blurred', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T01:04:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Military Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5ea9cce-e7d7-5f19-90d4-03049f0d7d07', 'word_count': 1056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5ea9cce-e7d7-5f19-90d4-03049f0d7d07'}, {'abstract': 'The cuisine at Bistro 12 is Mediterranean, but reflects the owners’ origins, in Madeira.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/nyregion/a-review-of-bistro-12-in-tarrytown.html', 'snippet': 'The cuisine at Bistro 12 is Mediterranean, but reflects the owners’ origins, in Madeira.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a sultry August night, two women stood just inside the door at Bistro 12, appraising the menu. Regrettably, their eyes did not wander to our table, where summery dishes were arrayed like so many luminous seashells: grilled octopus on a bed of wilted, garlic-strewn escarole; red and golden beets crowned with crescents of fresh orange; chunky red tomatoes and slips of purple onion tossed in a oregano-flecked vinaigrette; and fresh sardines cradled in endive leaves. As they turned to leave, having decided to try their luck elsewhere, my impulse was to jump up and tell them to stay. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/nyregion/01DINEWE2/01DINEWE2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 490, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/09/01/nyregion/01DINEWE2/01DINEWE2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 490}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/nyregion/01DINEWE2/01DINEWE2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 836, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/nyregion/01DINEWE2/01DINEWE2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1673, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/nyregion/01DINEWE2/01DINEWE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/09/01/nyregion/01DINEWE2/01DINEWE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/nyregion/01DINEWE2/01DINEWE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tilting Toward Portugal', 'kicker': 'Dining Review | Westchester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tilting Toward Portugal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tarrytown (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bistro 12 (Tarrytown, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T01:07:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a4c3e5a-59d8-5532-8a79-4b808cfc1c32', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a4c3e5a-59d8-5532-8a79-4b808cfc1c32'}, {'abstract': '“Mother of George,” a new film by the Nigerian-born director Andrew Dosunmu, looks at a newlywed immigrant in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/movies/mother-of-george-a-film-by-andrew-dosunmu.html', 'snippet': '“Mother of George,” a new film by the Nigerian-born director Andrew Dosunmu, looks at a newlywed immigrant in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the Yoruba of Africa, said Andrew Dosunmu, the Nigerian-born director and photographer, uncles are held in special regard. “If my uncle walks in here,” he said over lunch in Brooklyn, “I introduce him as my dad, because he’s responsible for me if my father’s not around. Your uncle is the same as your dad. The idea is, it’s the same blood, and there’s an obligation.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/movies/01DOSUNMU1_SPAN/01DOSUNMU1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/09/01/movies/01DOSUNMU1_S