w-york-city/', 'snippet': 'How do you feel about these graffiti projects popping up around New York City? Which murals do you like best? Why?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the article “A Feast of Urban Scrawl, Luminous and Legal,” Randy Kennedy provides a guided tour of what he considers to be the best graffiti art around New York City.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '6 Q’s About the News | A Tour of Graffiti Art Around New York City', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T08:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c82e308-2720-5f87-a99c-7ef014a77e0e', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c82e308-2720-5f87-a99c-7ef014a77e0e'}, {'abstract': 'When Nicolas Janowski travels the western reaches of the Amazon, he is stirred by “the exuberance of the jungle” — its spirituality, humanity and “voluptuousness.”', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/30/an-ex-anthropologists-eye-on-the-amazon/', 'snippet': 'When Nicolas Janowski travels the western reaches of the Amazon, he is stirred by “the exuberance of the jungle” — its spirituality, humanity and “voluptuousness.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nicolas Janowski lives in Buenos Aires, one of the most cosmopolitan cities in South America. But in recent years he has spent as much time as he can traveling around a region that is about as different from his home town as can be imagined — the western reaches of the Amazon, with its dizzying and imposing mix of jungle, rivers, mountains and savannah extending over Bolivia, Ecuador and Peru.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Amazon, Through an Anthropologist’s Eye', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTHROPOLOGY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMAZON RIVER BASIN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T09:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdeed6ca-f6e0-5d94-85c8-dfc75280a301', 'word_count': 1867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdeed6ca-f6e0-5d94-85c8-dfc75280a301'}, {'abstract': 'The Latin American telecommunications giant has threatened to walk away from its proposed 7.2 billion euro, or $9.5 billion, bid for the Dutch cellphone operator KPN after a local foundation moved to block the takeover.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/08/30/america-movil-threatens-to-pull-bid-for-dutch-cellphone-operator/', 'snippet': 'The Latin American telecommunications giant has threatened to walk away from its proposed 7.2 billion euro, or $9.5 billion, bid for the Dutch cellphone operator KPN after a local foundation moved to block the takeover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The Latin American telecommunications giant América Móvil threatened on Friday to walk away from its proposed bid of 7.2 billion euros, or $9.5 billion, for the Dutch cellphone operator KPN after a local foundation moved to block the takeover.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'America Movil Threatens to Pull Bid for Dutch Cellphone Operator', 'kicker': 'Dea