n': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da644ce6-7b3a-53b5-a71c-bcddf9869e99', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da644ce6-7b3a-53b5-a71c-bcddf9869e99'}, {'abstract': 'The recently opened eatery Vinatería is a case study in sustainable interior design that’s simply chic, rather than conspicuously eco-conscious.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/30/the-making-of-a-restaurant-in-harlem-where-everything-old-is-new-again/', 'snippet': 'The recently opened eatery Vinatería is a case study in sustainable interior design that’s simply chic, rather than conspicuously eco-conscious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We can all agree on the value of reuse, repurposing, recycling, upcycling. But too often in interior design projects, these processes are treated as ends rather than means, with results that are usually more earnest than elegant. At Vinatería, a Harlem restaurant that opened in April, almost every material has had a previous life (or lives), but that’s not what you notice about the room. Instead, you see a subtle layering of color and form and sophisticated details. Yes, the design is environmentally friendly. But above all, Vinatería is chic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Making Of | A Restaurant in Harlem Where Everything Old Is New Again', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T13:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/859153be-d67e-53df-b176-eef3ce30c41f', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/859153be-d67e-53df-b176-eef3ce30c41f'}, {'abstract': 'Asia recovered; why can’t Europe?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/30/the-baht-and-the-bubble-excuse/', 'snippet': 'Asia recovered; why can’t Europe?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kevin O’Rourke has been saying for a while that it’s useful to think of Ireland as “Thailand without the baht“. In this context, the history of the Asian crisis sheds some light on one of the ways defenders of European austerity policies move the goalposts: by claiming that the pre-crisis peak isn’t relevant for comparison purposes, because it was inflated by a bubble.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Baht and the Bubble Excuse', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T13:21:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9100ab6f-5bc5-51a3-bb89-fde4774a04ae', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9100ab6f-5bc5-51a3-bb89-fde4774a04ae'}, {'abstract': 'Indian spiritual leader Asaram Bapu, who often condemned sexual desire, is on the run from police after charges of sexual assault.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/30/the-advantages-of-being-asaram-bapu/', 'snippet': 'Indian spiritual leader Asaram Bapu, who often condemned sexual desire, is on the run from police after charges of sexual assault.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Asumal Sirumalani, a popular Indian spiritual leader who is known to his followers as Asaram Bapu, has fought a long battle against sex.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credi