e}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9caab17-7b2d-510e-bf6d-f1c9c5b4c20a', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9caab17-7b2d-510e-bf6d-f1c9c5b4c20a'}, {'abstract': 'Memories afflict a woman as her brother struggles with AIDS.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/books/review/paris-was-the-place-by-susan-conley.html', 'snippet': 'Memories afflict a woman as her brother struggles with AIDS.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Paris, during his sabbatical in the early 1980s, a dear friend proposed we meet not for drinks at the Café de Flore but for ice cream at Berthillon. “The doctors have forbidden me alcohol,” he said. “In France! Can you imagine?” He’d been having odd health problems, one after the other, that they couldn’t explain. Months later, he developed Pneumocystis pneumonia and got his explanation. He died soon thereafter; our naïve days were at an end.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/books/review/01KLINE/01KLINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 907, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/09/01/books/review/01KLINE/01KLINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 907}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/books/review/01KLINE/01KLINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 678, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/books/review/01KLINE/01KLINE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1356, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/books/review/01KLINE/01KLINE-thumbSt