stract': 'This week, Judith Newman talks about Teddy Gaston Getty’s new memoir and Evan J. Mandery discusses “A Wild Justice.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/08/30/books/review/01books_pod-blog.html', 'snippet': 'This week, Judith Newman talks about Teddy Gaston Getty’s new memoir and Evan J. Mandery discusses “A Wild Justice.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Judith Newman talks about Teddy Gaston Getty’s new memoir and Evan J. Mandery discusses “A Wild Justice.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside The New York Times Book Review: Life With J. Paul Getty', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T15:13:07+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/be843aba-0010-5876-a11d-a91dee165b14', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/be843aba-0010-5876-a11d-a91dee165b14'}, {'abstract': '“If you can say ‘no’ to persistent Indian grandparents, you can say ‘no’ to anyone.”', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/30/for-girls-in-india-the-pressure-to-conform-comes-from-family/', 'snippet': '“If you can say ‘no’ to persistent Indian grandparents, you can say ‘no’ to anyone.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I recently watched the remarkable Malala Yousafzai speak at the United Nations to commemorate a day that is named after her. The 16-year-old who was shot by the Taliban, and has since become a celebrated activist for education and women’s rights, said that Malala Day was for “every boy and every girl who have raised their voice for their rights.” She bravely reinterpreted Islam and accused the extremists of being afraid of books, pens and education. “The power of the voice of women frightens them,” she said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Girls in India, the Pressure to Conform Comes From Family', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grandparents', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yousafzai, Malala', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T15:14:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shoba Narayan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shoba', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Narayan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51df877d-2f08-530f-b02e-0fcf6a8c9377', 'word_count': 942, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51df877d-2f08-530f-b02e-0fcf6a8c9377'}, {'abstract': 'Beirutis returning from France bring a craving for Parisian life, while the young embrace a Franco-flavored hybrid.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/travel/call-it-beyrouth-beirut-with-a-french-accent.html', 'snippet': 'Beirutis returning from France bring a craving for Parisian life, while the young embrace a Franco-flavored hybrid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was finishing an aperitif on the porch at Villa Clara while other guests tossed pétanque balls in the nearby yard. The hotel’s 4-year-old namesake cozied up to her papa, showing off her latest crayon creation. 