2013/08/30/business/Some-Banks-Recover-Most-Dont.html', 'snippet': 'Five years ago, the financial crisis was on the verge of getting much worse. Now, an index of bank stocks around the world has recovered most of the ground it lost. But most large banks are still down, some by significant amounts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five years ago, the financial crisis was on the verge of getting much worse. Now, an index of bank stocks around the world has recovered most of the ground it lost. But most large banks are still down, some by significant amounts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/30/business/0831CHARTS-FOR-FRONT/0831CHARTS-FOR-FRONT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1081, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/30/business/0831CHARTS-FOR-FRONT/0831CHARTS-FOR-FRONT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1081}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/30/business/0831CHARTS-FOR-FRONT/0831CHARTS-FOR-FRONT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 569, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/30/business/0831CHARTS-FOR-FRONT/0831CHARTS-FOR-FRONT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1081, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/30/business/0831CHARTS-FOR-FRONT/0831CHARTS-FOR-FRONT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/30/business/0831CHARTS-FOR-FRONT/0831CHARTS-FOR-FRONT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/30/business/0831CHARTS-FOR-FRONT/0831CHARTS-FOR-FRONT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Charts: Some Banks Recover, Most Don’t', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T15:29:23+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/612fc222-645a-532e-8f03-0b6ba602c358', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/612fc222-645a-532e-8f03-0b6ba602c358'}, {'abstract': 'The truly underwhelming Obama stimulus.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/30/too-little-gone-too-soon/', 'snippet': 'The truly underwhelming Obama stimulus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the things you always heard, back when we were actually talking about stimulus rather than fighting a rearguard action against destructive austerity, was the claim that stimulus spending would inevitably end up becoming a permanent fixture of the economy. This was always said with an air of worldly wisdom — of course that’s how these things work! — even though history said very much the opposite.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Little, Gone Too Soon', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T15:29:59+0000', 'document_type': 'arti