rly 300 comments. And the overwhelming sentiment among the respondents was more generous than the empty-handed guests: they would ignore the oversight, whether it was intentional or not.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Empty-Handed Guests? Just Forgive or Forget', 'kicker': 'Comments', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Empty-Handed Guests? Just Forgive or Forget', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Timothy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T17:15:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy R. Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08960aa7-8e81-5055-8586-c6874f37929b', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08960aa7-8e81-5055-8586-c6874f37929b'}, {'abstract': 'As the administration’s frontman for American intervention, Secretary of State John Kerry is able and willing to be more outspoken than the president he serves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/31/world/middleeast/john-kerry-syria.html', 'snippet': 'As the administration’s frontman for American intervention, Secretary of State John Kerry is able and willing to be more outspoken than the president he serves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Jabbing his finger at the lectern, his voice forceful, his words brimming with indignation, John Kerry laid out the case like the prosecutor he once was, making a closing argument to a skeptical jury.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kerry Becomes Chief Advocate for U.S. Attack', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kerry Becomes Chief Advocate For U.S. Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T17:17:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker and Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/839a88cc-dac9-58bf-9785-30cb0706c2aa', 'word_count': 1210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/839a88cc-dac9-58bf-9785-30cb0706c2aa'}, {'abstract': 'A vote in Parliament left President Obama without a key ally after misjudging the politics of military action in the Middle East.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/31/world/after-british-vote-unusual-isolation-for-us-on-syria.html', 'snippet': 'A vote in Parliament left President Obama without a key ally after misjudging the politics of military action in the Middle East.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — With a few exceptions in the past half-century, there has been a simple rule of thumb when it comes to international conflict: America does not use force without Britain at its side.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After British Vote, Unusual Isolation for U.S. on Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T17:32:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By David E. Sanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Sanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37e60169-da6e-5997-9335-06b412436a5d', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37e60169-da6e-5997-9335-06b412436a5d'}, {'abstract': 'Five dishes featuring cucumbers — a perfect food for hot end-of-summer days — inspired by cuisines around the globe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/02/health/cucumber-and-radish-salad-with-yogurt-and-cumin.html', 'snippet': 'Five dishes featuring cucumbers — a perfect food for hot end-of-summer days — inspired by cuisines around the globe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last spring, on a whim, I planted one cucumber plant in my small tomato garden and it grew like Jack’s beanstalk. It’s been putting out long, straight, sturdy seedless cucumbers all summer and I’ve been inspired to go beyond the Greek salads and Balkan cucumber and yogurt soups that I customarily enjoy throughout the season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/31/science/02recipehealth/02recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/31/science/02recipehealth/02recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/31/science/02recipehealth/02recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/31/science/02recipehealth/02recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/31/science/02recipehealth/02recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/31/science/02recipehealth/02recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/31/