ng singer and songwriter John Legend, 34, has a new album, “Love in the Future,” scheduled for release on Tuesday. He lives with his fiancée, Christine Teigen, a model, in New York and Los Angeles.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For John Legend, No Colors Anymore, Except for Swimming', 'kicker': 'What I Wore ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Colors Anymore, Except for Swimming', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T19:14:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bee Shapiro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shapiro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ca40dc6-f68a-5899-8028-b466f3c3fc21', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ca40dc6-f68a-5899-8028-b466f3c3fc21'}, {'abstract': 'In his Driven review for The Times, Tom Voelk finds the full-size sedan holds its own against rivals like the Toyota Avalon and Chevrolet Impala.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/30/video-with-the-cadenza-kia-moves-into-a-nicer-neighborhood/', 'snippet': 'In his Driven review for The Times, Tom Voelk finds the full-size sedan holds its own against rivals like the Toyota Avalon and Chevrolet Impala.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five years ago, the suggestion of a Kia with a retail price of nearly $42,000 would have been met with laughter and incredulous looks. But just as Toyota and Honda moved up in the 1970s and ’80s from their economy car roots, Kia has branched out with a range of new models, each generation showing more polish and sophistication than the cars that came before.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: With the Cadenza, Kia Moves Into a Nicer Neighborhood', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kia Motors Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T19:14:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Voelk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Voelk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b5ccd3b-1043-5e95-9f95-83f26e964fb7', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b5ccd3b-1043-5e95-9f95-83f26e964fb7'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Coughlin, known for his ranting style and strict discipline, has mellowed after the birth of his grandchildren, but some of his rules will never go away.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/sports/football/a-kinder-gentler-coughlin-still-makes-the-giants-stand-up-straight.html', 'snippet': 'Tom Coughlin, known for his ranting style and strict discipline, has mellowed after the birth of his grandchildren, but some of his rules will never go away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — When Tom Coughlin’s children were growing up, they developed a routine when it came time to ask their father for something.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/sports/01giants1/01giants1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/09/01/sports/01giants1/01giants1-articleLarge.jpg', 'x