t of the U.S. Open this week, Venus Williams made quite a statement with her purple braids. Seeing her made me think of Alexander McQueen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before getting knocked out of the U.S. Open this week, Venus Williams made quite a statement with her purple braids, piled in a knot above her visor and complimenting her printed tennis dress. You may cry fault: what about another player, Bethanie Mattek-Sands, who seems to be working on the colors of the rainbow? She’s also tattooed. People who grew up in the Evert-Connors era may gag, but exotic hair color on the courts is merely a step from the streets, and, in fact, it’s a lot more compelling.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From McQueen to Venus: Brave Women', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From McQueen to Venus, a Salute to the Brave', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McQueen, Alexander', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Venus', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T19:40:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/849e5395-cc16-5996-8e17-beb8e8b64cd8', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/849e5395-cc16-5996-8e17-beb8e8b64cd8'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama said that he had not made a final decision about Syria, but that he was not considering any mili