', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/arts/music/putting-poetry-above-politics.html', 'snippet': 'The songwriter Mohsen Namjoo stirs things up in Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The songwriter\xa0Mohsen Namjoo\xa0stirs things up in Iran. Mr. Namjoo, who performs\xa0Saturday\xa0at the Asia Society, plays the setar, a long-necked lute, and is steeped in Persian classical and literary traditions. But in Iran, where Western music was banned in 2005, Mr. Namjoo decided to fuse Persian music with rock and jazz and to sing — in a voice that can push from the nuances of Persian improvisation to the rougher attack of the blues — about the conditions facing his generation: unemployment, repression, violence. Though he was not allowed to perform in public or licensed to sell CDs, his music spread in private events, on the black market and via YouTube and radio. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting Poetry Above Politics', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putting Poetry Above Politics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Asia Society', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Namjoo, Mohsen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Avenue (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T21:33:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bd2f150-084e-5033-8a9f