 Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/c77e283b-fcef-52d9-b161-93a8fb44ef6b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/c77e283b-fcef-52d9-b161-93a8fb44ef6b'}, {'abstract': 'Will Sheff has drawn on his childhood in New Hampshire for his band Okkervil River’s new record, “The Silver Gymnasium.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/31/arts/music/a-treasure-map-of-a-childhood-filled-with-magic-and-newts.html', 'snippet': 'Will Sheff has drawn on his childhood in New Hampshire for his band Okkervil River’s new record, “The Silver Gymnasium.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'MERIDEN, N.H. — The singer, songwriter and multi-instrumentalist Will Sheff founded the indie-rock band Okkervil River in Austin, Tex., in 1998 and now lives in Brooklyn. But memories of his years growing up in this bucolic New England hamlet in the 1980s have never been far from his mind, so when it came time to make a new CD, he decided to return home — in song and in person.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Treasure Map of a Childhood, Filled With Magic and Newts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Treasure Map of a Childhood, Filled With Magic and Newts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Okkervil River', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheff, Will', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-30T23:15:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5ddd929-d4bb-5d57-865b-47a64c437480', 'word_count': 1188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5ddd929-d4bb-5d57-865b-47a64c437480'}, {'abstract': 'George J. Mitchell, the former senator and Mideast envoy, is trying to mediate the Minnesota Orchestra’s bitter labor dispute.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/31/arts/music/minnesota-orchestra-calls-in-big-gun-in-dispute.html', 'snippet': 'George J. Mitchell, the former senator and Mideast envoy, is trying to mediate the Minnesota Orchestra’s bitter labor dispute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He brokered peace in Northern Ireland and spent two frustrating years as an envoy in the Middle East. Now George J. Mitchell, the former senator from Maine, is trying to bring peace to the Midwest, as the mediator in the Minnesota Orchestra’s bitter labor dispute.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/31/arts/31VANSKA/31VANSKA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/31/arts/31VANSKA/31VANSKA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/31/arts/31VANSKA/31VANSKA-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/31/arts/31VANSKA/31VANSKA-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1398, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/3