organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/043d03e7-fa2d-51ab-b266-d1abb697d51a', 'word_count': 1612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/043d03e7-fa2d-51ab-b266-d1abb697d51a'}, {'abstract': 'A mysterious document offers a rare glimpse into the mind of a former slave living through the Civil War.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/08/30/a-colored-mans-constitution/', 'snippet': 'A mysterious document offers a rare glimpse into the mind of a former slave living through the Civil War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Patrolling the streets of New Orleans on the evening of Sept. 1, 1863, a police officer found a small sheaf of handwritten papers. They were hard to read, written mostly in halting, misspelled English. Glancing over a page, the policeman may have seen at first only snatches of apparently incoherent prose: “Carrige Drivers preachers of the Gospel the best Soldiers the united States Can Raise but the tel lies Sometimes and so dos all negro traders the get Drunk and lawiers and merchants.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Colored Man’s Constitution', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-31T00:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Hager', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hager', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1212dde-1662-5444-9676-c6df19795fc0', 'word_count': 1806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1212dde-1662-5444-9676-c6df19795fc0'}, {'abstract': 'A police inspection of a barbershop in Ridgewood, 