1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae42fa5e-8c7d-501d-891c-f0cdb33621b0'}, {'abstract': 'Liberia doesn’t deserve its reputation for press freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/31/opinion/jailed-for-journalism.html', 'snippet': 'Liberia doesn’t deserve its reputation for press freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONROVIA, Liberia — IT’S not uncommon in African countries like Zimbabwe and Ethiopia for newspapers to be shut, and their editors jailed. But the newspaper I edit doesn’t operate in a dictatorship. We are in Liberia, the West’s poster child for postwar democracy building. Our president, Ellen Johnson Sirleaf, is a Nobel laureate who is celebrated by the likes of Bill Gates, Warren E. Buffett and Bono and has positioned herself as a champion of a free press. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jailed for Journalism', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jailed for Journalism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson Sirleaf, Ellen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libel and Slander', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-31T01:10:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rodney Sieh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rodney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sieh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/491df598-38a7-5c1f-961a-60bed78db557', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'ny