ragraph': 'For most of the summer, Bill de Blasio maintained a robust public appearance schedule as he ran across New York City in an attempt to meet voters. On an average day, Mr. de Blasio could be found greeting commuters at subway stations in the morning, visiting with people at senior centers during lunch and holding news conferences later in the day to introduce initiatives or proposals he would follow as mayor.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'De Blasio Campaigns Less as Quinn Steps Up Her Pace', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'De Blasio Campaigns Less As Quinn Steps Up Her Pace', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, William C Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-31T01:58:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Burgess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burgess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7d89cb9-c8a3-5db4-a83f-bd282ab7a823', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7d89cb9-c8a3-5db4-a83f-bd282ab7a823'}, {'abstract': 'The judge, Frederik Harhoff from Denmark, drew attention in June when he questioned recent acquittals of top Serb and Croat commanders who had been convicted of grave crimes during the wars in the former Yugoslavia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/08/31/world/europe/international-judge-is-removed-from-case-over-apparent-bias.html', 'snippet': 'The judge, Frederik Harhoff from Denmark, drew attention in June when he questioned recent acquittals of top Serb and Croat commanders who had been convicted of grave crimes during the wars in the former Yugoslavia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE HAGUE — An international judge who criticized the president of the United Nations tribunal for the former Yugoslavia and the court’s recent decisions has been removed from his current case on the grounds that his remarks make him appear to be biased.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'International Judge Is Removed From Case Over Apparent Bias', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'International Judge Is Removed From Case Over Apparent Bias', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simons, Marlise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Tribunal for the former Yugoslavia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harhoff, Frederik', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seselj, Vojislav', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yugoslavia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Croatia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bosnia and Herzegovina', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-31T01:59:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': Non