5:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b400a065-67ab-57a7-b236-452836d67adc', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b400a065-67ab-57a7-b236-452836d67adc'}, {'abstract': 'Income inequality has grown for decades in the United States, but by one measure it has accelerated during the Obama administration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/business/income-gap-grows-wider-and-faster.html', 'snippet': 'Income inequality has grown for decades in the United States, but by one measure it has accelerated during the Obama administration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INCOME inequality in the United States has been growing for decades, but the trend appears to have accelerated during the Obama administration. One measure of this is the relationship between median and average wages.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Income Gap Grows Wider (and Faster)', 'kicker': 'Datapoints', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Income Gap Grows Wider (And Faster)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Katz, Lawrence F', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-31T16:57:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Bernasek', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernasek', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dea434ef-6a45-5c03-82a3-95cd7ed0167f', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dea434ef-6a45-5c03-82a3-95cd7ed0167f'}, {'abstract': 'In trying to help the long-term unemployed, a career counselor says patience and understanding are vital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/jobs/conquering-frustration-on-the-road-back-to-work.html', 'snippet': 'In trying to help the long-term unemployed, a career counselor says patience and understanding are vital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’VE been the director of a career counseling and consulting practice, BBCS Counseling Services, with my husband, Mitch Baskin, for 17 years. Our clients range from seasoned executives to recent college graduates. Across all age groups over the past few years, we’ve been counseling more of the long-term unemployed than ever before.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/business/01-PRESUB/01-PRESUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 520, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/09/01/business/01-PRESUB/01-PRESUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 520}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/business/01-PRESUB/01-PRESUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 887, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/business/01-PRESUB/01-PRESUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1775, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJum