'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/sunday-review/political-choices-image/political-choices-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Political Choices', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-31T18:16:24+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sunday Review', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/431e58eb-6b3b-57c5-8615-1ab0d9a6b0b7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/431e58eb-6b3b-57c5-8615-1ab0d9a6b0b7'}, {'abstract': 'It’s time to pause and take stock of the accomplishments and shortcomings from the first year on the job.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/opinion/sunday/a-year-in-the-life-of-a-watchdog.html', 'snippet': 'It’s time to pause and take stock of the accomplishments and shortcomings from the first year on the job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S a Monday morning in August — last Monday, to be precise — and more than 500 e-mails have arrived in the public editor’s in-box. Some are spam. Some are requests for corrections or assignments, which can be sent to another desk. But a bunch, maybe two dozen, are legitimate topics for investigation or exposition. As my crack assistant, Meghan Gourley, does triage on the e-mail, I pick a subject for a blog post that seems timely, important and of broad interest — The Times’s use of anonymous sources, particularly on that day’s front page — and start reporting it.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'x