'uri': 'nyt://article/cbf48160-e949-551b-aa07-3af696693893'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo is clearly a fan of the Adirondacks. Now he can make sure that a major addition to the park is preserved.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/opinion/sunday/new-yorks-living-wilderness.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo is clearly a fan of the Adirondacks. Now he can make sure that a major addition to the park is preserved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For those who cherish New York State’s magnificent Adirondack Park, Gov. Andrew Cuomo’s summertime efforts to promote tourism there — like racing Mayor Michael Bloomberg in a white-water rafting competition on the Indian River — have offered diversions from local economic worries, uncertain weather and supersized mosquitoes. He has also been busy hawking the region’s wine, beer, food, hikes and kayaking.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/sunday-review/01editorialSUB/01editorialSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/09/01/sunday-review/01editorialSUB/01editorialSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/sunday-review/01editorialSUB/01editorialSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/sunday-review/01editorialSUB/01editorialSUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1538, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/sunday-review/01editorialSUB/01editorialSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/09/01/sunday-review/01editorialSUB/01editorialSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/09/01/sunday-review/01editorialSUB/01editorialSUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s Living Wilderness', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York’s Living Wilderness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Randolph, Eleanor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ADIRONDACK MOUNTAINS (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wilderness Areas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature Conservancy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADIRONDACK COUNCIL', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADIRONDACK PARK AGENCY', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Adirondack Park (NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-31T18:39:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eleanor Randolph', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eleanor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Randolph', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f76a2f09-03d0-51bc-8434-921033a8af15', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f76a2f09-03d0-51bc-8434-921033a8af15'}, {'abstract': 'A new strategy for protecting access to the ballot box is coming into focus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/01/opinion/sunday/plan-b-for-voting-rights.html', 'snippet': 'A new strategy for protecting access to the ballot box is coming into focus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Voting-rights advocates generally don’t look to Justice Antonin Scalia for comfort. During oral arguments earlier this year in Shelby County v. Holder, the case in which the Supreme Court struck down a central part of the Voting Rights Act of 1965, Justice Scalia called the act a “perpetuation of racial entitlement.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plan B for Voting Rights', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plan B for Voting Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalia, Antonin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-08-31T18:39:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Wegman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wegman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ae640dc-9d34-5